      "comment": "Initialize SEH exception frame fields before protected block execution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get pointer to dwCurrentLevel field in SEH frame\n2. Zero dwCurrentLevel (initial handler state = disabled)\n3. Clear pUnwindTable (no unwind records registered)\n4. Store self-referential pointer in dwCurrentLevel for canary validation\n5. Clear pExceptionRecord pointer\n6. Store bitwise NOT of pointer in pUnwindTable as validation signature\n\nParameters:\npSehFrame (SehFrame *) - Pointer to SEH frame structure to initialize\n\nReturns:\nvoid - SEH frame fields initialized for use with __try/__except blocks\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset   Size   Field              Type               Description\n  0x00     4      pExceptionRecord   void *             Pointer to exception record\n  0x04     4      dwCurrentLevel     uint               Current exception level / self-ptr canary\n  0x08     4      pUnwindTable       SehUnwindRecord *  Pointer to unwind chain / inverted canary\n\nPhantom Variables:\n  local_4  - SEH handler address pushed to stack (optimized away)\n  local_c  - Previous FS:[0] handler saved for restoration\n\nNotes:\n- Self-pointer and inverted pointer create linked-list validation canary\n- Used by MSVC runtime for __try/__except block protection\n- Called from initialization routines before entering protected code",
