      "comment": "Inserts a node into a doubly linked list at either the head or tail position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pNodeToInsert is NULL, use the list sentinel at this+0x4 as the target node\n2. Check if target node is already in a list (node->pNext != NULL)\n3. If already linked, unlink from current position:\n   a. Calculate previous node address from offset or pointer at node+0x4\n   b. Update prev->pNext to skip over current node\n   c. Update next->pPrev to point to prev node\n   d. Clear node's pNext and pPrevOrOffset fields\n4. Get list head from implicit ECX register or use this+0x4 if NULL\n5. Check nInsertMode: 0 = insert at head, 1 = insert at tail\n6. For head insertion (mode 0):\n   a. Set node->pNext = head->pNext (first node in list)\n   b. Copy first node's pPrev to new node\n   c. Update first node's pPrev to point to new node\n   d. Update head->pNext to point to new node\n7. For tail insertion (mode 1):\n   a. Set node->pNext = head (sentinel node)\n   b. Copy head's pPrevOrOffset to new node's pPrev\n   c. Calculate last node address from offset\n   d. Update last node's pNext to point to new node\n   e. Update head's pPrev to point to new node\n\nParameters:\n  this            - Pointer to ListManager structure (ECX, __thiscall)\n  pNodeToInsert   - Node to insert, or NULL to use list sentinel at this+0x4\n  nInsertMode     - Insertion position: 0 = head, 1 = tail\n  IMPLICIT ECX    - Secondary list head pointer (if non-NULL, overrides this+0x4)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Node is inserted in place, list pointers updated atomically\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pNodeToInsert uses internal sentinel at this+0x4\n  - Node already in list is automatically unlinked before reinsertion\n  - pPrevOrOffset field uses negative values as inverted direct addresses\n  - Positive pPrevOrOffset values are relative offsets requiring calculation\n\nStructure Layout (ListNode):\nOffset | Size | Field         | Type        | Description\n-------|------|---------------|-------------|--------------------------------\n0x0    | 4    | pNext         | ListNode*   | Next node or head sentinel\n0x4    | 4    | pPrevOrOffset | int         | Previous ptr or offset value\n0x8    | 4    | reserved      | uint        | Reserved/payload data\n-------|------|---------------|-------------|--------------------------------\n\nFlag Bits (pPrevOrOffset encoding):\n  Bit 31 set (negative): Value is inverted direct pointer (~value = address)\n  Bit 31 clear (positive): Value is relative offset from next node's pPrev",
