      "comment": "Cleans up container items by zeroing item fields and freeing the data buffer.\n\nCalled during exception unwinding to safely release container resources.\nSets up SEH frame for safe cleanup during exception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Install SEH frame with handler at 0x6ff746a2\n2. Initialize loop counter to 0\n3. For each item index from 0 to capacity-1:\n   a. Compute item entry address: pData[index] + size (base offset)\n   b. Zero the field at entry+4 (likely next pointer or reference)\n   c. Zero the field at entry+8 (likely prev pointer or state)\n4. Mark exception state as -1 (cleanup complete)\n5. If pData buffer is non-NULL, free via SMemFree\n6. Restore previous exception handler and return\n\nParameters:\n  pContainer (ContainerData *) - Pointer to container structure to clean up\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If capacity is 0, skips item cleanup loop entirely\n  - If pData is NULL, skips memory deallocation\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6ff746a2 - SEH exception handler address\n  0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Exception state indicating cleanup complete\n  -2 - Error code parameter for SMemFree (normal deallocation)\n\nStructure Layout (ContainerData, 20 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field     Type         Description\n  0x00    4     field_0   uint         Unknown field\n  0x04    4     capacity  uint         Number of items in container\n  0x08    4     pData     byte *       Pointer to item offset table\n  0x0C    4     field_C   uint         Unknown field  \n  0x10    4     size      uint         Base offset for item entries\n\nItem Entry Layout (computed from pData[index] + size):\n  Offset  Size  Field     Description\n  +0x04   4     field_4   Cleared to 0 (likely link pointer)\n  +0x08   4     field_8   Cleared to 0 (likely state/reference)",
