      "comment": "Inserts an element into a min-heap priority queue with automatic capacity growth.\\n\\nThis function maintains heap invariant by bubbling the new element up from its insertion\\npoint until the parent element compares less than the new element. If the heap is at\\ncapacity, it grows the heap using either a fixed growth size or a callback function.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load current heap size from heap header at offset +0x4\\n2. Increment size to accommodate new element (newSize = currentSize + 1)\\n3. Compare new size against capacity at offset +0x0\\n4. If capacity exceeded, perform heap growth:\\n   a. Load growSize from offset +0xc (0 means use callback)\\n   b. If growSize is 0, call GetHighestPowerOfTwo to determine growth amount\\n   c. Calculate aligned capacity: alignedSize = newSize + (growSize - newSize % growSize)\\n   d. Call GrowHeapCapacity with aligned capacity\\n5. Store incremented size back to heap header at offset +0x4\\n6. Begin bubble-up loop starting at position (currentSize - 1):\\n   a. Calculate parent index: parentIdx = (currentIdx - 1) >> 1\\n   b. Exit loop if currentIdx reaches 0 (root position)\\n   c. Load parent element pointer from array at offset +0x8\\n   d. Call comparison function via vtable at parent element offset +0x0\\n   e. Pass basePtr + elementOffset as comparison parameter\\n   f. If comparison returns non-zero (parent <= new element), exit loop\\n   g. Copy parent element down to current position\\n   h. Update parent element's position index at offset +0x8\\n   i. Update parent element's heap pointer at offset +0x4\\n   j. Move to parent position and repeat\\n7. Insert element offset into final position in element array\\n8. Update element's position index at offset +0x8\\n9. Update element's heap pointer at offset +0x4\\n\\nParameters:\\nIMPLICIT pHeap - Pointer to HeapHeader structure passed in EAX register\\n  elementOffset - Byte offset from basePtr to element being inserted (on stack)\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - Modifies heap structure in-place\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Growth size of 0 triggers callback to determine optimal growth amount\\n- Alignment calculation ensures capacity grows in multiples of growSize\\n- Comparison function uses vtable indirection for polymorphic behavior\\n- Element offset is relative to basePtr stored at heap offset +0x10\\n- Position indices allow O(1) access for decrease-key operations\\n\\nStructure Layout (HeapHeader):\\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type        Description\\n0       4     capacity          uint        Maximum elements before growth\\n4       4     currentSize       uint        Current number of elements\\n8       4     pElementArray     void**      Pointer to element pointer array\\n12      4     growSize          uint        Growth chunk size (0=callback)\\n16      4     basePtr           void*       Base address for offset calculations\\nTotal: 20 bytes\\n\\nStructure Layout (HeapElement):\\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type        Description\\n0       4     pVTable           void*       Comparison function vtable pointer\\n4       4     pHeap             HeapHeader* Back-pointer to parent heap\\n8       4     positionIndex     uint        Current position in heap array\\n12+     var   userData          varies      Application-specific element data\\nTotal: 12+ bytes (minimum)",
