      "comment": "Removes the last element from a binary min-heap and performs sift-down to restore ordering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear removed element's parent pointer and index fields at offsets +0x4 and +0x8\n2. Load current heap size from header offset +0x4\n3. Get pointer to last element (array[size-1] if size > 0, else NULL)\n4. Calculate new size = oldSize - 1\n5. Check if capacity needs resizing: if (newSize > capacity && newSize > size)\n6. Get growth size from header +0xc (or call CountVectorBits if zero)\n7. Align capacity: if (newSize % growthSize != 0) capacity = newSize + (growthSize - remainder)\n8. Call ResizeVectorStorage to expand array if needed\n9. Update heap size to newSize in header\n10. If removed element not at last position, perform sift-down:\n    a. Calculate parent boundary = (size - 3) >> 1\n    b. Loop while currentIndex <= parentBoundary:\n       - Left child = currentIndex * 2 + 1\n       - If right child exists and smaller, use right child (index + 1)\n       - Compare removed element vs selected child via vtable call\n       - If removed >= child, break (heap property satisfied)\n       - Move child up to current position\n       - Update child's parent pointer and heap index\n       - Continue at child position\n    c. Place removed element at final position\n    d. Update element's parent pointer and index\n\nParameters:\npHeap (ECX) - Pointer to HeapHeader structure\ndwRemovedIndex (EAX, IMPLICIT) - Index of element being removed\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic 3 at 0x6ff51597: (size - 3) >> 1 gives parent boundary for sift loop\n- Comparison result: 0 means child smaller (continue sift), non-zero means done\n\nHeapHeader Structure (20 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n0x00    4     dwCapacity      uint    Maximum elements heap can hold\n0x04    4     dwSize          uint    Current element count\n0x08    4     pElementArray   uint*   Array of element offsets\n0x0c    4     dwGrowthSize    uint    Capacity increment (0 = dynamic)\n0x10    4     dwBaseOffset    uint    Base added to element offsets\n\nHeapElement Structure (at baseOffset + elementArray[index]):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n0x00    4     pCompareFunc    void*   Vtable pointer for comparison\n0x04    4     pParentHeap     void*   Parent heap pointer (cleared on remove)\n0x08    4     dwHeapIndex     uint    Element's index in heap",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "CALLEE_2", "CALLER_5", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
