      "comment": "Checks if a character is a decimal digit (0-9).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get thread-local storage context via GetOrCreateTlsContext\n2. Extract locale info pointer from TLS context offset 0x64\n3. Compare locale info with global default locale pointer\n4. If different, update thread locale info via ___updatetlocinfo\n5. Check if multibyte character handling is required (refcount > 1)\n6. If multibyte: delegate to ___isctype_mt with _DIGIT mask (0x4)\n7. If single-byte: lookup character in locale ctype table directly\n8. Return masked result (non-zero if digit, zero otherwise)\n\nParameters:\n  nCharCode (int) - Character code to test. Valid range 0-255 for single-byte\n                    or extended range for multibyte locales.\n\nReturns:\n  int - Non-zero (4) if character is a digit '0'-'9', zero otherwise.\n        The return value is the _DIGIT flag (0x4) ANDed from ctype table.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses thread-local locale for thread-safe operation\n  - Falls back to global locale if thread locale matches default\n  - Multibyte locales use ___isctype_mt for proper handling\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x4 - _DIGIT character class bitmask in ctype table\n  0x64 - Offset to locale pointer in TLS context (_tfpecode)\n  0x28 - Offset to lc_category refcount for multibyte check\n  0x48 - Offset to ctype table pointer in locale structure",
