      "comment": "Checks if a character is a hexadecimal digit (0-9, A-F, a-f).\n\nStandard C runtime library function from Visual Studio 2003. Uses the current\nthread's locale information to determine character classification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve thread-local storage context via GetOrCreateTlsContext\n2. Extract locale information pointer from TLS context\n3. Compare against default locale - if different, call ___updatetlocinfo\n4. Check locale reference count to determine lookup method:\n   - If refcount > 1: Use multi-threaded ___isctype_mt for thread-safe lookup\n   - Otherwise: Direct table lookup via character type array\n5. Test character against 0x80 bitmask (XDIGIT flag in ctype table)\n6. Return non-zero if character is hex digit, zero otherwise\n\nParameters:\n  nCharCode - Character code to test (int, typically ASCII value 0-127)\n              Values 0x30-0x39 ('0'-'9'), 0x41-0x46 ('A'-'F'),\n              0x61-0x66 ('a'-'f') will return non-zero\n\nReturns:\n  Non-zero (0x80) - Character is a hexadecimal digit\n  Zero (0x00) - Character is not a hexadecimal digit\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x80 - XDIGIT bitmask in Windows ctype classification table\n  0x28 - Offset to locale category refcount field in threadlocinfo\n  0x48 - Offset to character type table pointer in threadlocinfo\n  0x64 - Offset to locale info pointer in TLS thread data\n\nCallers:\n  ParseFormatStringInput - Used for validating hex format specifiers",
