      "comment": "Checks if a character is a whitespace character (space, tab, newline, etc).\n\nThis is a locale-aware CRT function that checks the _SPACE character class (0x08)\nin the locale's character type table. Thread-safe via TLS locale context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get thread-local locale context via GetOrCreateTlsContext\n2. Compare locale info pointer against global default (g_ppDefaultLocInfo)\n3. If different, call ___updatetlocinfo to synchronize locale\n4. Check locale reference count at offset 0x28\n5. If refcount > 1, call ___isctype_mt for thread-safe lookup\n6. Otherwise, use fast path: direct table lookup from locale type array\n7. Index into character type table at [pLocaleInfo+0x48] using nCharCode\n8. Mask result with _SPACE flag (0x08) and return\n\nParameters:\n  nCharCode - Character code to test (int, passed via stack at ESP+4)\n              Typically an unsigned char cast to int, or EOF (-1)\n\nReturns:\n  Non-zero (0x08) - Character is whitespace (space, tab, CR, LF, VT, FF)\n  Zero (0x00) - Character is not whitespace\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Characters > 255 handled via ___isctype_mt multibyte path\n  - EOF (-1) returns 0 (not whitespace)\n  - Thread-safe when multiple threads use different locales\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x08 - _SPACE character class flag in CRT locale table\n  0x64 - Offset to locale info pointer in TLS context\n  0x28 - Offset to reference count in locale info structure\n  0x48 - Offset to character type table pointer in locale info\n\nCallers:\n  ParseFormatStringInput - Skips whitespace in format strings\n  ParseExpressionToken - Tokenizes expressions, identifies delimiters",
