      "comment": "Checks if a character is alphanumeric (letter or digit).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetOrCreateTlsContext to obtain thread-local storage context\n2. Extract locale info pointer from TLS context at offset 0x64 (_tfpecode)\n3. Compare locale info pointer with global g_ppDefaultLocInfo\n4. If different from default, call ___updatetlocinfo to sync thread locale\n5. Check lc_category[1].refcount at offset 0x28 for multibyte mode\n6. If refcount > 1 (multibyte locale active):\n   - Push _ALPHA|_DIGIT mask (0x107) onto stack\n   - Push character code onto stack  \n   - Push locale info pointer\n   - Call ___isctype_mt for proper multibyte character classification\n   - Return result from ___isctype_mt\n7. If refcount <= 1 (single-byte locale):\n   - Load ctype table pointer from locale offset 0x48\n   - Index into ctype table using character code * 2 (word entries)\n   - AND result with _ALPHA|_DIGIT mask (0x107)\n   - Return masked result\n\nParameters:\n  nCharCode (int) - Character code to test. Valid range 0-255 for single-byte\n                    locales, extended range for multibyte locales.\n\nReturns:\n  int - Non-zero if character is alphanumeric (letter A-Z, a-z or digit 0-9).\n        Returns 0 if character is not alphanumeric.\n        Actual non-zero value is bitwise AND of ctype flags with 0x107.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Thread-safe via thread-local locale storage\n  - Falls back to global locale if thread locale matches default\n  - Multibyte locales use ___isctype_mt for proper wide character handling\n  - Single-byte path uses direct ctype table lookup for performance\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x107 - _ALPHA|_DIGIT character class bitmask (_UPPER|_LOWER|_DIGIT = 0x100|0x02|0x01|0x04)\n  0x64  - Offset to locale pointer in TLS context (_tfpecode field)\n  0x28  - Offset to lc_category[1].refcount for multibyte detection\n  0x48  - Offset to ctype table pointer in threadlocinfo structure\n  0x0C  - Stack cleanup size after ___isctype_mt call (3 * 4 b