      "comment": "CRT initialization/termination table iterator - calls each function pointer in the table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Receive start pointer in EAX (IMPLICIT), end pointer on stack\n2. Loop from ppfnCurrent to ppfnEnd (exclusive)\n3. For each entry, check if function pointer is non-null\n4. Call non-null function pointers with no arguments\n5. Increment pointer by sizeof(void*) (4 bytes)\n6. Return when current pointer reaches end\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ppfnCurrent (EAX): void** - Start of function pointer table\n  ppfnEnd: void** - End of function pointer table (exclusive)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Null function pointers are skipped (safety check)\n  - Empty table (start >= end) results in no calls\n  - Called functions receive no arguments\n\nUsage:\n  Used by CRT to call static initializers (__xc_a to __xc_z)\n  and static destructors (__xt_a to __xt_z) during module\n  load/unload. The MSVCRT uses this for C++ constructor\n  and destructor invocation order.",
