      "comment": "Executes C Runtime initialization routines including pre-init callbacks, XI initializers, and XC constructors.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if optional pre-init callback (g_pfnPreInit) is set and call it with nReserved parameter\n2. Save ESI/EDI registers for loop iteration\n3. Set up pointers to XI initialization table (g_ppfnXiInit to g_ppfnXiInitEnd)\n4. Loop through XI table entries (C runtime internal initializers):\n   a. If function pointer is non-NULL, CALL the initializer\n   b. If any initializer returns non-zero, abort and return error\n   c. Advance to next 4-byte entry until end of table\n5. Register atexit handler by calling AddToDynamicBufferWithErrorCode\n6. Set up pointers to XC initialization table (g_ppfnXcInit to g_ppfnXcInitEnd)\n7. Loop through XC table entries (C++ static constructors):\n   a. If function pointer is non-NULL, CALL the constructor\n   b. Advance to next 4-byte entry until end of table\n8. Return 0 on success\n\nParameters:\n- nReserved (int): Reserved parameter passed to pre-init callback\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success, all initializers executed successfully\n- Non-zero: Error from XI initializer (early termination)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Pre-init callback is optional (only called if g_pfnPreInit is non-NULL)\n- NULL function pointers in tables are safely skipped\n- XI initializers can abort initialization by returning non-zero\n- XC constructors return value is ignored\n\nDecompiler Note:\n- iVar1, puVar1, puVar2 are SSA temporaries representing EAX/ESI/EDI register usage\n- These phantom variables cannot be renamed as they are decompiler-generated\n\nCRT Initialization Tables:\nOffset  Size  Field           Type      Description\n0x000   0x18  XI Table        void*[6]  C runtime internal initializers (g_ppfnXiInit)\n0x018   0x14  XC Table        void*[5]  C++ static constructors (g_ppfnXcInit)\n\nFlag Bits:\n- EAX != 0: Error flag causes immediate function return",
