      "comment": "ProcessTerminationHandler\n\nCore C runtime process termination handler that orchestrates the orderly shutdown\nof a Windows application. Manages execution of cleanup handlers, critical section\nsynchronization, and final process exit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Install SEH exception handler to protect termination sequence\n2. Acquire critical section lock (ordinal 8) to serialize exit operations\n3. Check g_dwTerminateImmediately flag - if set, force immediate process termination\n4. Set g_fCleanupInProgress flag to indicate termination is underway\n5. Store nQuickExit parameter in g_byQuickExitFlag for later access\n6. If nExecuteAtexitHandlers is non-zero, iterate atexit table backwards and call handlers\n7. Execute pre-terminator initialization table via __initterm()\n8. Execute post-terminator initialization table via __initterm()\n9. Mark SEH record as unwound by setting to 0xFFFFFFFF\n10. Call VerifyCriticalSectionExitLock() to release lock if appropriate\n11. If nQuickExit is zero, set g_dwTerminateImmediately and call ___crtExitProcess()\n12. Otherwise return for quick exit without full CRT cleanup\n\nParameters:\n  dwExitCode (uint) - Exit code to pass to operating system (0 = success)\n  nExecuteAtexitHandlers (int) - Non-zero to execute atexit() registered handlers\n  nQuickExit (int) - Non-zero for quick exit without full CRT cleanup\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return if nQuickExit is 0 (calls ___crtExitProcess)\n        Returns only if nQuickExit is non-zero for quick exit path\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_dwTerminateImmediately is already set, immediately calls TerminateProcess()\n  - Atexit handlers execute in reverse registration order (LIFO)\n  - Null function pointers in atexit table are skipped\n  - Critical section ordinal 8 serializes all exit operations\n  - Pre/post terminator tables execute regardless of atexit handler flag\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_dwTerminateImmediately (0x6ff80244) - DWORD flag for immediate termination\n  g_fCleanupInProgress (0x6ff80240) - DWORD flag indicating exit is active\n  g_byQuickExitFlag (0x6ff8023c) - BYTE flag for quick exit mode\n  g_pPreTerminatorTable (0x6ff7e03c) - Pointer to pre-terminator init table\n  g_pPostTerminatorTable (0x6ff7e048) - Pointer to post-terminator init table",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "CALLER_3", "CALLEE_8"]
