      "comment": "__exit\n\nC runtime library function that terminates the current process with a specified exit code.\nThis is the internal implementation called by the public exit() function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push termination flags onto stack (fullterm=0, doexitspawn=1)\n2. Push the exit code parameter from caller's stack frame\n3. Call ProcessTerminationHandler to perform cleanup and shutdown\n4. Clean up stack frame (though never returns)\n\nParameters:\n  nExitCode (int): Process exit code returned to operating system\n                   - 0 indicates success\n                   - Non-zero indicates error or specific exit condition\n\nReturns:\n  noreturn - Function does not return to caller; process terminates\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Marked as noreturn - all callers must expect no return\n  - Called from error handlers (HandleSecurityError, ExceptionCleanupAndExit)\n  - Called from signal handlers (DispatchSignalHandler)\n  - Used by runtime startup/shutdown (AmsgExit)\n\nStack Layout at CALL instruction:\n  [ESP+0x0] = nExitCode (exit code)\n  [ESP+0x4] = return address\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0 - fullterm flag: not a full termination (exit vs _exit)\n  0x1 - doexitspawn flag: perform exit spawn processing\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release (MSVCR71.dll)",
