      "comment": "Formats a string using printf-style format specifiers into a destination buffer.\n\nCreates a fake FILE structure on the stack configured for string output mode,\nthen delegates to FormatOutputToStream for the actual formatting work. After\nformatting completes, null-terminates the destination buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create stack-based FILE structure (stFakeFile) with 32 bytes\n2. Configure FILE for string mode: _cnt=0x7FFFFFFF, _flag=0x42, _ptr/_base=szDest\n3. Call FormatOutputToStream(stFakeFile, szFormat, pArgs) to format string\n4. If szDest is valid (non-NULL), null-terminate the result:\n   a. Decrement _cnt to account for null terminator\n   b. If _cnt >= 0, write null byte at current _ptr position\n   c. If _cnt < 0 (overflow), call __flsbuf(0, stFakeFile) to flush\n\nParameters:\n  szDest (char*) - Destination buffer to receive formatted string. Must be\n                   large enough to hold the formatted result plus null terminator.\n                   If NULL, function returns without writing.\n  szFormat (char*) - Printf-style format string with optional format specifiers.\n  pArgs (va_list) - Variable argument list containing values for format specifiers.\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of characters written (excluding null terminator) on success.\n        Returns the count from FormatOutputToStream regardless of null-termination.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If szDest is NULL, formatting still occurs but no output is written\n  - Buffer overflow handled via __flsbuf when _cnt goes negative\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7FFFFFFF - Maximum 32-bit signed value, effectively unlimited buffer size\n  0x42 - FILE flag indicating string output mode (write + string)\n  0x20 - Stack space for FILE structure (32 bytes)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field  | Type   | Description\n  -------|------|--------|--------|----------------------------------\n  -0x20  | 4    | _ptr   | char*  | Current write position pointer\n  -0x1c  | 4    | _cnt   | int    | Remaining character count\n  -0x18  | 4    | _base  | char*  | Base of buffer (same as szDest)\n  -0x14  | 4    | _flag  | int    | Mode flags (0x42 = string mode)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "CALLER_2", "CALLEE_2", "STRUCT_Control"]
