      "comment": "Registers a callback function pointer in the atexit/onexit table.\n\nThis is a CRT (C Runtime) library function that manages the onexit callback table.\nThe callback function pointer is passed implicitly via EDI register by the caller.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current allocation size of the onexit table via __msize\n2. Calculate required space: (pTableEnd - pTableBase) + sizeof(void*)\n3. If current size is insufficient:\n   a. Calculate new size: min(currentSize, 0x800) + currentSize (growth strategy)\n   b. Attempt _realloc with calculated size\n   c. If realloc fails, try minimal growth of currentSize + 0x10 (16 bytes)\n   d. If both allocations fail, return without registering callback\n   e. Update table end pointer to preserve relative offset in new allocation\n   f. Update table base pointer to new allocation\n4. Store callback function pointer at current table end position\n5. Increment table end pointer by one entry (4 bytes)\n6. Return the registered callback pointer\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT EDI - pfnCallback: Pointer to callback function to register (void*)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX - Pointer to the registered callback function (same as input EDI)\n        Returns without modifying EAX if memory allocation fails\n\nDecompiler Variables (SSA temporaries):\n  sVar1 (size_t): Current allocation size from __msize - ESI register\n  sVar3 (size_t): Growth increment, capped at 0x800 - ECX register\n  pvVar2 (void*): Result of _realloc call - EAX register\n  unaff_EDI (void*): Implicit input callback pointer - EDI register\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_pOnExitTableBase (0x6ffa829c) - Base pointer of the onexit callback table\n  g_pOnExitTableEnd (0x6ffa8298) - Current end pointer of the onexit table\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x800 (2048) - Maximum growth increment for table reallocation\n  0x10 (16) - Minimum growth increment (4 function pointers) for fallback allocation\n  0x4 - Size of a function pointer (32-bit)\n\nCalled By: __onexit\nCalls: __msize, _reallo