      "comment": "Allocates and initializes the onexit callback function pointer table used by CRT atexit mechanism.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 128 bytes (0x80) for the initial onexit table via _malloc\n2. If allocation fails, return error code 0x18 (ENOMEM - out of memory)\n3. Zero-initialize the first entry of the table\n4. Set g_pOnExitTableEnd to point to g_pOnExitTableBase (empty table)\n5. Return 0 indicating successful initialization\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success, onexit table initialized and ready for callback registration\n- 0x18: Failure, memory allocation failed (out of memory)\n\nCalled By:\n- InitializeCrtStaticConstructors (via XI initializer table)\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- g_pOnExitTableBase (0x6ffa829c): Base pointer to the allocated callback table\n- g_pOnExitTableEnd (0x6ffa8298): Current end pointer (next free slot)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x80 (128): Initial table size in bytes, holds 32 function pointers\n- 0x18 (24): CRT error code ENOMEM indicating memory allocation failure\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release CRT",
