      "comment": "Converts a double-precision floating-point value to extended precision (float10) with rounding toward zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if SSE2 is available via g_fSse2Available global flag\n2. If not SSE2, jump to fallback path at 0x6ff548cd\n3. Verify MXCSR exception mask bits (0x1F80) are all set (exceptions masked)\n4. Verify FPU control word exception mask bits (0x7F) are all set\n5. If exceptions not fully masked, use fallback path\n6. Load input double into XMM0, extract biased exponent (bits 62:52) via PSRLQ by 52\n7. Test sign bit (bit 11 of exponent field = 0x800):\n   - If clear (positive): go to positive truncation path\n   - If set (negative): go to negative rounding path\n8. For positive values with exponent < 0x3FF (magnitude < 1.0): return 0.0\n9. For positive values with exponent in [0x3FF, 0x432]: truncate mantissa and return\n10. For values with exponent > 0x432: check for NaN (UCOMISD self-compare)\n    - If NaN: call HandleMathLibraryError with error code 0x3ED (1005)\n    - If not NaN (infinity or very large): return unchanged\n11. For negative values with exponent < 0xBFF (magnitude < 1.0): return -0.0 or -1.0\n12. For negative values in range: apply rounding by subtracting 1.0 if truncation changed value\n\nParameters:\n  dInputValue (double): Input double-precision value to convert\n\nReturns:\n  float10: Extended precision result rounded toward zero (truncated)\n  - For |x| < 1.0: returns 0.0 (positive) or -0.0/-1.0 (negative)\n  - For normal range: returns truncated integer value\n  - For NaN: triggers math error and returns input unchanged\n  - For infinity: returns input unchanged\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero input returns zero\n  - Subnormal inputs treated as zero\n  - NaN triggers HandleMathLibraryError(0x3ED) domain error\n  - Infinity returns unchanged\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1F80 - MXCSR exception mask bits (PM|UM|OM|ZM|DM|IM)\n  0x7F   - FPU CW exception mask bits (PM|UM|OM|ZM|DM|IM)\n  0x3FF  - Double exponent bias (10