      "comment": "Formats a string into a destination buffer using printf-style format specifiers.\n\nStandard C library sprintf implementation that wraps FormatOutputToStream with\na stack-based pseudo-file structure. Supports all standard format specifiers\n(%d, %s, %x, %f, etc.) with unlimited output length (INT_MAX buffer size).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save destination buffer pointer to ESI for null-termination later\n2. Build pseudo-FILE structure on stack:\n   - szCurrentPos (offset -0x20): Current write position pointer\n   - nMaxCount (offset -0x1c): Set to 0x7FFFFFFF (INT_MAX)\n   - pBuffer (offset -0x18): Base buffer pointer (copy of lpszDest)\n   - dwFlags (offset -0x14): Set to 0x42 (string mode flags)\n3. Push variadic args pointer (LEA from EBP+0x10), format string, stream struct\n4. Call FormatOutputToStream to perform actual formatting\n5. If lpszDest was not NULL:\n   a. Decrement remaining count\n   b. If count >= 0: Write null terminator at current position\n   c. If count < 0: Call __flsbuf to flush/extend buffer, then terminate\n6. Return character count (excluding null terminator) in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  lpszDest   - char* - Destination buffer to receive formatted string.\n               Must be large enough for result. NULL skips output.\n  lpszFormat - char* - Printf-style format string with conversion specifiers.\n  ...        - Variadic arguments matching format specifiers.\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of characters written (excluding null terminator).\n        Returns count even if lpszDest is NULL (useful for size calculation).\n\nStructure Layout (Pseudo-FILE on stack):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n  -0x24   4     szCurrentPos  char*   Current write position in buffer\n  -0x20   4     pBufferStart  char*   Start of output buffer (= lpszDest)\n  -0x1c   4     nMaxCount     int     Maximum chars remaining (0x7FFFFFFF)\n  -0x18   4     pBufferBase   char*   Base buffer pointer (= lpszDest)\n  -0x14   4     dwFlags       uint    Stream flags (0x42 = string mode)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7FFFFFFF - INT_MAX, effectively unlimited buffer size\n  0x42       - Stream flags indicating string output mode\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL lpszDest: Skips null-termination, just returns count\n  - Buffer overflow: Calls __flsbuf for emergency flush before terminating",
