      "comment": "Parses formatted data from a string using scanf-style format specifiers.\n\nThis is the C runtime library implementation of sscanf that creates a pseudo-FILE\nstructure on the stack to enable reuse of the internal format string parsing logic.\nThe source string is wrapped in a FILE structure with read-only flags set.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate stack space for pseudo-FILE structure (32 bytes)\n2. Initialize FILE._flag to 0x49 (read-only, string-backed, no buffer)\n3. Set FILE._base and FILE._ptr to point to input string\n4. Get source string length via GetStringLength\n5. Store length in FILE._cnt for bounds checking\n6. Call ParseFormatStringInput with FILE, format, and variadic args\n7. Return the count of successfully parsed fields\n\nParameters:\n  lpszSrc    - char*: Null-terminated source string to parse\n  lpszFormat - char*: Printf-style format string with conversion specifiers\n  ...        - Variadic: Pointers to variables receiving parsed values\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of fields successfully parsed and assigned\n        Returns EOF (-1) on input failure before any conversion\n        Returns 0 if no fields matched the format specifiers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty source string returns 0 (no fields matched)\n  - Mismatched format specifiers stop parsing at first failure\n  - Whitespace in format matches any amount of input whitespace\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x49 - FILE._flag value: _IOREAD|_IOSTRG|_IOMYBUF (read, string, internal buffer)",
