      "comment": "Opens a file stream with specified sharing permissions.\n\nThis is the C runtime library __fsopen implementation. It acquires a file stream\nfrom the internal stream pool, opens the file with the given mode and sharing flags,\nthen releases the stream lock before returning.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call __getstream() to acquire an available FILE stream from the internal pool\n2. If no stream available (NULL returned):\n   a. Get thread-local errno pointer via GetThreadContextFieldAt8()\n   b. Set errno to EMFILE (0x18 = 24 = too many open files)\n   c. Return NULL\n3. If stream acquired successfully:\n   a. Call __openfile() with filename, mode, share flag, and stream pointer\n   b. Call UnlockFileHandle() to release stream lock acquired by __getstream()\n   c. Return the FILE pointer (may be NULL if __openfile failed)\n\nParameters:\n- lpszFilename (char*): Path to the file to open (null-terminated ANSI string)\n- lpszMode (char*): File access mode string (\"r\", \"w\", \"a\", \"rb\", \"wb\", etc.)\n- nShareFlag (int): File sharing permissions passed to _sopen:\n    0x10 (_SH_DENYRW) - Deny read and write access\n    0x20 (_SH_DENYWR) - Deny write access\n    0x30 (_SH_DENYRD) - Deny read access\n    0x40 (_SH_DENYNO) - Permit read and write access\n\nReturns:\n- FILE*: Pointer to opened file stream on success\n- NULL: On failure, with errno set to error code:\n    EMFILE (0x18/24): Too many open files (no streams available)\n    Other codes set by __openfile for file access errors\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18: EMFILE errno value (too many open files)\n- 0x10: Stack frame size for SEH prolog\n- 0x6ff75360: SEH exception handler address\n\nRelated Functions:\n- OpenFileReadShare: Wrapper calling this with _SH_DENYNO (0x40)\n- __getstream: Internal CRT function to acquire FILE stream\n- __openfile: Internal CRT function to open file with given parameters",
