      "comment": "Reads data from a file stream into a buffer (locked/internal version).\n\nThis is the internal locked version of fread() that assumes the stream lock\nis already held by the caller. Reads up to dwElementCount elements of\ndwElementSize bytes each from pStream into pbBuffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total bytes to read (dwElementSize * dwElementCount)\n2. If total is zero, return 0 immediately\n3. Check stream flags for buffering mode (0x10c mask)\n4. If buffered and data available in stream buffer:\n   a. Copy min(remaining, buffer_available) bytes via memmove\n   b. Update stream buffer pointers and remaining count\n5. If remaining >= buffer size (0x1000 default):\n   a. Calculate aligned read size (multiple of buffer size)\n   b. Call __lseek to read directly to destination buffer\n   c. Handle EOF (returns 0) or error (returns -1)\n6. If remaining < buffer size:\n   a. Call __filbuf to refill stream buffer and get one byte\n   b. Store byte in output buffer, decrement remaining\n   c. Update buffer size from stream\n7. Loop until all bytes read or EOF/error encountered\n8. On EOF: set stream EOF flag (0x10), return elements read\n9. On error: set stream error flag (0x20), return elements read\n\nParameters:\n  pbBuffer (byte*): Destination buffer for read data\n  dwElementSize (uint): Size of each element in bytes\n  dwElementCount (uint): Number of elements to read\n  pStream (FILE*): Pointer to FILE stream structure\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Number of complete elements successfully read (0 to dwElementCount)\n        Returns 0 if dwElementSize * dwElementCount is zero\n        Returns partial count on EOF or error\n\nFILE Structure Offsets Used:\n  +0x00: _ptr - Current buffer pointer\n  +0x04: _cnt - Bytes remaining in buffer\n  +0x0C: _flag - Stream status flags\n  +0x10: _file - File descriptor\n  +0x18: _bufsiz - Buffer size\n\nFlag Bits:\n  0x010: _IOEOF - End of file reached\n  0x020: _IOERR - I/O error occurred\n  0x10C: Buffering mode mask (_IOFBF|_IOLBF|_IONBF)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero-length read returns 0 without accessing stream\n  - Unbuffered streams use default 0x1000 buffer size for alignment\n  - Direct reads bypass buffer for large requests\n  - Single-byte reads use __filbuf for efficiency",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "PARAM_4", "CALLEE_3", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
