      "comment": "Writes data elements to a file stream (locked version).\n\nThis is the thread-safe locked implementation of fwrite from Visual Studio 2003 CRT.\nIt writes dwElementCount elements of dwElementSize bytes each from pbBuffer to pStream.\nThe function handles both buffered and unbuffered I/O, with direct writes when the\ntotal bytes exceed the stream's buffer size.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total bytes to write (dwElementSize * dwElementCount)\n2. Return 0 immediately if total bytes is zero\n3. Determine buffer size: use stream's _bufsiz if buffered (flag 0x10C), else 4096\n4. Loop while bytes remain to write:\n   a. Check if stream has buffered output space (flag 0x108 set and _cnt > 0)\n   b. If buffered space available: copy min(remaining, _cnt) bytes via memmove\n   c. If no buffer space and remaining >= buffer size:\n      - Flush existing buffer if needed (FlushOutputBuffer)\n      - Write directly via __lseek in buffer-sized chunks\n      - Set error flag 0x20 on stream if write fails\n   d. If remaining < buffer size: write single byte via __flsbuf\n5. Return number of complete elements written\n\nParameters:\n   pbBuffer (byte *): Source data buffer to write from\n   dwElementSize (uint): Size in bytes of each element\n   dwElementCount (uint): Number of elements to write\n   pStream (FILE *): Target file stream structure\n\nReturns:\n   uint: Number of complete elements successfully written\n         Returns dwElementCount on full success\n         Returns partial count on error (calculated as bytes_written / dwElementSize)\n         Returns 0 if dwElementSize * dwElementCount == 0\n\nFILE Structure Fields Used:\n   Offset  Size  Field    Description\n   0x00    4     _ptr     Current buffer position pointer\n   0x04    4     _cnt     Remaining bytes in buffer\n   0x0C    2     _flag    Stream status flags\n   0x10    4     _file    File descriptor number\n   0x18    4     _bufsiz  Buffer size in bytes\n\nStream Flags (FILE._flag):\n   0x0020 - _IOERR: Stream error indicator (set on write failure)\n   0x0100 - _IOMYBUF: Buffer allocated by CRT\n   0x0008 - _IORW: Stream open for both read and write\n   0x0004 - _IOWRT: Stream open for writing\n   0x010C - Mask for checking if stream has valid buffer settings\n\nMagic Numbers:\n   0x1000 (4096): Default buffer size when stream has no buffer\n   0xFFFFFFFF (-1): Error return from __lseek and __flsbuf\n\nError Handling:\n   On write failure, sets _IOERR (0x20) flag on stream and returns partial count",
