      "comment": "Writes data elements to a file stream with thread-safe locking.\n\nStandard C runtime fwrite wrapper that acquires file lock before writing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call __SEH_prolog to set up structured exception handler frame\n2. Call AcquireSynchronizationLock on FILE handle to obtain exclusive access\n3. Clear exception state flag at [EBP-0x4] to indicate normal operation\n4. Push all four parameters and call __fwrite_lk for actual write operation\n5. Store result (bytes written) in local variable at [EBP-0x1c]\n6. Set exception state to -1 to mark cleanup phase\n7. Call ReleaseFileLockCallback to release file lock\n8. Restore result to EAX and call __SEH_epilog to clean up exception frame\n9. Return number of elements successfully written\n\nParameters:\n    pSrcBuf      - void* - Pointer to source buffer containing data to write\n    nElementSize - size_t - Size in bytes of each element to write\n    nCount       - size_t - Number of elements to write\n    pFile        - FILE* - Pointer to FILE structure for output stream\n\nReturns:\n    size_t - Number of elements successfully written (not bytes)\n           - Returns nCount on success\n           - Returns less than nCount on error or EOF\n           - Check ferror() or feof() for failure reason\n\nThread Safety:\n    Thread-safe via AcquireSynchronizationLock/ReleaseFileLockCallback pair\n\nSEH Frame:\n    Uses __SEH_prolog/__SEH_epilog for structured exception handling\n    Local at [EBP-0x4] tracks exception state (0=normal, -1=cleanup)",
