      "comment": "Returns the current file position for a stream with file lock held.\n\nThis is the internal implementation of ftell() used by the CRT. It retrieves the current\nOS file position via __lseek(), then adjusts for buffered data and text mode newline\ntranslation (CR/LF to LF conversion).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get OS file handle from FILE structure (_file field)\n2. Reset negative buffer count to zero if invalid\n3. Call __lseek() with SEEK_CUR to get current OS file position\n4. If lseek fails, return -1\n5. If unbuffered (no _IOMYBUF|_IOREAD flags), return position minus buffer count\n6. Calculate buffer offset as (_ptr - _base)\n7. For text mode files with read/write flags, count newlines in buffer for CR/LF adjustment\n8. For read mode files, adjust for unread buffered data accounting for newline translation\n9. Return final adjusted position\n\nParameters:\npFile - Pointer to FILE structure (stream with lock already held)\n\nReturns:\nCurrent file position as byte offset from start of file on success\n-1 on error (sets errno to EINVAL for invalid flags)\n\nFlag Bits (FILE._flag):\n0x001 (_IOREAD)   - Read mode\n0x002 (_IOWRT)    - Write mode  \n0x008 (_IOMYBUF)  - Buffer allocated\n0x100 (_IORW)     - Read/write mode\n0x400             - UTF mode flag\n\nIOInfo Flags (at osfile + 4):\n0x80 (FTEXT)      - Text mode (CR/LF translation active)\n0x04 (FCRLF)      - Last char was CR (pending LF)\n0x20              - CTRL-Z seen\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x16 - EINVAL (invalid argument)\n0x24 - sizeof(ioinfo) structure (36 bytes)\n0x200 - Default buffer size (512 bytes)",
