      "comment": "Returns the current file position indicator for a file stream.\n\nThread-safe wrapper around __ftell_lk that acquires and releases the file stream\nlock before and after reading the position. Part of the Visual Studio 2003 CRT.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire synchronization lock on the FILE structure to ensure thread safety\n2. Call __ftell_lk to retrieve the current byte offset from the file beginning\n3. Release the file stream lock\n4. Return the file position\n\nParameters:\n    pFile (FILE *): Pointer to an open FILE structure representing the stream.\n                    Must be a valid, open file stream. Cannot be NULL.\n\nReturns:\n    long: On success, returns the current byte position from the file beginning (>= 0).\n          On failure, returns -1L (0xFFFFFFFF) and sets errno.\n\nError Handling:\n    Returns -1L if the stream is invalid or an I/O error occurs.\n    The errno value is set by __ftell_lk on failure.\n\nSEH Frame:\n    Uses structured exception handling with __SEH_prolog/__SEH_epilog for safe\n    resource cleanup if an exception occurs during file access.",
