      "comment": "Repositions the file position indicator for a stream with file lock held.\n\nThis is the CRT __fseek_lk library function from Visual Studio 2003 Release.\nIt is the internal locked version of fseek() that performs the actual seek\noperation after the stream lock has been acquired by _fseek().\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate stream flags: must have read/write mode bits (0x83 mask)\n2. Validate origin parameter: must be 0 (SEEK_SET), 1 (SEEK_CUR), or 2 (SEEK_END)\n3. If validation fails, set errno to EINVAL (0x16) and return -1\n4. Clear EOF flag (0x10) from stream flags\n5. If SEEK_CUR (origin=1), convert to absolute position:\n   a. Call __ftell_lk() to get current position\n   b. Add offset to current position\n   c. Change origin to SEEK_SET (0)\n6. Flush output buffer via FlushOutputBuffer()\n7. Check and update buffer state based on flags:\n   - If error flag set (sign bit), clear read/write bits\n   - If read+buffered+non-UTF, set buffer size to 512 (0x200)\n8. Call __lseek() with file descriptor, offset, and origin\n9. Return 0 on success (lseek != -1), or -1 on failure\n\nParameters:\npFile   - Pointer to FILE structure (stream must have lock held by caller)\nnOffset - Byte offset for seek operation (signed, can be negative)\nnOrigin - Seek origin: 0=SEEK_SET, 1=SEEK_CUR, 2=SEEK_END\n\nReturns:\n0  - Success: file position indicator moved to new position\n-1 - Error: invalid stream flags, invalid origin, or lseek failed\n    Sets errno to EINVAL (0x16) for validation failures\n\nFlag Bits (FILE._flag):\n0x001 (_IOREAD)  - Read mode\n0x002 (_IOWRT)   - Write mode\n0x008 (_IOMYBUF) - Buffer allocated by CRT\n0x010 (_IOEOF)   - End-of-file reached (cleared by seek)\n0x080 (_IOERR)   - I/O error flag\n0x100 (_IORW)    - Read/write mode\n0x400            - UTF mode flag\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x16  - EINVAL error code (invalid argument)\n0x83  - Validation mask (_IOREAD | _IOWRT | _IORW)\n0xEF  - Clears _IOEOF flag (AND mask ~0x10)\n0xFC  - Clears read/write bits (AND mask ~0x03)\n0x200 - Default buffer size (512 bytes)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- SEEK_CUR with buffered data requires position calculation via __ftell_lk\n- Flushes output buffer before any seek to ensure data consistency\n- Resets buffer size to 512 for non-UTF buffered read streams",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "CALLER_1", "CALLEE_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
