      "comment": "Converts a character to lowercase using locale-specific rules (multi-threaded safe).\n\nVisual Studio 2003 CRT library function handling single-byte and multi-byte character\nconversion to lowercase with proper locale support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if locale has case mapping support (pLocaleInfo->hLocale != 0)\n2. If C locale or ASCII char (<0x80) with single-byte codepage: use fast path\n   - If char is 'A'-'Z' (0x41-0x5A): return char + 0x20 for lowercase\n3. For extended chars (>=0x100): check if MBCS lead byte via ctype table\n4. For single-byte extended: check ctype table for uppercase flag (bit 0)\n5. If uppercase detected: call ___crtLCMapStringA with LCMAP_LOWERCASE (0x100)\n6. Handle result: return single-byte or combined MBCS lowercase result\n\nParameters:\n  pLocaleInfo (ThreadLocaleInfo*) - Pointer to thread locale info structure:\n    +0x04 (dwCodePage): Code page identifier\n    +0x14 (hLocale): Locale handle (0 = C locale)\n    +0x24 (fSingleByteCodePage): Is single-byte codepage flag\n    +0x28 (nCtypeVersion): Character type table version\n    +0x48 (pCtypeTable): Pointer to character type lookup table\n  dwCharCode (uint) - Character code to convert (supports MBCS encoding)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Lowercase equivalent of the input character code\n         Returns original character if no lowercase mapping exists\n         Returns original character if LCMapStringA conversion fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  C locale (hLocale == 0): Only converts ASCII A-Z range\n  Single-byte codepage with ASCII (<0x80): Fast path using +0x20\n  MBCS characters: Uses ___crtLCMapStringA for proper conversion\n  Extended ASCII (0x80-0xFF): Checks ctype table before conversion\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release CRT (___tolower_mt)",
