      "comment": "Converts a character to uppercase using locale-aware multi-threaded conversion.\n\nThis is the internal CRT implementation of toupper that handles multi-byte \ncharacter sets and locale-specific case conversion rules.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if locale handle exists at pLocaleInfo->lc_handle[LC_CTYPE]\n2. If no locale or ASCII range (0x00-0x7F), use simple ASCII conversion\n3. For extended characters (>=0x100), check lead byte in character type table\n4. If character is lowercase (ctype & 0x02), prepare for conversion\n5. For multi-byte characters, build 2-byte sequence in stack buffer\n6. Call LCMapStringA with LCMAP_UPPERCASE (0x200) flag\n7. Reconstruct result from output buffer (1 or 2 bytes)\n8. For ASCII lowercase (0x61-0x7A), subtract 0x20 to convert\n\nParameters:\n    pLocaleInfo - Pointer to threadlocaleinfostruct containing:\n                  +0x04: lc_codepage - Code page identifier\n                  +0x14: lc_handle[LC_CTYPE] - Locale handle (LCID)\n                  +0x24: lc_collate_cp - High ASCII flag\n                  +0x28: lc_clike - Character width indicator\n                  +0x48: pctype - Pointer to character type table\n    nChar       - Character to convert (may be single or multi-byte value)\n\nReturns:\n    uint - The uppercase equivalent of nChar\n           Returns nChar unchanged if:\n           - Character is not lowercase\n           - LCMapStringA conversion fails\n           - Character is already uppercase\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - ASCII range (0x61-0x7A): Direct arithmetic conversion (subtract 0x20)\n    - Extended characters: Uses LCMapStringA for proper locale conversion\n    - Multi-byte lead bytes: Reconstructs 16-bit character from 2-byte result\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x02   - CT_CTYPE1 lowercase flag (C1_LOWER)\n    0x20   - Offset between lowercase and uppercase ASCII letters\n    0x61   - ASCII code for 'a'\n    0x7A   - ASCII code for 'z'\n    0x7F   - End of 7-bit ASCII range\n    0x80   - Lead byte indicator mask in character type table\n    0x100  - Extended character threshold (requires locale handling)\n    0x200  - LCMAP_UPPERCASE flag for LCMapStringA API",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "CALLER_1", "STRUCT_Skill", "CALLEE_2", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
