      "comment": "Converts a character to uppercase using locale-aware conversion.\n\nStandard C runtime library function that retrieves the current thread's locale\ninformation and delegates to the multithreaded-safe toupper implementation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get thread-local storage context via GetOrCreateTlsContext\n2. Extract locale info pointer from TLS context offset 0x64\n3. If locale differs from default global locale, update thread locale info\n4. Call ___toupper_mt with locale and character for actual conversion\n5. Return the uppercase character (or original if not convertible)\n\nParameters:\n  nChar - int: Character value to convert (typically 0-255 ASCII range)\n\nReturns:\n  int: Uppercase equivalent if nChar is lowercase letter (a-z -> A-Z)\n       Original character value if not a lowercase letter\n       Undefined behavior if nChar is outside valid range\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Non-alphabetic characters pass through unchanged\n  - Extended ASCII behavior depends on active locale settings\n  - Thread-safe: uses per-thread locale when available",
      "tags": ["CALLER_1", "CALLEE_3", "PARAM_1", "PROP_SMALL"]
