      "comment": "Performs case-insensitive string comparison using current thread locale settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve thread-local storage context via GetOrCreateTlsContext\n2. Get thread's locale info from TLS context (_tfpecode field at offset 0x64)\n3. If locale differs from default, update to current locale via ___updatetlocinfo\n4. Check if locale has wide character support (lc_category[0].wlocale)\n5. If no wide locale, use fast ASCII-only comparison via ___ascii_stricmp\n6. Otherwise, enter locale-aware comparison loop:\n   a. Convert current char from lpszStr1 to lowercase via ConvertCharToLowerMT\n   b. Advance lpszStr1 pointer\n   c. Convert current char from lpszStr2 to lowercase via ConvertCharToLowerMT  \n   d. Advance lpszStr2 pointer\n   e. If dwLower1 is null terminator (0), exit loop\n   f. If dwLower1 equals dwLower2, continue loop\n7. Return difference between final lowercase character values\n\nParameters:\nlpszStr1 - First null-terminated string to compare\nlpszStr2 - Second null-terminated string to compare\n\nReturns:\n< 0 - lpszStr1 is lexicographically less than lpszStr2 (case-insensitive)\n  0 - Strings are equal (case-insensitive)\n> 0 - lpszStr1 is lexicographically greater than lpszStr2 (case-insensitive)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty strings: Returns 0 if both empty, otherwise difference of first chars\n- Identical strings: Returns 0 after comparing all characters\n- Different lengths: Null terminator comparison determines result\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field                  Type         Description\n0x64    4     _tfpecode              pthreadlocinfo Thread locale info pointer\n0x14    4     lc_category[0].wlocale wchar_t*     Wide locale string (NULL=ASCII only)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "CALLER_2", "CALLEE_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
