      "comment": "Atomically swaps the thread-local Non-Local Goto (NLG) dispatch code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call __getptd() to retrieve pointer to thread-local data (_ptiddata structure)\n2. Load current _NLG_dwCode value from thread-local storage at offset +0x74\n3. Call __getptd() again to get thread-local data pointer\n4. Store new code value to _NLG_dwCode field at offset +0x74\n5. Return previously saved old code value in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  newCode (ulong) - New NLG dispatch code value to store in thread-local storage\n\nReturns:\n  ulong - The previous NLG_dwCode value that was stored before the swap\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  This function implements atomic exchange semantics for the NLG (Non-Local Goto)\n  dispatch mechanism used by MSVC exception handling. The NLG code is used to\n  direct exception unwinding to the appropriate handler target. Multiple calls to\n  __getptd() ensure thread safety by retrieving the current thread context.",
