      "comment": "Deallocates a memory block previously allocated by the CRT memory allocator.\n\nThis is a CRT library function (_free) that implements the standard free() behavior\nwith Small Block Heap (SBH) optimization for improved performance on small allocations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pMemory is NULL, return immediately (no-op per C standard)\n2. If heap allocation strategy is SBH mode (value 3):\n   a. Acquire memory lock (critical section 4)\n   b. Search SBH regions for the block via ___sbh_find_block\n   c. If found in SBH, free via ___sbh_free_block and return\n   d. Release memory lock\n3. If not found in SBH or not using SBH strategy:\n   a. Delegate to HeapFree with process heap handle\n\nParameters:\n  pMemory - Pointer to memory block to free, or NULL (safe to call with NULL)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; always succeeds (NULL is safely ignored)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pointer: Returns immediately without any operation\n  - SBH block: Freed through optimized small block heap path\n  - Non-SBH block: Freed through Windows HeapFree API\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_dwHeapAllocStrategy (0x6ffa714c) - Heap strategy (3 = SBH enabled)\n  g_hSbhHeap (0x6ffa7148) - Handle to the process heap for HeapFree\n\nCalled By: realloc, cleanup functions, fiber local storage, locale management",
