      "comment": "Allocates memory using a two-tier strategy: first attempts small block heap (SBH) allocation for eligible sizes, then falls back to Win32 HeapAlloc.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if heap allocation strategy is SBH mode (value 3)\n2. If SBH mode and size <= threshold, acquire lock and try ___sbh_alloc_block\n3. Release critical section after SBH attempt\n4. If SBH succeeded, return the allocated block pointer\n5. If size is zero, set minimum allocation to 1 byte\n6. If strategy != 1 (not exact mode), align size up to 16-byte boundary\n7. Call HeapAlloc on CRT heap handle with adjusted size\n8. Return the allocated memory pointer (may be NULL on failure)\n\nParameters:\n  cbSize (size_t) - Number of bytes to allocate. Zero is treated as 1.\n\nReturns:\n  void* - Pointer to allocated memory block on success\n  NULL  - If both SBH and HeapAlloc fail (out of memory)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero-size requests allocate 1 byte minimum\n  - Sizes <= g_dwSbhThreshold attempt SBH first in strategy 3\n  - Strategy 1 preserves exact size; other strategies align to 16 bytes\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_dwHeapAllocStrategy (0x6ffa714c) - Allocation strategy (1=exact, 3=SBH)\n  g_dwSbhThreshold (0x6ffa7138) - Maximum size for SBH allocation\n  g_hCrtHeap (0x6ffa7148) - CRT heap handle for HeapAlloc fallback\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release (__heap_alloc)",
