      "instructions": ["0x2FD8|PUSH|EBP", "0x2FD9|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x2FDB|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBP + 0xc]", "0x2FDE|CMP|EAX, 0x1", "0x2FE1|PUSH|ESI", "0x2FE2|JNZ|0x6ff530c8", "0x2FE8|MOV|EAX, 0x94", "0x2FED|CALL|0x6ff58270", "0x2FF2|MOV|ESI, ESP", "0x2FF4|PUSH|ESI", "0x2FF5|MOV|dword ptr [ESI], 0x94", "0x2FFB|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff75068]", "0x3001|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x3003|JZ|0x6ff5313d", "0x3009|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x10]"],
      "comment": "C Runtime Library DLL initialization/termination handler.\n\nThis is a Visual Studio 2003 CRT library function that handles DLL attachment\nand detachment notifications during DllMain. It initializes or cleans up the\nCRT environment based on the notification reason.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH (nReason == 1):\n   a. Retrieve OS version info via GetVersionExA into stack OSVERSIONINFOA\n   b. Store platform info in global OS version variables\n   c. Initialize CRT heap via __heap_init\n   d. Initialize multi-threading support via __mtinit\n   e. Initialize runtime error checking via __RTC_Initialize\n   f. Cache command line and environment strings\n   g. Initialize standard I/O via __ioinit\n   h. Parse command line arguments via __setargv\n   i. Set up environment variables via __setenvp\n   j. Call C initializers via __cinit\n   k. Increment CRT init reference count\n   \n2. DLL_PROCESS_DETACH (nReason == 0):\n   a. Decrement CRT init reference count\n   b. If no cleanup in progress, call InitializeCleanupSequence\n   c. Terminate I/O, multi-threading, and heap\n   \n3. DLL_THREAD_ATTACH (nReason == 2):\n   a. Allocate thread data structure (0x8C bytes)\n   b. Get TLS value and initialize per-thread data\n   c. Store current thread ID in thread data\n   \n4. DLL_THREAD_DETACH (nReason == 3):\n   a. Free per-thread data via __freeptd\n\nParameters:\n  hModule  - HINSTANCE of the DLL being loaded/unloaded (unused)\n  nReason  - DLL notification reason:\n             0 = DLL_PROCESS_DETACH\n             1 = DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH\n             2 = DLL_THREAD_ATTACH\n             3 = DLL_THREAD_DETACH\n\nReturns:\n  TRUE (1)  - Initialization/termination succeeded\n  FALSE (0) - Initialization failed (only during DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH)\n\nError Handling:\n  - GetVersionExA failure returns FALSE immediately\n  - __heap_init failure returns FALSE\n  - __mtinit failure calls __heap_term and returns FALSE\n  - __ioinit failure calls __mtterm, __heap_term and returns FALSE\n  - __setargv/__setenvp failure calls __ioterm and continues cleanup\n  - __cinit failure calls __ioterm and continues cleanup\n  - Thread allocation failure returns FALSE\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x94      - sizeof(OSVERSIONINFOA) = 148 bytes\n  0x8C      - sizeof(_tiddata) = 140 bytes for per-thread data\n  0x7FFF    - Mask for build number (low 15 bits)\n  0x8000    - Flag OR'd into build flags when not VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT\n  2         - VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT constant\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_dwOsMajorVersion     - OS platform ID from OSVERSIONINFOA.dwPlatformId\n  g_dwOsPlatformId       - OS major version from OSVERSIONINFOA.dwMajorVersion\n  g_dwOsMinorVersion     - OS minor version from OSVERSIONINFOA.dwMinorVersion\n  g_dwOsBuildFlags       - Build number with platform flag\n  g_dwOsVersionCombined  - (MajorVersion * 256) + MinorVersion\n  g_lpszCommandLine      - Cached command line string\n  g_lpszEnvironmentStrings - Cached environment block\n  g_nCrtInitCount        - Reference count of CRT initializations",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "CALLER_1", "CALLEE_18", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
