      "comment": "Updates the current thread's locale information to match the global default.\n\nThis function synchronizes thread-local locale info with the process-wide default,\nmanaging reference counts to ensure proper memory lifecycle of locale structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get or create TLS context for current thread via GetOrCreateTlsContext\n2. Retrieve thread's current locinfo pointer from TLS context offset 0x64\n3. Compare against global default locinfo (g_ppDefaultLocInfo)\n4. If already synchronized, return current locinfo (early exit)\n5. If old locinfo exists, decrement reference counts on sub-structures:\n   - LC_COLLATE info at offset 0x2c\n   - LC_NUMERIC info at offset 0x34\n   - LC_MONETARY info at offset 0x30\n   - LC_TIME info at offset 0x40\n   - Multibyte info refcount at offset 0x4c->0xb4\n6. Store pointer to global default locinfo in thread's TLS slot\n7. Increment reference counts on new locinfo's sub-structures\n8. If old locinfo refcount reached zero and not static default, free via ___freetlocinfo\n9. Return pointer to updated thread locinfo\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses thread-local storage implicitly)\n\nReturns:\n  pthreadlocinfo - Pointer to the thread's updated locale information structure\n                   Always returns valid pointer from TLS context offset 0x64\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If thread locinfo already matches global, no ref counting occurs\n  - Static default locinfo (g_DefaultLocInfo at 0x6ff7e080) is never freed\n  - NULL sub-structure pointers are skipped during ref count operations\n\nStructure Offsets (threadlocinfo):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x00    4     refcount        Reference count for this locinfo\n  0x2c    4     lc_collate      LC_COLLATE category info pointer\n  0x30    4     lc_monetary     LC_MONETARY category info pointer\n  0x34    4     lc_numeric      LC_NUMERIC category info pointer\n  0x40    4     lc_time         LC_TIME category info pointer\n  0x4c    4     mbcinfo         Multibyte character info pointer\n\nTLS Context Offset:\n  0x64    4     ptlocinfo       Thread's current locale info pointer",
      "tags": ["CALLER_1", "CALLEE_2", "PARAM_0"]
