      "comment": "Initializes per-thread data structure with default locale and random seed values.\n\nThis CRT internal function performs minimal initialization of a _tiddata structure\nduring thread startup or CRT initialization. Sets the thread locale pointer to the\nglobal default locale and initializes the random number generator seed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load _Ptd pointer from stack parameter\n2. Store g_pDefaultLocaleInfo pointer into _Ptd->ptlocinfo (offset 0x54)\n3. Store initial random seed value (1) into _Ptd->_holdrand (offset 0x14)\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  _Ptd      - Pointer to per-thread data structure (_tiddata) to initialize\n  _Locale   - Locale info pointer (UNUSED in this implementation)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nStructure Layout (_tiddata offsets used):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Type             Description\n  0x14    4     _holdrand    unsigned long    Random seed for rand()\n  0x54    4     ptlocinfo    pthreadlocinfo   Per-thread locale pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - _Locale parameter is ignored; function always uses g_pDefaultLocaleInfo\n  - Called during CRT initialization before full thread context exists\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6ff7e770 - g_pDefaultLocaleInfo: Global default threadlocinfo structure\n  0x1        - Default random seed for rand() function (C standard)",
