      "comment": "Gets or creates the per-thread data (_ptiddata) context for the current thread.\n\nLibrary Match: Visual Studio 2003 Release __getptd\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current last error code to preserve caller's error state\n2. Query Fiber Local Storage (FLS) for existing thread context using g_dwTlsIndex\n3. If context exists, skip to step 8 (return existing context)\n4. Allocate new _ptiddata structure (140 bytes / 0x8C) via _calloc\n5. If allocation fails, call AmsgExit(0x10) to terminate with R6016 error\n6. Store allocated context in FLS via FlsSetValue\n7. Initialize structure fields:\n   - _initaddr: pointer to g_pDefaultMbcInfo (multibyte code page info)\n   - _holdrand: seed value 1 for rand() function\n   - _thandle: -1 (invalid handle, no associated thread handle)\n   - _tid: current thread ID from GetCurrentThreadId()\n8. Restore original last error code to hide internal API calls\n9. Return pointer to thread context\n\nParameters:\n  None (void) - Uses implicit thread context from TLS\n\nReturns:\n  _ptiddata - Pointer to per-thread data structure for current thread\n              Never returns NULL (calls AmsgExit on allocation failure)\n\nError Handling:\n  - Allocation failure triggers AmsgExit(0x10) which displays\n    \"R6016 - not enough space for thread data\" and terminates\n\nStructure Layout (_ptiddata at offset 0x8C = 140 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Type      Description\n  0x00    4     _tid         DWORD     Thread ID from GetCurrentThreadId\n  0x04    4     _thandle     DWORD     Thread handle (-1 if not set)\n  0x14    4     _holdrand    int       Random seed for rand()\n  0x54    4     _initaddr    void*     Pointer to multibyte info\n\nCalled By: 46 functions including __stricmp, _isalpha, _toupper, GetDosErrnoPtr",
