      "comment": "Initializes CRT multi-threading support for thread-local storage.\n\nSets up Fiber Local Storage (FLS) or Thread Local Storage (TLS) infrastructure\nfor managing per-thread data in the C runtime library. Attempts to use modern\nFLS APIs (Vista+) with fallback to legacy TLS APIs for older Windows versions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call __mtinitlocks to initialize multi-threading lock structures\n2. If lock initialization fails, call __mtterm for cleanup and return failure\n3. Get handle to kernel32.dll via GetModuleHandleA\n4. Resolve FLS API addresses via GetProcAddress:\n   - FlsAlloc -> g_pfnFlsAlloc\n   - FlsGetValue -> g_pfnFlsGetValue  \n   - FlsSetValue -> g_pfnFlsSetValue\n   - FlsFree -> g_pfnFlsFree\n5. If FlsSetValue not available, use TLS fallback:\n   - g_pfnFlsAlloc = AllocateTlsSlot (internal wrapper)\n   - g_pfnFlsGetValue = TlsGetValue\n   - g_pfnFlsSetValue = TlsSetValue\n   - g_pfnFlsFree = TlsFree\n6. Allocate TLS/FLS slot via g_pfnFlsAlloc with FreeFiberLocalStorage callback\n7. Store slot index in g_dwTlsIndex (-1 indicates failure)\n8. Allocate thread data structure (0x8C bytes) via _calloc(1, 0x8C)\n9. Associate thread data with TLS slot via g_pfnFlsSetValue\n10. Initialize thread data structure fields:\n    - Offset 0x54: pointer to g_pDefaultMbcInfo\n    - Offset 0x14: set to 1 (initialized flag)\n    - Offset 0x04: set to -1 (invalid handle marker)\n    - Offset 0x00: current thread ID from GetCurrentThreadId\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 on success (multi-threading initialized)\n        0 on failure (lock init failed, TLS allocation failed, or memory allocation failed)\n\nError Handling:\n  On any failure, calls __mtterm to clean up partially initialized state\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_pfnFlsAlloc (0x6ff8026c) - FLS/TLS allocation function pointer\n  g_pfnFlsGetValue (0x6ff80270) - FLS/TLS get value function pointer\n  g_pfnFlsSetValue (0x6ff80274) - FLS/TLS set value function pointer\n  g_pfnFlsFree (0x6ff8027