      "comment": "Initializes critical section locks for CRT multithreading support.\n\nIterates through the lock table (36 slots) and initializes critical sections\nfor each slot marked as requiring synchronization. Critical sections are \nallocated from a pre-allocated pool with spin count optimization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to 0 and critical section pool pointer\n2. For each lock slot (0 to 35):\n   a. Check if lock flag indicates initialization required (flag == 1)\n   b. If required, assign next critical section from pool to lock table\n   c. Advance pool pointer by sizeof(CRITICAL_SECTION) (0x18 bytes)\n   d. Call ___crtInitCritSecAndSpinCount with spin count 4000 (0xFA0)\n   e. If initialization fails, clear the slot pointer and return failure\n3. If all locks initialized successfully, return success\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 on success (all locks initialized)\n        0 on failure (critical section initialization failed)\n\nLock Table Structure (g_apLockTable at 0x6ff7e210):\n  Offset  Size  Field                Description\n  0x00    4     LPCRITICAL_SECTION   Pointer to critical section\n  0x04    4     dwFlag               1=needs init, 0=unused\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x24 (36)  - Total number of lock slots in table\n  0xFA0 (4000) - Spin count for critical section (performance optimization)\n  0x18 (24)  - sizeof(CRITICAL_SECTION) in bytes\n\nError Handling:\n  On failure, clears the failed slot pointer before returning 0.\n  Caller (InitializeMultithreadingSupport) should handle cleanup.",
