      "comment": "Releases a critical section lock by index from a global critical section array.\n\nThis is a wrapper function that provides indexed access to a global array of\nCRITICAL_SECTION objects. It retrieves the critical section at the specified\nindex and calls the Windows API LeaveCriticalSection to release the lock.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Accept nLockIndex parameter via stack (EBP+0x8)\n2. Load lockIndex value into EAX\n3. Calculate critical section address using stride: (nLockIndex * 8) + 0x6fc402c0\n4. Load the critical section pointer at calculated address\n5. Push the critical section pointer onto stack as parameter\n6. Call LeaveCriticalSection Windows API\n7. Pop EBP and return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  nLockIndex (int) - Zero-based index into the global critical section array\n                     at 0x6fc402c0. Valid range determined by array size.\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. The function is a pass-through to LeaveCriticalSection.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Critical sections are stored in an array with 8-byte stride (2 DWORD entries per element)\n  - Invalid/out-of-bounds nLockIndex values will access undefined memory\n  - Function is called from various lock release wrappers throughout codebase\n  - Used by: ReleaseStreamTableLock, UnlockHeapAllocationSection, ReleaseCriticalSection8,\n    and 18 other lock release functions\n\nStructure Layout (Global Critical Section Array @ 0x6fc402c0):\n  Each array element is 8 bytes (2 DWORDs) in size\n  Entry at index N: address = 0x6fc402c0 + (N * 8)\n  Contents: Pointer to CRITICAL_SECTION object",
