      "comment": "Acquires a CRT synchronization lock by lock number index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate pointer to lock entry in g_apLockTable using lock number index\n2. Check if critical section at that index is initialized (non-NULL)\n3. If NULL, call __mtinitlocknum to initialize the lock structure\n4. If initialization fails (returns 0), call AmsgExit(0x11) for fatal error\n5. Enter the critical section to acquire exclusive access\n\nParameters:\n  nLockNum (int) - Lock index number into g_apLockTable. Valid range depends\n                   on CRT lock table size. Common values: file handles, heap locks.\n\nReturns:\n  void - Does not return a value. Function either succeeds or terminates\n         the process via AmsgExit on initialization failure.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - First access to an uninitialized lock triggers lazy initialization\n  - Fatal error 0x11 (17) indicates lock initialization failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x11 - AmsgExit error code for _RT_LOCK (lock assertion failure)\n  *8   - Stride in lock table (8 bytes per entry: pointer + padding/state)\n\nError Handling:\n  If __mtinitlocknum returns 0, AmsgExit(0x11) terminates the process.\n  This is a non-recoverable CRT initialization error.",
