      "comment": "Establishes Structured Exception Handling (SEH) frame for caller function.\n\nThis compiler-generated prolog installs an exception handler on the thread's SEH chain\n(via FS:[0]) and sets up the standard Visual C++ exception frame layout. Called at the\nstart of functions that use __try/__except blocks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push exception handler address (__except_handler3 at 0x6ff53a24) onto stack\n2. Read current SEH chain head from Thread Information Block (FS:[0])\n3. Push previous handler pointer to link into chain\n4. Save caller's EBP and establish new frame pointer at ESP+0x10\n5. Allocate local variable space by subtracting dwLocalVarsSize from ESP\n6. Preserve non-volatile registers EBX, ESI, EDI on stack\n7. Save current ESP at [EBP-0x18] for stack unwinding during exceptions\n8. Store scope table pointer at [EBP-0x8] for exception dispatch\n9. Initialize try level at [EBP-0x4] to -1 (outside all __try blocks)\n10. Install new EXCEPTION_REGISTRATION record at FS:[0] chain head\n11. Return to caller to continue function execution\n\nParameters:\n  dwLocalVarsSize (uint) - Size in bytes to allocate for caller's local variables\n  pScopeTable (SCOPETABLE_ENTRY*) - Pointer to scope table for __try/__except nesting\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; modifies stack and SEH chain in-place\n\nImplicit Register Inputs (unaff_* phantom variables):\n  unaff_EBX (uint) - Caller's EBX value, preserved and restored during unwind\n  unaff_ESI (uint) - Caller's ESI value, preserved and restored during unwind\n  unaff_EDI (uint) - Caller's EDI value, preserved and restored during unwind\n  unaff_retaddr (void*) - Return address, manipulated for frame setup\n\nStack Frame Layout After Prolog:\n  Offset     Size  Field              Description\n  [EBP+0x08]  4    dwLocalVarsSize    Stack allocation size parameter\n  [EBP+0x04]  4    pScopeTable        Scope table pointer parameter  \n  [EBP+0x00]  4    SavedEBP           Caller's frame pointer\n  [EBP-0x04]  4    nTryLevel          Current __try level (-1 = none)\n  [EBP-0x08]  4    pScopeTableCopy    Copy of scope table pointer\n  [EBP-0x0C]  4    pPrevHandler       Previous SEH handler link\n  [EBP-0x10]  4    pExceptionHandler  Pointer to __except_handler3\n  [EBP-0x14]  4    SavedEDI           Preserved EDI register\n  [EBP-0x18]  4    pSavedESP          Stack pointer for unwinding\n  [EBP-0x1C]  4    SavedESI           Preserved ESI register\n  [EBP-0x20]  4    SavedEBX           Preserved EBX register\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6ff53a24 - Address of __except_handler3 exception dispatcher\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Try level -1 indicating outside all __try blocks\n  FS:[0x0] - Thread Information Block offset to ExceptionList\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Decompilation fails due to non-standard stack manipulation (stack frame is built \n  from caller's context). The unaff_* variables are phantom register inputs that\n  cannot be typed - they represent caller's register state for preservation.",
