      "comment": "Restores SEH exception handler chain and performs standard function epilog.\n\nThis is a Visual Studio compiler-generated inlined function that terminates\nfunctions using Structured Exception Handling. It restores the previous\nexception handler, pops callee-saved registers, and returns to the caller.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve saved exception handler pointer from [EBP-0x10]\n2. Restore FS:[0x0] (TIB ExceptionList) to previous handler\n3. Pop return address into ECX for later use\n4. Restore callee-saved registers (EDI, ESI, EBX)\n5. Execute LEAVE to restore EBP and ESP\n6. Push return address and execute RET\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT EBP - Stack frame pointer with SEH frame layout\n  IMPLICIT [EBP-0x10] - Saved previous exception handler pointer\n  IMPLICIT [EBP+0x4] - Return address (standard calling convention)\n  \nPhantom Variables (compiler-synthesized, cannot be typed/renamed):\n  unaff_EBP (undefined4*) - Caller's EBP register, provides SEH frame access\n  unaff_retaddr (undefined4) - Return address from stack at [EBP+4]\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return a value\n  Control transfers to caller via RET instruction\n\nStructure Layout (SEH Stack Frame):\n  Offset    Size  Field              Description\n  -------   ----  -----------------  -----------------------------------\n  EBP-0x10   4    PrevExceptionPtr   Pointer to previous SEH handler\n  EBP-0x0C   4    ExceptionHandler   Current exception handler address\n  EBP-0x08   4    ScopeTable         Pointer to scope table\n  EBP-0x04   4    TryLevel           Current try block level (-1 = none)\n  EBP+0x00   4    SavedEBP           Caller's EBP\n  EBP+0x04   4    ReturnAddress      Caller's return address\n\nRegister Usage:\n  ECX - Scratch: holds exception handler ptr, then return address\n  EDI, ESI, EBX - Restored from stack (callee-saved)\n  EBP, ESP - Restored via LEAVE instruction\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function is always inlined by compiler, never called directly\n  - Must be paired with corresponding __SEH_prolog at function entry\n  - FS:[0x0] points to Thread Information Block ExceptionList field\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  FS:[0x0] - TIB.ExceptionList (first field of Thread Information Block)\n  EBP-0x10 - Standard offset for saved exception handler in SEH frame",
