      "comment": "Flushes a single character to a file buffer and writes to disk if necessary.\n\nThis is a CRT library function (Visual Studio 2003) that handles buffer flushing\nfor file output. It writes pending buffer data to disk and adds the new character.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file flags - must be open for write (0x82) and not in error state (0x40)\n2. If file was in read mode (0x01), reset buffer pointer and clear read flag\n3. Clear buffer count and set write mode flag (0x02)\n4. If unbuffered and stdout/stderr, check if terminal via __isatty()\n5. If not terminal, allocate buffer via __getbuf()\n6. If buffered (0x108 flag), calculate bytes to flush from ptr-base\n7. Call __lseek() to write buffer data to file\n8. For append mode (0x20 flag in OS handle), seek to end first\n9. Store new character at buffer base position\n10. Return character on success, -1 on error (sets error flag 0x20)\n\nParameters:\n  nChar - Character to write (as int, only low byte used)\n  pFile - Pointer to FILE structure to write to\n\nReturns:\n  Success: Character written (nChar & 0xFF)\n  Failure: -1 (sets _IOERR flag 0x20 in file flags)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x82 - _IOREAD|_IOWRT check for valid file mode\n  0x40 - _IOERR error flag\n  0x01 - _IOREAD flag (file is in read mode)\n  0x10 - _IOMYBUF flag (buffer allocated by CRT)\n  0x02 - _IOWRT flag (file is in write mode)\n  0x108 - _IONBF|_IOMYBUF check for buffered file\n  0x20 - _IOERR flag / append mode in OS handle flags\n  0x1F - Mask for file handle index within block\n  0x24 - Size of OS file handle entry structure (36 bytes)\n\nGlobals:\n  g_StdoutFile (0x6ff7e360) - stdout FILE structure\n  g_StderrFile (0x6ff7e380) - stderr FILE structure\n  g_pOsFileHandleTable - Array of pointers to OS file handle blocks\n  g_InvalidFileHandleEntry (0x6ff7e730) - Sentinel entry for invalid handles",
