      "comment": "Printf-style format string parser and output generator for C runtime library.\n\nParses format specifiers from szFormat and writes formatted output to pStream using\narguments from pVaArgs. Implements the core logic for sprintf, printf, vsprintf, etc.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save stack canary for security check on exit\n2. Initialize parsing state (flags, width, precision to defaults)\n3. For each character in format string:\n   a. If not '%', write character directly to output\n   b. If '%', enter state machine to parse format specifier:\n      - State 1: Reset all format flags and field values\n      - State 2: Parse flag characters (-, +, 0, #, space)\n      - State 3: Parse field width (number or * for va_arg)\n      - State 4: Period found, begin precision parsing\n      - State 5: Parse precision value (number or *)\n      - State 6: Parse size modifiers (h, l, I64, I32, w)\n      - State 7: Process conversion specifier (d,i,o,u,x,X,e,E,f,g,G,c,C,s,S,n,p,Z)\n4. Handle conversion based on type:\n   - Integers: Convert via __aulldvrm with specified base (8, 10, 16)\n   - Floats: Call __fptrap function pointers for conversion\n   - Strings: Copy with width/precision handling\n   - Characters: Handle wide/narrow conversion via _wctomb\n5. Apply padding (left/right/zero) based on flags\n6. Clean up any allocated buffer for large float conversions\n7. Verify stack canary before return\n\nParameters:\n- pStream: FILE structure pointer for output destination\n- szFormat: Printf format string with conversion specifiers\n- pVaArgs: Pointer to variable argument list on stack\n\nReturns:\n- Number of characters written to output stream\n\nFormat Flags (dwFormatFlags):\n- 0x0001: '+' flag - prefix positive numbers with plus sign\n- 0x0002: ' ' flag - prefix positive numbers with space\n- 0x0004: '-' flag - left-justify within field width\n- 0x0008: '0' flag - zero-pad numbers to field width\n- 0x0010: 'l' modifier - long int\n- 0x0020: 'h' modifier - short int\n- 0x0040: signed conversion (d, i)\n- 0x0080: '#' flag - alternate form (0x prefix for hex)\n- 0x0100: negative value detected\n- 0x0200: octal alternate form\n- 0x0800: 'w' modifier - wide character\n- 0x8000: 'I64' modifier - 64-bit integer\n\nParse State Machine:\n- 0: Normal text, output directly\n- 1: '%' found, initialize format parsing\n- 2: Flag character parsing\n- 3: Field width parsing\n- 4: '.' found, start precision\n- 5: Precision value parsing\n- 6: Size modifier parsing\n- 7: Conversion specifier processing\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x200: Maximum precision for float conversion\n- 0xa3 (163): Float buffer threshold before malloc\n- 0x15d (349): Additional buffer size for large floats\n- 0x7fffffff: Unlimited string length sentinel\n\nCallers: _sprintf, _vsprintf, WriteFormattedWideStringToFile, __vsnprintf, __snprintf",
