      "comment": "Returns the size in bytes of a memory block allocated on the heap.\n\nThis CRT library function queries the size of an allocated memory block using\neither the Small Block Heap (SBH) internal tracking or the Windows HeapSize API.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if heap allocation strategy is SBH mode (strategy == 3)\n2. If SBH mode:\n   a. Acquire heap lock via __lock(4) for thread safety\n   b. Call ___sbh_find_block to check if block is in SBH\n   c. If found in SBH, extract size from block header at [pMemory-4] minus 9-byte overhead\n   d. Release lock via LeaveCriticalSectionForMemoryFree\n   e. Return SBH-calculated size if block was found\n3. If not SBH or block not found in SBH:\n   a. Call HeapSize(g_hSbhHeap, 0, pMemory) to query Windows heap\n   b. Return Windows heap size\n\nParameters:\n  pMemory - Pointer to allocated memory block to query size of\n\nReturns:\n  size_t - Size in bytes of the allocated memory block\n           Returns (size_t)-1 if pMemory is invalid or not a valid heap block\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  3 - SBH heap allocation strategy constant (g_dwHeapAllocStrategy == 3)\n  4 - Lock index for heap critical section (__lock parameter)\n  9 - SBH block header overhead bytes (subtracted from stored size)\n  -4 - Offset to SBH block size field (4 bytes before user data)\n\nCalled By: RegisterOnExitCallback",
