      "instructions": ["0x453C|PUSH|EBP", "0x453D|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x453F|SUB|ESP, 0x24", "0x4542|MOV|EAX, [0x6ff7e990]", "0x4547|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x4], EAX", "0x454A|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBP + 0x14]", "0x454D|MOV|ECX, 0xa1", "0x4552|CMP|EAX, ECX", "0x4554|PUSH|ESI", "0x4555|JG|0x6ff5466e", "0x455B|JZ|0x6ff54662", "0x4561|CMP|EAX, 0x18", "0x4564|JG|0x6ff545f2", "0x456A|JZ|0x6ff545df", "0x456C|PUSH|0x2"],
      "comment": "Handle math library error conditions for various math functions.\n\nDispatches error handling based on error codes to appropriate paths,\nsets errno to EDOM (0x21) or ERANGE (0x22), and invokes the matherr\ncallback handler when configured.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store stack canary for security validation\n2. Decode nErrorCode to determine function name and error type:\n   - Error type 1: Domain error (EDOM)\n   - Error type 2: Range underflow (ERANGE)\n   - Error type 3: Range overflow (ERANGE)\n   - Error type 4: Singularity/pole error (ERANGE)\n3. Build error context structure with arg values\n4. Call matherr handler via g_pfnMatherrHandler\n5. If handler returns 0, set errno appropriately\n6. Copy result value to output parameter\n7. Verify stack canary before return\n\nParameters:\npdArg1 - double* - First argument value passed to math function\npdArg2 - double* - Second argument value (for binary ops like pow)\npdResult - double* - Output: result value after error handling\nnErrorCode - int - Error code identifying function and error type\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Result stored in pdResult, errno set on error\n\nError Codes Reference:\n0x02: log domain error (type 2)\n0x03: log domain error (type 1)\n0x08: log10 domain error (type 2)\n0x09: log10 domain error (type 1)\n0x0E: exp overflow (type 3)\n0x0F: exp overflow (type 4)\n0x18: pow domain error (type 3)\n0x19: pow domain error (type 4)\n0x1A: pow(0,0) - returns 1.0\n0x1B: pow domain error (type 2)\n0x1C: pow domain error (type 1)\n0x1D: pow domain error (type 1)\n0xA1: exp2 overflow (type 3)\n0xA2: exp2 overflow (type 4)\n0xA6: exp10 overflow (type 3)\n0xAA: log2 domain error (type 2)\n0xAB: log2 domain error (type 1)\n0x3E8: log domain error (type 1)\n0x3E9: log10 domain error (type 1)\n0x3EA: exp overflow (type 1)\n0x3EB: atan domain error (type 1)\n0x3EC: ceil domain error (type 1)\n0x3ED: floor domain error (type 1)\n0x3EE: pow domain error (type 1)\n0x3EF: modf domain error (type 1)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3ff0000000000000 - IEEE 754 representation of 1.0 (double)\n0x21 (33) - EDOM errno value (domain error)\n0x22 (34) - ERANGE errno value (range error)",
