      "instructions": ["0x48CD|PUSH|EBP", "0x48CE|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x48D0|PUSH|ECX", "0x48D1|PUSH|ECX", "0x48D2|PUSH|EBX", "0x48D3|PUSH|ESI", "0x48D4|MOV|ESI, 0xffff", "0x48D9|PUSH|ESI", "0x48DA|PUSH|dword ptr [0x6ff7e33c]", "0x48E0|CALL|0x6ff5a03f", "0x48E5|FLD|double ptr [EBP + 0x8]", "0x48E8|POP|ECX", "0x48E9|POP|ECX", "0x48EA|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x48EC|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBP + 0xe]"],
      "comment": "Computes the floor of a double-precision floating-point value.\n\nReturns the largest integer value not greater than the input. Handles special\nIEEE 754 cases including infinity, NaN (quiet and signaling), and denormals.\nUses FPU rounding with control word manipulation for proper rounding direction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current FPU control word via __ctrlfp\n2. Extract exponent field and check for special values (exponent == 0x7FF)\n3. If special value, classify via __sptype:\n   a. Type 1-2 (infinity): Restore control word and return input unchanged\n   b. Type 3 (QNaN): Delegate to __handle_qnan1 with floor operation code\n   c. Other: Add 1.0 to trigger inexact exception, set flags to 0x8\n4. If normal value:\n   a. Round toward negative infinity via __frnd\n   b. If rounded equals input OR rounding mode already set, return rounded\n   c. Otherwise set exception flags to 0x10 for inexact result\n5. Call __except1 to handle FPU exceptions with appropriate flags\n6. Return floor result as float10 (80-bit extended precision)\n\nParameters:\n  dValue - Input double-precision value to compute floor of\n\nReturns:\n  float10 - Floor of input as 80-bit extended precision\n            For normal values: largest integer <= dValue\n            For +/-infinity: returns infinity unchanged\n            For NaN: returns NaN (may signal if SNaN)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Positive infinity (0x7FF0...): Returns +infinity\n  - Negative infinity (0xFFF0...): Returns -infinity\n  - Quiet NaN: Handled by __handle_qnan1, returns QNaN\n  - Signaling NaN: Converted to QNaN, may raise invalid exception\n  - Zero: Returns zero (preserves sign)\n  - Denormals: Treated as normal values\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7FF0 - IEEE 754 exponent mask for infinity/NaN detection\n  0x20   - FPU control word rounding direction bit\n  0x8    - Exception flags for special value path (invalid/overflow)\n  0x10   - Exception flags for inexact result\n  0xB    - Floor operation code for exception handler\n\nCalled Functions:\n  __ctrlfp - Get/set FPU control word\n  __sptype - Classify special FP values (0=normal, 1=+inf, 2=-inf, 3=NaN)\n  __frnd   - Round to integer using current rounding mode\n  __handle_qnan1 - Handle quiet NaN with operation code\n  __except1 - Process FPU exception with context",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "CALLEE_5"]
