      "comment": "Reads the next character from a FILE stream buffer (Visual Studio 2003 CRT).\n\nThis is a low-level buffered input helper that manages the FILE structure's\ninternal buffer pointer and count. It handles buffer underflow by calling\n__filbuf to refill when the buffer is exhausted.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decrement pFile->_cnt (buffer remaining character count)\n2. If count >= 0 (buffer has data):\n   a. Read byte at pFile->_ptr\n   b. Increment pFile->_ptr to next position\n   c. Return the byte as unsigned int\n3. If count < 0 (buffer empty):\n   a. Call __filbuf(pFile) to refill buffer and get next char\n   b. Return result from __filbuf\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused (ECX) - Unused parameter (artifact of __fastcall convention)\n  pFile (EDX)   - Pointer to FILE structure with buffer state\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Next character from stream as unsigned int (0-255)\n         Returns EOF (0xFFFFFFFF) on end-of-file or error via __filbuf\n\nFILE Structure Fields Used:\n  Offset  Size  Field   Description\n  0x00    4     _ptr    Current position in buffer (char*)\n  0x04    4     _cnt    Characters remaining in buffer (int)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - When _cnt becomes negative, buffer is exhausted and __filbuf refills it\n  - First parameter is unused but required by __fastcall calling convention",
