      "comment": "Parses a format string and reads input from a FILE stream, implementing the core scanf/sscanf logic.\nThis is the Visual Studio 2003 CRT __input function that processes printf-style format specifiers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH handler and stack canary for security\n2. Loop through each character in the format string (pbFormatString)\n3. For whitespace in format: consume all whitespace from input\n4. For literal characters: match exactly against input\n5. For '%' specifier:\n   a. Parse optional flags: '*' (suppress), width, size modifiers (h/l/L/I64)\n   b. Identify conversion type (d/i/u/o/x/s/c/n/e/f/g/[)\n   c. Read characters from input stream via __inc()\n   d. Convert based on specifier type:\n      - Integer types: decimal, octal, hex parsing with sign handling\n      - Float types: mantissa, decimal point, exponent parsing\n      - String types: copy chars until whitespace or field width\n      - Scanset []: copy chars matching character class\n   e. Store result to output pointer unless suppressed\n6. Validate stack canary before return\n\nParameters:\n  pFile          - FILE stream to read input characters from (via __inc)\n  pbFormatString - Printf-style format string with conversion specifiers  \n  pdwArgList     - Pointer to va_list argument array for output storage\n\nReturns:\n  Number of fields successfully parsed and assigned (via nFieldsAssigned)\n  Returns early on EOF (-1) or format mismatch\n\nFormat Specifier Flags:\n  0x25 '%' - Start format specifier\n  0x2A '*' - Suppress assignment (read but don't store)\n  0x68 'h' - Short modifier\n  0x6C 'l' - Long modifier  \n  0x4C 'L' - Long double modifier\n  0x49 'I' - I32/I64 size prefix\n  \nConversion Types:\n  0x64 'd' - Signed decimal integer\n  0x69 'i' - Integer (auto-detect base from prefix)\n  0x6F 'o' - Unsigned octal\n  0x75 'u' - Unsigned decimal\n  0x78 'x' - Unsigned hexadecimal\n  0x70 'p' - Pointer (hex)\n  0x65/66/67 'e/f/g' - Floating point\n  0x73 's' - String (null-terminated)\n  0x63 'c' - Character(s)\n  0x6E 'n' - Store count of chars read\n  0x5B '[' - Scanset character class\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - I64 prefix enables 64-bit parsing via __allmul\n  - Wide string mode (S/C or 'l' prefix) converts via mbtowc\n  - Scanset supports ranges (a-z) and negation (^)\n  - Floating point parsed via __fptrap callback\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release CRT",
