      "comment": "Parses file mode string and opens a file with appropriate flags.\n\nCRT internal function that translates fopen-style mode strings into low-level\nopen flags, then calls __sopen to open the file and initializes the FILE structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read first mode character to determine base operation (r/w/a)\n2. Set initial open flags: 'r'=0x0, 'w'=0x301, 'a'=0x109\n3. Set file flags from g_dwDefaultFileFlags with read(|1) or write(|2) mask\n4. Parse remaining mode characters in loop:\n   - '+': Enable read/write mode (flags |= 0x2, file flags |= 0x80)\n   - 'b': Binary mode (open flags |= 0x8000)\n   - 't': Text mode (open flags |= 0x4000)\n   - 'T': Temporary file (open flags |= 0x1000)\n   - 'D': Delete on close (open flags |= 0x40)\n   - 'R': Random access hint (open flags |= 0x10)\n   - 'S': Sequential access hint (open flags |= 0x20)\n   - 'c': Commit flag (file flags |= 0x4000)\n   - 'n': No commit flag (file flags &= ~0x4000)\n5. Call __sopen(filename, openFlags, shareFlag, 0x1a4)\n6. If successful, increment g_nOpenFileCount and initialize FILE structure\n7. Return FILE pointer or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n    lpszFilename - Path to file to open\n    lpszMode     - Mode string: base (r/w/a) + optional modifiers (+btTDRScn)\n    nShareFlag   - Share mode for __sopen (_SH_DENYNO, _SH_DENYRD, etc.)\n    pFile        - Preallocated FILE structure to initialize\n\nReturns:\n    FILE* - Initialized FILE pointer on success\n    NULL  - On invalid mode or __sopen failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x109  - O_APPEND | O_CREAT (append mode)\n    0x301  - O_TRUNC | O_CREAT | O_WRONLY (write mode)\n    0x1a4  - File permissions (octal 0644: rw-r--r--)\n    0x8000 - O_BINARY\n    0x4000 - O_TEXT\n    0x1000 - O_TEMPORARY\n    0x0040 - O_SHORT_LIVED (delete on close)\n    0x0010 - O_RANDOM\n    0x0020 - O_SEQUENTIAL\n\nRelated Globals:\n    g_dwDefaultFileFlags (0x6ff805cc) - Base file flags OR'd with mode\n    g_nOpenFileCount (0x6ff803d0) - Count of successfully opened files",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "PARAM_4", "CALLEE_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "RET_STRUCT_PTR", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
