      "comment": "Maps a Windows DOS/system error code to a C runtime errno value.\n\nThis is a CRT library function from Visual Studio that translates Windows\nerror codes (from GetLastError) into portable C errno values stored in\nthread-local storage.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Store the DOS error code in TLS _tdoserrno field for later retrieval\n  2. Search the error mapping table (45 entries) for exact match\n  3. If found in table, set TLS _terrno to the corresponding errno value\n  4. If not found, check special ranges:\n     - Range 0x13-0x24 (19-36): EACCES (permission denied)\n     - Range 0xBC-0xCA (188-202): ENOMEM (out of memory)\n  5. Default unmapped errors: EINVAL (invalid argument)\n\nParameters:\n  dwDosErrorCode - Windows system error code (from GetLastError or similar)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Sets errno via thread-local storage (_terrno field)\n\nError Mapping Table Structure (at g_adwDosToErrnoMap):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x00    4     dwDosError      Windows error code\n  0x04    4     nErrno          Corresponding C errno value\n  Total: 8 bytes per entry, 45 entries (0x2D)\n\nCommon Mappings:\n  ERROR_INVALID_FUNCTION (1)    -> EINVAL (22)\n  ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND (2)      -> ENOENT (2)\n  ERROR_PATH_NOT_FOUND (3)      -> ENOENT (2)\n  ERROR_TOO_MANY_OPEN_FILES (4) -> EMFILE (24)\n  ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED (5)       -> EACCES (13)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x2D (45)  - Number of entries in error mapping table\n  0x13 (19)  - Start of EACCES range (ERROR_WRITE_PROTECT)\n  0x24 (36)  - End of EACCES range (ERROR_SHARING_BUFFER_EXCEEDED)\n  0xBC (188) - Start of ENOMEM range (ERROR_INVALID_SYSTEM_SERVICE)\n  0xCA (202) - End of ENOMEM range (ERROR_STACK_OVERFLOW)\n  0x0D (13)  - EACCES errno value\n  0x08 (8)   - ENOMEM errno value\n  0x16 (22)  - EINVAL errno value (default)",
      "tags": ["CALLEE_1", "CALLER_6", "PARAM_1"]
