      "comment": "Acquires an available FILE stream from the global stream pool for file I/O operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Lock the stream table using __lock(1) to ensure thread-safe access\n2. Iterate through the global file stream array (g_ppFileStreamArray)\n3. For each slot, check if stream exists and is available (flag & 0x83 == 0)\n4. If slot is empty (NULL), allocate new 0x38-byte FILE structure via _malloc\n5. Initialize critical section with ___crtInitCritSecAndSpinCount (spin count 4000)\n6. If critical section init fails, deallocate memory and continue search\n7. For streams at indices 3-19, call __mtinitlocknum for multi-thread lock init\n8. Acquire stream lock via AcquireStreamLock before claiming stream\n9. If stream becomes unavailable after lock, release and continue search\n10. Once stream found, zero-initialize all FILE fields (_ptr, _cnt, _base, _flag, _tmpfname)\n11. Set _file field to -1 (invalid file descriptor)\n12. Call CrtFlushAllFileStreamsCount to update stream counts\n13. Return pointer to acquired stream or NULL if none available\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- FILE*: Pointer to acquired and initialized FILE stream structure on success\n- NULL: No available stream slot found or memory allocation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Streams 0-2 (stdin/stdout/stderr) skip __mtinitlocknum initialization\n- Streams 3-19 require additional multi-thread lock initialization\n- Newly allocated streams require critical section initialization before use\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x38: Size of FILE structure plus critical section (56 bytes)\n- 0x83: Flag mask for stream-in-use bits (READ|WRITE|EOF)\n- 0x10: Lock number offset for stream indices\n- 4000 (0xFA0): Critical section spin count for performance\n- -1 (0xFFFFFFFF): Invalid file descriptor marker\n\nStructure Layout (FILE at offset 0x00):\nOffset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n0x00    4     _ptr        char*   Current buffer position\n0x04    4     _cnt        int     Characters remaining in buffer\n0x08    4     _base       char*   Base of buffer\n0x0C    4     _flag       int     Stream status flags\n0x10    4     _file       int     File descriptor (-1 = invalid)\n0x1C    4     _tmpfname   char*   Temporary filename for tmpfile()\n0x20    24    CritSec     CRIT    Critical section for thread safety",
