      "comment": "Reads data from a file descriptor with text mode CR/LF translation.\n\nThis is a low-level CRT file read function that handles text mode translation\nfor Windows line endings. When in text mode, CR/LF pairs are converted to LF,\nand Ctrl+Z (0x1A) is treated as EOF.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwBytesToRead is non-zero; return 0 if zero\n2. Calculate file handle table entry from nFileDescriptor (index / 32 for table, index % 32 * 0x24 for offset)\n3. Check if handle is closed (flag 0x02); return 0 if closed\n4. If text mode with pending lookahead byte (not LF), consume it first\n5. Call ReadFile() to read dwBytesToRead bytes into buffer\n6. On ReadFile failure: map error 5 (ACCESS_DENIED) to errno 9 (EBADF), error 0x6D (broken pipe) returns 0, others via __dosmaperr\n7. If binary mode (flag 0x80 clear), return bytes read directly\n8. Process text mode translation loop:\n   a. Ctrl+Z (0x1A) in non-pipe mode sets EOF flag (0x02) and exits\n   b. CR (0x0D) followed by LF becomes single LF\n   c. Lone CR at buffer end requires lookahead read; if next is LF, emit LF, else seek back and emit CR\n   d. Store pending lookahead byte in file handle structure at offset 5\n9. Return count of translated bytes written to buffer\n\nParameters:\n  nFileDescriptor - CRT file descriptor index (not Windows HANDLE)\n  szBuffer - Destination buffer for read data\n  dwBytesToRead - Maximum bytes to read\n\nReturns:\n  >= 0: Number of bytes read (after text mode translation)\n  -1: Error occurred (errno set via __dosmaperr)\n  0: EOF, zero-length read, or invalid handle\n\nFile Handle Table Entry Layout (0x24 bytes per entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Description\n  0x00    4     hOsHandle    Windows HANDLE for the file\n  0x04    1     bFlags       File state flags\n  0x05    1     bLookahead   Pending lookahead byte for text mode\n\nFlag Bits (offset 0x04):\n  0x02 - Handle closed/invalid\n  0x04 - First char of buffer was LF (after CR/LF translation)\n  0x08 - Console/device mode\n  0x40 - Pipe mode (Ctrl+Z not treated as EOF)\n  0x48 - Text mode with device (0x08 | 0x40)\n  0x80 - Binary mode (no CR/LF translation)\n\nError Handling:\n  - ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED (5) -> errno 9 (EBADF), DOS error 5\n  - ERROR_BROKEN_PIPE (0x6D) -> returns 0 (EOF)\n  - Other errors -> __dosmaperr() for errno mapping\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Lookahead byte mechanism handles CR at buffer boundary\n  - Text mode files store pending byte at handle offset 5\n  - Ctrl+Z only signals EOF in non-pipe text mode",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "CALLER_2", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "CALLEE_6", "STRUCT_Control"]
