      "comment": "Sets up temporary stream buffering for stdout/stderr before formatted output.\n\nThis is a CRT library function that allocates or reuses a 4KB buffer for\nunbuffered TTY streams (stdout/stderr) to improve I/O performance during\nformatted output operations like printf/vfprintf.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if file descriptor is a TTY device via __isatty()\n2. Return 0 (no buffering needed) if not a TTY\n3. Identify stream: 0 for stdout (0x6ff7e360), 1 for stderr (0x6ff7e380)\n4. Return 0 if stream is neither stdout nor stderr\n5. Increment global open file counter (_g_nOpenFileCount)\n6. Check if stream already has buffering flags (0x10C) set - return 0 if so\n7. Check cached buffer pointer in g_apStdStreamBuffers[nStreamIndex]\n8. If no cached buffer, allocate 4KB (0x1000) via malloc()\n9. On allocation failure, use minimal 2-byte internal charbuf as fallback\n10. Configure FILE structure: set _base, _ptr, _bufsiz, _cnt\n11. Set buffering flags (_flag |= 0x1102) to mark temporary buffering active\n12. Return 1 to indicate buffering was set up\n\nParameters:\n    pFile (FILE*) - Pointer to FILE structure for stdout or stderr stream\n\nReturns:\n    1 - Buffering was successfully set up (caller must call __ftbuf to cleanup)\n    0 - No buffering needed (not TTY, not stdout/stderr, or already buffered)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Non-TTY streams: Returns 0 immediately, no buffering applied\n    - Unknown streams: Only stdout/stderr are handled, others return 0\n    - Allocation failure: Falls back to 2-byte internal FILE::_charbuf buffer\n    - Already buffered: Streams with flags 0x10C set are skipped\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x1000 - Standard buffer size (4096 bytes)\n    0x10C  - Buffering flags mask (_IOMYBUF | _IONBF | _IOLBF)\n    0x1102 - Temporary buffering flags to set (_IOSTRG | _IOMYBUF | _IORW)\n    0x6ff7e360 - Address of stdout FILE structure (g_StdoutFile)\n    0x6ff7e380 - Address of stderr FILE structure (g_StderrFile)\n\nStructure Layout (FILE at ESI):\n    Offset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n    0x00    4     _ptr        char*   Current buffer position\n    0x04    4     _cnt        int     Characters remaining in buffer\n    0x08    4     _base       char*   Base of buffer\n    0x0C    4     _flag       int     Stream status flags\n    0x10    4     _file       int     File descriptor number\n    0x14    2     _charbuf    short   Fallback 2-byte buffer\n    0x18    4     _bufsiz     int     Buffer size in bytes",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "CALLEE_2", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
