      "comment": "Flushes temporary file buffering and resets the FILE stream buffer state.\n\nThis CRT helper function is called after formatted I/O operations to clean up\ntemporary buffering that was enabled during the write operation. It checks if\ntemporary buffering is active (flag 0x1000) and if so, flushes any pending data\nand resets the stream to an unbuffered state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nFlag is non-zero (flush requested)\n2. Check if temporary buffering flag (0x1000) is set in pFile->_flag\n3. If both conditions met, call FlushOutputBuffer to write pending data\n4. Clear buffering mode flags in high byte of _flag (AND with 0xEE)\n5. Reset _bufsiz to 0 (no buffer size)\n6. Reset _ptr to NULL (no current position)\n7. Reset _base to NULL (no buffer base)\n\nParameters:\nnFlag - Non-zero to request flush operation, zero to skip\npFile - Pointer to FILE structure to flush and reset\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nFlag Bits:\n0x1000 - Temporary buffering active (checked before flush)\n0x11   - Buffer mode bits cleared by AND with 0xEE\n\nFILE Structure Fields:\nOffset 0x00 - _ptr: Current buffer position pointer\nOffset 0x08 - _base: Buffer base address  \nOffset 0x0C - _flag: Stream status flags (2 bytes)\nOffset 0x18 - _bufsiz: Buffer size in bytes\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release CRT",
