      "comment": "Flushes the buffered output data from a FILE stream to disk.\n\nThis is the CRT __flush library function from Visual Studio 2003 Release.\nIt writes any pending buffered data to the file descriptor and resets\nthe buffer pointers to their base positions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize return value to 0 (success)\n2. Check if file is in write mode: (_flag & 0x03) == 0x02\n3. Check if buffering is enabled: (_flag & 0x108) != 0\n4. Calculate bytes to write: _ptr - _base\n5. If bytes > 0, call __lseek to write buffer to file descriptor\n6. If write successful and sign bit set in _flag, clear read-write bit\n7. If write failed, set error flag (0x20) and return -1\n8. Reset buffer: set _cnt to 0, restore _ptr to _base\n9. Return result (0 success, -1 error)\n\nParameters:\n  pFile - Pointer to FILE structure containing stream state and buffers.\n          Must be non-NULL and opened for writing.\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Success: buffer flushed and pointers reset\n  -1 - Error: write failed, FILE error flag (0x20) set\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x02  - _IOWRT flag: file open for writing\n  0x03  - Mode mask: read/write mode bits\n  0x108 - _IOFBF|_IOLBF: full or line buffering enabled\n  0x20  - _IOERR flag: I/O error occurred\n  0xFFFFFFFD - Clears bit 1 (read-write bit) from flags\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - No-op if file not in write mode or unbuffered\n  - No-op if buffer is empty (ptr == base)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLEE_1", "CALLER_5", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
