      "instructions": ["0x6703|PUSH|0x14", "0x6705|PUSH|0x6ff757c0", "0x670A|CALL|0x6ff539d0", "0x670F|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x6711|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x1c], EDI", "0x6714|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x24], EDI", "0x6717|PUSH|0x1", "0x6719|CALL|0x6ff53915", "0x671E|POP|ECX", "0x671F|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x4], EDI", "0x6722|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x6724|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x20], ESI", "0x6727|CMP|ESI, dword ptr [0x6ffa8280]", "0x672D|JGE|0x6ff567b4", "0x6733|MOV|EAX, [0x6ffa7260]"],
      "comment": "Flushes all open file streams based on the specified mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call __SEH_prolog to set up structured exception handling\n2. Acquire the IO lock via __lock(1) for thread-safe access\n3. Initialize loop counter nStreamIndex to 0\n4. Loop while nStreamIndex < g_nFileStreamCount:\n   a. Get pFile from g_ppFileStreamArray[nStreamIndex]\n   b. Skip if pFile is NULL\n   c. Skip if (pFile->_flag & 0x83) == 0 (no read/write activity)\n   d. Acquire stream lock via AcquireStreamLock(nStreamIndex, pFile)\n   e. If nFlushMode == 1: flush and count successful flushes\n   f. If nFlushMode == 0 and (pFile->_flag & 0x02): flush for errors\n   g. Release stream lock via ReleaseStreamLockByIndex\n   h. Increment nStreamIndex\n5. Release IO lock and call __SEH_epilog\n6. Return count (mode 1) or error status (mode 0)\n\nParameters:\n  nFlushMode (int): Flush mode selector\n    - 1: Count mode - returns number of streams successfully flushed\n    - 0: Error mode - returns -1 if any flush failed, 0 otherwise\n\nReturns:\n  int: Depends on nFlushMode:\n    - Mode 1: Number of streams successfully flushed (0 to n)\n    - Mode 0: 0 if all flushes succeeded, -1 if any failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Streams with NULL pointer are skipped\n  - Only streams with activity flags (0x83: read|write|read-write) are processed\n  - Uses SEH for exception safety during file operations\n  - Thread-safe via IO lock and per-stream locks\n\nFlag Bits (pFile->_flag at offset +0xC):\n  0x01 - Read mode active\n  0x02 - Write mode active  \n  0x80 - Read-write mode active\n  0x83 - Combined mask for activity check",
