      "comment": "Releases the stream lock for the current file stream during flush-all iteration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read stream index from implicit ESI register (set by caller flsall)\n2. Load FILE* pointer from global stream array at g_ppFileStreamArray[ESI]\n3. Call ReleaseStreamLock to unlock the stream (via __unlock or LeaveCriticalSection)\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ESI (int) - Stream index into g_ppFileStreamArray, passed from flsall loop\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - ESI must be valid stream index (0 to nMaxStreams-1)\n  - Called after AcquireStreamLock and stream processing in flsall\n  - Thunk wrapper that preserves ESI across the lock release call\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - flsall: Caller that iterates streams and sets ESI\n  - AcquireStreamLock (0x6ff55917): Acquires the lock this function releases\n  - ReleaseStreamLock (0x6ff55969): Actually called by this wrapper (mislabeled as AcquireStreamLock)",
