      "comment": "Moves the file pointer of an open file to a specified position with thread safety.\n\nThis is the thread-safe wrapper for __lseek_lk that validates the file handle,\nacquires a lock before seeking, and releases the lock afterward. This is a\nstandard CRT library function matching the Visual Studio 2003 Release implementation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up SEH exception frame via __SEH_prolog\n2. Validate nFileHandle against g_dwMaxFileHandles; fail if >= max\n3. Calculate file handle table slot: index = nFileHandle >> 5, offset = (nFileHandle & 0x1f) * 0x24\n4. Check if handle slot is valid (flag bit 0x1 set at offset +4)\n5. Call __lock_fhandle to acquire thread lock on the file handle\n6. Re-verify handle validity after acquiring lock (handle could be closed)\n7. If still valid, call __lseek_lk(nFileHandle, lOffset, nOrigin) to perform seek\n8. If invalid after lock, set errno=EBADF (9) and return -1\n9. Release lock via UnlockFileHandleThunk\n10. Return seek result via __SEH_epilog\n\nParameters:\n  nFileHandle - File descriptor from _open/_creat (validated against g_dwMaxFileHandles)\n  lOffset     - Number of bytes to move file pointer (signed, can be negative)\n  nOrigin     - Seek origin: SEEK_SET(0)=beginning, SEEK_CUR(1)=current, SEEK_END(2)=end\n\nReturns:\n  Success: New file position as byte offset from beginning of file (>= 0)\n  Failure: -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) with errno set to:\n    EBADF (9) - Invalid file handle or handle not open\n\nCallers: __flsbuf, __ftell_lk, __fseek_lk\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xC        - SEH frame size\n  0x6ff757d8 - SEH handler address\n  0x1F       - Mask for handle slot within table entry (32 handles per entry)\n  0x5        - Shift count for table index (divide by 32)\n  0x24       - Size of each file handle info structure (36 bytes)\n  0x9        - EBADF errno value (bad file descriptor)",
