      "comment": "Closes a file descriptor and releases associated OS handle (CRT internal with lock held).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve OS file handle via __get_osfhandle\n2. If handle invalid (-1), skip to cleanup\n3. For stdout(1)/stderr(2), check if they share same handle (avoid double-close)\n4. Call CloseHandle on the OS handle\n5. If CloseHandle fails, capture error via GetLastError\n6. Call __free_osfhnd to release internal handle tracking\n7. Clear the file handle entry in g_pOsFileHandleTable\n8. If error occurred, map to errno via __dosmaperr and return -1\n\nParameters:\n- nFileDescriptor (int): CRT file descriptor index (0=stdin, 1=stdout, 2=stderr, 3+=user files)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) on failure with errno set\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- stdout/stderr sharing: If fd 1 and 2 point to same OS handle, only first close actually closes\n- Invalid handle: Returns success (0) without calling CloseHandle\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1F (31): Mask for slot index within table block (32 entries per block)\n- 0x24 (36): Size of each file handle entry structure in bytes\n- 0x5 (>>5): Division by 32 to get table block index\n\nStructure Access:\ng_pOsFileHandleTable[nFileDescriptor >> 5] + 4 + (nFileDescriptor & 0x1F) * 0x24\n  - Array of pointers to 32-entry blocks\n  - Each entry: 36 bytes with flag byte at offset +4\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release CRT",
