      "comment": "Closes a file handle after validating it against the CRT file descriptor table.\n\nThis is the CRT library function __close that provides thread-safe file handle\nclosure. It validates the handle, acquires a lock, and delegates to __close_lk\nfor the actual close operation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file handle is within valid range (< g_nMaxFileDescriptors)\n2. Calculate table index: high bits select table segment, low 5 bits select entry\n3. Check if file handle entry is marked as active (flag bit 0x1)\n4. Acquire lock on the file handle via __lock_fhandle\n5. Re-validate handle is still active after acquiring lock (race condition check)\n6. If still valid, call __close_lk to perform actual close\n7. If invalidated during lock acquisition, set errno to EBADF (9)\n8. Release lock via UnlockFileHandleThunk\n9. Return close result or -1 on error\n\nParameters:\n  nFileHandle - CRT file descriptor index to close (0-based)\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Success, file handle closed\n  -1 - Error: invalid handle, handle not open, or close failed\n       errno set to EBADF (9) for invalid handle\n\nError Handling:\n  Sets errno (via GetThreadContextFieldAt8) to EBADF (9) for invalid handles\n  Clears _doserrno (via GetDosErrnoPtr) to 0 on invalid handle error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1f (31) - Mask for entry index within table segment (32 entries per segment)\n  0x24 (36) - Size of each file handle entry structure in bytes\n  0x1       - Active flag bit in file handle entry\n  9         - EBADF errno value (Bad file descriptor)\n\nStructure Layout (File Handle Entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Description\n  0x00    4     osHandle    Win32 HANDLE value\n  0x04    1     flags       Status flags (bit 0 = active)\n  0x05    31    reserved    Padding to 0x24 bytes total",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "PARAM_1", "CALLEE_7"]
