      "comment": "Performs case-insensitive ASCII string comparison (stricmp).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to 0xFF (max 255 iterations)\n2. Load current byte from lpszStr2 into AL, advance pointer\n3. Load current byte from lpszStr1 into AH, advance pointer\n4. If bytes equal, continue to step 2 (fast path)\n5. If bytes differ, convert both to lowercase:\n   - Subtract 0x41 ('A') to get offset from 'A'\n   - If offset < 0x1A (26 letters), add 0x20 to convert to lowercase\n   - Add 0x41 back to restore character value\n6. Compare lowercase versions\n7. If equal after case conversion, continue to step 2\n8. If not equal, compute result: -1 if str1<str2, +1 if str1>str2\n9. Return result via sign-extended AL to EAX\n\nParameters:\n  lpszStr1 [char*] - First null-terminated ASCII string to compare\n  lpszStr2 [char*] - Second null-terminated ASCII string to compare\n\nReturns:\n  < 0 (-1) - lpszStr1 is less than lpszStr2 (case-insensitive)\n  = 0      - Strings are equal (case-insensitive)\n  > 0 (+1) - lpszStr1 is greater than lpszStr2 (case-insensitive)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xFF  - Initial counter/null terminator check value\n  0x41  - ASCII 'A' for uppercase range base\n  0x1A  - 26 letters in alphabet (range check)\n  0x20  - Difference between uppercase and lowercase ASCII\n  0xBF  - Equivalent to -0x41 (subtract 'A')\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Null terminator (0x00) causes immediate exit\n  - Only ASCII A-Z/a-z are case-converted; other chars compared as-is\n  - Empty strings (\"\") compare as equal\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release",
