      "comment": "Selects the appropriate heap allocation strategy based on Windows version.\n\nThis CRT runtime function determines whether to use the Windows Small Block Heap (SBH)\nor the default CRT heap based on the operating system platform ID and major version.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare g_dwOsMajorVersion against value 2 (Windows Server 2003)\n2. If not equal, jump to default return (return 3)\n3. Compare g_dwOsPlatformId against threshold 5 (VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT check)\n4. If platform ID < 5, jump to default return (return 3)\n5. If both conditions pass: XOR EAX, INC EAX to set EAX=1 and return\n6. Otherwise: PUSH 3, POP EAX to set return value 3\n\nParameters:\n  None - Function takes no parameters (reads global OS version state)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Use Small Block Heap (optimized allocation for Windows Server 2003+ NT platform)\n  3 - Use default CRT heap strategy (fallback for older or non-NT systems)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  2   - dwMajorVersion value indicating Windows Server 2003\n  5   - VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT comparison threshold (> 4 means NT-based)\n  1   - SBH heap strategy selector (optimized small block allocation)\n  3   - Default CRT heap strategy selector (standard allocation)\n\nGlobals:\n  g_dwOsMajorVersion (0x6ff80204) - Cached OS major version from GetVersionEx\n  g_dwOsPlatformId (0x6ff80210) - Cached platform ID from GetVersionEx",
