      "instructions": ["0x72C2|MOV|EAX, [0x6ffa7130]", "0x72C7|LEA|ECX, [EAX + EAX*0x4]", "0x72CA|MOV|EAX, [0x6ffa7134]", "0x72CF|LEA|ECX, [EAX + ECX*0x4]", "0x72D2|JMP|0x6ff572e6", "0x72D4|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0x72D8|SUB|EDX, dword ptr [EAX + 0xc]", "0x72DB|CMP|EDX, 0x100000", "0x72E1|JC|0x6ff572ec", "0x72E3|ADD|EAX, 0x14", "0x72E6|CMP|EAX, ECX", "0x72E8|JC|0x6ff572d4", "0x72EA|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x72EC|RET|"],
      "comment": "Finds the SBH (Small Block Heap) region entry containing a given pointer.\n\nSearches through the active SBH region table to find which region owns the\nspecified memory address. Each region manages a 1MB (0x100000) memory block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pRegionEntry to start of g_pSbhRegionTable\n2. Calculate end boundary as table base + (active count * entry size)\n3. Loop through each region entry (20 bytes each):\n   a. Check if pRegionEntry >= end boundary, return NULL if past end\n   b. Calculate offset = dwAddress - region base address (offset 0x0C)\n   c. If offset < 0x100000 (1MB), pointer belongs to this region\n   d. Otherwise advance to next entry (add 0x14)\n4. Return pointer to matching region entry, or NULL if not found\n\nParameters:\n    dwAddress - Memory address (as uint) to locate within SBH regions\n\nReturns:\n    Pointer to SBH region entry (20-byte structure) containing the address\n    NULL (0) if address does not belong to any active SBH region\n\nStructure Layout (SBH Region Entry - 0x14 bytes):\n    Offset  Size  Field           Description\n    0x00    4     pHeader         Pointer to region header\n    0x04    4     pGroupTable     Pointer to group allocation table\n    0x08    4     dwGroupCount    Number of groups in region\n    0x0C    4     pBaseAddress    Base address of 1MB memory block\n    0x10    4     dwFlags         Region state flags\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x14 (20)     - Size of each region entry structure\n    0x100000      - Region size (1MB), used for bounds check\n    0x0C          - Offset to pBaseAddress field in region entry",
      "tags": ["CALLEE_0", "CALLER_3", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LEAF", "PROP_SMALL"]
