      "instructions": ["0x72ED|PUSH|EBP", "0x72EE|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x72F0|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0x72F3|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EBP + 0x8]", "0x72F6|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ECX + 0x10]", "0x72F9|PUSH|ESI", "0x72FA|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EBP + 0xc]", "0x72FD|PUSH|EDI", "0x72FE|MOV|EDI, ESI", "0x7300|SUB|EDI, dword ptr [ECX + 0xc]", "0x7303|ADD|ESI, -0x4", "0x7306|SHR|EDI, 0xf", "0x7309|MOV|ECX, EDI", "0x730B|IMUL|ECX, ECX, 0x204", "0x7311|LEA|ECX, [ECX + EAX*0x1 + 0x144]"],
      "comment": "Frees a small block in the Visual Studio 2003 Small Block Heap (SBH) allocator.\n\nThis function implements block deallocation with coalescing in the SBH system. It merges\nadjacent free blocks, updates the free list bitmaps, and handles deferred region cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate group index from block address using region base (shift by 15 = 32KB groups)\n2. Validate block header (bit 0 clear = free block marker)\n3. Check next block for coalescing opportunity - if free, merge and unlink from free list\n4. Check previous block for coalescing opportunity - if free, merge and unlink from free list\n5. Calculate bucket index from merged block size (size >> 4 - 1, max 63)\n6. Insert merged block into appropriate free list bucket\n7. Update free list bitmaps (bit set = bucket has entries)\n8. Decrement group allocation count\n9. If group becomes completely empty, mark for deferred cleanup\n10. If previous deferred region exists, free its virtual memory and possibly remove from table\n\nParameters:\nparam_1 (pRegionHeader) - Pointer to SBH region header structure containing:\n  [0]: Region bitmap 0 (bits for buckets 0-31)\n  [1]: Region bitmap 1 (bits for buckets 32-63)\n  [2]: Decommit bitmap\n  [3]: Base address of region memory\n  [4]: Group data base pointer\nparam_2 (nBlockAddress) - Address of block being freed (points past header)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Updates global state and free lists.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x8000 - Group size (32KB virtual pages)\n0xf (>> 15) - Group index shift (32KB alignment)\n0x3f (63) - Maximum bucket index\n0x20 (32) - Bitmap boundary between low/high bitmaps\n0x204 (516) - Group header stride in bytes\n0x144 (324) - Offset to first group header\n0x44 - Offset to low bitmap array\n0xc4 - Offset to high bitmap array\n0x43 - Offset to high bitmap group count\n0x4000 - MEM_DECOMMIT flag for VirtualFree\n0x8000 - MEM_RELEASE flag for VirtualFree\n\nStructure Layout (Block Header at address-4):\nOffset  Size  Field      Description\n0x0     4     dwSize     Block size with flags (bit 0 = allocated)\n0x4     4     pNext      Next pointer in free list\n0x8     4     pPrev      Previous pointer in free list\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_pSbhDeferredFreeRegion - Region pending cleanup\ng_dwSbhDeferredFreeGroupIndex - Group index in deferred region\ng_pSbhRegionTable - Base of region table\ng_dwSbhActiveRegionIndex - Count of active regions\ng_pSbhCurrentRegion - Currently selected region\ng_hSbhHeap - Win32 heap handle for metadata",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "CALLER_2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "CALLEE_3", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
