      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new Small Block Heap (SBH) region structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current region count and max region capacity\n2. If region table is full (count == max), expand table via HeapReAlloc\n   - New size = (max * 5 + 0x50) * 4 bytes (grows by 16 entries)\n   - If realloc fails, return NULL\n   - Update max count by 16, store new table pointer\n3. Calculate region structure offset: pTable + regionIndex * 20 (0x14)\n4. Allocate 0x41C4 bytes (16,836) for region metadata via HeapAlloc (HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY)\n5. Store metadata pointer at [pRegion + 0x10]\n6. Allocate 1MB (0x100000) virtual memory via VirtualAlloc (MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_READWRITE)\n7. If VirtualAlloc fails, free metadata and return NULL\n8. Store virtual memory pointer at [pRegion + 0x0C]\n9. Initialize region structure:\n   - [pRegion + 0x08] = 0xFFFFFFFF (no active group)\n   - [pRegion + 0x00] = 0 (first free group index)\n   - [pRegion + 0x04] = 0 (group count)\n10. Increment global region count\n11. Set first dword of metadata to 0xFFFFFFFF (sentinel)\n12. Return pointer to region structure\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void* - Pointer to newly allocated SBH region structure (20 bytes)\n          NULL if HeapReAlloc, HeapAlloc, or VirtualAlloc fails\n\nStructure Layout (SBH Region - 20 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type    Description\n  0x00    4     dwFirstFreeGroup   uint    Index of first free group slot\n  0x04    4     dwGroupCount       uint    Number of allocated groups\n  0x08    4     dwActiveGroup      int     Currently active group (-1 = none)\n  0x0C    4     pVirtualMemory     void*   1MB reserved virtual memory block\n  0x10    4     pMetadata          void*   16,836-byte metadata buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x41C4    - Region metadata size (16,836 bytes)\n  0x100000  - Virtual memory reservation (1MB per region)\n  0x10      - Region table growth increment (16 entries)\n  0x14      - SBH region structure size (20 bytes)\n  0x50      - Initial region table allocation offset\n  0x8       - HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag for HeapAlloc\n  0x2000    - MEM_RESERVE flag for VirtualAlloc\n  0x4       - PAGE_READWRITE protection for VirtualAlloc",
