      "comment": "Resizes a block within the Small Block Heap (SBH) allocator in-place.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate group index from block offset and region base\n2. Compute aligned size (16-byte boundary) from requested size\n3. Extract current block size from header (block[-4] - 1)\n4. Locate next block header for coalescing check\n5. If growing (new > current):\n   a. Check if next block is free (LSB == 0) and has sufficient space\n   b. Return 0 if cannot grow in-place\n   c. Unlink next block from its free list bucket\n   d. Update bitmap to clear bit if bucket becomes empty\n   e. Split remainder if leftover > 0, add to appropriate bucket\n   f. Update block header with new size (marked as allocated with +1)\n6. If shrinking (new < current):\n   a. Update block header with new size\n   b. If next block is free, coalesce with freed portion\n   c. Otherwise create new free block from released space\n   d. Insert free block into appropriate size bucket\n   e. Update bitmaps to mark bucket as non-empty\n7. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n  pSbhHeader - Pointer to SBH header (64 size class bitmaps at offset 0,4)\n  pBlock     - Pointer to user data area (header at pBlock-4)\n  dwNewSize  - Requested new size in bytes (will be aligned to 16 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Block successfully resized in-place\n  0 - Cannot resize (next block busy or insufficient space)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x17       - Alignment padding (rounds up to 16-byte boundary)\n  0xFFFFFFF0 - Alignment mask for 16-byte boundary\n  0x0F       - Shift to convert block address to group (32KB groups)\n  0x204      - Size of group descriptor (516 bytes)\n  0x144      - Offset to bucket lists within region\n  0x3F       - Maximum bucket index (63, for blocks >= 1024 bytes)\n  0x20       - Threshold for bitmap word selection (buckets 0-31 vs 32-63)\n  0x44       - Offset to low group bitmap array (buckets 0-31)\n  0xC4       - Offset to high group bitmap array (buckets 32-63)\n  0x80000000 - Base bit for bucket bitmap operations\n\nStructure Layout (SBH Header):\n  Offset  Size  Field             Description\n  0x00    4     dwBitmapLow       Bitmap for buckets 0-31 (bit set = non-empty)\n  0x04    4     dwBitmapHigh      Bitmap for buckets 32-63\n  0x0C    4     dwRegionStart     Start address of managed region\n  0x10    4     dwRegionBase      Base address for offset calculations\n\nBlock Header Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field             Description\n  -0x04   4     dwSizeTag         Size | 1 if allocated, Size if free\n  +0x00   N     data              User data area\n  +N      4     dwSizeTag         Duplicate of size tag (for reverse coalescing)\n\nFree Block Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field             Description\n  0x00    4     dwSize            Block size (no LSB set)\n  0x04    4     pPrev             Previous free block in bucket list\n  0x08    4     pNext             Next free block in bucket list\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release (CRT SBH Allocator)",
