      "instructions": ["0x7AA1|PUSH|EBP", "0x7AA2|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x7AA4|SUB|ESP, 0x14", "0x7AA7|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EBP + 0x8]", "0x7AAA|MOV|EAX, [0x6ffa7130]", "0x7AAF|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6ffa7134]", "0x7AB5|ADD|ECX, 0x17", "0x7AB8|AND|ECX, 0xfffffff0", "0x7ABB|PUSH|EBX", "0x7ABC|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x10], ECX", "0x7ABF|SAR|ECX, 0x4", "0x7AC2|PUSH|ESI", "0x7AC3|LEA|EAX, [EAX + EAX*0x4]", "0x7AC6|PUSH|EDI", "0x7AC7|DEC|ECX"],
      "comment": "Allocates a memory block from the Small Block Heap (SBH).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Round requested size up to 16-byte aligned value (+0x17, AND 0xFFFFFFF0)\n2. Calculate size class index from aligned size (SAR 4, DEC)\n3. Build bit masks for the size class (high/low 32-bit masks)\n4. Search region table starting from g_pSbhCurrentRegion for available blocks\n5. If no block found in current region, wrap around to search from start\n6. If still no block found, call ___sbh_alloc_new_region to create new region\n7. Once suitable region found, update g_pSbhCurrentRegion\n8. Search within region's group for block with sufficient free space\n9. If group exhausted, call ___sbh_alloc_new_group for new group\n10. Find free list entry of appropriate size class within group\n11. Unlink block from free list (update prev/next pointers)\n12. Split block if remainder is large enough for another allocation\n13. Update group/region bitmaps to reflect allocation\n14. Clear deferred free region if this allocation emptied it\n15. Return pointer to allocated memory (block + 4 for header)\n\nParameters:\n  pdwRequestedSize (uint*): Pointer to requested allocation size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  int*: Pointer to allocated memory block, or NULL if allocation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Sizes > 1016 bytes are not handled by SBH (use regular heap)\n  - Returns NULL if unable to allocate new region or group\n  - Deferred free optimization cleared when allocating from deferred region\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x17 (23): Alignment padding for 16-byte boundary\n  0xFFFFFFF0: Mask for 16-byte alignment\n  0x20 (32): Bits per bitmap word boundary\n  0x14 (20): Size of region table entry (SBHREGION structure)\n  0x204 (516): Size of group data structure\n  0x144 (324): Offset to free lists within region\n  0x44 (68): Offset to low bitmap array in region\n  0xC4 (196): Offset to high bitmap array in region\n  0x3F (63): Maximum size class index\n  0x80000000: MSB mask for bitmap operations\n\nStructure Layout (SBHREGION - 20 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field          Type        Description\n  0x00    4     dwLowBitmap    uint        Low 32-bit free block bitmap\n  0x04    4     dwHighBitmap   uint        High 32-bit free block bitmap  \n  0x08    4     dwGroupCount   uint        Number of active groups\n  0x0C    4     reserved       uint        Reserved/padding\n  0x10    4     pGroupData     void*       Pointer to group data array\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_dwSbhActiveRegionIndex: Index of active region in table\n  g_pSbhRegionTable: Base pointer to region table\n  g_pSbhCurrentRegion: Current region for allocation search\n  g_pSbhDeferredFreeRegion: Region with deferred free blocks\n  g_dwSbhDeferredFreeGroupIndex: Group index in deferred region",
