      "comment": "Invokes the registered new-handler callback when memory allocation fails.\n\nThis is the MSVC CRT __callnewh implementation. When malloc/realloc/calloc\ncannot satisfy a request, they call this function to give the application\na chance to free memory or terminate gracefully.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if a new-handler function pointer is registered (g_pfnNewHandler)\n2. If NULL, return 0 indicating no recovery possible\n3. Call the registered handler with the requested allocation size\n4. If handler returns non-zero, return 1 (retry allocation)\n5. If handler returns zero, return 0 (allocation should fail)\n\nParameters:\n  nRequestedSize - The size in bytes of the failed allocation request\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Handler succeeded, caller should retry allocation\n  0 - No handler registered or handler returned failure\n\nCallers:\n  __nh_malloc - Called on malloc failure before returning NULL\n  _realloc - Called on realloc failure\n  _calloc - Called on calloc failure\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_pfnNewHandler (0x6ff803e0) - Pointer to registered new-handler callback\n                                 Set via _set_new_handler() CRT function\n\nNote: The new-handler pattern allows applications to implement custom\nmemory exhaustion strategies (e.g., freeing caches, logging, graceful exit).",
