      "comment": "Parse command-line arguments from a raw command string into argv/argc format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize character count to zero and argc to 1 (program name)\n2. Store first argument pointer in ppszArgv if provided\n3. Parse first argument handling quotes and DBCS characters\n4. For each remaining argument after whitespace:\n   a. Count consecutive backslashes before quotes\n   b. Handle quote escaping: 2N backslashes + quote = N backslashes + toggle quote mode\n   c. Handle escaped quote: 2N+1 backslashes + quote = N backslashes + literal quote\n   d. Copy non-whitespace characters to output buffer\n   e. Handle DBCS multi-byte characters (lead byte check via g_abMbcTypeTable)\n5. Null-terminate each argument and increment argc\n6. Store sentinel null pointer at end of argv array\n\nParameters:\nppszArgv - Pointer to char* array for storing argument pointers (stack param)\npnArgc - Pointer to int for storing argument count (stack param)\nIMPLICIT pbRawCmdLine (in_EAX) - Pointer to raw command string to parse\nIMPLICIT pbOutputBuffer (in_ECX) - Destination buffer for parsed argument strings\nIMPLICIT pnCharCount (unaff_ESI) - Pointer to character count accumulator\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results stored via output pointers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- ppszArgv can be NULL to just count characters without storing pointers\n- pbOutputBuffer can be NULL to just count characters without copying\n- Handles Windows-style backslash escaping per MSVC CRT conventions\n- Supports DBCS (Double-Byte Character Set) via locale character type table\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x22: Double quote character\n- 0x20: Space character (whitespace delimiter)\n- 0x09: Tab character (whitespace delimiter)\n- 0x5C: Backslash character (escape prefix)\n- 0x04: DBCS lead byte flag in character type table",
