      "instructions": ["0x80A6|PUSH|EBP", "0x80A7|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x80A9|PUSH|ECX", "0x80AA|PUSH|ECX", "0x80AB|PUSH|EBX", "0x80AC|PUSH|ESI", "0x80AD|PUSH|EDI", "0x80AE|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x80B0|CMP|dword ptr [0x6ffa82a0], EDI", "0x80B6|JNZ|0x6ff580bd", "0x80B8|CALL|0x6ff59342", "0x80BD|PUSH|0x104", "0x80C2|MOV|ESI, 0x6ff803e8", "0x80C7|PUSH|ESI", "0x80C8|PUSH|EDI"],
      "comment": "Initializes the C runtime argument vector (argc/argv) from the command line.\n\nThis CRT startup function parses the Windows command line into the standard\nargc/argv format used by main(). It is called during CRT initialization before\nthe application's main() entry point.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize multibyte character table if not already done\n2. Clear module filename terminator and get full module path via GetModuleFileNameA\n3. Store module path as program name (argv[0])\n4. Check if explicit command line is provided; if empty, use module path\n5. First pass: call ParseCommandLine with NULL buffer to count arguments and calculate total buffer size\n6. Allocate combined buffer for argv pointers and argument strings (nArgCount * 4 + nCharBufferSize)\n7. If allocation fails, return -1; otherwise proceed with second pass\n8. Second pass: call ParseCommandLine with allocated buffer to populate argv array\n9. Store final argc (decremented by 1) and argv pointer to global CRT variables\n\nParameters:\n    None (void)\n    IMPLICIT in_ECX: Character buffer size hint (used by ParseCommandLine)\n\nReturns:\n    0: Success - argv array allocated and populated\n   -1: Failure - memory allocation failed\n\nGlobals Modified:\n    g_fMbcTableInitialized (0x6ffa82a0): Checked to ensure MBC table is initialized\n    g_szModuleFilePath (0x6ff804ec): Null terminator set\n    g_szModuleFileNameBuffer (0x6ff803e8): Receives full module file path (MAX_PATH=260 bytes)\n    g_lpszProgramName (0x6ff80234): Pointer to program name (argv[0] source)\n    g_lpszCommandLine (0x6ffa828c): Checked for explicit command line override\n    g_nArgc (0x6ff80218): Stores final argument count (argc - 1)\n    g_ppszArgv (0x6ff8021c): Stores pointer to argv array\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x104 (260): MAX_PATH - maximum path length for GetModuleFileNameA buffer\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release CRT",
      "tags": ["CALLER_1", "PARAM_0", "CALLEE_4"]
