      "instructions": ["0x8148|PUSH|ECX", "0x8149|PUSH|ECX", "0x814A|MOV|EAX, [0x6ff804f0]", "0x814F|PUSH|EBX", "0x8150|PUSH|EBP", "0x8151|PUSH|ESI", "0x8152|PUSH|EDI", "0x8153|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [0x6ff7516c]", "0x8159|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x815B|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x815D|CMP|EAX, EBX", "0x815F|PUSH|0x2", "0x8161|POP|EBP", "0x8162|JNZ|0x6ff58191", "0x8164|CALL|EDI"],
      "comment": "Retrieves the process environment block as an ANSI string buffer.\n\nThis CRT helper function obtains environment strings in ANSI format, handling\nthe Win9x/NT compatibility layer automatically. On first call, it probes for\nUnicode API support and caches the result for subsequent calls.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_nEnvStringMode for cached API selection (0=unknown, 1=wide, 2=ANSI)\n2. If unknown, try GetEnvironmentStringsW first\n3. If wide API fails with ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED (0x78), set mode to ANSI\n4. For wide mode: call GetEnvironmentStringsW, calculate buffer size by\n   scanning for double-null terminator, convert via WideCharToMultiByte\n5. For ANSI mode: call GetEnvironmentStringsA, calculate size, allocate\n   and copy buffer via _memmove\n6. Free the original OS-provided buffer before returning\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- Success: Heap-allocated ANSI environment block (caller must free with free())\n- Failure: NULL if memory allocation fails or no environment available\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First call performs API probe and caches result in g_nEnvStringMode\n- Win9x systems lacking Unicode support fall back to ANSI path\n- Empty environment returns minimal buffer with single null terminator\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x78: ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED - indicates wide API unsupported\n- Mode 0: Unknown/uninitialized\n- Mode 1: Use wide (Unicode) environment APIs\n- Mode 2: Use ANSI environment APIs\n\nStructure:\n- Environment block format: VAR1=VALUE1\\0VAR2=VALUE2\\0\\0 (double-null terminated)",
      "tags": ["CALLER_1", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "CALLEE_7"]
