      "comment": "Filters structured exceptions by looking up handler in thread's exception action table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get thread-local storage context via GetOrCreateTlsContext\n2. Search exception action table for matching exception code (stride 12 bytes)\n3. If no match found, delegate to UnhandledExceptionFilter\n4. If handler is XCPT_HANDLER_USE_DEFAULT (5), clear entry and return EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_EXECUTION (1)\n5. If handler is XCPT_HANDLER_ABORT (1), return EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH (-1)\n6. For SIGFPE (8), reset all FPU exception entries and map NTSTATUS to C signal code\n7. Invoke user-registered signal handler with appropriate arguments\n8. Restore saved TLS state and return EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH (-1)\n\nParameters:\n  dwExceptionNum [Stack+0x4] - NTSTATUS exception code to filter (e.g., 0xC000008E)\n  pExceptionPtr [Stack+0x8] - Pointer to EXCEPTION_POINTERS with exception/context records\n\nReturns:\n  EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_EXECUTION (1) - Exception handled, resume execution\n  EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH (-1) - Continue searching for handlers\n  Result from UnhandledExceptionFilter if no handler registered\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Handler value 0x5 (XCPT_HANDLER_USE_DEFAULT): Clears entry, returns 1\n  Handler value 0x1 (XCPT_HANDLER_ABORT): Returns -1 immediately\n  Handler value 0x8 (SIGFPE): Special FPU exception processing with code mapping\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xC000008D - STATUS_FLOAT_DENORMAL_OPERAND -> FPE_DENORMAL (0x82)\n  0xC000008E - STATUS_FLOAT_DIVIDE_BY_ZERO -> FPE_ZERODIVIDE (0x83)\n  0xC000008F - STATUS_FLOAT_INEXACT_RESULT -> FPE_INEXACT (0x86)\n  0xC0000090 - STATUS_FLOAT_INVALID_OPERATION -> FPE_INVALID (0x81)\n  0xC0000091 - STATUS_FLOAT_OVERFLOW -> FPE_OVERFLOW (0x84)\n  0xC0000092 - STATUS_FLOAT_STACK_CHECK -> FPE_STACKCHECK (0x8A)\n  0xC0000093 - STATUS_FLOAT_UNDERFLOW -> FPE_UNDERFLOW (0x85)\n\nStructure Layout (Exception Action Table Entry - 12 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n  0x00    4   