      "comment": "CRT wrapper for GetStringType that handles ANSI/Unicode conversion.\n\nRetrieves character type information for a string, automatically selecting\nbetween GetStringTypeW (Unicode) and GetStringTypeA (ANSI) based on\nOS capability detection cached in g_dwGetStringTypeWState.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwGetStringTypeWState for cached OS capability:\n   - 0: Uninitialized, probe GetStringTypeW with test call\n   - 1: GetStringTypeW available, use Unicode path\n   - 2: GetStringTypeW failed (error 0x78), use ANSI path\n2. Unicode path (state=1):\n   a. Use default code page if _Code_page is 0\n   b. Call MultiByteToWideChar to get required buffer size\n   c. Allocate wide char buffer (stack or heap based on size)\n   d. Convert ANSI to Unicode via MultiByteToWideChar\n   e. Call GetStringTypeW on converted Unicode string\n   f. Free heap buffer if allocated\n3. ANSI path (state=2 or 0):\n   a. Use default locale if _BError is 0\n   b. Use default code page if _Code_page is 0\n   c. Convert code page via ___convertcp if needed\n   d. Call GetStringTypeA directly\n\nParameters:\n  _Plocinfo  - Locale info structure (unused in current implementation)\n  _DWInfoType - Character type flags (CT_CTYPE1, CT_CTYPE2, CT_CTYPE3)\n  _LpSrcStr  - Source ANSI string to analyze\n  _CchSrc    - Character count (-1 for null-terminated)\n  _LpCharType - Output buffer for character type values\n  _Code_page - Code page for conversion (0=use default)\n  _BError    - Error handling flag (0=use default locale)\n\nReturns:\n  BOOL - TRUE on success, FALSE on failure\n\nLocals:\n  pSehFrame        - SEH exception handler frame pointer\n  wTestCharType    - Temporary for GetStringTypeW capability test\n  fHeapAllocated   - Flag indicating wide buffer was heap-allocated\n  nWideCharCount   - Required wide character buffer size\n\nPhantom Variables (assembly-only):\n  local_24 [EBP-0x24] - GetStringTypeW result storage\n  local_2c [EBP-0x2c] - Wide char buffer pointer (stack alloc)\n  local_30 [EBP-0x30] - Saved ESP for stack unwinding\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If MultiByteToWideChar returns 0, function fails\n  - Small buffers use stack allocation via __chkstk\n  - Large buffers fall back to heap via _calloc\n  - Error 0x78 from GetStringTypeW triggers ANSI fallback\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x78 - ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED (Win9x indicator)\n  0x1  - MB_PRECOMPOSED flag for MultiByteToWideChar\n  0x9  - MB_PRECOMPOSED | MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS",
