      "comment": "Frees dynamically allocated monetary locale strings from an lconv structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pLconv is NULL, return immediately if so\n2. For each monetary field (int_curr_symbol, currency_symbol, mon_decimal_point,\n   mon_thousands_sep, mon_grouping, positive_sign, negative_sign):\n   a. Compare field against corresponding field in default lconv (g_pDefaultLconv)\n   b. Compare field against static default string pointer\n   c. If field differs from both defaults, deallocate it with DeallocateMemory\n\nParameters:\n  pLconv - Pointer to lconv structure containing monetary locale strings to free.\n           If NULL, function returns immediately without action.\n           IMPLICIT: Structure must have been previously allocated with matching allocator.\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Function always succeeds (safe to call with NULL).\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pLconv pointer: Returns immediately without error\n  - Default strings: Not freed to prevent double-free of static memory\n  - Already freed fields: Caller responsibility to avoid double-free\n\nStructure Layout (lconv monetary fields freed):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type    Description\n  0x0C    4     int_curr_symbol    char*   International currency symbol (e.g., \"USD\")\n  0x10    4     currency_symbol    char*   Local currency symbol (e.g., \"$\")\n  0x14    4     mon_decimal_point  char*   Monetary decimal point character\n  0x18    4     mon_thousands_sep  char*   Monetary thousands separator\n  0x1C    4     mon_grouping       char*   Monetary digit grouping pattern\n  0x20    4     positive_sign      char*   Positive monetary value sign\n  0x24    4     negative_sign      char*   Negative monetary value sign\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - ___free_lconv_num: Frees numeric locale fields\n  - ___freetlocinfo: Caller that frees entire thread locale info",
