      "comment": "Calculates length of initial segment of string not containing any charset characters.\n\nStandard C library function that scans lpszString and returns the length of the\ninitial substring that consists entirely of characters NOT found in lpszCharSet.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 256-bit bitmap (32 bytes) to track charset characters\n2. Build bitmap by iterating lpszCharSet, setting bit for each character\n3. Initialize length counter to -1 (increments before first check)\n4. For each character in lpszString:\n   a. Increment length counter\n   b. Check if character bit is set in bitmap\n   c. If set (char in charset), return current length\n   d. If null terminator, return current length\n5. Return length when charset character found or string ends\n\nParameters:\nlpszString  - char* - Input string to scan from beginning\nlpszCharSet - char* - Null-terminated set of characters to reject\n\nReturns:\nsize_t - Length of initial segment NOT containing any charset characters\n         Returns 0 if first char of lpszString is in lpszCharSet\n         Returns strlen(lpszString) if no charset characters found\n\nBitmap Optimization:\nUses 256-bit (32-byte) bitmap for O(1) character lookup\nBit position = char_value, stored as abCharBitmap[char >> 3] bit (char & 7)\n\nExample:\nstrcspn(\"hello world\", \"aeiou\") returns 1 (stops at 'e')\nstrcspn(\"xyz\", \"aeiou\") returns 3 (no vowels found)",
