      "comment": "Fills a block of memory with a specified byte value.\n\nStandard C library memset implementation with DWORD-aligned optimizations.\nUses REP STOSD for bulk filling when destination is aligned.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. If cbSize is zero, return pDst immediately (early exit)\n  2. Extract low byte from nVal (fill value)\n  3. If cbSize > 3 bytes, perform alignment optimization:\n     a. Calculate bytes needed to align pDst to 4-byte boundary\n     b. Fill alignment bytes one at a time\n     c. Expand fill byte to DWORD pattern (0x01010101 * byte)\n     d. Use REP STOSD to fill aligned DWORDs\n  4. Fill any remaining bytes (0-3) one at a time\n  5. Return original destination pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pDst   - void* destination buffer to fill (preserved in return)\n  nVal   - int fill value (only low byte 0xFF mask used)\n  cbSize - size_t number of bytes to fill\n\nReturns:\n  void* - original pDst pointer (enables chained calls)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1010101 - DWORD expansion multiplier (byte -> all 4 positions)\n  0x3       - Alignment mask (4-byte boundary check)\n\nRegister Usage:\n  EDI - current write pointer (preserved/restored)\n  EAX - fill value (byte expanded to DWORD)\n  ECX - loop counter / alignment bytes\n  EDX - remaining size\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio CRT (2003/2019)",
