      "comment": "Compares up to dwMaxCount characters of two null-terminated strings lexicographically.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return 0 immediately if dwMaxCount is 0 (nothing to compare)\n2. Scan lpszStr1 to find its length, capped at dwMaxCount bytes\n3. Calculate effective comparison length as min(strlen(lpszStr1)+1, dwMaxCount)\n4. Compare characters byte-by-byte using CMPSB.REPE instruction\n5. If all compared bytes match and both hit null terminator, return 0\n6. If mismatch found, return negative if lpszStr1 < lpszStr2, positive otherwise\n\nParameters:\nlpszStr1 - First null-terminated string to compare\nlpszStr2 - Second null-terminated string to compare\ndwMaxCount - Maximum number of characters to compare\n\nReturns:\n0 - Strings are equal up to dwMaxCount characters or both terminate at same point\n<0 - First differing character in lpszStr1 is less than in lpszStr2\n>0 - First differing character in lpszStr1 is greater than in lpszStr2\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If dwMaxCount is 0, returns 0 without any comparison\n- Comparison is unsigned byte comparison (treats chars as unsigned)\n- Stops at first null terminator in either string\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xfffffffe - Pre-result value for lpszStr1 < lpszStr2 case (NOT yields 1)\n~uVar5 - Final result: 0 for greater, 1 for less, 0 for equal\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release",
