      "comment": "Scans lpszStr for the first occurrence of any character from lpszControl.\n\nStandard C library strpbrk implementation using a 256-bit bitmap for O(n+m) performance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize 32-byte (256-bit) bitmap to zero on stack\n  2. Build character set: For each char in lpszControl, set corresponding bit\n     - Byte index = char_value >> 3 (divide by 8)\n     - Bit position = char_value & 7 (mod 8)\n     - Uses BTS (Bit Test and Set) instruction\n  3. Scan lpszStr: For each char, test if bit is set in bitmap\n     - Uses BT (Bit Test) instruction for efficient lookup\n  4. Return pointer to first matching character, or NULL if none found\n\nParameters:\n  lpszStr     - [in] Null-terminated string to scan\n  lpszControl - [in] Null-terminated string containing characters to match\n\nReturns:\n  char* - Pointer to first occurrence of any control character in lpszStr\n  NULL  - If no characters from lpszControl are found in lpszStr\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x20 (32)   - Bitmap size in bytes (256 bits / 8 bits per byte)\n  >> 3        - Divide by 8 to get byte index in bitmap\n  & 7         - Mod 8 to get bit position within byte\n\nPerformance: O(n + m) where n = strlen(lpszStr), m = strlen(lpszControl)",
