      "comment": "Initializes uppercase/lowercase character conversion tables for multibyte code page support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save stack canary for security verification\n2. Call GetCPInfo to query current code page information\n3. If GetCPInfo fails, fall back to simple ASCII case mapping (A-Z <-> a-z)\n4. Initialize 256-byte character type buffer with 0x20 (space) for non-letter bytes\n5. For each lead byte range from CPINFO:\n   a. Mark bytes in range with 0x20 in type buffer using REP STOSD/STOSB\n   b. Advance through range pairs until null terminator\n6. Call ___crtGetStringTypeA to get Windows character type flags (CT_CTYPE1)\n7. Call ___crtLCMapStringA twice:\n   a. First with LCMAP_UPPERCASE to build uppercase conversion table\n   b. Second with LCMAP_LOWERCASE to build lowercase conversion table\n8. For each byte 0-255, examine string type flags:\n   a. If C1_UPPER (0x01): set 0x10 flag in type table, store lowercase mapping\n   b. If C1_LOWER (0x02): set 0x20 flag in type table, store uppercase mapping\n   c. Otherwise: store 0 (no case conversion)\n9. Verify stack canary and return\n\nParameters:\n  None - Uses global code page state (CodePage_6ffa7004, g_dwMbcLocaleHandle)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Tables are stored in global variables\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\n  g_abMbcTypeTable+1 (0x6ffa6f01) - Character type flags (0x10=upper, 0x20=lower)\n  g_abUpperLowerMap (0x6ffa7020)  - 256-byte case conversion lookup table\n\nGlobal Variables Read:\n  CodePage_6ffa7004 (0x6ffa7004) - Current active code page\n  g_dwMbcLocaleHandle (0x6ffa6ee4) - Locale handle for string operations\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x100 (256)     - Size of character tables (ESI loop counter)\n  0x200 (512)     - LCMAP_LOWERCASE flag for LCMapString\n  0x20            - Space character / lowercase type flag\n  0x10            - Uppercase type flag in g_abMbcTypeTable\n  0x01 (C1_UPPER) - Windows character type: uppercase letter\n  0x02 (C1_LOWER) - Windows character type: lowercase letter\n  0x41-0x5A       - ASCII uppercase range (A-Z)\n  0x61-0x7A       - ASCII lowercase range (a-z)\n\nCalled By:\n  SetMultibyteCodePageLocked - After code page tables are initialized\n\nDependencies:\n  GetCPInfo           - Windows API for code page information\n  ___crtGetStringTypeA - CRT wrapper for GetStringTypeA\n  ___crtLCMapStringA   - CRT wrapper for LCMapStringA\n  VerifyStackCanary   - Stack buffer overrun detection",
