      "comment": "Initializes multibyte code page tables for CRT string functions (locked version).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save stack canary for security verification\n2. If dwCodePage is 0, call setSBCS to reset to single-byte mode and return\n3. Search predefined code page table (5 entries at 0x30 byte stride) for match\n4. If match found in predefined table:\n   a. Clear 257-byte type table (g_abMbcTypeTable) to zero\n   b. Copy lead byte ranges and character type flags from predefined entry\n   c. Set g_dwMbcFlags to 1 (DBCS enabled)\n   d. Call MapMessageIdToCommand to set locale handle\n   e. Copy lead byte ranges to global array\n5. If not in predefined table, call GetCPInfo to query Windows:\n   a. If GetCPInfo fails and g_dwAllowCodePageChange is 0, return -1\n   b. If GetCPInfo fails and g_dwAllowCodePageChange is 1, call setSBCS\n   c. If GetCPInfo succeeds with MaxCharSize <= 1, reset to SBCS mode\n   d. If MaxCharSize > 1 (DBCS), build type table from CPINFO lead byte ranges\n6. Call setSBUpLow to initialize uppercase/lowercase tables\n7. Verify stack canary and return 0 on success\n\nParameters:\n  dwCodePage - Windows code page identifier (e.g., 932=Japanese, 936=Chinese)\n               Pass 0 to reset to single-byte character set mode\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Success, code page tables initialized\n  -1 - Failure, code page not supported or GetCPInfo failed\n\nStructure Layout (CPINFO at EBP-0x18):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x00    4     MaxCharSize     Maximum bytes per character (1=SBCS, 2=DBCS)\n  0x04    2     DefaultChar     Default character for unmappable chars\n  0x06    12    LeadByte        Lead byte ranges (up to 5 pairs + null terminator)\n\nPredefined Code Page Table Entry (0x30 bytes each):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x00    4     dwCodePage      Code page identifier\n  0x08    8     LeadByteRanges  Lead byte range pairs\n  0x10    32    CharTypeFlags   Character type flags for each range\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x30 (48)  - Size of predefined code page entry\n  0xF0 (240) - 5 entries * 0x30 = search limit\n  0x40 (64)  - DWORDs to clear in type table (256/4)\n  0x04       - Lead byte type flag (indicates lead byte of DBCS pair)\n  0x08       - Trail byte type flag\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\n  g_abMbcTypeTable (0x6ffa6f00)    - 257-byte character type lookup table\n  CodePage_6ffa7004               - Current active code page\n  g_dwMbcFlags (0x6ffa6eec)       - MBCS flags (0=SBCS, 1=DBCS)\n  g_dwMbcLocaleHandle (0x6ffa6ee4) - Locale handle for string operations\n  g_awLeadByteRanges (0x6ffa7010) - Lead byte range pairs",
      "tags": ["CALLER_1", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_1", "CALLEE_4", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
