      "instructions": ["0x91F2|PUSH|0x14", "0x91F4|PUSH|0x6ff76278", "0x91F9|CALL|0x6ff539d0", "0x91FE|OR|dword ptr [EBP + -0x20], 0xffffffff", "0x9202|PUSH|0xd", "0x9204|CALL|0x6ff53915", "0x9209|POP|ECX", "0x920A|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x920C|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x4], EDI", "0x920F|MOV|dword ptr [0x6ff80570], EDI", "0x9215|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBP + 0x8]", "0x9218|CMP|EAX, -0x2", "0x921B|JNZ|0x6ff5922f", "0x921D|MOV|dword ptr [0x6ff80570], 0x1", "0x9227|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff7518c]"],
      "comment": "Sets the multibyte code page for the CRT library.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire lock on CRT data structures via __SEH_prolog and __lock(0xD)\n2. Clear g_dwAllowCodePageChange flag initially\n3. Handle special code page values:\n   - CP_ACP (-2): Use system ANSI code page via GetACP()\n   - CP_OEMCP (-3): Use system OEM code page via GetOEMCP()\n   - CP_THREAD_ACP (-4): Use thread-specific default code page\n4. If requested code page matches current, return success (0)\n5. Allocate or reuse MBC info buffer (0x220 bytes):\n   - Check if g_pMbcInfo exists and is valid\n   - If not, allocate new buffer via _malloc(0x220)\n6. Call SetMultibyteCodePageLocked to configure code page tables\n7. If configuration succeeds, copy locale data:\n   - Copy current code page to buffer offset 0x4\n   - Copy MBC flags to buffer offset 0x8\n   - Copy locale handle to buffer offset 0xC\n   - Copy lead byte ranges (5 words at offset 0x10)\n   - Copy MBC type table (257 bytes at offset 0x1C)\n   - Copy upper/lower case map (256 bytes at offset 0x11D)\n8. Update g_pMbcInfo global pointer\n9. On failure, deallocate buffer if it differs from current\n10. Release lock and return result\n\nParameters:\nnCodePage (int): Code page identifier to set. Special values:\n  -2 (CP_ACP): Use system ANSI code page\n  -3 (CP_OEMCP): Use system OEM code page  \n  -4 (CP_THREAD_ACP): Use thread default code page\n\nReturns:\n0: Success - code page was set or already active\n-1: Failure - code page not supported or allocation failed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xD: CRT lock ID for multibyte code page data\n0x220: Size of MBC info structure (544 bytes)\n-2: CP_ACP constant\n-3: CP_OEMCP constant\n-4: CP_THREAD_ACP constant\n\nStructure Layout (MBC Info Buffer at pMbcInfo):\nOffset  Size  Field              Description\n0x00    4     dwRefCount         Reference count (0 when initializing)\n0x04    4     dwCodePage         Active code page number\n0x08    4     dwMbcFlags         Multibyte character flags\n0x0C    4     dwLocaleHandle     Locale handle for this code page\n0x10    10    awLeadByteRanges   5 WORD pairs for lead byte ranges\n0x1C    257   abMbcTypeTable     Character type classification table\n0x11D   256   abUpperLowerMap    Case conversion mapping table",
