      "instructions": ["0x93FB|PUSH|EBP", "0x93FC|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x93FE|SUB|ESP, 0x20", "0x9401|PUSH|EBX", "0x9402|PUSH|ESI", "0x9403|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EBP + 0x8]", "0x9406|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x8]", "0x9409|TEST|BL, 0x3", "0x940C|JNZ|0x6ff59429", "0x940E|MOV|EAX, FS:[0x18]", "0x9414|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + 0x8], EAX", "0x9417|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBP + 0x8]", "0x941A|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EAX + 0x8]", "0x941D|CMP|EBX, ECX", "0x941F|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x4], ECX"],
      "comment": "Validates an EH3 exception handler registration node for security and integrity.\n\nThis is a Visual Studio 2003 CRT security function that validates exception handler\nregistrations to prevent exploitation via SEH (Structured Exception Handling) overwrites.\nIt checks pointer alignment, stack bounds, scope table validity, and uses a page cache\nto optimize repeated validations from the same memory page.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check handler table pointer alignment (must be 4-byte aligned)\n2. Verify handler table is not within current thread's stack bounds (TEB check)\n3. If scope table count is -1 (no handlers), return valid immediately\n4. Iterate scope table entries validating parent indices are properly ordered\n5. Count entries with non-null filter functions for later validation\n6. Check page address against validated page cache (16-entry MRU cache)\n7. If cache hit at index 0, return valid immediately (hot path)\n8. If cache hit elsewhere, acquire lock and promote entry to front (MRU update)\n9. If cache miss, call VirtualQuery to validate memory region\n10. Verify memory is MEM_IMAGE type (0x1000000 = loaded from executable)\n11. If memory has executable protection, validate PE header structure\n12. Check MZ signature (0x5A4D), PE signature (0x4550), optional header magic (0x10B)\n13. Verify handler is not in discardable section (section flags bit 0x80)\n14. Add validated page to cache with spinlock synchronization\n15. Return validation result\n\nParameters:\npExceptionFrame (ExceptionFrame*) - Pointer to exception registration node\n    containing handler pointer at offset +8 and scope table count at offset +0xC\n\nReturns:\n1  - Handler registration is valid\n0  - Handler registration is invalid (potential exploit attempt)\n-1 (0xFFFFFFFF) - Memory query failed or non-image memory type\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Scope table count of -1 indicates no exception handlers (early valid return)\n- Cache index 0 hit returns immediately without lock acquisition (optimization)\n- InterlockedExchange failure returns valid (assumes concurrent validation)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3            - Pointer alignment mask (must be 4-byte aligned)\n0xFFFFFFFF (-1)- No handlers sentinel / error return value\n0xFFFFF000     - Page address mask (4KB page alignment)\n0x1000000      - MEM_IMAGE type (memory mapped from executable file)\n0xCC           - PAGE_EXECUTE_* protection flags mask\n0x5A4D         - DOS MZ signature\n0x4550         - PE signature\n0x10B          - PE32 optional header magic\n0x10           - Maximum cache size (16 entries)\n0x80           - IMAGE_SCN_MEM_DISCARDABLE flag\n\nError Handling:\n- VirtualQuery failure returns -1 (query error)\n- Non-image memory type returns -1 (suspicious)\n- Invalid PE headers return -1 (corrupted executable)\n- Discardable section handler returns 0 (invalid handler location)\n\nThread Safety:\nUses InterlockedExchange spinlock (g_lPageCacheLock) for cache updates.\nCache reads before lock acquisition use snapshot for consistency.\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_nValidatedPageCount (0x6ff80578) - Number of cached page addresses (max 16)\ng_adwValidatedPageCache (0x6ff80580) - Array of 16 validated page addresses\ng_lPageCacheLock (0x6ff805c0) - Spinlock for thread-safe cache updates",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "CALLEE_1", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
