      "instructions": ["0x9624|INC|dword ptr [0x6ff803d0]", "0x962A|PUSH|0x1000", "0x962F|CALL|0x6ff52e19", "0x9634|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x9636|POP|ECX", "0x9637|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0x963B|MOV|dword ptr [ECX + 0x8], EAX", "0x963E|JZ|0x6ff5964d", "0x9640|OR|dword ptr [ECX + 0xc], 0x8", "0x9644|MOV|dword ptr [ECX + 0x18], 0x1000", "0x964B|JMP|0x6ff5965e", "0x964D|OR|dword ptr [ECX + 0xc], 0x4", "0x9651|LEA|EAX, [ECX + 0x14]", "0x9654|MOV|dword ptr [ECX + 0x8], EAX", "0x9657|MOV|dword ptr [ECX + 0x18], 0x2"],
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a stream buffer for a FILE structure.\n\nAttempts to allocate a 4KB (0x1000 byte) heap buffer for buffered I/O. If\nallocation succeeds, sets the _IOMYBUF flag indicating a dynamically allocated\nbuffer. If malloc fails, falls back to using the FILE's internal 2-byte\n_charbuf as an unbuffered fallback with _IONBF flag set.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment global open file count (g_nOpenFileCount)\n2. Attempt to allocate 0x1000 (4096) bytes via _malloc\n3. Store allocated pointer in pFile->_base\n4. If allocation succeeded:\n   a. Set _IOMYBUF flag (0x8) in pFile->_flag\n   b. Set pFile->_bufsiz to 0x1000 (4096 bytes)\n5. If allocation failed (NULL returned):\n   a. Set _IONBF flag (0x4) in pFile->_flag (unbuffered mode)\n   b. Point pFile->_base to internal pFile->_charbuf\n   c. Set pFile->_bufsiz to 2 (minimal buffer)\n6. Reset pFile->_cnt to 0 (no characters in buffer)\n7. Set pFile->_ptr to pFile->_base (read/write position at start)\n\nParameters:\n  pFile - FILE * - Pointer to FILE structure requiring buffer initialization.\n          Must be a valid, opened FILE stream. The _base, _ptr, _cnt,\n          _flag, and _bufsiz fields will be modified.\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Buffer state reflected in FILE structure fields.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1000 - Standard CRT buffer size (4096 bytes, one memory page)\n  0x8    - _IOMYBUF flag: buffer was allocated by CRT (must be freed)\n  0x4    - _IONBF flag: stream is unbuffered (using minimal internal buffer)\n  0x2    - Fallback buffer size (sizeof(_charbuf) in FILE structure)\n\nFILE Structure Layout (relevant fields):\n  Offset  Size  Field     Type    Description\n  0x00    4     _ptr      char*   Current position in buffer\n  0x04    4     _cnt      int     Characters remaining in buffer\n  0x08    4     _base     char*   Base address of buffer\n  0x0C    4     _flag     int     Stream status flags\n  0x14    2     _charbuf  char[2] Internal minimal buffer for unbuffered I/O\n  0x18    4     _bufsiz   int     Total buffer size in bytes\n\nError Handling:\n  malloc failure handled gracefully by falling back to unbuffered mode using\n  the internal 2-byte _charbuf. No error code returned; caller must check\n  _flag for _IONBF to detect fallback occurred.",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_3", "CALLEE_1", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
