      "comment": "Converts a wide character to a multibyte string representation (multi-threaded version).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if lpszMultiByte is NULL; return 0 if so (validation check)\n2. Check if pLocaleInfo->dwLocaleFlags (+0x14) is zero:\n   a. If zero and wchWideChar < 0x100: direct single-byte copy, return 1\n   b. If non-zero: use WideCharToMultiByte() for conversion\n3. Call WideCharToMultiByte() with:\n   - CodePage from pLocaleInfo (+0x4)\n   - cbMultiByte from pLocaleInfo (+0x28)\n   - wchWideChar as input (1 character)\n4. Verify conversion succeeded and no default char was used\n5. On error: set errno to EILSEQ (0x2A) and return -1\n\nParameters:\n  pLocaleInfo (threadlocaleinfostruct*): Pointer to thread locale info structure\n    +0x04: CodePage (UINT) - code page for conversion\n    +0x14: dwLocaleFlags (DWORD) - if 0, single-byte locale; else multi-byte\n    +0x28: cbMultiByte (int) - max bytes for output buffer\n  lpszMultiByte (LPSTR): Destination buffer for multibyte string\n  wchWideChar (WCHAR): Wide character to convert\n\nReturns:\n  >0: Number of bytes written to lpszMultiByte (1 for single-byte, varies for multi-byte)\n  0: If lpszMultiByte is NULL\n  -1: Conversion error (errno set to EILSEQ/0x2A)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL output buffer returns 0 (no error)\n  - Single-byte locales bypass WideCharToMultiByte for ASCII chars\n  - Default character substitution triggers error\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x14 - Offset to locale flags in threadlocaleinfostruct\n  0x04 - Offset to CodePage in threadlocaleinfostruct\n  0x28 - Offset to max multibyte length in threadlocaleinfostruct\n  0xFF - Maximum single-byte character value\n  0x2A - EILSEQ (illegal sequence) errno value",
