      "comment": "Converts a wide character to its multibyte representation using the current thread locale.\n\nThis is a CRT library wrapper function that retrieves thread-local locale information\nand delegates to ___wctomb_mt for the actual conversion. Uses thread-local storage\nto maintain per-thread locale state for thread-safe multibyte conversions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetOrCreateTlsContext to get thread-local data pointer\n2. Extract locale info pointer from TLS context at offset 0x64\n3. Compare with g_pDefaultLocaleInfo to check if thread has custom locale\n4. If locale differs from default, call ___updatetlocinfo to synchronize\n5. Push wide character and output buffer onto stack\n6. Call ___wctomb_mt with locale info to perform conversion\n7. Return conversion result (byte count or -1 on error)\n\nParameters:\n  szMultiByte (char*) - Output buffer for multibyte character sequence.\n                        If NULL, function returns 0 without conversion.\n  wchWideChar (wchar_t) - Wide character to convert to multibyte.\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of bytes written to szMultiByte on success (1 for ASCII, 1-2 for MBCS)\n        0 if szMultiByte is NULL\n       -1 on conversion error (errno set to EILSEQ/0x2A)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL output buffer returns 0 immediately without conversion\n- ASCII characters (< 0x100) in C locale are stored directly as single byte\n- Non-ASCII in C locale triggers error (no MBCS support)\n- MBCS locales use WideCharToMultiByte for conversion\n\nDecompiler Variables (register temporaries, not renameable):\n  p_Var1 (_ptiddata*) - TLS context pointer from GetOrCreateTlsContext\n  ptVar2 (pthreadlocinfo) - Locale info pointer extracted from TLS at offset 0x64\n  iVar3 (int) - Return value from ___wctomb_mt conversion",
