      "comment": "Raises a Windows structured exception for FPU floating-point errors.\n\nThis is a Visual Studio 2003 CRT library function that translates x87 FPU exception \nstatus bits to Windows NT exception codes and raises an SEH exception via \nRaiseException. After the exception handler returns (if not unwound), the function \nrestores the FPU control word and copies the result operand back.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize exception context fields at offsets +4, +8, +0xC to zero\n2. Check each FPU exception flag in dwExcFlags and map to NT exception code:\n   - 0x10 (Inexact)     -> 0xC000008F STATUS_FLOAT_INEXACT_RESULT\n   - 0x02 (Overflow)    -> 0xC0000093 STATUS_FLOAT_OVERFLOW\n   - 0x01 (Underflow)   -> 0xC0000091 STATUS_FLOAT_UNDERFLOW\n   - 0x04 (Div by Zero) -> 0xC000008E STATUS_FLOAT_DIVIDE_BY_ZERO\n   - 0x08 (Invalid)     -> 0xC0000090 STATUS_FLOAT_INVALID_OPERATION\n3. Set exception mask bits in context[1] corresponding to triggered exceptions\n4. Convert FPU control word exception mask bits to internal format in context[2]\n5. Call __statfp to get current FPU status and map sticky flags to context[3]\n6. Extract rounding control (bits 10-11) and precision control (bits 8-9) from \n   FPU control word and encode into context[0]\n7. Encode exception cause into context[0] bits 5-16\n8. Store operand1 at context offset 0x10 with valid tag at context[8]\n9. Store operand2 at context offset 0x50 with valid tag at context[0x18]\n10. Call __clrfp to clear FPU status flags\n11. Call RaiseException with computed exception code and context pointer\n12. On return: restore modified exception masks to FPU control word from context[2]\n13. Restore rounding control and precision control to FPU control word\n14. Copy result operand from context[0x50] back to pdOperand2\n\nParameters:\n  pFpuExcContext - Pointer to FPU exception context structure (minimum 0x64 bytes)\n                   Layout: [0]=flags/rounding, [1]=exc mask, [2]=restored mask,\n                   [3]=status, [8]=op1 tag, [0x10]=operand1, [0x18]=op2 tag, [0x50]=operand2\n  pFpuControlWord - Pointer to current x87 FPU control word (updated on return)\n  dwExcFlags - FPU exception flags bitmask (x87 status word format):\n               0x01=Underflow, 0x02=Overflow, 0x04=DivByZero, 0x08=Invalid, 0x10=Inexact\n  nExcCause - Exception cause code (shifted and stored in bits 5-16 of context[0])\n  pdOperand1 - Pointer to first 64-bit floating-point operand\n  pdOperand2 - Pointer to second 64-bit floating-point operand (also receives result)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function returns normally if exception handler continues execution.\n         On return, pFpuControlWord is updated with modified exception masks,\n         rounding mode, and precision control. pdOperand2 receives the result\n         operand from the exception context.\n\nFPU Control Word Bit Layout (x87):\n  Bits 0-5:   Exception mask (IM, DM, ZM, OM, UM, PM)\n  Bits 8-9:   Precision Control (00=24bit, 01=reserved, 10=53bit, 11=64bit)\n  Bits 10-11: Rounding Control (00=nearest, 01=down, 10=up, 11=truncate)",
