      "comment": "Handles FPU exception recovery by processing exception flags and returning appropriate special values.\n\nVisual Studio 2003 CRT library function that processes floating-point exceptions and modifies\nthe result value based on exception type and FPU control word rounding mode settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exception flags from dwExceptionFlags (bits 0-4)\n2. Check for overflow exception (bit 3) with mask enabled - return infinity\n3. Check for zero-divide exception (bit 2) with mask enabled - return infinity  \n4. Check for divide-by-zero/invalid (bit 0) with mask (bit 3) - compute special value based on rounding mode:\n   - Round nearest (0x000): +/- infinity based on operand sign\n   - Round down (0x400): +DBL_MAX or -infinity based on sign\n   - Round up (0x800): +infinity or -DBL_MAX based on sign\n   - Truncate (0xC00): +/- DBL_MAX based on sign\n5. Check for underflow/denormal (bit 1) with mask (bit 4) - denormalize the result\n6. Check for precision loss (bit 4) with mask (bit 5) - signal inexact\n7. Return true if all exceptions handled, false if unhandled exceptions remain\n\nParameters:\n  dwExceptionFlags (uint) - FPU exception status flags:\n    Bit 0 (0x01): Invalid operation / requires special value computation\n    Bit 1 (0x02): Denormal operand / underflow requiring denormalization\n    Bit 2 (0x04): Zero divide exception\n    Bit 3 (0x08): Overflow exception  \n    Bit 4 (0x10): Underflow / precision loss\n  pdResult (double*) - Pointer to result value, modified with special value on exception\n  dwControlWord (uint) - FPU control word with exception masks and rounding mode:\n    Bit 0: Overflow exception mask\n    Bit 2: Zero-divide exception mask\n    Bit 3: Invalid operation mask\n    Bit 4: Underflow exception mask\n    Bit 5: Precision exception mask\n    Bits 10-11 (0xC00): Rounding control mode\n\nReturns:\n  true - All exceptions were successfully handled\n  false - Unhandled exceptions remain in the flags\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1F   - Exception flag mask (bits 0-4)\n  0x17   - Clear overflow flag (AND mask)\n  0x1B   - Clear zero-divide flag (AND mask)\n  0x1E   - Clear invalid operation flag (AND mask)\n  0xC00  - Rounding mode mask (bits 10-11)\n  0x400  - Round toward negative infinity\n  0x800  - Round toward positive infinity\n  0x432  - Minimum biased exponent threshold for denormalization\n  0x3FD  - Denormal exponent adjustment constant\n  0x600  - Exponent bias adjustment for decomposition\n\nCalled By: __except1, ProcessFpuExceptionHandler\nCalls: InitializeFloatingPointExceptions, __decomp",
