      "comment": "Converts FPU status word exception flags to CRT math error codes.\n\nThis is a Visual Studio 2003 CRT library function that maps x87 FPU exception\nbits from the status word to corresponding C runtime error codes for math\nexception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load FPU status flags from stack parameter\n2. Test bit 5 (precision exception) - if set, return 5\n3. Test bit 3 (invalid operation) - if set, return 1\n4. Test bit 2 (zero divide) - if set, return 2\n5. Test bit 0 (overflow) - if set, return 3\n6. Test bit 1 (underflow) - if set, return 2; otherwise return 0\n\nParameters:\n    bFpuStatusFlags (byte): Lower byte of x87 FPU status word containing:\n        Bit 0 (0x01): Overflow Exception (OE)\n        Bit 1 (0x02): Underflow Exception (UE)\n        Bit 2 (0x04): Zero Divide Exception (ZE)\n        Bit 3 (0x08): Invalid Operation Exception (IE)\n        Bit 5 (0x20): Precision Exception (PE)\n\nReturns:\n    int - CRT math error code:\n        0: No error (or only underflow without bit 1 set)\n        1: DOMAIN error (invalid operation, e.g., sqrt of negative)\n        2: SING error (singularity/zero divide) or underflow result\n        3: OVERFLOW error\n        5: TLOSS error (total loss of precision)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n    0x20 = Precision exception flag mask\n    0x08 = Invalid operation flag mask\n    0x04 = Zero divide flag mask\n    0x01 = Overflow flag mask\n    0x02 = Underflow flag mask\n\nNote: The uStack_4 in decompiled output is a phantom variable - the actual\nimplementation uses PUSH/POP to return the error code via EAX.",
