      "comment": "Handles C runtime math library errors by invoking user-defined matherr callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search g_adwMathExceptionCodeTable for matching exception code (up to 29 entries)\n2. If match found, retrieve associated error handler index from table[match+4]\n3. If no match, nErrorIndex = 0 (unknown error type)\n4. If nErrorIndex is non-zero:\n   a. Build _exception struct on stack with type, name, arg1, arg2, retval\n   b. Set FPU control word mask to 0xFFFF via __ctrlfp\n   c. Call user matherr() callback with _exception struct pointer\n   d. If matherr returns 0 (not handled), call ProcessParameterValue to set errno\n   e. Return dRetval from _exception struct\n5. If nErrorIndex is zero:\n   a. Set FPU control word via __ctrlfp\n   b. Call ProcessParameterValue with nExceptionType\n   c. Return original dRetval parameter\n\nParameters:\n- nExceptionType (int): Math exception type code (DOMAIN=1, SING=2, OVERFLOW=3, etc.)\n- lpszFunctionName (char*): Name of math function that caused exception (e.g., \"sqrt\", \"log\")\n- dArg1 (double): First argument to the math function\n- dArg2 (double): Second argument (if applicable, otherwise undefined)\n- dRetval (double): Default return value for the exception\n- dwFpuControlWord (dword): FPU control word state to restore\n\nReturns:\n- double: Return value from _exception.retval if matherr handled, otherwise dRetval\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1D (29): Maximum entries in exception code lookup table\n- 0xFFFF: FPU control word mask for all exceptions\n\nStructure Layout (_exception built at EBP-0x20):\nOffset  Size  Field       Type      Description\n0x00    4     type        int       Exception type code\n0x04    4     name        char*     Function name pointer  \n0x08    8     arg1        double    First function argument\n0x10    8     arg2        double    Second function argument\n0x18    8     retval      double    Return value\n\nError Handling:\n- If matherr callback returns 0, ProcessParameterValue sets appropriate errno\n- Unknown exception codes (no table match) skip matherr and go directly to errno",
