      "comment": "Sets the exponent field of a floating-point number while preserving the mantissa.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the input double value from the stack into FPU (FLD)\n2. Store to local stack buffer for bit manipulation (FSTP)\n3. Add IEEE 754 double exponent bias (0x3FE = 1022) to new exponent\n4. Shift biased exponent left by 4 bits to position in high word\n5. Mask original high word preserving sign bit and high mantissa bits (0xFFFF800F)\n6. OR new exponent into masked high word\n7. Store modified high word back to stack buffer\n8. Reload modified double as float10 and return\n\nParameters:\n  param_1 (double) - Input floating-point value whose exponent will be replaced\n  param_2 (short) - New unbiased exponent value to apply\n  Note: param_1 is undefined8 in signature due to library function lock\n\nReturns:\n  float10 - Modified floating-point number with new exponent and original mantissa\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  The function assumes valid IEEE 754 double format input\n  Exponent bias 0x3FE (1022) is applied to convert from unbiased to biased form\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3FE (1022) - IEEE 754 double-precision exponent bias minus 1\n  0x10 - Left shift to position exponent in bits 52-62 of double\n  0xFFFF800F - Mask preserving sign bit (15), unused bits (11-14), and low mantissa (0-3)\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release\n\nNote: in_stack_0000000a is an assembly-only phantom variable at [EBP+0xA] representing\nthe high word of param_1 accessed directly for exponent manipulation. The variable\n__return_storage_ptr__ is auto-generated by Ghidra for returning float10 values.",
