      "comment": "Classifies IEEE 754 double-precision floating-point special values.\n\nThis is a Visual Studio 2003 CRT helper function used by __fpclass and __floor_default\nto detect infinities, NaNs, and subnormal values. Takes a 64-bit double split into\ntwo 32-bit words and returns a classification code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if high word equals 0x7FF00000 (positive infinity exponent)\n2. If positive infinity pattern and low word is zero, return FP_PINF (1)\n3. Check if high word equals 0xFFF00000 (negative infinity exponent)\n4. If negative infinity pattern and low word is zero, return FP_NINF (2)\n5. Extract exponent+mantissa bits at offset 2 (param_2._2_2_) and mask with 0x7FF8\n6. If masked value equals 0x7FF8, this is a Quiet NaN, return FP_QNAN (3)\n7. If masked value equals 0x7FF0 and mantissa bits are non-zero, return FP_SNAN (4)\n8. Otherwise return FP_NORMAL (0) indicating normal number, zero, or denormal\n\nParameters:\n  dwDoubleLow   [in] uint - Low 32 bits of IEEE 754 double (mantissa bits 0-31)\n  dwDoubleHigh  [in] uint - High 32 bits of IEEE 754 double (sign, exponent, mantissa bits 32-51)\n\nReturns:\n  0 = FP_NORMAL  - Normal number, zero, or denormalized value\n  1 = FP_PINF    - Positive infinity (+INF, 0x7FF0000000000000)\n  2 = FP_NINF    - Negative infinity (-INF, 0xFFF0000000000000)\n  3 = FP_QNAN    - Quiet NaN (non-signaling, has 0x7FF8 pattern)\n  4 = FP_SNAN    - Signaling NaN (triggers exception on use)\n\nIEEE 754 Double Format:\n  Bit 63:      Sign bit (0=positive, 1=negative)\n  Bits 62-52:  Exponent (11 bits, biased by 1023)\n  Bits 51-0:   Mantissa (52 bits, implicit leading 1)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7FF00000 - High word of positive infinity (exponent all 1s, sign 0)\n  0xFFF00000 - High word of negative infinity (exponent all 1s, sign 1)\n  0x7FF8     - Mask for quiet NaN detection (includes quiet bit)\n  0x7FF0     - Mask for signaling NaN detection (exponent only)\n  0x7FFFF    - Mantissa mask for high word (bits 51-32)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "CALLER_2", "CALLEE_0", "PROP_LEAF"]
