      "instructions": ["0x9F6C|PUSH|EBP", "0x9F6D|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x9F6F|PUSH|ECX", "0x9F70|PUSH|ECX", "0x9F71|FLD|double ptr [0x6ff78fe8]", "0x9F77|FLD|double ptr [EBP + 0x8]", "0x9F7A|FUCOMPP|", "0x9F7C|FNSTSW|AX", "0x9F7E|TEST|AH, 0x44", "0x9F81|JP|0x6ff59f8c", "0x9F83|FLDZ|", "0x9F85|XOR|EDX, EDX", "0x9F87|JMP|0x6ff5a01b", "0x9F8C|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x9F8E|TEST|word ptr [EBP + 0xe], 0x7ff0"],
      "comment": "Decomposes a double-precision floating-point value into normalized fraction and exponent.\n\nThis is the internal CRT implementation of frexp(). It extracts the mantissa\n(normalized to range [0.5, 1.0)) and the binary exponent from an IEEE 754 double.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if input value equals zero (compare with g_dZero constant)\n  2. If zero, return 0.0 with exponent 0\n  3. Check if exponent bits (bits 52-62) are all zero (denormalized number)\n  4. For denormalized: normalize by left-shifting mantissa until implicit bit set\n     - Track shifts in exponent adjustment (starts at -1021 for denormalized)\n     - Preserve sign bit during normalization\n  5. For normal numbers: extract exponent from bits 52-62\n     - Subtract bias (0x3FE = 1022) to get unbiased exponent\n  6. Call __set_exp to set the normalized mantissa exponent to -1 (range [0.5, 1.0))\n  7. Store computed exponent via output pointer\n\nParameters:\n  dwMantissaLo  - Low 32 bits of IEEE 754 double (bits 0-31 of mantissa)\n  dwMantissaHi  - High 32 bits: sign(1) + exponent(11) + mantissa(20)\n  pnExponent    - Output pointer for binary exponent value\n\nReturns:\n  float10 - Normalized fraction in range [0.5, 1.0) or (-1.0, -0.5] for negative\n  *pnExponent receives the power of 2 such that: value = fraction * 2^exponent\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero input: Returns 0.0, exponent = 0\n  - Denormalized: Normalizes mantissa, adjusts exponent accordingly\n  - Normal: Extracts and unbias exponent directly\n\nIEEE 754 Double Layout (64-bit):\n  Offset  Size  Field          Description\n  0       52    Mantissa       Fractional part (implicit 1.xxxxx)\n  52      11    Exponent       Biased exponent (bias = 1023)\n  63      1     Sign           0=positive, 1=negative\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7FF00000 - Exponent field mask (bits 52-62 in high word)\n  0x000FFFFF - Mantissa high bits mask (bits 32-51)\n  0x3FE      - Exponent bias minus 1 (1022) for frexp normalization\n  0xFFFFFC03 - Initial denormalized exponent (-1021 as signed)",
