      "instructions": ["0xA125|PUSH|EBP", "0xA126|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0xA128|PUSH|EBX", "0xA129|PUSH|ESI", "0xA12A|PUSH|EDI", "0xA12B|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [EBP + 0x10]", "0xA12E|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0xA130|CMP|EDI, EBX", "0xA132|JZ|0x6ff5a149", "0xA134|CMP|dword ptr [EBP + 0x14], EBX", "0xA137|JZ|0x6ff5a149", "0xA139|MOV|AL, byte ptr [EDI]", "0xA13B|CMP|AL, BL", "0xA13D|JNZ|0x6ff5a150", "0xA13F|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBP + 0xc]"],
      "comment": "Converts a multi-byte character to a wide character using thread-local locale settings.\n\nThis is the multi-threaded safe version of the C runtime mbtowc function. It handles \nsingle-byte and multi-byte character encodings based on the locale's code page.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (NULL check and byte count > 0)\n2. Check if first byte is null terminator - return 0 with null wide char if so\n3. If locale has no multi-byte support (hLocale == 0):\n   - Direct byte-to-wide cast for single-byte encoding\n   - Return 1 byte consumed\n4. Check character type table (pCtypeTable) for lead byte indicator (bit 0x80):\n   - If NOT a lead byte: Call MultiByteToWideChar with 1 byte\n   - If lead byte: Get max bytes from nCtypeVersion, call MultiByteToWideChar\n5. On conversion failure: Set errno to EILSEQ (0x2A) and return -1\n\nParameters:\npLocaleInfo - ThreadLocaleInfo structure pointer containing:\n              dwCodePage: Code page (UINT) at offset +0x04\n              hLocale: Multi-byte flag at offset +0x14 (0 = single-byte locale)\n              nCtypeVersion: Max bytes per character at offset +0x28\n              pCtypeTable: Pointer to character type table at offset +0x48\nwszOut      - Output buffer for wide character (may be NULL for length query)\npbMultibyte - Input multi-byte character string\ndwMaxBytes  - Maximum bytes to examine from input\n\nReturns:\n0  - Empty input or null terminator encountered\n1  - Single-byte character converted successfully\nN  - N bytes consumed for multi-byte character (value from nCtypeVersion)\n-1 - Conversion error (errno set to EILSEQ/0x2A)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x09  - MB_ERR_INVALID_CHARS flag for MultiByteToWideChar\n0x2A  - EILSEQ errno value (illegal byte sequence)\n0x80  - Lead byte indicator in character type table",
