      "instructions": ["0xA334|PUSH|0x10", "0xA336|PUSH|0x6ff76350", "0xA33B|CALL|0x6ff539d0", "0xA340|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0xA342|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x1c], EBX", "0xA345|PUSH|0x1", "0xA347|CALL|0x6ff53915", "0xA34C|POP|ECX", "0xA34D|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x4], EBX", "0xA350|PUSH|0x3", "0xA352|POP|EDI", "0xA353|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x20], EDI", "0xA356|CMP|EDI, dword ptr [0x6ffa8280]", "0xA35C|JGE|0x6ff5a3b4", "0xA35E|MOV|ESI, EDI"],
      "comment": "Closes all open file streams except stdin, stdout, and stderr.\n\nIterates through the global file stream table starting at index 3 (skipping\nthe standard streams) and closes each stream that has active flags. For\nstreams beyond the initial 20, also deletes associated critical sections\nand deallocates memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire file stream table lock via __lock(1)\n2. Initialize closed stream counter to zero\n3. Loop through stream indices 3 to g_nFileStreamCount-1\n4. For each stream pointer in g_ppFileStreamArray:\n   a. Skip if stream pointer is NULL\n   b. Check if stream has active flags (0x83 mask: _IOREAD | _IOWRT | _IORW)\n   c. Call CloseFileStreamIfNotLocked to flush and close\n   d. Increment counter if close succeeded (not -1)\n5. For streams at index >= 20 (dynamically allocated):\n   a. Delete critical section at stream+0x20\n   b. Deallocate stream memory\n   c. Clear pointer in table\n6. Release file stream table lock\n7. Return count of successfully closed streams\n\nParameters:\n   None - operates on global file stream table\n\nReturns:\n   int - Number of file streams successfully closed (not including failures)\n         Returns 0 if no streams were open or all closes failed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n   0x83 - Flag mask for active streams (_IOREAD=0x01 | _IOWRT=0x02 | _IORW=0x80)\n   3    - Starting index (skip stdin=0, stdout=1, stderr=2)\n   0x14 - Threshold index 20 for dynamically allocated streams\n   0x20 - Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION within FILE structure",
