      "comment": "Releases the file stream table critical section lock (index 1).\n\nThis is a simple wrapper function that unlocks the critical section protecting\nthe global file stream table. It pairs with __lock(1) to provide thread-safe\naccess to the stream array during file close operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push lock index 1 onto stack\n2. Call AcquireCriticalSectionByIndex (which actually releases the lock)\n3. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called at the end of __fcloseall after all stream processing complete\n- Lock index 1 corresponds to the file stream table critical section\n- Must be called after __lock(1) to properly release the lock\n\nNote: AcquireCriticalSectionByIndex is misnamed - it calls LeaveCriticalSection,\nso it releases rather than acquires locks.",
