      "instructions": ["0xA3CF|PUSH|EBP", "0xA3D0|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0xA3D2|SUB|ESP, 0x1c", "0xA3D5|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [EBP + 0x14]", "0xA3D8|PUSH|EBX", "0xA3D9|PUSH|ESI", "0xA3DA|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0xA3DC|TEST|DL, DL", "0xA3DE|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x1c], 0xc", "0xA3E5|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x18], ESI", "0xA3E8|JNS|0x6ff5a3f3", "0xA3EA|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x14], ESI", "0xA3ED|MOV|byte ptr [EBP + -0x1], 0x10", "0xA3F1|JMP|0x6ff5a3fe", "0xA3F3|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x14], 0x1"],
      "comment": "Opens a file with thread-safe locking using the C runtime file handle system.\nThis is a low-level CRT function that wraps CreateFileA with additional C runtime\nfile descriptor management and text/binary mode handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize security attributes based on O_NOINHERIT flag (bit 7 of dwOpenFlags)\n2. Set text mode flag (0x80) based on O_BINARY/O_TEXT flags and default text mode\n3. Translate access mode (bits 0-1) to Windows dwDesiredAccess:\n   - 0 (O_RDONLY) -> GENERIC_READ (0x80000000)\n   - 1 (O_WRONLY) -> GENERIC_WRITE (0x40000000)\n   - 2 (O_RDWR) -> GENERIC_READ|GENERIC_WRITE (0xC0000000)\n4. Translate share mode (dwShareModeFlag in ECX) to Windows dwShareMode:\n   - 0x10 (SH_DENYRW) -> 0 (no sharing)\n   - 0x20 (SH_DENYWR) -> FILE_SHARE_READ (1)\n   - 0x30 (SH_DENYRD) -> FILE_SHARE_WRITE (2)\n   - 0x40 (SH_DENYNO) -> FILE_SHARE_READ|WRITE (3)\n5. Translate creation flags (bits 8-10) to Windows dwCreationDisposition:\n   - 0x000/0x400 (O_OPEN) -> OPEN_EXISTING (3)\n   - 0x100 (O_CREAT) -> OPEN_ALWAYS (4)\n   - 0x200 (O_TRUNC) -> TRUNCATE_EXISTING (5)\n   - 0x300 (O_CREAT|O_TRUNC) -> CREATE_ALWAYS (2)\n   - 0x500/0x700 (O_CREAT|O_EXCL) -> CREATE_NEW (1)\n6. Build file attributes from additional flags:\n   - O_RANDOM (0x10) -> FILE_FLAG_RANDOM_ACCESS (0x10000000)\n   - O_SEQUENTIAL (0x20) -> FILE_FLAG_SEQUENTIAL_SCAN (0x8000000)\n   - O_TEMPORARY (0x40) -> FILE_FLAG_DELETE_ON_CLOSE (0x4000000)\n   - O_SHORT_LIVED (0x1000) -> FILE_ATTRIBUTE_TEMPORARY (0x100)\n7. Allocate a CRT file handle via __alloc_osfhnd\n8. Call CreateFileA with translated parameters\n9. Detect file type (disk, character device, pipe) via GetFileType\n10. Store OS handle and set file flags in CRT handle table\n11. If text mode and O_RDWR, check for Ctrl-Z EOF marker and truncate if found\n12. Set O_APPEND flag (0x20) in handle table if requested\n\nParameters:\n  dwShareModeFlag (ECX) - Share mode constant (0x10-0x40)\n  pdwFlags (Stack+0x04) - OUT: Returns 1 on success\n  pdwFileHandle (Stack+0x08) - OUT: Receives allocated CRT file handle\n  lpszFilePath (Stack+0x0C) - Path to file to open\n  dwOpenFlags (Stack+0x10) - Open mode flags (O_RDONLY, O_CREAT, O_BINARY, etc.)\n  bPermission (Stack+0x14) - Permission mode (used with O_CREAT)\n\nReturns:\n  Success: CRT file descriptor (non-negative integer)\n  Failure: -1 (0xFFFFFFFF), errno set to:\n    - EINVAL (0x16): Invalid access mode or creation flags\n    - EMFILE (0x18): Too many open files\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8000 - O_BINARY flag\n  0x4000 - O_TEXT flag\n  0x80000000 - GENERIC_READ\n  0x40000000 - GENERIC_WRITE\n  0xC0000000 - GENERIC_READ | GENERIC_WRITE\n  0x4000000 - FILE_FLAG_DELETE_ON_CLOSE\n  0x8000000 - FILE_FLAG_SEQUENTIAL_SCAN\n  0x10000000 - FILE_FLAG_RANDOM_ACCESS\n  0x1A - Ctrl-Z (text mode EOF marker)\n  0x83 - ERROR_NEGATIVE_SEEK",
      "tags": ["PARAM_6", "PROP_LARGE", "CALLEE_13", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
