      "comment": "Opens a file with sharing mode and optional file permissions.\n\nC runtime library wrapper that provides shared file open functionality with\nSEH exception handling. This is the variadic version that accepts optional\npermission mode for file creation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH prolog for exception handling\n2. Clear local variables (lock handle and SEH state)\n3. Call OpenFileWithLock with filename, flags, share mode, and output handles\n4. Store returned file handle\n5. Call UnlockFileHandleIfNeeded for cleanup\n6. Return file handle via SEH epilog\n\nParameters:\n  lpszFilename - Pointer to null-terminated filename string to open\n  nOpenFlag - File open flags (O_RDONLY, O_WRONLY, O_RDWR, O_APPEND, etc.)\n  nShareFlag - Sharing mode flags (SH_DENYRW, SH_DENYWR, SH_DENYRD, SH_DENYNO)\n  ... - Optional permission mode (int) when O_CREAT is specified\n\nReturns:\n  >= 0: Valid file handle on success\n  -1: Error occurred (errno set to indicate error)\n\nStack Layout:\n  [EBP-0x08] nSehState - SEH exception state tracking\n  [EBP-0x1c] Cleared to 0 during init\n  [EBP-0x20] nLockHandle - Output lock handle from OpenFileWithLock\n  [EBP-0x24] nFileHandle - Returned file descriptor\n  [EBP+0x08] lpszFilename - Input filename parameter\n  [EBP+0x0c] nOpenFlag - Input open flags\n  [EBP+0x10] nShareFlag - Input share flags (passed in ECX to callee)\n  [EBP+0x14] Optional permission mode for file creation",
