      "comment": "Sets an OS file handle in the CRT file descriptor table.\n\nThis function stores a Windows HANDLE value in the internal ioinfo table\nat the slot specified by the file descriptor number. For standard handles\n(stdin=0, stdout=1, stderr=2), it also updates the Windows standard handle\nvia SetStdHandle when console output mode is enabled.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file descriptor is within maximum range (g_nMaxFileDescriptors)\n2. Calculate ioinfo table offset: block index = fd >> 5, entry index = fd & 0x1F\n3. Each ioinfo entry is 0x24 (36) bytes; compute byte offset = (fd & 0x1F) * 0x24\n4. Verify slot is empty (current handle == -1 / INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE)\n5. If console mode and fd is 0/1/2, call SetStdHandle with appropriate constant\n6. Store new handle value at computed table offset\n7. Return 0 on success, -1 on error\n\nParameters:\n  nFileDescriptor - CRT file descriptor number (0-based index)\n  hOsHandle       - Windows HANDLE value to store (cast to intptr_t)\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Success, handle stored in ioinfo table\n  -1 - Failure, errno set to EBADF (9), _doserrno cleared\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - fd 0: Maps to STD_INPUT_HANDLE  (0xFFFFFFF6 = -10)\n  - fd 1: Maps to STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE (0xFFFFFFF5 = -11)\n  - fd 2: Maps to STD_ERROR_HANDLE  (0xFFFFFFF4 = -12)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1F  - Mask for entry index within 32-entry block\n  0x24  - Size of ioinfo structure (36 bytes)\n  0x05  - Right shift to get block index (fd / 32)\n  9     - EBADF errno value (bad file descriptor)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "CALLER_1", "CALLEE_3"]
