      "comment": "Frees an OS file handle entry from the CRT file handle table.\n\nInvalidates the file descriptor by setting its OS handle to -1 (INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE).\nFor standard handles (stdin=0, stdout=1, stderr=2), also calls SetStdHandle to reset\nthe Windows standard handle when running in console output mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file descriptor is within bounds (< g_dwMaxFileHandles)\n2. Calculate table index: entry = table[fd >> 5] + (fd & 0x1F) * 0x24\n3. Check entry is allocated (flags & 1) and has valid handle (!= -1)\n4. If console mode and fd is 0/1/2, call SetStdHandle(STD_xxx_HANDLE, NULL)\n5. Set OS handle to -1 to mark entry as free\n6. On any validation failure, set errno=EBADF(9) and _doserrno=0\n\nParameters:\n  nFileDescriptor - CRT file descriptor index (0-based)\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success (handle freed)\n  -1 on error (invalid descriptor, sets errno=EBADF)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x24 (36) - Size of file handle table entry structure\n  0x1F (31) - Mask for entry index within table segment (32 entries per segment)\n  0xFFFFFFF6 (-10) - STD_INPUT_HANDLE\n  0xFFFFFFF5 (-11) - STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE  \n  0xFFFFFFF4 (-12) - STD_ERROR_HANDLE\n  9 - EBADF (Bad file descriptor)",
