      "comment": "Acquires exclusive lock on a file handle for thread-safe I/O operations.\n\nCalculates the file handle entry offset into the global OS file handle table\n(g_pOsFileHandleTable) using a two-level indexing scheme. If the critical\nsection for this handle entry is not initialized, initializes it with a spin\ncount of 4000 before entering. Uses SEH for cleanup on initialization failure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up SEH frame for exception handling\n2. Calculate file entry offset: table[handle >> 5] + (handle & 0x1F) * 0x24\n3. Check if critical section is initialized (offset + 8)\n4. If not initialized:\n   a. Acquire global lock (lock 10)\n   b. Double-check initialization (race condition protection)\n   c. Initialize critical section with spin count 4000\n   d. On failure, unwind SEH and return 0\n   e. Increment initialization counter\n   f. Release global lock\n5. Enter the critical section for this file handle\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  nFileHandle - File handle index to lock. Used to calculate entry offset\n                via (handle >> 5) for table index and (handle & 0x1F) * 0x24\n                for entry offset within the table block.\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Lock acquired successfully\n  0 - Critical section initialization failed (unwind performed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First access to a file handle requires critical section initialization\n- Uses double-checked locking pattern for thread safety\n- Spin count of 4000 (0xFA0) optimizes for short waits\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x24 (36) - Size of each file handle entry structure\n  0x1F (31) - Mask for 32 handles per table block\n  0x0A (10) - Global MT initialization lock identifier\n  0xFA0 (4000) - Critical section spin count\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field               Description\n  0x00    4     dwFlags             File handle flags\n  0x04    4     dwFileHandle        OS file handle value\n  0x08    4     dwCritSecInitialized  1 if critical section valid\n  0x0C    24    criticalSection     CRITICAL_SECTION structure\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release CRT",
