      "comment": "Releases the critical section lock for a file handle entry in the I/O info table.\n\nThis is the counterpart to __lock_fhandle(). Must be called after completing\nfile I/O operations to allow other threads to access the file handle. Part of\nthe Visual Studio 2003 CRT thread-safe file handle management system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract table index from file handle (upper 27 bits via SAR 5)\n2. Extract entry index within table (lower 5 bits via AND 0x1F)\n3. Look up ioinfo table pointer from g_pIoInfoTable[tableIndex]\n4. Calculate critical section offset: base + 0x0C + (entryIndex * 0x24)\n5. Call LeaveCriticalSection to release the lock\n\nParameters:\n- nFileHandle (int): CRT file handle (not OS handle). Contains packed indices:\n  - Bits 5-31: Table index into g_pIoInfoTable array\n  - Bits 0-4: Entry index within the 32-entry ioinfo block\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value. Critical section is always released.\n\nStructure Layout (ioinfo entry, 0x24 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field               Description\n0x00    4     osfhnd              OS file handle (HANDLE)\n0x04    1     osfile              File flags (FOPEN, FTEXT, etc.)\n0x05    1     pipech              Pipe character buffer\n0x06    2     padding             Alignment padding\n0x08    4     lockinitflag        Lock initialization state\n0x0C    24    lock                CRITICAL_SECTION for thread safety\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1F: Mask for entry index (5 bits = 32 entries per block)\n- 0x24: Size of ioinfo structure (36 bytes)\n- 0x0C: Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION within ioinfo structure\n- SAR 5: Divide by 32 to get table block index",
