      "instructions": ["0xA909|PUSH|0x14", "0xA90B|PUSH|0x6ff76380", "0xA910|CALL|0x6ff539d0", "0xA915|OR|dword ptr [EBP + -0x1c], 0xffffffff", "0xA919|PUSH|0xb", "0xA91B|CALL|0x6ff53875", "0xA920|POP|ECX", "0xA921|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xA923|JZ|0x6ff5a9aa", "0xA929|PUSH|0xb", "0xA92B|CALL|0x6ff53915", "0xA930|POP|ECX", "0xA931|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0xA933|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x4], EDI", "0xA936|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x24], EDI"],
      "comment": "Allocates a free OS file handle slot from the CRT file handle table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize multi-threading lock for file handle table access (lock 0xb)\n2. If lock initialization fails, return -1 immediately\n3. Acquire the file handle table lock\n4. Iterate through 64 possible handle table slots (0x40 slots)\n5. For each slot, check if table chunk is allocated:\n   a. If NULL, allocate new chunk (0x480 bytes = 32 entries x 36 bytes each)\n   b. Initialize all 32 entries: flags=0, handle=-1, pipech=10, lockinitflag=0\n   c. Update g_dwMaxFileHandles by 32\n6. Search chunk for free entry (flags bit 0 not set)\n7. If entry's critical section not initialized, initialize it with spin count 4000\n8. Enter the entry's critical section to claim it\n9. Double-check entry still free, if so mark handle=-1 and calculate index\n10. Release locks and return allocated handle index\n\nParameters:\nNone - void function\n\nReturns:\nint - File handle index (0 to g_dwMaxFileHandles-1) on success\n      -1 on failure (lock init failed, malloc failed, or no free slots)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Thread-safe via CRT lock 0xb and per-entry critical sections\n- Double-checked locking pattern for critical section initialization\n- SEH protected for proper cleanup on exceptions\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0xb: CRT lock number for file handle table\n- 0xa (10): Lock number for critical section initialization\n- 0x40 (64): Maximum number of handle table chunks\n- 0x480 (1152): Size of each chunk (32 entries x 36 bytes)\n- 0x24 (36): Size of each file handle entry structure\n- 0x20 (32): Entries per chunk\n- 4000: Spin count for critical section initialization\n\nStructure Layout (OsFileHandleEntry - 36 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n0x00    4     osHandle        int     OS file handle (-1 if free)\n0x04    1     flags           byte    Status flags (bit 0 = in-use)\n0x05    1     pipech          byte    Pipe character (default 10)\n0x06    2 