      "comment": "Seeks to a 64-bit file position using the Windows SetFilePointer API (locked version).\n\nThis is the CRT internal locked implementation of _lseeki64. It converts a CRT file \ndescriptor to an OS file handle, performs the seek operation, and clears the \nFEOF (end-of-file) flag in the file descriptor's ioinfo structure on success.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert CRT file descriptor to Windows HANDLE via GetOsFileHandle\n2. If handle invalid (0xFFFFFFFF), set errno to EBADF (9) and return -1\n3. Call SetFilePointer with 64-bit offset (low/high parts) and move method\n4. If SetFilePointer fails (returns 0xFFFFFFFF), check GetLastError\n5. If error non-zero, map Windows error code to errno via __dosmaperr and return -1\n6. On success, clear the FEOF bit (0x02) in the ioinfo flags at offset +4\n7. Return new 64-bit file position as longlong (high:low)\n\nParameters:\n  param_1 (dwFileDescriptor) - CRT file descriptor index (uint)\n  param_2 (lDistanceToMoveLow) - Low 32 bits of the seek offset (LONG)\n  param_3 (lDistanceToMoveHigh) - High 32 bits of the seek offset (LONG)\n  param_4 (dwMoveMethod) - Seek origin (DWORD):\n    FILE_BEGIN (0) - Seek from start of file\n    FILE_CURRENT (1) - Seek from current position\n    FILE_END (2) - Seek from end of file\n\nReturns:\n  Success: New 64-bit file position as longlong (CONCAT44 of high:low)\n  Failure: -1 (0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF) with errno set\n    - EBADF (9): Invalid file descriptor\n    - Other: Mapped from Windows error via __dosmaperr\n\nInternal Variables:\n  hFile - Windows HANDLE from GetOsFileHandle conversion\n  local_8/lNewPositionHigh - High 32 bits of new position (in/out for SetFilePointer)\n  pDVar2 - Pointer to thread-local errno from GetThreadContextFieldAt8\n  DVar3 - Windows error code from GetLastError\n  DVar4 - Low 32 bits of new position / error indicator\n  pbVar1 - Pointer to ioinfo flags byte\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - SetFilePointer returning 0xFFFFFFFF with GetLastError() == 0 is NOT an error\n  - This handles the edge case where the new position is exactly 0xFFFFFFFF\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xFFFFFFFF - INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE / error return from SetFilePointer\n  9 - EBADF (Bad file descriptor)\n  0x1F (31) - Mask for ioinfo array slot index (32 entries per segment)\n  5 - Shift for ioinfo segment index (divides by 32)\n  0x24 (36) - Size of each ioinfo structure entry\n  0xFD - Mask to clear FEOF flag (bit 1) in ioinfo flags byte\n\nStructure Layout (ioinfo at g_pIoInfoTable[fd >> 5] + (fd & 0x1F) * 0x24):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n  0x00    4     osfhnd      HANDLE  OS file handle\n  0x04    1     osflags     byte    File status flags (FEOF=0x02, FTEXT=0x80)\n  ...remaining 35 bytes of ioinfo structure",
