      "comment": "Retrieves the default ANSI code page identifier for the specified locale.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save stack canary for buffer overflow protection\n2. Initialize null terminator for code page string buffer\n3. Call GetLocaleInfoA with LOCALE_IDEFAULTANSICODEPAGE (0x1004) to get code page as string\n4. If GetLocaleInfoA succeeds, convert the ASCII string to integer via ConvertAsciiStringToLong\n5. If GetLocaleInfoA fails, set return value to -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n6. Verify stack canary before returning\n\nParameters:\n  lcidLocale - LCID locale identifier to query for ANSI code page\n\nReturns:\n  uint - ANSI code page number (e.g., 1252 for Western European)\n         Returns 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) if locale info retrieval fails\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1004 - LOCALE_IDEFAULTANSICODEPAGE: Retrieves default ANSI code page\n  6      - Buffer size for code page string (max 5 digits + null)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns -1 if GetLocaleInfoA fails (invalid locale or other error)\n  - Code page stored as null-terminated ASCII string before conversion\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release CRT",
