      "comment": "CRT internal wrapper for MessageBoxA with window station interactivity checking.\n\nDynamically loads user32.dll and resolves MessageBoxA, GetActiveWindow, \nGetLastActivePopup, GetProcessWindowStation, and GetUserObjectInformationA at \nfirst call. Checks if the current process window station is interactive before \nshowing a message box, preventing hangs in non-interactive sessions (services).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If MessageBoxA not already resolved, load user32.dll via LoadLibraryA\n2. Resolve MessageBoxA, GetActiveWindow, GetLastActivePopup via GetProcAddress\n3. If OS major version is 2 (NT), also resolve GetUserObjectInformationA and \n   GetProcessWindowStation for interactivity detection\n4. Check if window station allows user interaction via GetUserObjectInformationA\n5. If WSF_VISIBLE flag (0x1) is not set, adjust message box type for non-interactive\n6. Get active window via GetActiveWindow, then GetLastActivePopup for parent window\n7. Add MB_SETFOREGROUND (0x10000) if OS platform >= 4 (NT4+), else MB_TOPMOST (0x40000)\n8. Call MessageBoxA with resolved parent window and adjusted type flags\n\nParameters:\nlpszText   - LPCSTR - Message text to display in the message box body\nlpszCaption - LPCSTR - Caption text for the message box title bar\ndwType     - uint   - Message box type flags (MB_OK, MB_YESNO, etc.)\n\nReturns:\nint - MessageBoxA return value (IDOK, IDYES, IDNO, etc.) on success\n      0 if user32.dll failed to load or MessageBoxA not resolved\n\nPhantom Variables (assembly-only, cannot set type via decompiler):\nabUserObjInfo  - byte[8] at [EBP-0x10] - First 8 bytes of USEROBJECTFLAGS struct (fInherit, fReserved)\ndwUserObjFlags - uint at [EBP-0x8]    - USEROBJECTFLAGS.dwFlags (WSF_VISIBLE=0x1 if interactive)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x1        - WSF_VISIBLE flag in USEROBJECTFLAGS.dwFlags (interactive window station)\n0xC        - UOI_FLAGS (1) | sizeof(USEROBJECTFLAGS) (12 bytes)\n0x2        - OS major version 2 (Windows NT family)\n0x4        - OS platform VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT\n0x20       - MB_SETFOREGROUND (0x10000 >> 11)\n0x4        - MB_TOPMOST flag adjustment\n\nStructure Layout - USEROBJECTFLAGS (at EBP-0x10):\nOffset  Size  Field       Description\n0x00    4     fInherit    Object inheritance flag\n0x04    4     fReserved   Reserved, must be zero\n0x08    4     dwFlags     WSF_VISIBLE=0x1 if interactive",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "CALLER_2", "CALLEE_2"]
