      "comment": "Handles security cookie validation failures by displaying an error message and terminating.\n\nThis function is called when a stack buffer overrun or security check failure is detected.\nIt constructs an error message containing the module path and error description, then\ndisplays it via a message box before terminating the process.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save the current security cookie value for later reference\n2. Check if a custom security error handler is registered\n   a. If registered, call the custom handler with error code and exit\n3. Determine error type based on nErrorCode:\n   a. nErrorCode == 1: Stack buffer overrun detected\n   b. nErrorCode == 0: Unknown security check failure\n4. Get the module filename using GetModuleFileNameA\n   a. If GetModuleFileNameA fails, copy fallback string \"<program name unknown>\"\n5. Calculate message length and truncate path if necessary (max 60 chars display)\n   a. If path + message > 60 chars, truncate path with \"...\" prefix\n6. Allocate stack buffer for final formatted message\n7. Concatenate components: title + separator + module path + error description\n8. Display error message via ShowCrtMessageBoxA with MB_ICONHAND | MB_OK style\n9. Call __exit(3) to terminate the process with failure code\n\nParameters:\n  nErrorCode - Error type indicator (0=unknown failure, 1=buffer overrun)\n\nReturns:\n  Does not return - terminates process via __exit(3)\n\nError Handling:\n  If GetModuleFileNameA fails, uses \"<program name unknown>\" as fallback\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x104 (260) - MAX_PATH for module filename buffer\n  0x3c (60)   - Maximum display length for formatted path\n  0xd4 (212)  - String length for buffer overrun message\n  0xb9 (185)  - String length for unknown failure message\n  0x12010     - MB_ICONHAND | MB_OK | MB_SETFOREGROUND message box style\n  0x3         - Exit code passed to __exit (abnormal termination)\n\nPhantom Variables:\n  pbSavedCookie (undefined1 *): SEH prolog saved cookie - cannot be typed (no HighVariable)",
