      "comment": "Forces a locale-specific decimal point into a floating-point number string buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check first character - if uppercase is 'E' (0x65), found exponent marker\n2. Loop through buffer scanning for insertion point:\n   a. Increment buffer pointer\n   b. Call _isdigit() to check if current character is a digit\n   c. If not a digit (returns 0), found insertion point\n3. Save current character at insertion point\n4. Write locale decimal point (g_cDecimalPoint) at insertion point\n5. Shift all remaining characters right by one position:\n   a. Move to next position\n   b. Save next character, write saved character\n   c. Repeat until null terminator reached\n\nParameters:\n  szBuffer - Pointer to null-terminated string containing floating-point number\n             representation. Buffer is modified in-place to insert decimal point.\n             IMPLICIT: Must have space for one additional character.\n\nReturns:\n  void - Buffer is modified in-place with decimal point inserted.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If first char is 'E'/'e', decimal point inserted at start (exponent-only)\n  - String must be null-terminated for shift loop to complete\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x65 - ASCII 'e' (lowercase), matches 'E' after _toupper conversion\n\nCalled By:\n  InitializeFloatingPointConversion (0x6ff597d7)",
