      "comment": "Assigns a parsed floating-point value from a string to an output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check precision flag to determine float vs double parsing\n2. If nPrecisionFlag != 0 (double precision):\n   a. Call __atodbl to parse string into 8-byte double at stack\n   b. Copy low DWORD to output buffer [0]\n   c. Copy high DWORD to output buffer [4]\n3. If nPrecisionFlag == 0 (single precision):\n   a. Call __atoflt to parse string into 4-byte float\n   b. Copy result to output buffer [0]\n4. Return (void)\n\nParameters:\n  nPrecisionFlag - Precision selector: 0=float (4 bytes), non-zero=double (8 bytes)\n  lpszOutBuffer  - Output buffer receiving the parsed floating-point value\n  lpszNumberStr  - Null-terminated string containing the number to parse\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results are written directly to lpszOutBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - When nPrecisionFlag=0, only 4 bytes are written (float)\n  - When nPrecisionFlag!=0, 8 bytes are written (double)\n  - Buffer must be appropriately sized for the precision requested\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release CRT",
