      "comment": "Converts a double-precision floating-point value to a formatted string.\n\nCRT library function (__cftof) from Visual Studio 2003 Release. Part of the \nfloat-to-string conversion pipeline for printf-family functions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save stack canary from g_dwSecurityCookie for buffer overflow detection\n2. Load the 8-byte double value from pdValue pointer\n3. Call __fltout2 to decompose double into _strflt structure (sign, decimal point, mantissa)\n4. Call __fptostr to convert decomposed value to digit string, adjusting buffer start for sign\n5. Call __cftof2 to finalize output format with proper null termination\n6. Verify stack canary and return error code\n\nParameters:\n  pdValue (double*) - Pointer to the double value to convert\n  szBuf (char*) - Output buffer for the formatted string result\n  dwSizeInBytes (uint) - Size of the output buffer in bytes\n  nDecimalDigits (int) - Number of decimal digits for precision\n\nReturns:\n  int (errno_t) - 0 on success, error code on buffer overflow or conversion failure\n\nStack Layout:\n  EBP-0x04: dwStackCanary (uint) - Stack protection cookie\n  EBP-0x1C: szDigitBuffer[24] - Temporary buffer for digit string\n  EBP-0x2C: strfltResult (_strflt) - Decomposed float structure with sign, decpt, mantissa\n\nCalled By: __cfltcvt (0x6ff5b4ec)",
