      "comment": "Converts a floating-point value to general format string (g-format).\n\nThis is the CRT __cftog function that intelligently chooses between\nfixed-point (f-format) and exponential (e-format) representation\nbased on the value's magnitude and requested precision.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save stack canary for buffer overflow protection\n2. Extract floating-point representation via __fltout2\n3. Convert mantissa to string via __fptostr\n4. Evaluate format selection criteria:\n   - Use e-format if exponent < -4 (very small values)\n   - Use e-format if exponent >= buffer size (large values)\n5. For f-format: trim trailing zeros if decimal point moved\n6. Call __cftof2 for f-format or __cftoe2 for e-format\n7. Verify stack canary before return\n\nParameters:\n  pdValue (double*) - Pointer to the double value to convert\n  szOutputBuffer (char*) - Output buffer for the formatted string\n  nBufferSize (size_t) - Size of output buffer (precision limit)\n  nExponentWidth (int) - Width for exponent field in e-format\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result written to szOutputBuffer\n\nFormat Selection Logic:\n  if (decimalPoint < -4) OR (decimalPoint >= bufferSize):\n    Use exponential format (__cftoe2)\n  else:\n    Use fixed-point format (__cftof2)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2d - ASCII '-' (minus sign check)\n  -4   - Threshold for switching to e-format for small values\n  0x01 - Format flag passed to conversion functions\n\nStructure Layout (_strflt at EBP-0x30):\n  Offset  Size  Field   Type   Description\n  0x00    4     sign    int    Sign indicator (0x2d = negative)\n  0x04    4     decpt   int    Decimal point position\n  0x08    4     flag    int    Status flags\n  0x0c    4     mantissa char*  Pointer to mantissa string\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release (__cftog)",
