      "comment": "Detects the Intel Pentium FDIV floating-point division bug using known problematic values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load test divisor (3145727.0) and dividend (4195835.0) into FPU stack\n2. Compute remainder: dividend - (dividend / divisor) * divisor\n3. Compare computed remainder against expected value (1.0)\n4. Return 1 if remainder differs (FDIV bug present), 0 if correct\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - 1 if Pentium FDIV bug detected (faulty processor), 0 if FPU division is correct\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Affected processors: Early Pentium (P5) chips from 1994\n- The FDIV bug causes incorrect results for specific dividend/divisor pairs\n- Known affected value pairs produce incorrect remainders on buggy processors\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 3145727.0 (0x6ff76628): Test divisor value known to trigger FDIV bug\n- 4195835.0 (0x6ff76620): Test dividend value known to trigger FDIV bug  \n- 1.0 (0x6ff78fd8): Expected remainder for correct FPU operation\n- 0x41 in AH test: FPU status flags for C0 and C3 (equal/unordered)",
