      "comment": "Changes the size of a file with file descriptor locking.\n\nThis is a CRT internal function that modifies file size. If the new size is larger,\nit extends the file by writing zero bytes. If smaller, it truncates using SetEndOfFile.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save original file position via __lseek_lk with SEEK_CUR (1)\n2. Get current file size via __lseek_lk with SEEK_END (2)\n3. Calculate size difference (nNewSize - dwCurrentSize)\n4. If extending file (difference > 0):\n   a. Allocate 4KB zero-filled buffer on stack\n   b. Switch to binary mode via __setmode_lk (O_BINARY = 0x8000)\n   c. Write zero bytes in 4KB chunks until nNewSize reached\n   d. Restore original file mode\n5. If truncating file (difference < 0):\n   a. Seek to new size position\n   b. Call SetEndOfFile to truncate\n   c. On failure, set errno to EACCES (0xD) and doserrno to GetLastError\n6. Restore original file position\n7. Verify stack canary before return\n\nParameters:\n  nFileDescriptor - CRT file descriptor (not Win32 HANDLE)\n  nNewSize - Desired new file size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success, -1 on failure (errno/doserrno set)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1000 - 4KB buffer size for zero-fill writes\n  0x8000 - O_BINARY mode flag\n  0x0D   - EACCES errno value (permission denied)\n  0x05   - EIO errno (I/O error) from __write_lk\n\nError Handling:\n  - Returns -1 if __lseek_lk fails to get position/size\n  - Sets EACCES errno on SetEndOfFile failure (truncation)\n  - Converts EIO (5) to EACCES (13) on write failure during extension",
      "tags": ["CALLEE_11", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "CALLER_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
