      "comment": "Searches the exception handler table for an entry matching the specified signal number.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize search pointer to table base (passed via EDX register)\n2. Compare signal number at current entry offset +0x4 with target signal (ESI register)\n3. If match found, break out of loop early\n4. Increment pointer by entry size (0xC bytes) to next entry\n5. Compare current pointer against table end boundary (base + count * 0xC)\n6. Continue loop while within table bounds\n7. After loop, validate match by checking both bounds and signal equality\n8. Return entry pointer if valid match, or 0 if not found\n\nParameters:\n  in_EDX (IMPLICIT): Pointer to base of exception handler table\n  unaff_ESI (IMPLICIT): Signal number to search for (SIGILL=4, SIGFPE=8, SIGSEGV=11)\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Pointer to matching table entry, or 0 if no entry matches\n  - Non-zero: Address of 12-byte entry structure containing handler info\n  - Zero: Signal number not found in table (invalid signal or table empty)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Table can be empty (g_nXcptEntryCount = 0), returns 0 immediately\n  - Used only for signals 4, 8, 11 which use TLS-based exception handling\n  - Called from DispatchSignalHandler during C runtime signal dispatch\n\nException Entry Structure (size: 0x0C):\n  Offset | Size | Field        | Description\n  +0x00  |  4   | Unknown      | Entry identifier or flags\n  +0x04  |  4   | nSignalNum   | Signal number this entry handles\n  +0x08  |  4   | pHandler     | Pointer to signal handler function\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0C (12): Size of each exception table entry",
