      "comment": "Dispatches C runtime signal handlers based on the signal number.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH frame via __SEH_prolog\n2. Map signal number to handler function pointer:\n   - SIGINT (2): g_pfnSigIntHandler\n   - SIGILL (4), SIGFPE (8), SIGSEGV (11): TLS exception table via siglookup\n   - SIGTERM (15): g_pfnSigTermHandler\n   - SIGABRT (22): g_pfnSigAbrtHandler\n   - SIGBREAK (21): g_pfnSigBreakHandler\n3. Check if handler is SIG_IGN (1) - return 0 if so\n4. Check if handler is SIG_DFL (0) - call __exit(3) for default behavior\n5. Acquire lock via __lock for thread safety\n6. For SIGILL/SIGFPE/SIGSEGV, clear handler after retrieval\n7. For SIGFPE (8):\n   - Save FPU exception code from TLS context\n   - Clear FPU exception entries in table\n8. Release lock, call handler with signal number\n9. For SIGFPE, restore saved FPU exception code after handler returns\n\nParameters:\n  nSignalNumber (int): Signal number to dispatch (SIGINT=2, SIGILL=4, SIGFPE=8, SIGSEGV=11, SIGTERM=15, SIGBREAK=21, SIGABRT=22)\n\nReturns:\n  int: 0 on successful handler dispatch, -1 if signal number invalid\n\nSignal Constants:\n  SIGINT   = 2   - Interrupt (Ctrl+C)\n  SIGILL   = 4   - Illegal instruction\n  SIGFPE   = 8   - Floating-point exception\n  SIGSEGV  = 11  - Segmentation violation\n  SIGTERM  = 15  - Termination request\n  SIGBREAK = 21  - Ctrl+Break (Windows-specific)\n  SIGABRT  = 22  - Abnormal termination\n\nSpecial Values:\n  SIG_DFL = 0 - Default handler (causes __exit)\n  SIG_IGN = 1 - Ignore signal\n  0x8C = 140  - FPU exception code placeholder\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_pfnSigIntHandler (0x6ff806b0): SIGINT handler function pointer\n  g_pfnSigTermHandler (0x6ff806b4): SIGTERM handler function pointer\n  g_pfnSigBreakHandler (0x6ff806b8): SIGBREAK handler function pointer\n  g_pfnSigAbrtHandler (0x6ff806bc): SIGABRT handler function pointer\n  g_nXcptFpuStartIndex (0x6ff7e7e8): Start index in FPU exception table\n  g_nXcptFpuCount (0x6ff7e7ec): Count of FPU exception entries",
      "tags": ["CALLER_1", "PARAM_1", "CALLEE_7"]
