      "comment": "Case-insensitive ASCII string comparison (CRT library function).\n\nCompares two null-terminated strings character by character, converting\nuppercase ASCII letters (A-Z) to lowercase before comparison. Comparison\nstops when a difference is found, a null terminator is reached, or\nnMaxCount characters have been compared.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return 0 immediately if nMaxCount is 0\n2. Load character from each string into registers (AH from lpszStr1, AL from lpszStr2)\n3. Check for null terminators - if either string ends, exit loop\n4. Convert uppercase A-Z (0x41-0x5A) to lowercase by adding 0x20\n5. Compare converted characters\n6. If equal, decrement counter and advance pointers\n7. Repeat until mismatch found or nMaxCount exhausted\n8. Return comparison result based on final character difference\n\nParameters:\n  lpszStr1 (char*) - First null-terminated string to compare\n  lpszStr2 (char*) - Second null-terminated string to compare\n  nMaxCount (size_t) - Maximum number of characters to compare\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Strings are equal (up to nMaxCount characters)\n  -1 - lpszStr1 is less than lpszStr2 (lexicographically)\n  1  - lpszStr1 is greater than lpszStr2 (lexicographically)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x41 - ASCII 'A' (uppercase range start)\n  0x5A - ASCII 'Z' (uppercase range end)\n  0x20 - Case conversion offset (difference between upper/lower)\n\nNote: Decompiler shows SSA variables (cVar1, bVar2, uVar3, uVar4, bVar5) \nrepresenting register operations on AH/AL. These are compiler artifacts\nfrom optimized register-based character manipulation, not true locals.",
