      "comment": "Increments a multi-word mantissa at a specified bit position with carry propagation.\n\nThis is a Visual Studio 2003 runtime library function used for floating-point rounding.\nIt adds 1 at the specified bit position in a mantissa array and propagates any overflow\n(carry) to higher-order words until no overflow occurs or the array is exhausted.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate word index: nWordIndex = nBitPosition / 32\n2. Calculate bit offset within word: 31 - (nBitPosition % 32)\n3. Create bit mask: 1 << bitOffset\n4. Add bit mask to mantissa word at pMantissa[nWordIndex]\n5. If no overflow, return immediately\n6. Propagate carry: decrement word index, add 1 to previous word\n7. Repeat carry propagation until no overflow or word index < 0\n\nParameters:\n  pMantissa [in/out] - Pointer to mantissa array (array of 32-bit words, big-endian order)\n  nBitPosition [in]  - Bit position to increment (0 = MSB of word 0)\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Increment completed without overflow past word 0\n  1 - Overflow occurred past the most significant word (mantissa wrapped)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nBitPosition >= 32, targets a word beyond the first\n  - Carry propagation stops early if AddUintWithOverflowCheck returns 0\n  - Array is traversed in reverse order (high word to low word indices)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 (32) - Bits per word (sizeof(dword) * 8)\n  0x1F (31) - Bit index mask for calculating bit offset within word\n\nCallers:\n  RoundMantissa - Uses this to round up mantissa after checking rounding bit",
