      "comment": "Shifts a 96-bit extended precision mantissa right by a specified number of bits.\n\nThis is a Visual Studio 2003 runtime library helper function used during\nfloating-point format conversion to shift the mantissa for normalization\nor denormalization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate bit shift within DWORD (nShiftBits % 32) and DWORD offset (nShiftBits / 32)\n2. Phase 1 - Bit Shifting: Loop through 3 DWORDs from low to high\n   a. Extract current DWORD value\n   b. Shift right by bit position, OR with carry from previous iteration\n   c. Calculate new carry bits (low bits that will shift into next DWORD)\n3. Phase 2 - DWORD Shifting: Loop from high to low DWORD index\n   a. If index < DWORD offset, zero out the DWORD (shifted past boundary)\n   b. Otherwise copy from source position (index - DWORD offset)\n\nParameters:\n  pMantissa  - Pointer to 3-DWORD (96-bit) mantissa array to shift in-place\n  nShiftBits - Number of bits to shift right (0 to 95)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Mantissa array is modified in-place\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 (32)  - Bits per DWORD, used for division/modulo to separate bit/word shifts\n  0x3        - Mantissa array size in DWORDs (96 bits total)\n  0x2        - Last DWORD index (array indices 0, 1, 2)",
