      "comment": "Converts an ASCII decimal string to a double-precision floating-point value.\n\nThis is the CRT library function __atodbl (also matches __atoflt signature).\nPerforms string-to-double conversion through an intermediate 12-byte long double\nrepresentation for maximum precision during conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save stack canary from g_dwSecurityCookie for buffer overflow detection\n2. Parse input string and convert to 12-byte long double (_LDBL12) format\n3. Convert the extended precision value to IEEE 754 double format\n4. Verify stack canary before returning to detect stack corruption\n5. Return conversion status code\n\nParameters:\n  pResult  - Pointer to _CRT_FLOAT structure receiving the converted value\n  szInput  - Null-terminated ASCII string containing decimal number to convert\n\nReturns:\n  int - Conversion status code from ConvertExtendedFloatWithConfig\n        0 = Success\n        Non-zero = Conversion error (overflow, underflow, invalid format)\n\nStack Layout:\n  Offset   Size   Field              Description\n  -0x04    4      dwStackCanary      Security cookie for stack protection\n  -0x10    12     ldTemp             _LDBL12 intermediate long double value\n  -0x14    4      pszEndPtr          Pointer to end of parsed string\n\nCalled By: __fassign (floating-point assignment helper)\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release CRT",
