      "comment": "Converts IEEE 754 double-precision (64-bit) to x87 long double (80-bit) format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract sign bit, exponent, and mantissa from 64-bit double input\n2. Check for zero - if mantissa and exponent both zero, output zero representation\n3. Check for special exponents:\n   - Exponent 0x000: Denormalized number, bias exponent by 0x3C01, clear implicit bit\n   - Exponent 0x7FF: Infinity/NaN, convert to long double exponent 0x7FFF\n   - Normal range: Add 0x3C00 to convert from double bias (1023) to long double bias (16383)\n4. Construct 64-bit mantissa by shifting and combining high/low dwords\n5. Set implicit integer bit (bit 63) for normalized numbers\n6. For denormals, normalize by left-shifting until leading 1 found, adjusting exponent\n7. Combine sign bit with adjusted exponent into 16-bit exponent field\n\nParameters:\n  pLongDoubleOut: Pointer to 10-byte output buffer for 80-bit long double\n  pDoubleIn: Pointer to 8-byte input containing IEEE 754 double\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result written to pLongDoubleOut buffer\n\nIEEE 754 Double Layout (64-bit):\n  Bits 63: Sign (1 bit)\n  Bits 62-52: Exponent (11 bits, bias 1023)\n  Bits 51-0: Mantissa (52 bits, implicit leading 1)\n\nx87 Long Double Layout (80-bit):\n  Bits 79: Sign (1 bit)  \n  Bits 78-64: Exponent (15 bits, bias 16383)\n  Bit 63: Integer/Implicit bit (explicit in long double)\n  Bits 62-0: Mantissa (63 bits)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7FF: Maximum double exponent (infinity/NaN)\n  0x7FFF: Maximum long double exponent\n  0x3C00: Exponent bias adjustment (16383 - 1023 = 15360 = 0x3C00)\n  0x3C01: Denormal bias adjustment (0x3C00 + 1)\n  0x80000000: Implicit integer bit mask\n  0xFFFFF: 20-bit mantissa mask for high dword",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "CALLER_1", "CALLEE_0", "PROP_LEAF"]
    },
