      "comment": "Converts a double-precision floating-point value to a _strflt structure for string formatting.\n\nThis is the CRT internal function __fltout2 used by printf-style formatters. It bridges the\nIEEE 754 double representation to the _strflt structure needed by digit formatting routines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save stack canary from g_dwSecurityCookie for buffer overflow protection\n2. Convert double to 80-bit extended precision using ___dtold into local LDBL12 buffer\n3. Call FormatFloatToDecimalString with precision=17 to decompose the extended value:\n   - Decimal exponent (base-10 power)\n   - Sign character (0x2d '-' or 0x20 ' ')\n   - Digit string (ASCII digits of mantissa)\n4. Copy results from local _strflt buffer to caller's structure:\n   - pStrfltResult->decpt = decimal exponent position\n   - pStrfltResult->sign = sign character  \n   - pStrfltResult->mantissa = digit string pointer\n5. Copy formatted digit string to caller's buffer using CopyStringOptimized\n6. Store buffer size in _strflt structure for bounds checking\n7. Verify stack canary via VerifyStackCanary before returning\n\nParameters:\n  dValue (double) - IEEE 754 double-precision value to convert\n  pStrfltResult (_strflt*) - Output structure receiving decomposed float info\n  szDigitBuffer (char*) - Output buffer for ASCII digit string\n  nBufferSize (size_t) - Size of digit buffer in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  _strflt* - Returns pStrfltResult pointer for chained calls\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x11 (17) - Maximum precision for IEEE 754 double (15-17 significant digits)\n  0x0C (12) - Stack reservation for LDBL12 structure copy\n\nStructure Layout (_strflt at pStrfltResult):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n  0x00    4     decpt       int     Decimal point position (exponent)\n  0x04    4     sign        int     Sign (0x2d='-', 0x20=' ')\n  0x08    4     mantissa    char*   Pointer to digit string\n  0x0C    4     flag        int     Buffer size/flags\n\nLocal Stack Layout:\n  EBP-0x04: dwStackCanary (dword - saved security cookie)\n  EBP-0x0C: wExponent (ushort - 80-bit exponent field)\n  EBP-0x10: dwMantLow (uint - lower 32 bits of mantissa)\n  EBP-0x14: bLdbl12Buffer (byte[10] - 80-bit extended precision)\n  EBP-0x2C: szLocalDigits (char[24] - local digit string buffer)\n  EBP-0x2E: bSign (byte - sign character)\n  EBP-0x30: nDecimalExponent (short - decimal exponent)\n\nNote: SSA variables (dwMantissaHigh, wDecExp, szDigitSrc, pStrResult) are decompiler\ntemporaries with HASH storage that regenerate on each decompilation pass.",
