      "instructions": ["0xBE2C|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xBE2E|TEST|BL, 0x1", "0xBE31|JZ|0x6ff5be36", "0xBE33|PUSH|0x10", "0xBE35|POP|EAX", "0xBE36|TEST|BL, 0x4", "0xBE39|JZ|0x6ff5be3e", "0xBE3B|OR|EAX, 0x8", "0xBE3E|TEST|BL, 0x8", "0xBE41|JZ|0x6ff5be46", "0xBE43|OR|EAX, 0x4", "0xBE46|TEST|BL, 0x10", "0xBE49|JZ|0x6ff5be4e", "0xBE4B|OR|EAX, 0x2", "0xBE4E|TEST|BL, 0x20"],
      "comment": "Converts x87 FPU Control Word to Abstract Format\n\nConverts the native x87 FPU control word bits from the BX register into\nan abstracted format used by the CRT library for FPU state management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output flags to 0\n2. Map exception mask bits (bits 0-5) to abstract flags:\n   - Bit 0 (IM) -> 0x10 (Invalid Operation)\n   - Bit 2 (OM) -> 0x08 (Overflow)\n   - Bit 3 (ZM) -> 0x04 (Zero Divide)\n   - Bit 4 (DM) -> 0x02 (Denormal Operand)\n   - Bit 5 (PM) -> 0x01 (Precision/Inexact)\n   - Bit 1 (Unknown) -> 0x80000\n3. Map rounding control bits (10-11):\n   - 0x000 (Nearest) -> No flag\n   - 0x400 (Down) -> 0x100\n   - 0x800 (Up) -> 0x200\n   - 0xC00 (Truncate) -> 0x300\n4. Map precision control bits (8-9):\n   - 0x000 (Single/24-bit) -> 0x20000\n   - 0x200 (Double/53-bit) -> 0x10000\n   - 0x300 (Extended/64-bit) -> No flag\n5. Map infinity control bit (12):\n   - Bit 12 set -> 0x40000\n6. Return abstract flags in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  BX [IMPLICIT] - (ushort) Native x87 FPU control word\n\nReturns:\n  EAX - (uint) Abstract FPU control flags\n        Success: Abstract representation of FPU control word\n        The returned value contains mapped exception masks,\n        rounding mode, precision control, and infinity control.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  Input (FPU Control Word bits):\n    0x0001 - Invalid Operation Mask (IM)\n    0x0002 - Unknown mask (Stack Fault?)\n    0x0004 - Overflow Mask (OM)\n    0x0008 - Zero-Divide Mask (ZM)\n    0x0010 - Denormal Mask (DM)\n    0x0020 - Precision/Inexact Mask (PM)\n    0x0300 - Precision Control (PC) field\n    0x0C00 - Rounding Control (RC) field\n    0x1000 - Infinity Control (IC)\n\n  Output (Abstract flags):\n    0x00001 - Abstract Precision flag\n    0x00002 - Abstract Denormal flag\n    0x00004 - Abstract Zero-Divide flag\n    0x00008 - Abstract Overflow flag\n    0x00010 - Abstract Invalid flag\n    0x00100 - Round Down mode\n    0x00200 - Round Up mode\n    0x00300 - Truncate mode\n    0x10000 - Double precision\n    0x20000 - Single precision\n    0x40000 - Infinity control flag\n    0x80000 - Unknown flag (bit 1 mapping)\n\nLibrary:\n  Visual Studio 2003 Release __abstract_cw",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "CALLEE_0", "PARAM_0", "PROP_LEAF"]
