      "comment": "Converts abstract FPU control word to hardware x87 format.\n\nVisual Studio CRT helper function that translates a portable abstract\ncontrol word representation (passed in EBX) to the actual x87 FPU\ncontrol word format returned in EAX. Used by __control87 for masked\ncontrol word updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize result to 0 (XOR EAX,EAX)\n2. Map exception mask bits from abstract to hardware format:\n   - Abstract bit 0x10 -> Hardware bit 0x01 (Invalid operation)\n   - Abstract bit 0x08 -> Hardware bit 0x04 (Denormal)\n   - Abstract bit 0x04 -> Hardware bit 0x08 (Zero divide)\n   - Abstract bit 0x02 -> Hardware bit 0x10 (Overflow)\n   - Abstract bit 0x01 -> Hardware bit 0x20 (Underflow)\n   - Abstract bit 0x80000 -> Hardware bit 0x02 (Precision)\n3. Map rounding control from abstract bits 0x300 to hardware bits 0xC00:\n   - 0x000 -> 0x000 (Round to nearest)\n   - 0x100 -> 0x400 (Round down)\n   - 0x200 -> 0x800 (Round up)\n   - 0x300 -> 0xC00 (Round toward zero)\n4. Map precision control from abstract bits 0x30000 to hardware bits 0x300:\n   - 0x00000 -> 0x300 (Extended precision, 64-bit)\n   - 0x10000 -> 0x200 (Double precision, 53-bit)\n   - 0x20000 -> 0x000 (Single precision, 24-bit)\n5. Map infinity control: abstract bit 0x40000 -> hardware bit 0x1000\n6. Return assembled hardware control word in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT EBX (uint) - Abstract control word with portable bit layout\n\nReturns:\n  uint (in EAX) - Hardware x87 FPU control word ready for FLDCW\n\nBit Mapping Reference:\n  Abstract Format (EBX):        Hardware Format (EAX):\n  Bit 0x01 - UM (Underflow)     Bit 0x01 - IM (Invalid op)\n  Bit 0x02 - OM (Overflow)      Bit 0x02 - DM (Denormal)\n  Bit 0x04 - ZM (Zero div)      Bit 0x04 - DM (from 0x08)\n  Bit 0x08 - DM (Denormal)      Bit 0x08 - ZM (Zero div)\n  Bit 0x10 - IM (Invalid op)    Bit 0x10 - OM (Overflow)\n  Bits 0x300 - RC (Rounding)    Bit 0x20 - UM (Underflow)\n  Bits 0x30000 - PC (Precision) Bits 0x300 - PC (Precision)\n  Bit 0x40000 - IC (Infinity)   Bits 0xC00 - RC (Rounding)\n  Bit 0x80000 - PM (Precision)  Bit 0x1000 - IC (Infinity)\n\nCalling Convention:\n  Custom register-based; EBX holds input, EAX holds output.\n  ESI is preserved across call (saved/restored on stack).\n\nRelated Functions:\n  __abstract_cw - Inverse operation (hardware to abstract)\n  UpdateFpuControlBits - Uses both for masked control word updates",
