      "comment": "Modifies FPU control word bits using a masked update operation.\n\nCRT library function (__control87) that selectively updates floating-point\ncontrol word bits. Uses a mask to determine which bits to modify and\npreserves other bits unchanged.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store current hardware FPU control word to stack (FSTCW)\n2. Call __abstract_cw to get abstract (portable) control word representation\n3. Compute new control word: (previous & ~mask) | (newValue & mask)\n   - Clear bits specified by mask from previous value\n   - OR in new bits that are specified by mask\n4. Call __hw_cw to convert abstract control word to hardware format\n5. Load modified control word into FPU (FLDCW)\n6. Return previous abstract control word value\n\nParameters:\n  dwNewValue (uint) - New control word bits to apply where mask bits are set\n  dwMask (uint) - Bitmask indicating which control word bits to modify\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Previous abstract FPU control word value before modification\n\nFPU Control Word Bit Definitions:\n  Bits 0-5:   Exception masks (IM, DM, ZM, OM, UM, PM)\n  Bits 8-9:   Precision control (PC)\n  Bits 10-11: Rounding control (RC)\n  Bit 12:     Infinity control (IC)\n\nCommon Mask Values:\n  0x0003F - Exception mask bits\n  0x00300 - Precision control\n  0x00C00 - Rounding control\n  0x1F3F  - Full user-controllable mask\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If dwMask is 0, no bits are modified (returns current state)\n  - If dwMask is 0xFFFF, all bits are replaced with dwNewValue",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "CALLER_1", "CALLEE_2", "PROP_SMALL"]
