      "comment": "Sets the file translation mode for a CRT file descriptor (locked version).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate handle table slot index from file descriptor (fd >> 5)\n2. Calculate entry offset within slot ((fd & 0x1F) * 0x24)\n3. Read current mode flags byte from handle entry at offset +4\n4. If nMode == 0x8000 (_O_BINARY): Clear bit 0x80 (text mode flag)\n5. If nMode == 0x4000 (_O_TEXT): Set bit 0x80 (text mode flag)\n6. If nMode is invalid: Set errno to EINVAL (0x16) and return -1\n7. Return previous mode based on old flag state\n\nParameters:\n  dwFileDescriptor - CRT file descriptor index (0-2047 valid range)\n  nMode - New translation mode:\n          0x8000 (_O_BINARY) - Binary mode (no CR/LF translation)\n          0x4000 (_O_TEXT) - Text mode (CR/LF translation enabled)\n\nReturns:\n  Previous mode (0x8000 for binary, 0x4000 for text) on success\n  -1 on error with errno set to EINVAL (0x16) for invalid mode\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8000 - _O_BINARY mode constant\n  0x4000 - _O_TEXT mode constant\n  0x80   - Text mode flag bit in handle entry\n  0x24   - Size of each file handle entry (36 bytes)\n  0x16   - EINVAL error code\n\nStructure Layout (File Handle Entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Description\n  0x00    4     hOsHandle   Windows OS file handle\n  0x04    1     bModeFlags  Mode flags (bit 7 = text mode)\n  ...     ...   ...         Other CRT file state",
