      "comment": "Performs safe unsigned integer addition with overflow detection.\n\nAdds two unsigned 32-bit integers and detects if the result overflowed.\nThis is a critical arithmetic safety function from Visual Studio 2003 runtime.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute sum of dwOperandA + dwOperandB\n2. Initialize overflow flag to 0 (no overflow)\n3. Check if sum < dwOperandA (first overflow condition via carry)\n4. Check if sum < dwOperandB (second overflow condition via carry)\n5. If either condition is true, set overflow flag to 1\n6. Store computed sum in output pointer\n7. Return overflow status\n\nParameters:\n  dwOperandA [in]  - First unsigned 32-bit operand\n  dwOperandB [in]  - Second unsigned 32-bit operand\n  pdwResult  [out] - Pointer to receive the sum result (valid even on overflow)\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Addition completed without overflow\n  1 - Overflow occurred (result wrapped around)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - When either operand is 0, overflow cannot occur\n  - Maximum overflow occurs at (0xFFFFFFFF + 0xFFFFFFFF) = 0xFFFFFFFE with carry\n  - Result is always stored regardless of overflow status\n\nCallers: ___add_12, __IncMan, ___ld12mul (floating-point mantissa operations)",
