      "comment": "Shifts a 96-bit (12-byte) extended precision integer left by 1 bit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load low and middle 32-bit words from the 96-bit integer\n2. Shift low word left by 1 (multiply by 2)\n3. Shift middle word left by 1, OR with high bit from low word\n4. Shift high word left by 1, OR with high bit from middle word\n5. Store all three words back to memory\n\nParameters:\n- pdwInt96 (uint*): Pointer to 96-bit integer as 3 consecutive DWORDs\n  - [0]: Low 32 bits (least significant)\n  - [1]: Middle 32 bits  \n  - [2]: High 32 bits (most significant)\n\nReturns:\n- void: Operates in-place on the provided buffer\n\nStructure Layout (12-byte Int96):\nOffset  Size  Field   Type    Description\n0x0     4     dword0  uint    Low 32 bits (bits 0-31)\n0x4     4     dword1  uint    Middle 32 bits (bits 32-63)\n0x8     4     dword2  uint    High 32 bits (bits 64-95)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1f (31): Bit position of the sign/carry bit in a 32-bit word\n- Used with SHR to extract carry bit for inter-word propagation\n\nCaller Context:\n- FormatFloatToDecimalString: Decimal string formatting\n- ConvertMantissaToLongDouble12: Mantissa conversion\n- ___ld12mul: 12-byte long double multiplication\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release (___shl_12)",
