      "comment": "Converts ASCII decimal digit string to 12-byte (96-bit) long double internal format.\nThis CRT library function parses mantissa digits and produces a normalized LD12 value\nwith correctly computed exponent. Used by string-to-float conversion routines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize result LD12 to zero and exponent to 0x404E (bias for normalized form)\n2. For each digit in string:\n   a. Save current result to temp buffer\n   b. Multiply result by 10 using (shl * 2 + add) * 2 = *4 + orig then *2 = *10\n   c. Add current digit value (ASCII char - implicit '0' subtraction upstream)\n3. Coarse normalize: shift left 16 bits at a time until high word non-zero\n4. Fine normalize: shift left 1 bit at a time until MSB (bit 15) is set\n5. Store final exponent at offset +10 of result structure\n\nParameters:\n    pszDigits    - Pointer to ASCII digit characters (pre-validated, no '0' subtraction needed)\n    nDigitCount  - Number of digits to process\n    pLd12Result  - Pointer to 12-byte output buffer for LD12 result\n\nReturns:\n    void - Result written to pLd12Result buffer\n\nSSA Variables (decompiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\n    sVar1  - nExponent: current exponent value (short), tracks normalization shifts\n    puVar2 - pResult: cached copy of pLd12Result pointer for efficient access\n    uVar3  - dwTempHigh: temporary high word during coarse normalization loop\n\nStructure Layout (LD12 - 12-byte Long Double Internal):\n    Offset  Size  Field       Description\n    0x00    4     dwMantLow   Low 32 bits of 64-bit mantissa\n    0x04    4     dwMantHigh  High 32 bits of 64-bit mantissa  \n    0x08    2     wMantTop    Top 16 bits (includes implicit bit)\n    0x0A    2     wExponent   Biased exponent (bias = 16383 for 80-bit)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x404E  - Initial exponent (16462 decimal) representing normalized zero\n    0x8000  - MSB mask for normalization check (bit 15 of wMantTop)\n    0xFFF0  - -16 for coarse normalization exponent adjustment\n    0xFFFF  - -1 for fine normalization exponent adjustment\n\nCalled By:\n    ConvertStringToLongDouble12 - Main string-to-LD12 conversion",
