      "comment": "Converts a string representation of a floating-point number to a 12-byte long double format (_LDBL12).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace (space, tab, newline, carriage return)\n2. Parse optional sign ('+' or '-'), set dwSignFlag to 0x8000 for negative\n3. Parse integer part digits, accumulating into digit buffer (max 25 digits)\n4. If decimal point encountered (g_cDecimalPoint), parse fractional digits\n5. Parse optional exponent ('E', 'e', 'D', 'd') with optional sign\n6. Accumulate exponent value, clamped to +/-5200 to prevent overflow\n7. Call ___mtold12 to convert digit buffer to mantissa\n8. Apply exponent scaling via ___multtenpow12\n9. Combine mantissa with sign flag and store in output _LDBL12 structure\n10. Verify stack canary and return status code\n\nParameters:\n  pLdbl12Out (_LDBL12*) - Output 12-byte long double structure\n  pszEndPtr (char**) - Receives pointer to first unparsed character\n  szInput (char*) - Input string to parse\n  nMult12 (int) - Multiplication factor for intermediate calculations\n  nScale (int) - Scale factor added to exponent\n  nDecimalPointPos (int) - Decimal point position adjustment\n  nImplicitExponent (int) - Flag: if nonzero, allows implicit exponent parsing\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Success, valid number parsed\n  1 - Underflow, result too small\n  2 - Overflow, result too large  \n  4 - No valid digits found (empty or invalid input)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Leading zeros before decimal point are skipped\n  - Exponent values exceeding +/-5200 are clamped (0x1450 = 5200)\n  - Maximum 25 significant digits stored (0x19 = 25)\n  - Stack protected via security cookie (g_dwSecurityCookie)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x8000 - Negative sign bit flag\n  0x19 (25) - Maximum significant digits\n  0x1450 (5200) - Maximum exponent magnitude\n  0xEBB0 (-5200) - Minimum exponent (signed comparison)\n  0x7FFF - Overflow exponent value\n\nStructure Layout (_LDBL12):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n  0x00    2     wLow        ushort  Low word of mantissa\n  0x02    4     dwMidLow    uint    Mid-low mantissa bytes\n  0x06    4     dwMidHigh   uint    Mid-high mantissa bytes\n  0x0A    2     wExpSign    ushort  Exponent and sign bits\n\nState Machine (EAX register drives jump table at 0x6ff5c5bc):\n  0: Initial state, check for sign\n  1: After leading zeros\n  2: After sign, check for digits\n  3: Parsing integer digits\n  4: After decimal point, before fraction\n  5: Parsing fraction digits\n  6: After 'E'/'e', check exponent sign\n  7: Parsing exponent sign\n  8: After exponent sign, check digit\n  9: Parsing exponent digits\n  10: Invalid state\n  11: Handle sign after leading zeros",
