      "comment": "Multiplies two 12-byte extended precision floating-point numbers (80-bit IEEE 754 format).\nThe result is stored in-place in pResult. This is a CRT library function from Visual Studio 2003.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract and store security cookie for stack protection\n2. Extract sign bits from both operands and compute result sign (XOR)\n3. Extract biased exponents from both operands (mask 0x7FFF)\n4. Check for special cases:\n   a. If either exponent is 0x7FFF (infinity/NaN), return infinity\n   b. If combined exponent indicates overflow (>= 0xBFFE), return infinity\n   c. If combined exponent indicates underflow (< 0x3FC0), return zero\n5. Handle denormalized operands (exponent == 0) by adjusting exponent\n6. Perform 80-bit mantissa multiplication using 16-bit word convolution:\n   - Iterate through 5 word positions in outer loop\n   - For each position, multiply all crossing word pairs\n   - Accumulate partial products with overflow propagation via AddUintWithOverflowCheck\n7. Add exponent bias correction (0xC002 = -16382 to adjust for bias)\n8. Normalize result:\n   a. If exponent > 0, left-shift mantissa (___shl_12) until MSB is set\n   b. If exponent <= 0, right-shift mantissa (___shr_12) for denormalized result\n   c. Track sticky bit for proper rounding during right shifts\n9. Perform rounding (round to nearest, ties to even):\n   - Check if round bit (0x8000) or tie with odd LSB (0x18000)\n   - Propagate carry through mantissa words if needed\n10. Check for overflow after rounding, return infinity if exponent >= 0x7FFF\n11. Assemble final result: mantissa + exponent + sign bit\n12. Verify stack canary before return\n\nParameters:\n  pResult (Stack[0x4]) - Pointer to _LDBL12 structure; input operand and output destination\n  pMultiplier (Stack[0x8]) - Pointer to _LDBL12 structure; multiplier operand (read-only)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result stored in pResult in-place\n\nSSA Variables (Decompiler-Generated):\n  uStack_13, uStack_12, uStack_e, uStack_a - 12-byte product accumulator buffer\n    These represent overlapping views of Stack[-0x14] to Stack[-0x08] at different code points\n  piVar1/puVar1 - Combined exponent temporary (reused for different purposes)\n  piVar4/p_Var4 - Cached copy of pResult pointer\n  piVar5/p_Var5 - Cached copy of pMultiplier pointer\n  uVar6 - Result exponent (16-bit)\n  uVar7 - First operand exponent extracted\n  uVar10 - Second operand exponent extracted\n  uVar9 - Second operand exponent (16-bit copy)\n  uVar11 - Result sign bit (0x8000 or 0x0000)\n  iVar8/iVar3/sVar2 - Intermediate mantissa word values during assembly\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero * anything = Zero (preserving sign)\n  - Infinity * finite = Infinity (with XOR sign)\n  - Overflow = Infinity (0x7FFF8000 with appropriate sign)\n  - Underflow = Zero (denormalized or true zero)\n\nStructure Layout (_LDBL12):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Description\n  0x00    2     wMantissa0  Mantissa bits 0-15 (lowest)\n  0x02    2     wMantissa1  Mantissa bits 16-31\n  0x04    2     wMantissa2  Mantissa bits 32-47\n  0x06    2     wMantissa3  Mantissa bits 48-63\n  0x08    2     wMantissa4  Mantissa bits 64-79 (includes explicit integer bit)\n  0x0A    2     wSignExp    Sign bit (0x8000) + 15-bit biased exponent\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7FFF - Maximum exponent value (infinity/NaN indicator)\n  0x8000 - Sign bit mask\n  0x3FC0 - Underflow threshold (exp1 + exp2 below this = underflow)\n  0xBFFE - Overflow threshold (exp1 + exp2 above this = overflow)\n  0xC002 - Exponent bias adjustment (-16382 as signed, corrects for double bias)\n  0x7FFF8000 - Infinity representation (max exponent + implicit bit)",
