      "comment": "Multiplies a 12-byte long double by a power of 10.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save stack canary for buffer overflow protection\n2. Select power table based on exponent sign:\n   - Positive exponent: use g_aLd12PositivePowersOf10\n   - Negative exponent: negate exponent, use g_aLd12NegativePowersOf10\n3. If nClearOnZero is zero, clear the result's first word (exponent field)\n4. Process exponent in octal (3 bits at a time):\n   a. Extract low 3 bits (dwExpBits = nExponent AND 7)\n   b. Shift exponent right by 3 (divide by 8)\n   c. Advance table pointer by 0x54 bytes (7 entries * 12 bytes)\n   d. If dwExpBits != 0, lookup multiplier at table[dwExpBits]\n   e. If multiplier exponent > 0x7FFF, copy and decrement exponent\n   f. Call ___ld12mul to multiply result by power of 10\n5. Loop continues until exponent is fully processed\n6. Verify stack canary and return\n\nParameters:\n  pLd12Result (_LDBL12*): Pointer to 12-byte long double to multiply in-place\n  nExponent (int): Power of 10 exponent (can be positive or negative)\n  nClearOnZero (int): If 0, clears result's exponent field before processing\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result is modified in place via pLd12Result\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x54 (84): Table stride = 7 entries * 12 bytes per _LDBL12\n  0x7FFF: Maximum normal exponent value in 80-bit extended precision\n  0xC (12): Size of _LDBL12 structure\n\nStructure Layout (_LDBL12):\n  Offset  Size  Field      Type         Description\n  0x0     2     wExponent  ushort       Biased exponent (bits 0-14) + sign (bit 15)\n  0x2     2     wMantHi    ushort       High word of mantissa\n  0x4     4     dwMantMid  uint         Middle dword of mantissa\n  0x8     4     dwMantLo   uint         Low dword of mantissa\n\nNote: This is a CRT library function (Visual Studio 2003) used by float-to-string\nand string-to-float conversion routines. The function uses table-driven exponentiation\nfor efficient power-of-10 multiplication.",
