      "comment": "Thunk to WS2_32.setsockopt - Sets a socket option for the specified socket.\n\nThis is an import thunk that forwards to the Windows Winsock2 setsockopt function.\nUsed to configure socket behavior such as timeouts, buffer sizes, and protocol options.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Jump directly to WS2_32.dll setsockopt import\n\nParameters:\n  hSocket   - SOCKET handle to the target socket\n  nLevel    - Protocol level (SOL_SOCKET=0xFFFF, IPPROTO_TCP=6, IPPROTO_IP=0)\n  nOptname  - Option name constant (SO_REUSEADDR=4, SO_KEEPALIVE=8, TCP_NODELAY=1, etc.)\n  lpszOptval - Pointer to option value buffer\n  nOptlen   - Size of option value buffer in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  SOCKET_ERROR (-1) on failure, call WSAGetLastError() for error code\n\nCommon Options Used By Callers:\n  SOL_SOCKET + SO_REUSEADDR   - Allow address reuse for server sockets\n  SOL_SOCKET + SO_KEEPALIVE   - Enable TCP keepalive probes\n  IPPROTO_TCP + TCP_NODELAY   - Disable Nagle algorithm for low latency\n\nCallers:\n  InitializeServerListener (3 calls) - Server socket setup\n  CreateTcpConnection (3 calls)      - Client connection setup\n  InitializeNetworkServerSocket (3 calls) - Network server init",
