      "comment": "Deallocates a resource buffer by invoking the resource pool cleanup handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Preserve ECX register (may contain masked context value)\n2. Load resource buffer parameter from stack at [ESP + 0xc]\n3. Push resource buffer address onto stack as first cleanup handler argument\n4. Load global state update mask from g_dwStateUpdateFlag (address 0x6ff7f350)\n5. Negate the mask value to create AND-compatible form\n6. Store EDX (dwResourceBuffer) at stack offset +0x4\n7. Reload context parameter from [ESP + 0xc]\n8. Use SBB to sign-extend the negated mask across EAX\n9. Perform bitwise AND between masked value and ECX to filter context\n10. Push filtered context onto stack as second cleanup handler argument\n11. Load address of local variable [ESP + 0x8] into ECX register\n12. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement with prepared arguments\n13. Set return value EAX to 1 (success indicator)\n14. Restore ECX register from stack\n15. Return to caller with stack cleanup (RET 0xc removes 3 DWORD parameters)\n\nParameters:\n  pResourceContext: [ECX] Pointer to resource context or game instance object;\n                           may be filtered/masked by g_dwStateUpdateFlag negated\n  dwResourceBuffer: [EDX] Address or handle of resource buffer to deallocate\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: uint - Success status code (always returns 1 for success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Global mask at g_dwStateUpdateFlag is negated (NEG instruction) before applying\n    AND operation, suggesting mask represents disabled bits or inverted flags\n  - SBB (Sign Bit Borrow) performs sign extension of negated mask across EAX\n  - Context parameter may be filtered through AND operation with global mask\n  - Function serves as error cleanup handler in InitializeGameSessionConfig\n  - Delegates actual deallocation logic to DeallocateResourcePoolElement",
