      "comment": "Allocates memory from resource pool with automatic error logging on failure.\n\nUses the default resource pool (g_pDefaultResourcePool) if available, otherwise\nfalls back to the specified pool node ID. Logs an error via LogErrorWithContext\nif allocation fails.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_pDefaultResourcePool is non-null\n2. If available, use default pool; otherwise use dwPoolNodeId\n3. Call AllocateFromResourcePool with computed pool and size\n4. If allocation fails (NULL), log error with context info\n5. Return allocation result (may be NULL)\n\nParameters:\n  dwPoolNodeId - uint [ECX] Pool node ID to use if default pool unavailable\n  nSize - int [EDX] Size in bytes to allocate\n  lpszContext - char* [Stack+0x4] Context string for error logging (filename/function)\n  dwLineNumber - uint [Stack+0x8] Line number or context value for error logging\n\nReturns:\n  void* - Pointer to allocated memory, or NULL on failure\n\nError Handling:\n  On allocation failure, calls LogErrorWithContext(2, lpszContext, dwLineNumber, \"\")\n  Error severity level 2 indicates allocation failure",
