      "comment": "Allocates or acquires a resource with conditional behavior based on runtime feature flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global state update flag from g_dwStateUpdateFlag (determines if allocation should proceed)\n2. Negate the flag value and propagate sign to EDX (creates -1 if flag set, 0 if clear)\n3. AND the negated value with conditionalFlags parameter to conditionally zero it\n4. Call AllocateAndInitializeBuffer with potentially zeroed conditionalFlags and allocation parameters\n5. Test return value in EAX for null pointer (null indicates allocation failure)\n6. If allocation failed, call LogErrorAndShutdown with error code 2 and source file/line info\n7. Return the allocated buffer pointer in EAX (or NULL on failure)\n8. Callee cleanup: return with RET 0x10 to remove 4 stack parameters\n\nParameters:\n- conditionalFlags (ECX): Conditional mask controlling allocation behavior, passed to allocator\n- pBasePointer (Stack): Base pointer or context for allocation operation, passed to allocator\n- allocationSize (Stack): Size in bytes to allocate from pool, passed to allocator\n- pSourceFile (Stack): Source file name for error reporting on allocation failure\n- lineNumber (Stack): Line number for error reporting on allocation failure\n\nReturns:\n- void *: Pointer to allocated and initialized buffer on success, NULL on failure\n- Side effects: Calls LogErrorAndShutdown if allocation returns NULL (terminates execution)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- g_dwStateUpdateFlag acts as global feature flag to conditionally enable/disable allocation\n- When flag is clear, conditionalFlags is zeroed before allocation (disables conditional behavior)\n- When flag is set, conditionalFlags passed unchanged to allocator function\n- Negative EDX value is -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) when flag != 0, 0 when flag == 0\n- Error handling is fatal: allocation failure immediately calls shutdown handler\n- No error recovery available: callers must handle NULL return or expect program termination",
