      "comment": "Removes an error entry from the debug memory pool's hash table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate hash bucket index from error block address (address / 0x3FF)\n2. Enter critical section to protect the hash table\n3. Search the linked list in the calculated bucket for the target entry\n4. If found at head: update bucket head pointer to next entry\n5. If found in middle: update previous entry's next pointer\n6. Validate and leave critical section\n7. Deallocate the error memory block\n\nParameters:\n  pDebugPool - Pointer to debug pool structure containing:\n    - Critical section at offset 0x4\n    - Hash table buckets at offset 0x7AC (indexed by hash % 0x3FF)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3FF (1023) - Hash table bucket count for modulo operation\n  0x7AC (1964) - Offset to hash bucket array in debug pool structure\n  0x3C3, 0x3D3, 0x3E4 - Validation codes for critical section operations\n\nError Handling:\n  If entry not found in hash table, still deallocates memory block",
