      "instructions": ["0xD240|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xD242|PUSH|EBP", "0xD243|PUSH|ESI", "0xD244|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0xD246|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0xD248|JNZ|0x6ff5d24f", "0xD24A|MOV|EBP, 0x6ff9b004", "0xD24F|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0xD251|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xD253|JZ|0x6ff5d2f5", "0xD259|PUSH|EBX", "0xD25A|PUSH|EAX", "0xD25B|MOV|EAX, EBP", "0xD25D|CALL|0x6ff5cfc0", "0xD262|MOV|EBX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Deallocates an element from the resource pool by clearing its allocation bit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pDebugPool is NULL, use the default global resource manager (g_pDefaultResourceManager)\n2. Read the resource value from pResourceAddress; exit early if zero\n3. Call SearchResourceTableByThreshold to find the pool entry containing this resource\n4. If pool entry not found or resource address below pool base, call RemoveErrorFromDebugPool\n5. Calculate element index: (resourceAddress - poolBase) / elementSize\n6. Validate index is within pool bounds; if not, call RemoveErrorFromDebugPool\n7. Call ValidateCriticalSection with line number 0x5d2 (1490) for debug tracking\n8. Enter critical section on the pool metadata\n9. Calculate bitmask position: dwBitPosition = index % 32, dwordOffset = index / 32\n10. Check if allocation bit is set using gdwBitMasks lookup table\n11. If bit is set: clear it using gdwInvBitMasks, decrement pool count, update node position\n12. Call ValidateCriticalSection with line number 0x605 (1541) or 0x609 (1545)\n13. Leave critical section and return\n\nParameters:\n  pResourceAddress (ECX) - Pointer to the resource address to deallocate\n  pDebugPool (EDX) - Optional debug memory pool; uses global default if NULL\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x5d2 (1490) - Source line number for pre-critical section validation\n  0x605 (1541) - Source line number for post-deallocation validation\n  0x609 (1545) - Source line number when bit was already clear (skip case)\n  0x1f (31) - Bitmask for extracting bit position within dword (index & 0x1f)\n  0x5 - Right shift amount for dword offset calculation (index >> 5 = index / 32)\n\nGlobal Data:\n  gdwBitMasks (0x6ff76ef0) - Lookup table for single-bit masks (1 << n)\n  gdwInvBitMasks (0x6ff76f70) - Lookup table for inverted bit masks (~(1 << n))\n  g_pDefaultResourceManager (0x6ff9b004) - Default resource manager when none specified",
