      "comment": "Releases all resources and memory associated with a GameResourceManager instance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if memory pool system is initialized (g_fMemoryPoolInitialized)\n2. If pResourceManager is NULL, use default global instance at g_pDefaultResourceManager (0x6ff9b004)\n3. Validate resource manager has active pool count (offset 0x1c)\n4. Enter critical section at offset 0x4 for thread-safe cleanup\n5. Iterate through each pool slot (0x30 bytes each, starting at offset 0x20):\n   a. Enter pool slot critical section\n   b. Walk linked list of allocated blocks, calling VirtualFree(MEM_RELEASE) on each\n   c. Call DeallocateMemory to free node structures\n   d. Delete pool slot critical section\n6. Free hash table pointer at offset 0x7a8\n7. Walk 0x3ff hash buckets at offset 0x7ac, freeing all chained nodes\n8. Delete main critical section\n9. Zero entire structure (0x5f3 DWORDs = 6092 bytes) using REP STOSD\n10. Enter g_csMemoryPoolLock and record pool index in g_adwRecycledPoolIndices\n11. If cleaning default instance, clear g_fMemoryPoolInitialized and delete global lock\n\nParameters:\n    pResourceManager - Pointer to GameResourceManager structure to deinitialize.\n                       If NULL, uses default global instance at 0x6ff9b004.\n                       Structure contains critical sections, pool slots, and hash table.\n\nReturns:\n    void - No return value. Function always completes cleanup regardless of state.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - NULL parameter uses global default manager\n    - Early exit if pool not initialized (g_fMemoryPoolInitialized == 0)\n    - Early exit if pool count at offset 0x1c is zero\n    - Default instance cleanup also destroys global critical section\n\nStructure Layout (GameResourceManager):\n    Offset  Size   Field              Description\n    0x00    4      dwReserved         Reserved/unused\n    0x04    24     csCriticalSection  Main lock for pool access\n    0x1c    4      dwActivePoolCount  Number of active pool slots\n    0x20    N*48   aPoolSlots         Array of pool slot structures (0x30 each)\n    0x7a8   4      pHashTableData     Pointer to hash table auxiliary data\n    0x7ac   4092   apHashBuckets      Array of 0x3ff hash bucket pointers\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x7c6 - Line number for main critical section validation\n    0x7c9 - Line number for leave after empty check\n    0x7d2 - Line number for pool slot critical section validation\n    0x813 - Line number for global lock validation\n    0x81a - Line number for global lock leave validation\n    0x81f - Line number for final cleanup validation\n    0x8000 - MEM_RELEASE flag for VirtualFree\n    0x5f3 - DWORD count for structure zeroing (6092 bytes)\n    0x3ff - Hash bucket count (1023 buckets)\n    0x30 - Pool slot structure size (48 bytes)",
