      "comment": "Logs formatted memory status information with system memory statistics.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x1040 (4160) bytes on stack for local buffers\n2. Call stack probe (__chkstk) to commit stack pages for large allocation\n3. Load format string from parameter and call _vsprintf to format initial message\n4. Output separator line (32 dashes) via logging function\n5. Output error header message \"ERROR: Out of memory!\"\n6. Output another separator line for visual formatting\n7. Call GlobalMemoryStatus (Windows API via import table) to populate MEMORYSTATUS structure\n8. For each of 6 memory metrics (total physical, available physical, total page file, available page file, total virtual, available virtual):\n   a. Extract 32-bit value from MEMORYSTATUS structure at specific offset (+0x8, +0xc, +0x10, +0x14, +0x18, +0x1c)\n   b. Call FormatNumberWithCommas to format value with thousand separators into 32-byte buffer\n   c. Call logging function with formatted string and metric label\n9. Output final separator line for visual closure\n10. Clean up stack (ADD ESP, 0x1054) and return\n\nParameters:\n  pFormatString (char*): Format string pointer, typically for initial error context message passed with variable arguments via stack\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function returns no value, all output goes through logging function at 0x6ff690a0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Stack allocation: 0x1040 bytes total (4092-byte format buffer + 32-byte MEMORYSTATUS + padding)\n  - Separator line: 32 ASCII dash characters (0x2D) for visual formatting\n  - Memory value formatting: Uses thousand separators (commas) for readability\n  - Format buffer size: 4092 bytes limits the initial formatted message length\n  - Temporary number buffer: 32 bytes per formatted number (0x20 bytes)\n  - Windows API call: GlobalMemoryStatus accessed via indirect call through import table at 0x6ff75028\n\nStructure Layout - MEMORYSTATUS:\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type   Description\n0x0     4     dwLength                DWORD  Structure size (always 32 bytes)\n0x4     4     dwMemoryLoad            DWORD  Percent of physical memory currently in use\n0x8     4     dwTotalPhys             DWORD  Total installed physical RAM in bytes\n0xc     4     dwAvailPhys             DWORD  Available physical RAM in bytes\n0x10    4     dwTotalPageFile         DWORD  Total page file size in bytes\n0x14    4     dwAvailPageFile         DWORD  Available page file space in bytes\n0x18    4     dwTotalVirtual          DWORD  Total virtual address space in bytes\n0x1c    4     dwAvailVirtual          DWORD  Available virtual address space in bytes\nTotal size: 0x20 (32 bytes)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_6", "PARAM_1", "CALLEE_5", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
