      "instructions": ["0xD6E0|PUSH|ECX", "0xD6E1|PUSH|EBX", "0xD6E2|PUSH|EBP", "0xD6E3|PUSH|ESI", "0xD6E4|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0xD6E8|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0xD6EA|PUSH|EDI", "0xD6EB|JNZ|0x6ff5d710", "0xD6ED|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xD6EF|MOV|ECX, 0x2fa9", "0xD6F4|MOV|EDI, 0x6ff9afe8", "0xD6F9|PUSH|0x6ff9afec", "0xD6FE|STOSD.REP|ES:EDI", "0xD700|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff751a8]", "0xD706|MOV|dword ptr [0x6ff9afe8], 0x1"],
      "comment": "Initializes or retrieves a memory pool allocator block from the global pool array.\n\nThis function manages a pool of 8 pre-allocated memory pool structures, each 0x17cc (6092) \nbytes in size. On first call (ppPoolBase=NULL), it initializes the global pool infrastructure.\nSubsequent calls allocate a pool block either from recycled pools or by incrementing the \nactive pool counter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If ppPoolBase is NULL (first-time init):\n   - Zero-initialize 48676 bytes of global pool state\n   - Initialize g_csMemoryPoolLock critical section\n   - Set g_fMemoryPoolInitialized flag\n2. Enter critical section for thread-safe pool allocation\n3. Check recycled pool list (g_dwRecycledPoolCount):\n   - If available: pop index from g_adwRecycledPoolIndices, compute block address\n   - If none: check if active count < 8, allocate new slot\n   - If at capacity (8 pools): log error and raise exception 0xE0000001\n4. Leave critical section\n5. Zero-initialize pool block (6092 bytes)\n6. Store pool pointer to *ppPoolBase if not NULL\n7. Initialize pool's internal critical section at offset +0x4\n8. Copy config string (max 32 bytes) to offset 0x17ac if nConfigAddress provided\n9. Calculate bucket count from nBucketCapacity using BSR (clamped to 40 max)\n10. Initialize each bucket:\n    - Bucket 0: element size = 16 bytes\n    - Bucket N: element size = 1 << (N + 4) bytes, capped at 1MB\n    - Allocation chunk sizes: 64KB-512KB depending on element size\n11. Zero-initialize pool free list (4092 bytes) at offset 0x7ac\n12. Validate and leave pool critical section\n\nParameters:\n    ppPoolBase (void**) - Output pointer to receive allocated pool block address.\n                          Pass NULL for first-time global initialization only.\n    nConfigAddress (int) - Address of null-terminated config string (max 32 chars).\n                           Copied to pool block offset 0x17ac. Pass 0 to skip.\n    nBucketCapacity (int) - Desired allocation capacity hint for bucket sizing.\n                            Used to calculate number of size buckets (0-40).\n                            Values <= 16 result in 0 buckets.\n\nReturns:\n    uint - Always returns 0 on success. Does not return on fatal error (raises exception).\n\nStructure Layout (Pool Block at g_pDefaultResourcePool, size 0x17cc):\n    Offset  Size    Field                   Description\n    0x0000  4       dwPoolId                Pool identifier/index\n    0x0004  24      csCriticalSection       Per-pool critical section\n    0x001c  4       dwBucketCount           Number of size buckets (0-40)\n    0x0020  N*48    aBuckets[40]            Array of bucket descriptors\n            +0x00   csBucket                Bucket critical section (24 bytes)\n            +0x18   dwElementSize           Element size for this bucket\n            +0x1c   dwElementsPerChunk      Elements per allocation chunk\n            +0x20   dwChunkSize             Total chunk allocation size\n    0x07a8  4       dwFreeListHead          Free list head index\n    0x07ac  4092    adwFreeList             Free list index array (1023 entries)\n    0x17ac  32      szConfigName            Configuration name string\n    0x17cb  1       bConfigTerminator       Null terminator for config string\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x17cc - Pool block structure size (6092 bytes)\n    0x2fa9 - Global state size in dwords (48676 bytes)\n    0x5f3  - Pool block size in dwords (6092 bytes) \n    0x3ff  - Free list size in dwords (4092 bytes)\n    0xE0000001 - Fatal exception code for pool exhaustion\n    8      - Maximum number of concurrent pools\n    40     - Maximum number of size buckets per pool\n    0x863  - Source line 2147 (critical section validation)\n    0x86c  - Source line 2156 (bucket overflow error)\n\nError Handling:\n    - Pool exhaustion (8 pools active): Logs error, raises exception 0xE0000001\n    - Bucket count overflow (>40): Logs fatal error, calls ShutdownResourcesAndExit(-1)\n\nCalled By: AllocateFromResourcePool, InitializeGameInstance",
