      "instructions": ["0xD910|PUSH|ECX", "0xD911|PUSH|EBP", "0xD912|PUSH|ESI", "0xD913|PUSH|EDI", "0xD914|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0xD916|SUB|EDI, 0x4", "0xD919|MOV|EAX, EDI", "0xD91B|CDQ|", "0xD91C|MOV|ECX, 0x3ff", "0xD921|IDIV|ECX", "0xD923|LEA|ESI, [EBX + 0x4]", "0xD926|MOV|ECX, ESI", "0xD928|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0xD92A|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EDX", "0xD92E|MOV|EDX, 0x400"],
      "comment": "Rehash and reallocate a block within a hash table pool.\n\nThis function removes a memory block from its current position in a hash table's\ncollision chain, reallocates it to a new size, recalculates its hash bucket,\nand reinserts it into the appropriate collision chain.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate hash bucket index: hash = (address - 4) % 0x3FF\n2. Acquire critical section lock to protect hash table access\n3. Search the collision chain at hash bucket for the target block\n4. Unlink the block from the collision chain (either head or middle)\n5. Call _realloc to resize the block with new size\n6. If reallocation fails, log error and trigger fatal shutdown\n7. Recalculate hash bucket index for the reallocated address\n8. Insert the reallocated block at the head of its new collision chain\n9. Release critical section lock\n10. Return pointer to reallocated block (with +4 offset to skip metadata)\n\nParameters:\n  dwNewSize - New size in bytes for the block allocation (IMPLICIT: in_EAX contains block ptr)\n  IMPLICIT in_EAX - Pointer to existing block requiring reallocation\n  IMPLICIT unaff_EBX - Base pointer to pool/hash table structure\n\nReturns:\n  uint* - Pointer to reallocated block data (offset +4 from block start)\n  NULL (0) - If block not found in hash table (early exit before realloc)\n  Note: Function does NOT return on allocation failure (calls ReportError(-1))\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Block pointer refers to data at offset +4; metadata/next ptr at offset 0\n  - Hash table uses 0x3FF (1023) buckets with bucket array at offset 0x7AC\n  - Critical section at offset +4 from base protects all hash operations\n  - Chain is singly-linked list; next pointer stored at block offset 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3FF - Hash table bucket count (1023 buckets for modulo operation)\n  0x7AC - Offset from base to hash bucket array\n  0x400 - Validation code for EnterCriticalSection\n  0x44B - Validation code for LeaveCriticalSection (not found path)\n  0x432 - Validation code for LeaveCriticalSection (success path)\n  0x421 - Error code passed to LogErrorWithContext\n\nError Handling:\n  - If block not in hash table: releases lock, returns NULL\n  - If _realloc fails: logs memory status, WSACleanup, logs error, exits via ReportError(-1)",
      "tags": ["API_NETWORK", "CALLEE_10", "CALLER_1", "PARAM_1"]
