      "instructions": ["0xDAD0|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0xDAD3|PUSH|EBX", "0xDAD4|PUSH|EBP", "0xDAD5|PUSH|ESI", "0xDAD6|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0xDAD8|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x7a8]", "0xDADE|PUSH|EDI", "0xDADF|LEA|EDI, [ESI + 0x4]", "0xDAE2|MOV|EDX, 0x293", "0xDAE7|MOV|ECX, EDI", "0xDAE9|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0xDAED|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EDI", "0xDAF1|CALL|0x6ff6e0e0", "0xDAF6|PUSH|EDI", "0xDAF7|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff7504c]"],
      "comment": "Removes a resource node from the pool's sorted tracking array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate and acquire pool critical section at offset 0x4\n2. Binary search for the resource in the sorted array (offset 0x7a8)\n   - Array elements are 8-byte entries with key at offset +4\n   - Uses standard binary search with SAR for midpoint calculation\n3. If not found, log error and trigger fatal shutdown\n4. If found, use memmove to shift subsequent elements left\n5. Decrement resource count (offset 0x7a0)\n6. Update memory tracking total (offset 0x17a8) by subtracting resource size\n7. If count + 64 < capacity, shrink array by 32 entries via realloc\n8. Release critical section and return\n\nParameters:\n  pPool (ECX) - DebugMemoryPool*: Pool manager containing the resource array\n  pNode (EDX) - ResourcePoolNode*: Node to remove, key read from offset 0x0\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function triggers fatal error if resource not found\n\nError Handling:\n  - Resource not found: Logs error at line 0x2BE/0x2BF, calls ShutdownResourcesAndExit(-1)\n  - Realloc failure: Logs memory status, error at line 0x2B4, fatal shutdown\n\nStructure Layout (DebugMemoryPool offsets):\n  0x004 - CRITICAL_SECTION for thread safety\n  0x7A0 - int nResourceCount: Current number of tracked resources  \n  0x7A4 - int nResourceCapacity: Allocated capacity of resource array\n  0x7A8 - ResourceEntry* pResourceArray: Sorted array of 8-byte entries\n  0x17A8 - int nTotalMemoryUsage: Running total of allocated memory\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x293, 0x2BE, 0x2B9 - Source line numbers for ValidateCriticalSection\n  0x2BF, 0x2B4 - Source line numbers for error logging\n  0x40 (64) - Shrink threshold: shrink when count + 64 < capacity\n  0x20 (32) - Shrink amount: reduce capacity by 32 entries",
