      "comment": "Allocates a memory block from a resource pool using a power-of-two size class allocator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Use default pool (g_pDefaultResourcePool) if pPoolNode is NULL\n2. Initialize memory pool allocator if not yet initialized (g_fMemoryPoolInitialized == 0)\n3. If pool node is uninitialized (nodeData[0] == 0), fall back to AllocatePoolBlockFromSlot\n4. Calculate slot index using BSR (bit scan reverse) to find log2 of (nRequestedSize - 1)\n   - Size < 17: slot 0\n   - Size < 3: slot 1\n   - Otherwise: BSR(size-1) + 1 - 4 = log2-based index\n5. Compute slot address: poolNode + 0x20 + (slotIndex * 0x30)\n6. Enter critical section for thread-safe allocation\n7. Call AllocateNextPoolNode to get next available node from slot\n8. Mark allocation bit in bitmap: bitmap[nodeIndex/32] |= (1 << (nodeIndex & 0x1f))\n9. Manage linked list pointers when pool block becomes full\n10. Calculate final address: (blockSize * nodeIndex) + baseAddress\n11. Leave critical section and return allocated pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pPoolNode (ECX) - Pointer to ResourcePoolNode, uses g_pDefaultResourcePool if NULL\n  nRequestedSize (EDX) - Requested allocation size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  void* - Pointer to allocated memory block, or NULL on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pPoolNode defaults to global pool at 0x6ff9b004\n  - Uninitialized pool triggers InitializeMemoryPoolAllocator\n  - Pool exhaustion triggers error handlers (CleanupAndAbort, ReportError)\n\nError Handling:\n  - Validates critical section at entry/exit (lines 0x4ef, 0x4f7, 0x51d)\n  - Allocation failure (line 0x4f8): calls CleanupAndAbort then ReportError(-1)\n  - Double allocation detected (line 0x4ff): bit already set in bitmap\n  - List corruption (line 0x50d): SpinCount is NULL when expected\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x30 - Size of each pool slot structure\n  0x20 - Offset to first slot in pool node\n  0x1c - Offset to max slot count in pool node\n  0x1f - Bit mask for 32-bit bitmap index (nodeIndex & 0x1f)\n  0x4ef, 0x4f7, 0x51d - Line numbers for critical section validation\n  0x4f3, 0x4f8, 0x4ff, 0x50d - Error line numbers for diagnostics",
