      "comment": "Reallocates an existing buffer to a new size or allocates a new buffer if none exists.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pExistingBuffer is NULL, allocate new buffer via FUN_6ff5e0c0 with conditional flags and size\n2. If allocation fails, log fatal error (line 0x62D) and shutdown\n3. If pExistingBuffer is non-NULL, search resource table via SearchResourceTableByThreshold\n4. If table entry not found, call RehashAndReallocatePoolBlock to reallocate\n5. If reallocation fails, log fatal error (line 0x635) and shutdown\n6. If table entry found, calculate slot index: (existingBuffer - tableBase) / elementSize\n7. Validate slot index is within block bounds (LockCount field)\n8. Enter critical section for thread-safe access\n9. Check allocation bitmask to verify slot is allocated (gdwBitMasks array)\n10. If slot not allocated, exit critical section and report error (line 0x6A0)\n11. If requested size fits in current element size, return existing buffer\n12. If requested size exceeds element size, allocate new larger buffer\n13. Copy data from old buffer to new: first copy DWORDs, then remaining bytes\n14. Deallocate old buffer via DeallocateResourcePoolElement\n15. Return new buffer pointer\n\nParameters:\n- dwConditionalFlags (uint): Conditional allocation flags passed to allocator\n- pExistingBuffer (void *): Existing buffer to reallocate, or NULL for new allocation\n- dwRequestedSize (uint): Requested buffer size in bytes\n- szSourceFile (char *): Source file name for error logging\n- dwLineNumber (uint): Source line number for error logging\n\nReturns:\n- void *: Pointer to allocated/reallocated buffer on success\n- Does not return on failure (calls ReportError with exit code -1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pExistingBuffer triggers fresh allocation path\n- Buffer reuse if current element size >= requested size\n- Memory copy uses optimized DWORD-then-byte pattern (rep movsd / rep movsb)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x62D (1581): Error line for initial allocation failure\n- 0x635 (1589): Error line for table lookup reallocation failure\n- 0x63C (1596): Error line for out-of-bounds reallocation failure\n- 0x648 (1608): Error line for slot index exceeds block bounds\n- 0x682 (1666): Validation line for size-fits-in-element return\n- 0x688 (1672): Validation line for new allocation needed\n- 0x68B (1675): Error line for new allocation failed during resize\n- 0x69E (1694): Validation line for slot-not-allocated error\n- 0x6A0 (1696): Error line for slot not allocated in bitmask\n\nError Handling:\n- All allocation failures are fatal and trigger program shutdown\n- Uses CleanupAndAbort for non-null buffer path errors\n- Uses direct Ordinal_10028 + ShutdownResourcesAndExit for null buffer path\n\nSSA Variables (decompiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\n- lpCriticalSection: Pool block pointer (offset 0x14 of table entry)\n- p_Var1: Element size from pool block (DebugInfo field reinterpreted)\n- uVar6: Slot index within block, reused as loop counter\n- puVar7-9: Buffer pointers for memory copy operation\n- iVar10: Error line number for CleanupAndAbort calls",
