      "comment": "Queues a timed event into the event manager's priority queue for deferred execution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 24-byte TimedEvent structure using SMemAlloc from FogEvents.cpp\n2. Initialize vtable pointer to PTR_CompareFieldLessOrEqual for heap ordering\n3. Clear heap index fields (pOwnerHeap, dwHeapIndex, dwTriggerTime)\n4. Store custom event data at offsets 0x10 and 0x14\n5. Calculate trigger time: GetTickCount() + nDelayMilliseconds\n6. If trigger time differs from stored value and event is in a heap:\n   a. Remove from current heap position via HeapRemoveLastAndSiftDown\n   b. Re-insert with new priority via InsertHeapElement\n7. Enter critical section at pEventManager+0x14\n8. Insert event into manager's priority queue\n9. Signal event handle at pEventManager+0x3C to wake worker thread\n10. Leave critical section and return success\n\nParameters:\n- pEventManager (TimedEventManager*): Pointer to TimedEventManager structure containing:\n  - Offset 0x14: CRITICAL_SECTION for queue synchronization\n  - Offset 0x3C: HANDLE event to signal worker thread\n- nDelayMilliseconds (int): Delay in milliseconds before event triggers\n- dwCustomEventData1 (uint): User-defined event data stored at offset 0x10\n- dwCustomEventData2 (uint): User-defined event data stored at offset 0x14\n\nReturns:\n- int: Always returns 1 (success). Allocation failures are handled internally.\n\nStructure Layout (TimedEvent - 0x18 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field              Type      Description\n0x00    4     pVtable            void*     Pointer to comparison vtable\n0x04    4     pOwnerHeap         void*     Heap containing this element\n0x08    4     dwHeapIndex        uint      Current index in heap array\n0x0C    4     dwTriggerTime      uint      GetTickCount when event fires\n0x10    4     dwCustomData1      uint      User-defined event data 1\n0x14    4     dwCustomData2      uint      User-defined event data 2\n\nNotes:\n- Uses SEH exception handling frame (FS:[0] manipulation)\n- Source file: ..\\Source\\Fog\\Src\\FogEvents.cpp line 0x6A (106)\n- Thread-safe: Uses critical section for queue modification\n- Worker thread signaled via SetEvent to process new events",
