      "instructions": ["0xE890|MOV|EAX, [0x6ff9afcc]", "0xE895|PUSH|EBX", "0xE896|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0xE898|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xE89A|JNZ|0x6ff5e8a0", "0xE89C|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0xE89E|POP|EBX", "0xE89F|RET|", "0xE8A0|PUSH|ESI", "0xE8A1|PUSH|0x6ff9af24", "0xE8A6|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff7504c]", "0xE8AC|MOV|EAX, [0x6ff9af3c]", "0xE8B1|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xE8B3|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [0x6ff75040]", "0xE8B9|JZ|0x6ff5e8ee"],
      "comment": "Decrements the symbol handler initialization reference counter and invokes cleanup callback when counter reaches zero.\n\nThis function implements a reference counting mechanism for symbol handler initialization. It maintains thread safety through critical section locking and properly manages the lifecycle of the symbol handler. The counter tracks the number of active initialization contexts, and when the last context is released, the cleanup callback is invoked to properly shut down symbol handling resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if symbol handler initialization is enabled via g_dwSymbolHandlerInitEnabled flag\n2. Return 0 if initialization not enabled (early exit path)\n3. Acquire g_SymbolHandlerCriticalSection lock for thread-safe counter access\n4. Load current reference count from g_dwSymbolInitializeCallCount\n5. If counter is zero, skip to cleanup exit\n6. Decrement the reference counter by 1\n7. If counter is now zero, invoke cleanup callback via g_pfnSymCleanup\n8. Get current process handle via GetCurrentProcess for cleanup callback parameter\n9. Test context validity from caller context register (EDI)\n10. If context invalid, skip cleanup and proceed to exit\n11. Release critical section lock via LeaveCriticalSection\n12. Return cleanup status in EAX (0 if context invalid or not enabled, 1 if cleanup performed)\n\nParameters:\nNone - This function takes no explicit parameters but reads context state from EDI register set by caller\n\nReturns:\nEAX - DWORD cleanup status (0 = not enabled or context invalid, 1 = cleanup performed, >=0 = general success code)\n\nGlobal Data Items:\ng_dwSymbolHandlerInitEnabled - DWORD flag indicating if symbol handler initialization is globally enabled\ng_dwSymbolInitializeCallCount - DWORD reference counter tracking active initialization contexts\ng_SymbolHandlerCriticalSection - CRITICAL_SECTION lock for thread-safe counter modification\ng_pfnSymCleanup - Function pointer to cleanup callback invoked when reference count reaches zero\ng_pfnGetCurrentProcess - Function pointer to GetCurrentProcess Win32 API call\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early return if initialization disabled: avoids unnecessary locking overhead\n- Reference counting: supports multiple callers sharing single handler instance\n- Thread safety: critical section ensures atomic counter operations across threads\n- Context validation: EDI register checked to validate caller context before cleanup\n- Counter preservation: only invokes cleanup on transition from 1 to 0",
      "tags": ["CALLER_2", "PARAM_0", "CALLEE_3"]
