      "comment": "Enumerates all loaded modules for a process and builds a sorted linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Try loading toolhelp32 API from kernel32.dll then tlhelp32.dll\n2. Get function pointers: CreateToolhelp32Snapshot, Module32First, Module32Next\n3. Create snapshot with TH32CS_SNAPMODULE (0x8) flag for target process\n4. Iterate through modules using Module32First/Module32Next\n5. Allocate 0x210 byte node for each module using FUN_6ff5e0c0\n6. Zero-initialize node (0x84 dwords = 0x210 bytes)\n7. Copy module name and path, store base address and size\n8. Insert node into sorted linked list by base address (ascending order)\n9. Clean up: close snapshot handle and free library\n\nParameters:\n  dwProcessId - Target process ID for module enumeration (0 for current process)\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to head of sorted module list on success, NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8   - TH32CS_SNAPMODULE flag\n  0x210 - Module info node size (528 bytes)\n  0x104 - Offset to szExePath\n  0x204 - Offset to dwModuleBaseAddr\n  0x20C - Offset to pNextNode",
