      "comment": "Cleanup and release all system resources during shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load main thread/event handle from g_hStackWalkThread\n2. Check if main handle is valid (non-NULL)\n3. If main handle is NULL, jump to skip_thread_event_close\n4. Load associated thread event handle from g_hStackWalkCompleteEvent\n5. Check if thread event is valid (non-NULL)\n6. If thread event is NULL, jump to after_thread_event_cleanup\n7. Push thread event handle and call CloseHandle to close the event\n8. Clear g_hStackWalkCompleteEvent reference to NULL\n9. Load main handle and push 100ms timeout value\n10. Call WaitForSingleObject to wait for main thread with 100ms timeout\n11. Clear symbol handler initialization flag (g_dwSymbolHandlerInitEnabled = 0)\n12. Load module handle from g_hDebugHelperDllHandle\n13. Check if module is loaded (non-NULL)\n14. If module is NULL, jump to cleanup_critical_section\n15. Push module handle and call FreeLibrary to unload the library\n16. Clear g_hDebugHelperDllHandle reference to NULL\n17. Push address of g_SymbolHandlerCriticalSection and call DeleteCriticalSection\n18. Load return value 0x1 (success status) into EAX\n19. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - Operates on global module state without parameters\n\nReturns:\nint: Returns 1 (success status), always returns success\n\nSpecial Cases and Magic Numbers:\n- 0x64 (100ms): Timeout value for WaitForSingleObject to prevent indefinite waits\n- Handles NULL/zero pointer checks for all resources to prevent access violations\n- Critical section deletion is unconditional and always executed\n- Thread event is only closed if it exists; main thread wait happens on g_hStackWalkThread\n- Module is only freed if loaded; reference is cleared after successful unload\n- Initialization flag is cleared after thread event cleanup, before module cleanup",
      "tags": ["CALLER_1", "PARAM_0", "CALLEE_4"]
    },
