      "instructions": ["0xEDA0|SUB|ESP, 0x400", "0xEDA6|PUSH|EBP", "0xEDA7|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x408]", "0xEDAE|PUSH|ESI", "0xEDAF|PUSH|EDI", "0xEDB0|MOV|EAX, 0x200", "0xEDB5|LEA|ESI, [ESP + 0xc]", "0xEDB9|MOV|byte ptr [EBP], 0x0", "0xEDBD|CALL|0x6ff5ea00", "0xEDC2|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0xEDC4|JNZ|0x6ff5edcc", "0xEDC6|MOV|byte ptr [ESP + 0xc], AL", "0xEDCA|JMP|0x6ff5ee11", "0xEDCC|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0xc]", "0xEDD0|MOV|EDX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Builds a semicolon-delimited symbol search path for the debug symbol handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output buffer by setting first character to null terminator\n2. Call ExtractModuleDirectory to get module's directory path into szModuleDir buffer\n3. If module directory found, append it to output path with semicolon separator\n4. Call GetCurrentDirectoryA to get working directory into szCurrentDir buffer\n5. If current directory differs from module directory (via __stricmp), append it with separator\n6. Call GetEnvironmentVariableA for \"_NT_SYMBOL_PATH\" and append if present\n7. Call GetEnvironmentVariableA for \"_NT_ALTERNATE_SYMBOL_PATH\" and append if present\n8. Call GetEnvironmentVariableA for \"SYSTEMROOT\" and append if present\n9. Remove trailing semicolon from final path string\n10. Log the generated path via LogAppendFormat or error if path is empty\n\nParameters:\n    lpszOutputPath - Pointer to output buffer receiving the semicolon-delimited search path.\n                     Must be large enough to hold concatenated paths (recommended 2048+ bytes).\n\nReturns:\n    char* - Pointer to lpszOutputPath if path was built successfully, NULL if output buffer is empty.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Returns NULL if no path components could be retrieved\n    - Duplicate paths are avoided by comparing current directory against module directory\n    - Each path component is separated by semicolon (;) stored in g_szPathSeparator\n\nEnvironment Variables Checked:\n    - _NT_SYMBOL_PATH: Primary Microsoft symbol server path\n    - _NT_ALTERNATE_SYMBOL_PATH: Secondary symbol path\n    - SYSTEMROOT: Windows system directory (e.g., C:\\Windows)\n\nStack Layout:\n    Offset    Size    Description\n    -0x400    512     szModuleDir - Module directory buffer\n    -0x200    512     szCurrentDir - Current/environment variable buffer\n\nRelated Functions:\n    - ExtractModuleDirectory: Gets directory containing current module\n    - InitializeSymbolHandler: Caller that uses this path for SymInitialize\n    - DumpThreadCallStackWithSymbols: Uses symbol path for stack trace generation",
