      "comment": "Loads crash dump records from file and aggregates duplicate entries into output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Build file path by extracting module directory and appending \"Crashdump\"\n2. Create directory path if ExtractModuleDirectory succeeds\n3. Check if crash dump file exists via GetFileAttributesA\n4. Open file with read sharing, seek to end to get file size\n5. Allocate memory from resource pool for entire file contents\n6. Read file contents, close file, and delete the crash dump file\n7. Parse records from file buffer - each record contains:\n   - dwExceptionAddress (4 bytes) - crash location\n   - dwExceptionCode (4 bytes) - exception type\n   - dwModuleOffset (4 bytes) - module relative offset\n   - nStackFrameCount (4 bytes) - number of stack frames\n   - Stack frame data (nStackFrameCount * 4 bytes)\n8. For each record, search existing entries for duplicates\n9. If duplicate found (same address, code, offset, frame count, and stack data):\n   - Increment occurrence counter in existing entry\n10. If unique entry and buffer space available:\n    - Create new output record with count=1\n    - Copy all record fields and stack frame data\n11. Store total unique record count in output buffer byte 0\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (ECX): Output buffer for aggregated crash records\n    - Byte 0: Total unique record count\n    - Byte 1+: Array of aggregated record entries\n  pnBufferSize (EDX): Pointer to buffer size\n    - Input: Maximum buffer size\n    - Output: Number of bytes written (starts at 1, incremented per entry)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Success, crash dump loaded and processed\n  0 - Failure (file not found, open failed, seek failed)\n\nOutput Record Structure (variable size per entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field\n  0x00    2     wOccurrenceCount (number of times this crash occurred)\n  0x02    4     dwExceptionAddress\n  0x06    4     dwExceptionCode\n  0x0A    4     dwModuleOffset\n  0x0E    1     bStackFrameCount\n  0x0F    N*4   Stack frame return addresses\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If memory allocation fails, logs error but continues (undefined behavior)\n  - Loop breaks early if output buffer would overflow (checks +0x2F boundary)\n  - File is always deleted after successful read regardless of processing",
