      "comment": "Writes crash dump data to a file for debugging purposes.\n\nCreates a crash dump file in the module directory containing exception information.\nThe function builds the crash file path from the module directory and a predefined\nfilename, then writes the exception data structure to the file.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate stack space for path buffer (260 bytes) and crash data (32 bytes)\n2. Call ExtractModuleDirectory to get the executable's directory path\n3. If directory extraction succeeds, copy the base path to buffer\n4. Append the crash dump filename to form full path\n5. Open the crash dump file for writing\n6. If file opened successfully:\n   a. Copy exception parameters to local crash data structure\n   b. Copy additional exception data from pExceptionData based on nExceptionDataCount\n   c. Write crash data structure to file using fwrite\n   d. Close the file handle\n7. Restore stack and return\n\nParameters:\ndwExceptionCode - Exception code from Windows exception record (e.g., 0xC0000005)\ndwExceptionAddress - Address where exception occurred\ndwExceptionFlags - Exception flags (continuable/non-continuable)\npExceptionData - Pointer to additional exception-specific data (opaque buffer)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; file write errors are silently ignored\n\nStack Layout:\nOffset   Size   Variable              Type          Description\n-0x134   4      dwDataCount           uint          Copy of exception data count\n-0x130   4      dwExceptionFlagsCopy  uint          Copy of exception flags\n-0x12c   4      dwWriteFlags          uint          File write flags\n-0x128   4      local_128             uint          Temporary (phantom)\n-0x124   32     szCrashFilename       byte[32]      Crash dump filename buffer\n-0x104   260    szModuleDirectory     char[260]     Module directory path buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If ExtractModuleDirectory fails, continues with empty base path\n- If file cannot be opened, skips write and returns silently\n- nExceptionDataCount (in EDI) contains count of additional data elements\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x104 (260) - MAX_PATH for Windows path buffer\n0x10 (16) - Base size of crash header structure\n0x134 (308) - Total stack allocation for local variables\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error handling; failures are silently ignored to prevent\ncrash handler from causing additional crashes\n\nTechnical Notes:\n- szCrashFilename is typed as undefined1[32] in decompiler (should be char[32])\n- pExceptionData is intentionally void* as it holds opaque exception data",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "PARAM_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "CALLEE_7", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
