      "comment": "Frees all nodes in a module information linked list by iterating and deallocating each element.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Receive head of module info linked list in EAX (implicit parameter)\n2. Return immediately if list head is null\n3. For each node in the linked list:\n   a. Save pointer to next node from offset 0x20c (pNextNode field)\n   b. Store current node address in stack variable\n   c. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to free the current node\n   d. Advance to next node using saved pointer\n4. Continue until pNextNode is null (end of list)\n5. Return after all nodes are freed\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT in_EAX: Pointer to head of module info linked list; each node is a 0x210 byte structure containing module path, base name, base address, size, and pNextNode pointer at offset 0x20c\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value; all memory is freed as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Null list head: Returns immediately without any deallocation\n  Single node list: Deallocates the one node and returns\n  Memory ownership: Caller loses all references after this call; pointers become invalid\n\nStructure Layout - Module Info Node (0x210 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field             Type      Description\n  0x000   0x104 szModuleFilename  char[260] Full path to module (MAX_PATH)\n  0x104   0x100 szModuleBaseName  char[256] Base name of module\n  0x204   0x004 dwBaseAddress     uint      Module base address in memory\n  0x208   0x004 dwModuleSize      uint      Size of module in bytes\n  0x20C   0x004 pNextNode         pointer   Pointer to next node in linked list\n\nCalled By:\n  DumpThreadCallStackWithSymbols - cleanup after stack walk enumeration\n  EnumerateProcessModules - cleanup on error path during module enumeration",
      "tags": ["SRC_Exceptions.cpp", "CALLER_2", "CALLEE_1", "PARAM_0", "PROP_SMALL"]
    },
