      "instructions": ["0xFC10|MOV|EAX, 0x152c", "0xFC15|CALL|0x6ff58270", "0xFC1A|PUSH|EBP", "0xFC1B|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x10]", "0xFC1F|PUSH|EAX", "0xFC20|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0xFC22|PUSH|EBP", "0xFC23|PUSH|0x6ff78a68", "0xFC28|PUSH|0x6ff77628", "0xFC2D|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x20], EBP", "0xFC31|CALL|0x6ff5ccc2", "0xFC36|CMP|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EBP", "0xFC3A|JZ|0x6ff5fc5a", "0xFC3C|PUSH|0x6ff78448", "0xFC41|PUSH|0x6ff766a3"],
      "comment": "Dumps the current thread's call stack with symbolic information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check NoStackDump configuration flag - exit early if set\n2. Verify stack walk subsystem is initialized (g_fStackWalkInitialized)\n3. Duplicate current thread handle for symbol enumeration\n4. Initialize DbgHelp symbol engine with SymInitialize\n5. Build symbol search path and load module symbols\n6. Configure symbol options (SYMOPT_UNDNAME | SYMOPT_LOAD_LINES)\n7. Get current process ID and initialize stack frame structure\n8. Walk stack frames using StackWalk API (up to 64 frames max)\n9. For each frame:\n   a. Resolve symbol name using SymFromAddr\n   b. Get source file/line info using SymGetLineFromAddr\n   c. Find PE section containing the address\n   d. Log frame with address, symbol, file:line, section info\n10. Clean up: call SymCleanup and close thread handle\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses implicit thread context)\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 on success, 0 on failure/disabled\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x152c    - Stack frame size allocation\n  0x14c     - STACKFRAME structure size for x86\n  0x3       - Machine type (IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_I386)\n  0x40      - Maximum stack frames to walk (64)\n  0x10      - SYMOPT_UNDNAME flag for undecorated names\n  0x104     - MAX_PATH for module path buffer\n  0x23c     - IMAGEHLP_LINE structure size\n\nError Handling:\n  - Returns 0 if NoStackDump config is set\n  - Returns 0 if stack walk subsystem not initialized\n  - Returns 0 if SymInitialize fails (logs error code)\n  - Logs StackWalk failures with error code but continues\n\nCalled by: Ordinal_10028, Ordinal_10052, ProcessDebugThreadStack",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_3", "CALLEE_19", "STRUCT_Room2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path"]
