      "comment": "Initializes the debug symbol handler for stack walking and symbol resolution.\n\nThis function implements reference-counted initialization of the Windows Debug Help Library\n(dbghelp.dll) symbol handler. It ensures thread-safe access via critical section, manages \na reference count to allow multiple callers to share a single symbol handler instance, and\nbuilds the symbol search path before calling SymInitialize.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock for thread-safe access to initialization state\n2. Check if symbol handler is globally enabled (g_fDebugSymbolsInitialized)\n3. Increment reference count; if this is not the first initialization, return success\n4. Build symbol search path if not already constructed\n5. Get current process handle and call SymInitialize with the search path\n6. On SymInitialize failure, log error, call SymCleanup, reset counter, and return false\n7. Increment counter again (double-increment pattern for success tracking)\n8. Set symbol options with SYMOPT_LOAD_LINES flag (0x10)\n9. Get current process ID for module enumeration context\n10. Iterate through loaded modules via IterateModulesAndLoadSymbols\n11. Deallocate each module node after processing\n12. Release critical section lock and return success status\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nbool - true if symbol handler is initialized and ready, false on initialization failure\n\nGlobal Data Items:\ng_fDebugSymbolsInitialized - DWORD flag indicating symbol handler is globally enabled\ng_nSymbolInitRefCount - int reference counter for nested initialization calls\ng_szSymbolSearchPath - char buffer containing semicolon-delimited symbol search paths\nlpCriticalSection_6ff9af24 - CRITICAL_SECTION for thread-safe initialization\ng_pfnSymInitialize - Function pointer to dbghelp!SymInitialize\ng_pfnSymCleanup - Function pointer to dbghelp!SymCleanup\ng_pfnSymGetOptions - Function pointer to dbghelp!SymGetOptions\ng_pfnSymSetOptions - Function pointer to dbghelp!SymSetOptions\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if g_fDebugSymbolsInitialized is 0 (symbol handling disabled)\n- Reference counting allows multiple callers without reinitializing\n- Module list iteration continues even if individual modules fail to load\n- Critical section ensures thread-safe reference count modification\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 - SYMOPT_LOAD_LINES: Load line number information for source debugging\n0x20c - Offset to next module pointer in module list node structure\n\nError Handling:\n- Logs error code from GetLastError on SymInitialize failure\n- Calls SymCleanup before returning on error to release partial state\n- Resets reference count to 0 on failure to allow retry",
      "tags": ["SRC_Exceptions.cpp", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_Control", "CALLEE_8"]
