      "comment": "Initializes the stack walking subsystem for exception dump collection and debugging.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if stack dump disabled flag is set via SFileRead (output parameter)\n2. If disabled, log \"Stack dump turned off\" error and return\n3. Verify ImageHelp DLL is loaded by checking g_hDebugHelperImageHelpHandle\n4. If not loaded, log \"imagehlp.dll not loaded\" error and return\n5. Check if stack walk completion event exists at g_hStackWalkCompleteEvent\n6. If null, log \"No event to trigger stack walk thread\" error and return\n7. Check if stack walk thread exists at g_hStackWalkThread\n8. If null, log \"No stack walk thread\" error and continue to initialization\n9. Log informational messages about ImageHelp stack crawl initialization\n10. If hThreadHandle parameter is null, call GetCurrentThread() to auto-detect\n11. Duplicate current process thread handle into g_hDuplicatedVictimThread with flags:\n    - dwDesiredAccess=0 (DUPLICATE_SAME_ACCESS - keep original permissions)\n    - bInheritHandle=0 (don't inherit the handle in child processes)\n    - dwOptions=2 (DUPLICATE_SAME_ACCESS flag)\n12. Signal the stack walk complete event via SetEvent(g_hStackWalkCompleteEvent)\n13. Query current thread priority using GetThreadPriority(g_hDuplicatedVictimThread)\n14. If priority is 0x7fffffff (THREAD_PRIORITY_ERROR_RETURN), reset to 0\n15. Lower thread priority to -15 (THREAD_PRIORITY_HIGHEST - relative adjustment)\n16. Wait indefinitely for stack walk completion on event g_hStackWalkWaitEvent\n17. Restore original thread priority from saved value\n18. Close the duplicated thread handle via CloseHandle\n\nParameters:\nhThreadHandle: HANDLE\n    Thread handle to use for stack walking. If NULL/zero, function auto-detects\n    current thread via GetCurrentThread(). This is the victim thread whose stack\n    will be walked and dumped for exception analysis.\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns early without continuing if stack dump disabled, ImageHelp not loaded, or critical event/thread handles missing\n- Handles invalid priority (0x7fffffff) by resetting to 0 before thread priority adjustments\n- Uses global state variables for synchronization and handle management\n- Always restores original thread priority even if stack walk times out\n- Thread priority temporarily lowered to THREAD_PRIORITY_HIGHEST (-15) to ensure stack walk completes\n- Uses DUPLICATE_SAME_ACCESS flag to maintain exact handle access rights",
      "tags": ["CALLEE_10", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_2", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
