      "instructions": ["0x10380|PUSH|EBP", "0x10381|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x10383|AND|ESP, 0xfffffff8", "0x10386|SUB|ESP, 0x2d0", "0x1038C|MOV|EAX, [0x6ff9afd4]", "0x10391|PUSH|EBX", "0x10392|PUSH|EBP", "0x10393|PUSH|ESI", "0x10394|PUSH|EDI", "0x10395|PUSH|-0x1", "0x10397|PUSH|EAX", "0x10398|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff7500c]", "0x1039E|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x103A0|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [0x6ff7506c]", "0x103A6|JNZ|0x6ff60498"],
      "comment": "ProcessDebugThreadStack - Thread context capture and stack analysis coordinator\n\nThis function implements the main event loop for a debug helper thread that\nsuspends target threads, captures their execution context, and processes their\ncall stacks. It synchronizes with a producer thread using Windows events to\ncoordinate victim thread selection and completion notification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize by calling WaitForSingleObject on g_hDebugHelperEvent1 with infinite timeout\n2. Enter main event loop waiting for victim thread signals\n3. On wait failure (non-zero result), cleanup all event handles and return 0\n4. On wait success, compare victim thread handle with g_hMainThreadSentinel\n5. If victim thread equals sentinel: break to error termination path for process shutdown\n6. Attempt SuspendThread on victim thread handle\n7. On suspend failure (return 0xFFFFFFFF): log error via network, skip to cleanup\n8. On suspend success: initialize CONTEXT structure (704 bytes) by zeroing 0xB3 DWORD fields\n9. Set ContextFlags = 0x10007 (CONTEXT_ALL) to enable capture of all CPU register types\n10. Call GetThreadContext to capture suspended thread's CPU state (registers, ESP, EIP)\n11. On context capture failure (return 0): log error via network, skip stack walk\n12. On context capture success (non-zero): call DumpCallStackAndSymbols to analyze call stack\n13. Resume victim thread with ResumeThread to wake up suspended thread\n14. Close victim thread handle with CloseHandle and set g_hVictimThreadHandle = NULL\n15. Signal g_hDebugHelperEvent2 with SetEvent to notify producer thread of completion\n16. Loop back to step 2 to wait for next victim thread event signal\n17. On main thread sentinel match: call GetReturnAddress, WSACleanup for cleanup\n18. Log error code 0x11B via LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown with shutdown reason 6\n19. Call ShutdownResourcesAndExit to perform final cleanup\n20. Exit process with _exit(-1) (does not return)\n\nParameters:\n  g_hDebugHelperEvent1: HANDLE signaled by producer thread when victim thread is ready (0x6ffa6e5c)\n  g_hVictimThreadHandle: HANDLE to target thread for suspension and context capture (0x6ffa6e64)\n  g_hMainThreadSentinel: HANDLE sentinel marker to signal termination condition (0x6ffa6e58)\n  g_hDebugHelperEvent2: HANDLE signaled when processing complete to notify producer (0x6ffa6e60)\n\nReturns:\n  DWORD: Returns 0 if WaitForSingleObject fails on normal cleanup exit path\n  Does not return normally - terminates process with _exit(-1) on fatal error paths\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic value 0xFFFFFFFF: SuspendThread error code indicates suspend count overflow\n  - Magic value 0xB3: Count of DWORD fields (179 DWORDs × 4 bytes = 716 bytes) for CONTEXT zero-fill\n  - Magic value 0x10007: CONTEXT_ALL flag captures general registers, control, segment, debug registers\n  - Magic value 0x11B: Error code 283 passed to LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown\n  - Magic value -1 (0xFFFFFFFF): INFINITE timeout for WaitForSingleObject calls\n  - Stack allocation: 0x2D0 bytes (704 bytes) for CONTEXT structure with 8-byte ESP alignment\n\nThread Synchronization:\n  Producer thread: sets g_hVictimThreadHandle, signals g_hDebugHelperEvent1, waits for g_hDebugHelperEvent2\n  Consumer thread: waits for g_hDebugHelperEvent1, processes victim thread, signals g_hDebugHelperEvent2\n  Critical: victim thread remains suspended throughout entire context capture and stack analysis\n  Prevents stack modification and corruption from concurrent thread execution\nlpStartAddress parameter of CreateThread\n",
      "tags": ["API_NETWORK", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "CALLEE_14", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
