      "comment": "Initializes and performs a stack walk operation to capture call stack frames.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment global reference counter g_dwStackWalkRefCount atomically\n2. If counter overflow detected (re-entrancy), return 0 immediately\n3. Initialize timing structures for performance profiling\n4. Get current process handle via GetCurrentProcess\n5. Call FUN_6ff60120 to initialize symbol handler context\n6. If initialization fails, decrement reference counter and return 0\n7. Zero-initialize STACKFRAME64 structure (164 bytes at ESP+0xa0)\n8. Copy initial register values from pThreadContext (EIP, EBP, ESP)\n9. Set machine type to IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_I386 (0x14c)\n10. Loop through up to 16 stack frames:\n    a. Call StackWalk64 via g_pfnStackWalk64 function pointer\n    b. If StackWalk64 fails, accumulate timing and exit loop\n    c. Validate frame using ValidateStackFrameWithRetry\n    d. Retrieve symbol info via g_pfnSymGetSymFromAddr\n    e. If symbol found, retrieve source line via g_pfnSymGetLineFromAddr\n    f. Format frame output using LogAppendFormat\n11. Call DecrementReferenceCountAndCleanup for resource cleanup\n12. Calculate total cycles from all timing accumulators\n13. Compute average cycles per frame using 64-bit division\n14. Log summary with frame count and cycle breakdown\n15. Decrement g_dwStackWalkRefCount and return 1 for success\n\nParameters:\n    pContext (BufferContext*): Output context buffer for stack walk results\n    hProcess (HANDLE): Process handle for symbol resolution\n    pThreadContext (CONTEXT*): Thread context with initial register values\n                               EIP at +0xB8, EBP at +0xB4, ESP at +0xC4\n\nReturns:\n    int: 1 on successful stack walk completion\n         0 on failure (re-entrancy, init failure, or counter overflow)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    Re-entrancy protection via atomic counter check\n    First iteration limited to 3 frames, subsequent up to 16\n    Symbol lookup failure uses \"unknown\" placeholder\n    Line info optional if unavailable\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x14c - IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_I386 (x86 machine type)\n    0x29  - STACKFRAME64 DWORD count (164 bytes)\n    0x10  - Maximum stack frames (16)\n    0x3   - Initial frame limit on first pass\n    0x18  - IMAGEHLP_LINE64 structure size offset\n    0x100 - Symbol max name length (256 bytes)\n    0x23c - IMAGEHLP_SYMBOL64 extended size (572 bytes)\n\nStructure Layout (pThreadContext input):\n    Offset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n    0xB4    4     Ebp         DWORD   Frame base pointer\n    0xB8    4     Eip         DWORD   Instruction pointer\n    0xC4    4     Esp         DWORD   Stack pointer\n\nError Handling:\n    Counter overflow returns 0 without logging\n    Init failure decrements counter before return\n    StackWalk64 failure breaks loop but generates summary\n    SymGetLineFromAddr failure calls GetLastError",
