      "comment": "Initializes an MD5 hash context structure with standard initial values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear message length counters (offsets 0x0, 0x4)\n2. Initialize MD5 state variables A, B, C, D with RFC 1321 magic constants\n   - Offset 0x8: A = 0x67452301 (little-endian representation)\n   - Offset 0xC: B = 0xEFCDAB89\n   - Offset 0x10: C = 0x98BADCFE\n   - Offset 0x14: D = 0x10325476\n3. Initialize buffer counter at offset 0x18 = 0xC3D2E1F0\n4. Return void\n\nParameters:\npMD5Context: Pointer to 28-byte MD5 context structure\n  - Offset 0x0-0x3: Message length low (32-bit)\n  - Offset 0x4-0x7: Message length high (32-bit)\n  - Offset 0x8-0xB: State variable A (uint)\n  - Offset 0xC-0xF: State variable B (uint)\n  - Offset 0x10-0x13: State variable C (uint)\n  - Offset 0x14-0x17: State variable D (uint)\n  - Offset 0x18-0x1B: Buffer/temporary state (uint)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Initializes context in-place via pMD5Context pointer.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic constants are standard MD5 initial values from RFC 1321\n- Function assumes pMD5Context is writable and points to at least 28 bytes\n- All values written are little-endian 32-bit DWORDs",
