      "comment": "Performs the SHA-1 compression function on a 64-byte message block.\n\nThis is the core transform of the SHA-1 hash algorithm (FIPS PUB 180-1).\nIt processes a single 512-bit (64-byte) block and updates the hash state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Message expansion: Convert 16 big-endian 32-bit words from input to \n   80-word schedule W[0..79] using XOR and ROL(1) expansion\n2. Initialize working variables A,B,C,D,E from current hash state H[0..4]\n3. Rounds 0-19: Ch(B,C,D) = (B AND C) OR (NOT B AND D), K = 0x5A827999\n4. Rounds 20-39: Parity(B,C,D) = B XOR C XOR D, K = 0x6ED9EBA1  \n5. Rounds 40-59: Maj(B,C,D) = (B AND C) OR (B AND D) OR (C AND D), K = 0x8F1BBCDC\n6. Rounds 60-79: Parity(B,C,D) = B XOR C XOR D, K = 0xCA62C1D6\n7. Each round: T = ROL(A,5) + f(B,C,D) + E + K + W[t]\n              E=D, D=C, C=ROL(B,30), B=A, A=T\n8. Final: H[i] = H[i] + working[i] for i=0..4\n\nParameters:\n  pCtx - Pointer to SHA1_CTX_Context containing hash state H[0..4]\n  in_EAX (IMPLICIT) - Pointer to 64-byte input message block\n\nReturns:\n  None. Updates pCtx->H[0..4] with new intermediate hash values.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x5A827999 - Round constant K0, sqrt(2) * 2^30\n  0x6ED9EBA1 - Round constant K1, sqrt(3) * 2^30\n  0x8F1BBCDC - Round constant K2, sqrt(5) * 2^30\n  0xCA62C1D6 - Round constant K3, sqrt(10) * 2^30\n\nStructure Layout (SHA1_CTX_Context):\n  Offset  Size  Field   Type      Description\n  0x00    4     H[0]    uint      Hash word A (init: 0x67452301)\n  0x04    4     H[1]    uint      Hash word B (init: 0xEFCDAB89)\n  0x08    4     H[2]    uint      Hash word C (init: 0x98BADCFE)\n  0x0C    4     H[3]    uint      Hash word D (init: 0x10325476)\n  0x10    4     H[4]    uint      Hash word E (init: 0xC3D2E1F0)\n\nStack Frame Layout:\n  ESP+0x14 to ESP+0x150: W[0..79] message schedule (320 bytes)\n  ESP+0x10: Working variable temporary storage",
