      "comment": "Appends input data to SHA1 context and processes complete 64-byte blocks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Update 64-bit message bit count: bitCount += dwInputLength * 8\n2. Calculate current buffer offset: dwBufferOffset = (bitCountLo >> 3) & 0x3F\n3. If partial buffer exists (dwBufferOffset != 0):\n   a. Calculate bytes to fill: dwBytesToFill = 64 - dwBufferOffset\n   b. Copy input bytes to buffer at offset +0x1C\n   c. If buffer full (64 bytes), call SHA1Update() to process block\n   d. Advance input pointer, reduce remaining length\n4. Process complete 64-byte blocks:\n   a. Calculate number of full blocks: dwBlockCount = dwInputLength >> 6\n   b. Loop: call SHA1Update() for each block, advance by 64 bytes\n5. Copy remaining bytes to buffer at offset +0x1C\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT this (ECX): SHA1_CTX_Context* pContext - SHA1 hash context\n  - [+0x00]: dwBitCountLo - Lower 32 bits of message length in bits\n  - [+0x04]: dwBitCountHi - Upper 32 bits of message length in bits  \n  - [+0x08]: state[5] - Five 32-bit digest state words (H0-H4)\n  - [+0x1C]: buffer[64] - 64-byte message block buffer\n- pbInputData: byte* - Pointer to input data bytes to hash\n- dwInputLength: uint - Number of input bytes to process\n\nReturns:\n- void - Context updated in-place with new data\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3F (63): Mask for modulo-64 (block size alignment)\n- 0x40 (64): SHA1 block size in bytes\n- 0x1C (28): Offset to 64-byte message buffer in context\n- 0x08 (8): Offset to state array in context\n- 6: Right shift for dividing by 64 (block count calculation)\n- 3: Right shift for dividing by 8 (bit to byte conversion)\n\nCalled By:\n- SHA1_Final: Appends padding and bit count before finalization\n\nCalls:\n- SHA1Update (0x6ff60d90): Processes a single 64-byte block",
