      "comment": "Finalizes SHA1 digest computation by padding message and extracting the 160-bit hash.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load 64-bit message bit count from context offsets +0x00 (low) and +0x04 (high)\n2. Convert bit count to big-endian 8-byte buffer using SHRD/SHR sequence\n3. Calculate padding length: ((0xFFFFFFFF - (bitCount >> 3) - 8) & 0x3F) + 1\n4. Append padding block (0x80 followed by zeros) via SHA1InputUpdate\n5. Append 8-byte big-endian bit count via SHA1InputUpdate\n6. Extract 5 state DWORDs from context offset +0x08 (20 bytes total)\n7. Convert each DWORD to big-endian and write to output buffer\n8. Final hash is 20 bytes in pbDigestOutput\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT this (ECX): SHA1_CTX_Context* - SHA1 context with state and bit count\n  - [+0x00]: dwBitCountLo - Message length in bits (lower 32 bits)\n  - [+0x04]: dwBitCountHi - Message length in bits (upper 32 bits)\n  - [+0x08]: state[5] - Five 32-bit digest state words (H0-H4)\n- pbDigestOutput: byte* - Pointer to 20-byte buffer for final hash output\n\nReturns:\n- void - Hash written directly to pbDigestOutput buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6FF7FFB0: g_SHA1PaddingBlock - Standard SHA1 padding (0x80 + zeros)\n- 0x3F: Mask for modulo-64 calculation (block size alignment)\n- 0xFFFFFFF7: (-9) used in padding length calculation\n- 5: Number of 32-bit digest words (160 bits / 32 = 5)\n- 8: Size of appended bit count in bytes\n\nImplementation Notes:\n- Uses __thiscall convention with context in ECX\n- SHRD instruction pairs extract bytes from 64-bit value efficiently\n- Big-endian output matches FIPS 180-1 SHA1 specification\n- Loop unrolling avoided - processes one DWORD per iteration",
