      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a DataArray structure from the resource pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total size: 0x120 (header) + (nElementSize * nCapacity) bytes\n2. Allocate memory from resource pool (NULL pool = default)\n3. If allocation fails, log error and return NULL\n4. Zero-initialize the 0x120 byte header using REP STOSD\n5. Copy name string to header (max 0x100 chars)\n6. Initialize structure fields:\n   - Offset 0x100: nElementSize (element stride)\n   - Offset 0x104: nCapacity (max elements)\n   - Offset 0x108: Current count = 0\n   - Offset 0x11c: pData pointer (points to header + 0x120)\n7. Return pointer to initialized DataArray\n\nParameters:\n  lpszName (ECX) - Name identifier for the data array (max 256 chars)\n  nElementSize (EDX) - Size in bytes of each array element\n  nCapacity (Stack+4) - Maximum number of elements the array can hold\n\nReturns:\n  char* - Pointer to allocated DataArray structure, or NULL on failure\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x000   256   szName        Null-terminated array name\n  0x100   4     nElementSize  Bytes per element\n  0x104   4     nCapacity     Maximum element count\n  0x108   4     nCount        Current element count (initialized to 0)\n  0x11c   4     pData         Pointer to element data (at offset 0x120)\n  0x120   var   data[]        Array element storage\n\nError Handling:\n  Returns NULL and logs error (level 2) at DataArrays.cpp:52 if allocation fails\n\nSource: ..\\\\Source\\\\Fog\\\\Src\\\\DataArrays.cpp line 52 (0x34)",
