      "instructions": ["0x11480|PUSH|ESI", "0x11481|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x11483|CMP|EDX, -0x1", "0x11486|PUSH|EDI", "0x11487|JZ|0x6ff614ed", "0x11489|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x1148B|SAR|ESI, 0x10", "0x1148E|TEST|SI, SI", "0x11491|JL|0x6ff614f0", "0x11493|MOVSX|EDI, SI", "0x11496|CMP|EDI, dword ptr [ECX + 0x100]", "0x1149C|JGE|0x6ff614f0", "0x1149E|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ECX + 0x108]", "0x114A4|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x114A6|JNZ|0x6ff614c7"],
      "comment": "Retrieves a pointer to a socket queue item by packed index with optional mode validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if packedItemIndex equals -1 (null/uninitialized sentinel); return NULL if true\n2. Extract queue index from upper 16 bits of packedItemIndex via arithmetic right shift by 16\n3. Validate extracted index is non-negative; jump to error handler if negative\n4. Validate index is less than max queue size (read from pSocketQueue + 0x100); error if >= max\n5. Load active counter from pSocketQueue + 0x108; must be non-zero or trigger error handler\n6. Load stride per item from pSocketQueue + 0x104 and multiply by index to get byte offset\n7. Load base pointer to queue items from pSocketQueue + 0x11c\n8. Load item mode (16-bit word) at base + byte offset\n9. Calculate final item address as base + byte offset\n10. Check if item mode is non-zero (0=inactive, non-zero=active); return NULL if zero\n11. Extract mode filter from lower 16 bits of packedItemIndex\n12. If mode filter is 0x0000, accept any active item (mode != 0) and return pointer\n13. If mode filter is non-zero, validate item mode matches filter exactly; return pointer only if match\n14. Return NULL if any validation fails or mode does not match filter\n\nParameters:\n- pSocketQueue (ECX register): Pointer to socket queue structure containing:\n  - Offset 0x100: dwMaxQueueSize - maximum number of items allowed in queue (dword)\n  - Offset 0x104: dwStridePerItem - byte stride between consecutive items in array (dword)\n  - Offset 0x108: dwActiveCounter - non-zero indicates queue is initialized and active (dword)\n  - Offset 0x11c: pQueueItemsBase - pointer to first item in queue array (dword *)\n- packedItemIndex (EDX register): Packed 32-bit index and filter value:\n  - Upper 16 bits: queue index (0-based position, extracted via SAR 0x10)\n  - Lower 16 bits: mode filter (0=accept any active mode, non-zero=match exact mode)\n  - Special value -1 (0xFFFFFFFF): indicates null/uninitialized request\n\nReturns:\n- short *: Pointer to socket queue item if valid and matches mode filter\n- NULL (0): if packedItemIndex=-1, index out of bounds, queue inactive, item inactive, or mode mismatch\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- packedItemIndex = -1 is sentinel value for null request, returns NULL immediately without validation\n- Negative index (SAR EDX,0x10 produces negative) triggers error handler that calls GetReturnAddress(), LogErrorAndShutdown(), and _exit()\n- Index >= dwMaxQueueSize triggers same error shutdown sequence\n- dwActiveCounter == 0 (inactive queue) triggers error with code 0xde via CleanupAndAbort() then _exit()\n- itemMode == 0 indicates inactive item, silently returns NULL (not an error condition)\n- Mode filter == 0 acts as wildcard matching any non-zero mode; enables querying items regardless of mode\n- Mode filter != 0 acts as exact match filter; only items with matching mode are returned\n\nSocket Queue Item Structure (inferred from offset patterns):\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type        Description\n+0x00   2     wItemMode       word        Item mode/state flag (0=inactive)\n+...    ...   (other fields)  (varies)    Additional item structure members",
