      "comment": "SHA1_Update - Process data blocks through SHA-1 hash compression algorithm\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SHA-1 state variables to standard initialization vectors (A=0x67452301,\n   B=0xefcdab89, C=0x98badcfe, D=0x10325476, E=0xc3d2e1f0)\n2. If input data size is zero, skip processing and return initial state\n3. For each 64-byte data block:\n   a. Calculate chunk size (minimum of remaining bytes and 64)\n   b. Copy chunk data into local 64-byte blockBuffer using word-aligned copying (MOVSD.REP)\n   c. Pad remaining buffer with zeros if chunk is less than 64 bytes\n   d. Call ProcessSHA1Block to execute SHA-1 compression rounds on current block\n   e. Advance to next data block by adding dataStride to pDataBuffer\n   f. Increment processedBytes by 0x40 (64 bytes)\n   g. Loop if more data remains (processedBytes < dataSize)\n4. Store final hash state (A, B, C, D, E) back to pHashState output buffer at offsets 0x0, 0x4,\n   0x8, 0xc, 0x10\n\nParameters:\npHashState: uint* - Pointer to SHA-1 state array [5 DWORDs] - on entry may contain initial or\n   partial hash, on return contains updated hash values\npDataBuffer: uint* - Pointer to input data buffer containing message bytes to hash\ndwDataSize: uint - Total bytes to process (may span multiple 64-byte blocks)\ndwDataStride: uint - Byte stride/offset between data chunks in input buffer (e.g., stride=64 for\n   contiguous blocks)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Hash state updated in-place at pHashState (5 DWORDs)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty input (dwDataSize=0): Outputs initial SHA-1 IV without processing any blocks\n- Partial blocks: Padded with zeros to 64 bytes before processing through compression rounds\n- Multiple blocks: Loop processes entire input in 64-byte chunks with stride offset\n- Chunk size calculation: min(remaining_bytes, 64) = (dwDataSize - dwProcessedBytes) clamped to 0x40\n- Final storage: Hash values stored at pHashState[0..4] corresponding to state variables A, B, C, D, E\n\nSSA Phantom Variables:\nuVar1: Loop counter for zero-padding (reuse of dwLoopCounter for second loop iteration)\npuVar2 (undefined4*): Padding pointer to blockBuffer offset (type cast of pdwPadPtr)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOutput Hash State Array at pHashState (5 DWORD elements):\nOffset | Size | Field Name   | Type | Description\n0x00   | 0x04 | hashStateA   | uint | SHA-1 state variable A (initialized 0x67452301)\n0x04   | 0x04 | hashStateB   | uint | SHA-1 state variable B (initialized 0xefcdab89)\n0x08   | 0x04 | hashStateC   | uint | SHA-1 state variable C (initialized 0x98badcfe)\n0x0c   | 0x04 | hashStateD   | uint | SHA-1 state variable D (initialized 0x10325476)\n0x10   | 0x04 | hashStateE   | uint | SHA-1 state variable E (initialized 0xc3d2e1f0)",
