      "instructions": ["0x12200|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0x12203|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x12205|MOV|dword ptr [ESP], EAX", "0x12208|PUSH|EBX", "0x12209|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x8], EAX", "0x1220D|PUSH|ESI", "0x1220E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0x12212|PUSH|EDI", "0x12213|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EAX", "0x12217|MOV|EAX, 0x0", "0x1221C|CPUID|", "0x1221E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EBX", "0x12222|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EDX", "0x12226|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], ECX", "0x1222A|MOV|EDI, 0x6ff78298"],
      "comment": "Identifies the CPU vendor by executing CPUID instruction with EAX=0 and comparing the\nreturned 12-byte vendor ID string against known vendor signatures (Intel, AMD, Cyrix).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 16 bytes on stack and save EBX, ESI, EDI registers\n2. Execute CPUID(0) to get vendor ID string in EBX:EDX:ECX\n3. Store vendor ID bytes on stack: EBX (chars 0-3), EDX (chars 4-7), ECX (chars 8-11)\n4. Compare vendor string against \"GenuineIntel\" (13 bytes including null)\n5. If match, return 1 indicating Intel processor\n6. Compare vendor string against \"AuthenticAMD\" (13 bytes including null)\n7. If match, return 2 indicating AMD processor\n8. Compare vendor string against \"CyrixInstead\" (13 bytes including null)\n9. If match, return 3 indicating Cyrix processor\n10. If no match, return 0 indicating unknown vendor\n\nParameters:\nNone - This function takes no parameters.\n\nReturns:\nbyte - CPU vendor identifier code:\n  1 = Intel processor (GenuineIntel vendor string)\n  2 = AMD processor (AuthenticAMD vendor string)\n  3 = Cyrix processor (CyrixInstead vendor string)\n  0 = Unknown vendor (no match found)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- CPUID(0) returns 12-byte vendor string in EBX:EDX:ECX register order\n- Vendor strings are compared with 13 bytes to include null terminator\n- Unknown vendors return 0 to indicate unrecognized CPU type\n- Stack frame: [ESP] reserved, [ESP+0xC-0x17] vendor buffer (12 bytes)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLEE_0", "CALLER_3", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "PROP_LEAF", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
