      "instructions": ["0x12330|PUSH|ECX", "0x12331|PUSH|EBX", "0x12332|PUSH|ESI", "0x12333|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x12335|PUSH|EDI", "0x12336|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], EBX", "0x1233A|CALL|0x6ff61c70", "0x1233F|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x12341|MOV|ESI, EDI", "0x12343|SHR|ESI, 0x8", "0x12346|AND|ESI, 0xf", "0x12349|CALL|0x6ff62200", "0x1234E|CMP|EAX, 0x1", "0x12351|JNZ|0x6ff6237f", "0x12353|CMP|ESI, 0x7"],
      "comment": "Retrieves CPU vendor string via CPUID instruction for processor identification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetCpuVersionInfo() to retrieve CPU signature with model/family/stepping bits\n2. Extract model field from signature bits 4-7: (signature >> 8) & 0xF\n3. Call GetCpuVendorId() to check CPUID instruction support (returns 1 if supported)\n4. Validate processor: Check if model >= 7 (always valid) OR (model == 6 AND stepping >= 0x80)\n5. If validation fails, return 0 (processor too old or CPUID unsupported)\n6. If validation passes, execute CPUID(1) to get CPU Version/Brand/Feature info\n7. Store vendor string from CPUID EBX register at stack offset +0xC\n8. Load 32-bit vendor string result from stack and return as 64-bit value (EDX:EAX)\n\nParameters:\nNone (no function parameters)\n\nReturns:\n- Success: 64-bit value containing vendor string from CPUID EBX register\n          Example: 0x756e6547 = uneG (part of GenuineIntel)\n- Failure: 0 (processor does not support CPUID function 1 or model validation failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Model field must be >= 6 to support CPUID function 1 (Intel requirement)\n- For model 6 processors, stepping (bits 4-7) must be >= 0x80\n- CPUID EBX contains first 4 bytes of 12-byte vendor string\n- Some older Pentium/386 processors lack CPUID instruction entirely\n\nCPU Signature Structure (from GetCpuVersionInfo):\nOffset  Size  Field        Type      Description\n0       8     dwCpuSig     ulonglong Full CPU signature (EDX:EAX from CPUID 0)\n- bits 0-3: stepping ID (revision level)\n- bits 4-7: model ID (processor variant)\n- bits 8-11: family ID (processor family)\n- bits 12-31: extended model/family/reserved\n\nStack Frame Layout:\nOffset   Size  Variable     Purpose\n[ESP+0]  4     (saved ECX)  Caller saved\n[ESP+4]  4     (saved EBX)  Preserved register\n[ESP+8]  4     (saved ESI)  dwModelField storage\n[ESP+C]  4     dwResult     Vendor string result (local_4 - phantom)\n\nPhantom Variables:\n- local_4 at Stack[-0x4]: uint - optimized away, used only at [ESP+0xC] in assembly\n  (Stores CPUID EBX result before return)\n\nImplicit Register Usage:\n- extraout_var: Upper 24 bits after GetCpuVendorId() byte return\n- extraout_EDX: EDX value when returning 0 (failure path)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xF: Mask for 4-bit model field extraction\n- 0x7: Model threshold for unconditional CPUID support\n- 0x6: Model value requiring stepping check\n- 0x80: Minimum stepping for model 6 processors\n- 0xF0: Mask for stepping bits (bits 4-7)\n- 0x1: CPUID leaf for version/brand/feature information\n\nCross-References:\n- Called by: PrintCpuVendorAndVersion (0x6ff624c9)\n- Calls: GetCpuVersionInfo, GetCpuVendorId, cpuid_Version_info",
      "tags": ["CALLER_1", "CALLEE_2", "PARAM_0"]
