      "comment": "Formats a 64-bit unsigned integer into a string with comma separators.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clamp dwMaxLength to maximum of 32 characters\n2. If input number is zero, jump directly to output phase\n3. Loop: divide number by 10 using __alldvrm, convert remainder to ASCII digit\n4. Every 3 digits, insert a comma character (0x2C)\n5. Build reversed string in stack buffer (local_20)\n6. If buffer overflow would occur, fill output with asterisks (0x2A)\n7. Copy reversed string to output buffer in correct order\n8. Null-terminate the output string\n\nParameters:\n  szOutput (ECX) - Destination buffer for formatted string\n  dwMaxLength (EDX) - Maximum buffer length (clamped to 32)\n  dwNumberLow (Stack+0x4) - Low 32 bits of 64-bit number\n  dwNumberHigh (Stack+0x8) - High 32 bits of 64-bit number\n\nReturns:\n  char* - Pointer to szOutput buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If number is 0, returns empty string or \"0\"\n  - If formatted result exceeds buffer, fills with asterisks\n  - Maximum 32 characters regardless of dwMaxLength\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 (32) - Maximum buffer length\n  0x0A (10) - Divisor for digit extraction\n  0x30 ('0') - ASCII offset for digit conversion\n  0x2C (',') - Comma separator character\n  0x2A ('*') - Overflow indicator character\n  0x03 - Digit grouping (thousands separator interval)",
