      "comment": "Computes a case-insensitive CRC16 checksum of a null-terminated string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize CRC accumulator to 0xFFFF (standard CRC16 seed value)\n2. Load first character from input string and convert to uppercase via _toupper()\n3. Loop until null terminator encountered:\n   a. XOR uppercase character with low byte of current CRC value\n   b. Mask result to 8 bits to form lookup table index (0-255)\n   c. Right-shift current CRC value by 2 bits\n   d. XOR shifted CRC with 16-bit value from g_awCrc16LookupTable[index]\n   e. Advance string pointer and load next character\n   f. Convert next character to uppercase via _toupper()\n4. Return final 16-bit CRC value\n\nParameters:\nszString (char*) - Pointer to null-terminated ASCII string to checksum\n\nReturns:\nushort - 16-bit CRC16 checksum value (0x0000-0xFFFF)\n         Returns 0xFFFF for empty string (null terminator at start)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Case-insensitive: all characters converted to uppercase before processing\n- Uses non-standard CRC16 variant with 2-bit right shift per iteration\n- Empty strings return initial seed value 0xFFFF unchanged\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFFFF - Standard CRC16 initial seed value\n0xFF   - 8-bit mask for table index extraction\n0x2    - Right shift amount per CRC iteration\n\nStructure Layout:\ng_awCrc16LookupTable (0x6ff7fd78):\nOffset  Size  Type        Description\n0x000   512   ushort[256] Pre-computed CRC16 polynomial values",
