      "comment": "Converts a null-terminated string to title case in-place.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input string pointer (exit early if null)\n2. Scan string to locate null terminator and calculate string length\n3. Check that calculated length is positive (non-empty string)\n4. Initialize capitalize flag to true (capitalize first character)\n5. Iterate through each character from index 0 to length-1:\n   a. Check if current character index exceeds 1024 (0x400) limit\n   b. If limit exceeded, log error, shutdown cleanup, and exit program\n   c. Load current character from string at current index\n   d. If character is space (0x20), set capitalize flag to true and continue\n   e. If not space and capitalize flag is set:\n      - Call _toupper() to convert character to uppercase\n      - Clear capitalize flag for next characters\n   f. If not space and capitalize flag not set:\n      - Call _tolower() to convert character to lowercase\n   g. Write transformed character back to input string at current index\n   h. Increment character index and loop until all characters processed\n6. Return with string transformed in-place\n\nParameters:\npInputString: Pointer to null-terminated ASCII string to transform (modified in-place)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (modifies input string in-place, no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null input pointer: Function returns immediately without processing\n- Empty string: Length check prevents processing zero-length strings\n- Single character: Capitalized if string is non-empty\n- Space character: Acts as word boundary, triggers capitalization of next non-space character\n- Maximum length: Strings exceeding 1024 characters trigger error handling and program exit\n- Character encoding: Uses CRT _toupper() and _tolower() for locale-aware case conversion\n- In-place modification: Input string is modified directly, original content lost\n\nCalling Convention:\n__stdcall - Stack parameters with callee cleanup (RET 0x4)",
