      "comment": "Atomically increments the reference count of an object.\n\nThis function implements thread-safe reference counting by adding 8 to the\nobject pointer to locate the embedded reference counter field, then calling\nthe Win32 InterlockedIncrement API to perform an atomic increment operation.\nThe reference count is used by resource management systems to track object\nownership and determine when to deallocate resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate reference counter address: pObject + 8\n2. Call InterlockedIncrement to atomically increment the counter\n3. Return (void function, no return value)\n\nParameters:\npObject (void *): Pointer to the object whose reference count should be incremented.\n  The object must have a 32-bit reference counter field at offset +8 bytes.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. The function performs the atomic increment as a side effect.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Offset +8: The reference counter is located 8 bytes from the object base.\n  This is typical for objects with a 2-DWORD header (object type/flags at +0,\n  size/reserved at +4, reference count at +8).\n- Thread Safety: InterlockedIncrement provides atomic semantics across multiple threads.\n- No validation: Function assumes pObject is valid; caller must ensure validity.\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type              Description\n0       4     dwObjectType      DWORD             Object type identifier or flags\n4       4     dwObjectSize      DWORD             Object size in bytes\n8       4     dwRefCount        DWORD             Reference count (incremented atomically)\n12+     var   dwObjectData      DWORD[]           Object-specific data fields",
      "tags": ["CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "CALLEE_1", "PARAM_0", "PROP_SMALL"]
