      "comment": "Removes a hash entry from its chain and deallocates when reference count reaches zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract hash key from entry at [pnHashKey]\n2. Calculate bucket index via hash % bucketCount (from [EDI+0x10])\n3. Get bucket head pointer from hash table array at [EDI+0x40]\n4. Traverse linked list comparing each entry's key with target key\n5. If entry not found, return 0 (failure)\n6. If found, decrement reference count at [entry+0x4]\n7. If reference count > 0, keep entry linked and return 1\n8. If reference count <= 0, unlink entry from chain:\n   - If not head: set prev->next to entry->next\n   - If head: update bucket head to entry->next\n9. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to free the entry\n10. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pnHashKey (EAX) - Pointer to hash key value to look up\n  IMPLICIT pHashTable (EDI) - Pointer to hash table structure:\n    - [+0x10]: dwBucketCount - Number of buckets for modulo\n    - [+0x40]: ppBuckets - Array of bucket head pointers\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Entry found and processed (decremented or removed)\n  0 - Entry not found in chain\n\nHash Entry Structure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field       Description\n  0x00    4     dwHashKey   Hash key value for comparison\n  0x04    4     nRefCount   Reference count (entry freed when <= 0)\n  0x08    4     pNext       Pointer to next entry in chain",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "LIB_FOG_NET", "CALLER_1", "CALLEE_1", "PARAM_1", "SRC_QServer.cpp"]
