      "comment": "Enqueues a server message received from the message callback into the queue server.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize output parameters (nMsgCount, nDataEnd, nDataOffset, nMsgHeader) to zero\n  2. Call message callback at pQueueServer+0xBC0 to retrieve message data\n  3. Validate return code (must be 1 or 2 for success, otherwise return 0)\n  4. Allocate message buffer (0x5C0 bytes) from free list at +0x878 or resource pool\n  5. Copy message data from callback buffer to allocated buffer using memcpy pattern\n  6. Set message size at buffer offset 0x5B4\n  7. Store GetTickCount() timestamp at buffer offset 0x5B8\n  8. Clear next pointer at buffer offset 0x5BC\n  9. Store message header at buffer offset 0x0\n  10. If queue slot index less than max count, link message to queue\n\nParameters:\n  pQueueServer - Pointer to QueueServer structure containing:\n    +0x854: CRITICAL_SECTION for thread synchronization\n    +0x870: Array of queue head pointers (per-slot)\n    +0x874: Array of queue tail pointers (per-slot)\n    +0x878: Free list head pointer for recycled buffers\n    +0x87C: Maximum queue slot count\n    +0xBC0: Message receive callback function pointer\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Message successfully enqueued to queue\n  0 - Message callback returned invalid status (not 1 or 2)\n\nMessage Buffer Layout (0x5C0 bytes total):\n  Offset   Size   Field         Description\n  0x000    4      nMsgHeader    Message header/identifier from callback\n  0x004    0x5B0  abData        Message payload data copied from callback\n  0x5B4    4      nMsgSize      Size of message data in bytes\n  0x5B8    4      dwTimestamp   GetTickCount() value when enqueued\n  0x5BC    4      pNextMsg      Pointer to next message in linked list\n\nThread Safety:\n  Uses EnterCriticalSection/LeaveCriticalSection at offset +0x854\n  ValidateCriticalSection called before entering with line numbers 0x9FD, 0xA03, 0xA1F\n\nError Handling:\n  LogErrorWithContext called with level 2 if allocation fails\n  Source file: ..\\\\Source\\\\Fog\\\\Src\\\\QServer\\\\QServer.cpp\n\nQueue Structure:\n  Messages are linked in a singly-linked list per slot\n  Head pointer at [pQueueServer+0x870 + slot*4]\n  Tail pointer at [pQueueServer+0x874 + slot*4]\n  New messages appended to tail, linked via pNextMsg at +0x5BC",
