      "comment": "Checks and enforces connection rate limiting for incoming requests.\n\nMaintains a linked list of rate limit entries tracking connection IDs,\ntimestamps, and request counts. Returns 0 (blocked) if a connection\nexceeds the allowed request rate within a 15-second sliding window.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if rate limiting is enabled (nRateLimit > 0 at EDI+0x884)\n2. Get current tick count and cleanup expired entries\n3. Enter critical section protecting the rate entry list\n4. Search linked list for existing entry matching connection ID\n5. If found and within 15s window: increment count, check threshold\n6. If found but expired: reset timestamp and count to 1\n7. If not found: allocate new entry and append to list\n8. Return 1 (allowed) unless request count exceeds (limit*2)+3\n\nParameters:\n  pnConnectionId - Pointer to connection identifier (socket/IP)\n  IMPLICIT EDI - Server context structure pointer\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Connection request allowed\n  0 - Connection blocked (rate limit exceeded)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3A98 (15000) - Rate limit window in milliseconds\n  0x10 (16) - Size of rate limit entry structure\n  0x534 (1332) - Critical section validation code\n\nStructure Layout (Rate Limit Entry - 16 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type   Description\n  0x00    4     nConnectionId int    Connection identifier\n  0x04    4     dwTimestamp   DWORD  Last request tick count\n  0x08    4     nCount        int    Request count in window\n  0x0C    4     pNext         ptr    Next entry in linked list\n\nServer Context Offsets (EDI-relative):\n  +0x84C  pRateListHead   - Head of rate entry linked list\n  +0x850  pRateListTail   - Tail of rate entry linked list\n  +0x854  CriticalSection - Thread synchronization lock\n  +0x884  nRateLimit      - Max requests per window base value",
