      "instructions": ["0x13810|PUSH|ESI", "0x13811|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff75080]", "0x13817|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [0x6ffa6ed4]", "0x1381D|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x1381F|SUB|EAX, EDX", "0x13821|CMP|EAX, 0x7d0", "0x13826|JBE|0x6ff63845", "0x13828|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x1382C|PUSH|ECX", "0x1382D|PUSH|0x6ff77fe8", "0x13832|PUSH|0x6ff77954", "0x13837|CALL|0x6ff665a0", "0x1383C|ADD|ESP, 0xc", "0x1383F|MOV|dword ptr [0x6ffa6ed4], ESI", "0x13845|POP|ESI"],
      "comment": "Executes a throttled action on a timer-based interval with configurable delay.\n\nSummary:\nThis function implements a throttling mechanism that limits action execution to no more than once per 2000 milliseconds. It retrieves the current system tick count, compares it against a stored timestamp, and only executes the provided action if sufficient time has elapsed since the last execution. The timestamp is updated after successful action execution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current system tick count in milliseconds via GetTickCount() API call\n2. Load previously stored tick count from global timestamp cache (g_dwLastThrottleTimestamp)\n3. Calculate elapsed time since last execution: dwCurrentTickCount - cached timestamp\n4. Compare elapsed time against fixed 2000ms threshold\n5. If elapsed time <= 2000ms: Skip action execution (jump to throttle_exit)\n6. If elapsed time > 2000ms:\n   - Load caller-provided action parameter from stack (pActionParameter)\n   - Push three parameters to stack:\n     * pActionParameter (action context/data from caller)\n     * szHacklistFormatString pointer (format string for logging)\n     * szHackModuleTag pointer (module identifier for logging)\n   - Call InitializeNetworkConnection() to execute throttled action\n   - Restore stack after function call (callee cleanup)\n7. Update global timestamp cache with current tick count\n8. Exit and return to caller with stack frame cleanup\n\nParameters:\npActionParameter (void *): Caller-provided parameter passed to action handler; contains action-specific data or context for the network connection initialization.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No direct return value; modifies global state (g_dwLastThrottleTimestamp).\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Throttle threshold is fixed at 2000 milliseconds (0x7d0 hex). To change throttle interval, modify the CMP instruction threshold.\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention: caller pushes parameters, callee cleans stack (RET 0x4).\n- Global timestamp cache (g_dwLastThrottleTimestamp) is shared with ProcessConnectionTimeouts and RemoveHashTableEntry functions.\n- Function returns early via JBE at throttle_exit if throttle condition is not met, preventing unnecessary action execution.\n- Timestamp is only updated after successful action execution, not at function entry.\n- Magic values: 0x7d0 = 2000 (milliseconds), 0xc = 12 bytes (3 parameters × 4 bytes cleanup).",
      "tags": ["CALLER_1", "CALLEE_2", "PARAM_0"]
    },
