      "comment": "Removes an entry from two independent hash tables (primary and secondary).\nThis function performs thread-safe removal of an entry identified by its unique ID\nfrom both the primary ID-based hash table and a secondary IP-based hash table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate hash bucket index by masking entry ID with dwHashMask\n2. Acquire primary hash table critical section for thread safety\n3. Search primary hash chain for entry matching dwEntryId\n4. If not found, release lock and return immediately\n5. Acquire count critical section at context+0x854\n6. Decrement global entry count at context+0x880\n7. Unlink entry from primary hash chain (update head or previous node)\n8. Release primary hash table critical section\n9. Perform sanity check - verify entry ID still matches\n10. Calculate elapsed time for performance logging\n11. Extract IP address from entry (offset +0x18)\n12. Acquire secondary hash table critical section at context+0x28\n13. Search secondary hash chain using IP address as key\n14. Unlink entry from secondary hash chain (link offset +0x1c)\n15. Call RemoveHashEntryFromChain for final cleanup\n16. Release all critical sections\n\nParameters:\n  dwEntryId: uint - Unique 32-bit identifier for the entry to remove\n  IMPLICIT in_EAX: Context structure pointer containing hash table state\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Entry may be head of hash chain requiring direct head pointer update\n  - If entry not found in primary table, function returns early\n  - Sanity check failure triggers fatal error via ReportError(-1)\n  - Two hash tables use different chain link offsets (+0x4 vs +0x1c)\n\nStructure Layout (Context at in_EAX):\n  Offset | Size | Field                | Description\n  0x0c   | 4    | dwHashMask           | Bucket mask for index calculation\n  0x14   | 4    | pFirstHashTable      | Primary hash table (ID-based)\n  0x1c   | 4    | pCriticalSections    | Per-bucket critical sections\n  0x20   | 4    | pSecondHashTable     | Secondary hash table (IP-based)\n  0x28   | 24   | secondaryCritSec     | Critical section for secondary table\n  0x854  | 24   | countCritSec         | Critical section for entry count\n  0x880  | 4    | dwEntryCount         | Total entries in tables\n\nEntry Structure:\n  Offset | Size | Field    | Description\n  0x00   | 4    | dwId     | Entry unique identifier\n  0x04   | 4    | pNext    | Next entry in primary chain\n  0x18   | 4    | dwIpAddr | IP address (in_addr format)\n  0x1c   | 4    | pIpNext  | Next entry in secondary chain",
      "tags": ["API_NETWORK", "CALLEE_11", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "STRUCT_Skill", "CALLER_4", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
