      "instructions": ["0x13A50|PUSH|ECX", "0x13A51|PUSH|ESI", "0x13A52|PUSH|EDI", "0x13A53|LEA|EDI, [EBX + 0x2c]", "0x13A56|MOV|EDX, 0x385", "0x13A5B|MOV|ECX, EDI", "0x13A5D|CALL|0x6ff6e0e0", "0x13A62|PUSH|EDI", "0x13A63|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff7504c]", "0x13A69|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EBX + 0x74]", "0x13A6C|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x13A6E|JZ|0x6ff63a92", "0x13A70|MOV|EAX, ESI", "0x13A72|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [ESI + 0x4]", "0x13A75|PUSH|0x3a3"],
      "comment": "Cleans up all pending socket operations and releases associated resources.\n\nThis function manages the cleanup of an asynchronous socket operation queue. It acquires\nexclusive access via a critical section, iterates through all queued operations, processes\neach one for cleanup, then clears the list and releases the critical section. Used during\nsocket shutdown, connection termination, or error recovery scenarios.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute address of CRITICAL_SECTION at implicit context+0x2c\n2. Call init routine to setup critical section reference counter\n3. Enter critical section for thread-safe access to pending operations list\n4. Load head pointer of linked list from context+0x74\n5. While list head is not NULL:\n   a. Save current node pointer\n   b. Load next node pointer from current[+0x4]\n   c. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to cleanup and release current node\n   d. Advance to next node and repeat loop\n6. Clear list head pointer by setting context+0x74 to NULL\n7. Delete and release the critical section\n8. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement for final cleanup/shutdown signal\n\nParameters:\n- Implicit (EBX): Pointer to socket context structure containing:\n  - [EBX+0x2c]: CRITICAL_SECTION (24 bytes) for thread synchronization\n  - [EBX+0x74]: Head pointer to linked list of pending socket operations\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pending operations list is empty, function still acquires and releases critical section\n- Each node in the linked list contains next pointer at offset +0x4\n- DeallocateResourcePoolElement handles per-node resource deallocation\n- Final DeallocateResourcePoolElement call after clearing list may signal completion or cleanup\n- Uses __stdcall convention (callee cleans up stack, RET instruction)\n- Function uses EBX, ESI, EDI registers (saved/restored via PUSH/POP)\n\nContext Structure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name                 | Type        | Description\n0x2c   | 24   | criticalSection            | CRITICAL_SEC| Thread synchronization object\n0x74   | 4    | pendingOperationsListHead  | void*       | Head pointer to linked operation list\n\nPending Operation Node Structure:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type   | Description\n0      | varies| data      | byte[] | Node payload/operation data\n+0x4   | 4    | next       | void*  | Pointer to next node in linked list",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "LIB_FOG_NET", "CALLER_4", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_0", "CALLEE_4", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "SRC_QServer.cpp"]
