      "instructions": ["0x13B80|PUSH|EBP", "0x13B81|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x13B85|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x13B87|JNZ|0x6ff63b8f", "0x13B89|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x13B8B|POP|EBP", "0x13B8C|RET|0x8", "0x13B8F|PUSH|EBX", "0x13B90|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x13B94|PUSH|ESI", "0x13B95|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EBP + 0xc]", "0x13B98|AND|ESI, EBX", "0x13B9A|PUSH|EDI", "0x13B9B|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [EBP + 0x1c]", "0x13B9E|LEA|EBX, [ESI + ESI*0x2]"],
      "comment": "Searches a hash table for an entry matching the specified key.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate hash table pointer is non-NULL, return NULL if invalid\n2. Calculate bucket index by masking search key with hash mask (offset +0x0C)\n3. Compute bucket offset as bucketIndex * 0x18 (24 bytes per bucket)\n4. Obtain pointer to critical section at pHashTable+0x1C + bucketOffset\n5. Validate and enter critical section for thread-safe access\n6. Get bucket head pointer from bucket array at pHashTable+0x14\n7. Traverse linked list comparing first DWORD of each entry to search key\n8. Leave critical section after search completes\n9. Return matching entry pointer or NULL if not found\n\nParameters:\n  pHashTable (HashTable*): Pointer to hash table structure containing:\n    +0x0C (dwHashMask): Hash mask for bucket index calculation\n    +0x14 (ppBuckets): Pointer to bucket array (array of linked list heads)\n    +0x1C (pCriticalSections): Pointer to critical section array (one per bucket)\n  dwSearchKey (uint): Key value to search for in the hash table\n\nReturns:\n  uint*: Pointer to hash entry if key found (first DWORD is key, second is next ptr)\n  NULL: If pHashTable is NULL or key not found in any bucket entry\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL hash table pointer returns NULL immediately without lock acquisition\n  - Empty bucket (NULL head pointer) returns NULL after releasing lock\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x18 (24): Size of each bucket's critical section structure\n  0x321 (801): Validation code passed to ValidateCriticalSection",
