      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new server connection structure for an incoming client.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x664 bytes from resource pool for connection structure\n2. Zero-initialize the entire structure (0x199 DWORDs = 0x664 bytes)\n3. Enter server critical section and increment connection ID counter\n4. Store socket handle and peer address in connection structure\n5. Initialize connection state fields (status=1, type=2, clear flags)\n6. Record current timestamp in 4 timestamp fields for connection tracking\n7. Initialize embedded critical section in structure at offset +0x2c\n8. Calculate hash bucket index from connection ID and server hash mask\n9. Link structure into connection ID hash table (linked list at bucket)\n10. Link structure into peer address hash table (separate hash)\n11. Call FUN_6ff629f0 for additional initialization\n12. Atomically increment reference count via InterlockedIncrement\n13. Increment server's active connection counter\n14. Convert peer address to string via inet_ntoa (for logging)\n15. Return pointer to initialized connection structure\n\nParameters:\n  dwSocketHandle: uint - Socket handle for the new connection\n  dwPeerAddress: uint - Peer IP address in network byte order\n  IMPLICIT in_EAX: Server context pointer containing hash tables and critical sections\n\nReturns:\n  uint* - Pointer to newly allocated and initialized connection structure\n  NULL if resource pool allocation fails (error logged)\n\nStructure Layout (Connection Structure - 0x664 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  0x00    4     dwConnectionId     Unique connection ID (incremented atomically)\n  0x04    4     pNextById          Next connection in ID hash bucket chain\n  0x08    4     dwRefCount         Reference count (InterlockedIncrement)\n  0x10    4     dwSocketHandle     Socket handle (param_1)\n  0x18    4     dwPeerAddress      Peer IP address (param_2)\n  0x1c    4     pNextByAddr        Next connection in address hash bucket\n  0x24    4     field_24           Reserved (initialized to 0)\n  0x28    4     field_28           Reserved (initialized to 0)\n  0x2c    24    criticalSection    Embedded CRITICAL_SECTION\n  0x58    4     dwStatus           Connection status (1=active)\n  0x70    4     dwType             Connection type (2=client)\n  0x74    4     field_74           Reserved (initialized to 0)\n  0x98    4     dwTimestamp1       Creation timestamp\n  0x9c    4     dwTimestamp2       Last activity timestamp\n  0xa0    4     dwTimestamp3       Reserved timestamp\n  0xa4    4     dwTimestamp4       Reserved timestamp\n\nServer Context Offsets (in_EAX):\n  +0x04   dwNextConnectionId   Next connection ID to assign\n  +0x0c   dwHashMask           Hash mask for bucket calculation\n  +0x14   ppIdHashTable        Pointer to connection ID hash table\n  +0x1c   ppIdCritSections     Pointer to per-bucket critical sections\n  +0x20   ppAddrHashTable      Pointer to address hash table\n  +0x28   addrCritSection      Critical section for address table\n  +0x854  serverCritSection    Main server critical section\n  +0x880  dwActiveConnections  Count of active connections\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x664: Connection structure size in bytes\n  0x199: Number of DWORDs to zero (0x664/4)\n  0x18: Size of hash bucket entry (ID hash stride)\n  0x241, 0x24c, 0x27c, 0x282, 0x289: Source line numbers for debugging\n\nError Handling:\n  If AllocateFromResourcePool returns NULL, logs error with source location\n  but continues execution (may crash on null pointer dereference)",
      "tags": ["CALLEE_10", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "LIB_FOG_NET", "CALLER_2", "STRUCT_Room1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "SRC_QServer.cpp"]
