      "instructions": ["0x13F60|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x13F62|JZ|0x6ff63fa2", "0x13F64|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0x13F68|PUSH|EAX", "0x13F69|PUSH|ESI", "0x13F6A|CALL|0x6ff63b80", "0x13F6F|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x13F71|JZ|0x6ff63fa2", "0x13F73|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EAX + 0xc]", "0x13F76|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x13F78|JNZ|0x6ff63fa2", "0x13F7A|CMP|dword ptr [ESI], 0x0", "0x13F7D|JZ|0x6ff63f8b", "0x13F7F|PUSH|EDI", "0x13F80|PUSH|EBX"],
      "comment": "Sends data to a socket identified by hash key lookup in the socket table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate hash table pointer (pHashTable in ESI) is non-null\n2. Look up socket entry using dwSocketKey via FindHashTableEntry\n3. Validate entry found and entry status field (+0xc) is zero (not closed/error)\n4. Check if hash table has buffered mode enabled (dwUnknown00 != 0):\n   a. If buffered: Delegate to SendSocketData for queued transmission\n   b. If direct: Call Winsock send() directly with buffer and length\n5. Check send() result for errors (-1 indicates failure)\n6. On send failure: Call WSAGetLastError to capture error code\n7. Return success (1) or failure (0)\n\nParameters:\ndwSocketKey (uint) - Hash key to locate socket entry in table\nIMPLICIT ESI: pHashTable (HashTable*) - Pointer to socket hash table manager\nIMPLICIT EBX: pBuffer (void*) - Pointer to data buffer to send\nIMPLICIT EDI: dwLength (uint) - Number of bytes to send from buffer\n\nReturns:\n1 - Data sent successfully (direct send returned bytes or SendSocketData succeeded)\n0 - Failure: null hash table, entry not found, entry closed, or send error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Entry offset +0xc: Status field (0=active, non-zero=closed/error)\n- Entry offset +0x10: SOCKET handle for Winsock send()\n- Hash table dwUnknown00: Mode flag (0=direct send, non-zero=buffered/queued)\n- WSAGetLastError called but result discarded (error logging elsewhere)",
