      "comment": "Initiates the thread shutdown sequence for the game engine.\n\nThis function sets up synchronization primitives and signals the game engine to\nbegin its shutdown procedure. It handles both the initial shutdown setup and\ngraceful handling of redundant calls through flag checking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if shutdown sequence is already initiated (flag at offset 0x0)\n2. If already shutdown, call CloseThreadHandlesAndWait() and return immediately\n3. Load critical section address at offset 0x854 with size 0x64 bytes\n4. Initialize critical section via ValidateDataStructureIntegrity()\n5. Enter critical section for exclusive access to shutdown state\n6. Set shutdown in-progress flag at offset 0xbf8 to 1\n7. Leave critical section to allow other threads to see the flag\n8. Load thread completion handle from offset 0xbd8\n9. Wait for thread completion with 2000ms (0x7d0) timeout\n10. Return after successful synchronization or timeout\n\nParameters:\n  pGameContext (void *) - Pointer to game engine context/state structure containing:\n    - Offset 0x0: Shutdown initiated flag (0=not started, 1=in progress)\n    - Offset 0x854: Critical section for synchronization (0x64 bytes)\n    - Offset 0xbd8: Thread completion event handle (HANDLE)\n    - Offset 0xbf8: Shutdown in-progress flag (0=not set, 1=active)\n\nReturns:\n  None (void) - Function always succeeds or blocks on handle wait\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If shutdown already initiated, short-circuits with early return via\n    shutdown_already_started label\n  - 2000ms timeout prevents indefinite blocking if handle is invalid\n  - Critical section ensures atomic state transitions in multi-threaded environment\n  - ValidateDataStructureIntegrity() may perform structure validation or initialization\n  - g_pfnEnterCriticalSection, g_pfnLeaveCriticalSection, and g_pfnWaitForSingleObject\n    are function pointers that dispatch to Windows synchronization APIs\n\nStructure Layout (pGameContext):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name                    Type    Description\n  0x0     4     dwShutdownInitiatedFlag       DWORD   Shutdown already started flag\n  0x854   0x64  pCriticalSection              CRITICAL_SECTION Synchronization primitive\n  0xbd8   4     hThreadCompletionEvent        HANDLE  Thread completion event handle\n  0xbf8   4     dwShutdownInProgressFlag      DWORD   Active shutdown flag",
      "tags": ["CALLER_1", "PARAM_0", "CALLEE_5"]
