      "comment": "Retrieves a value from a hash table entry using thread-safe lookup with critical sections.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize critical section pointer to NULL for safety\n2. Call FindHashTableEntry to locate the hash table node matching dwSearchKey\n3. If entry found, extract the value at offset +0x7c (field index 0x1f)\n4. If critical section was acquired during lookup, release the lock\n5. Return the extracted value or 0 if entry not found\n\nParameters:\n- pHashTable (HashTable*): Hash table manager structure containing hash slots and critical sections\n- dwSearchKey (uint): Key value to search for in the hash table\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Value stored at offset +0x7c in the matching hash entry\n- 0: If no matching entry exists or hash table is empty\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Thread-safe: Critical section automatically released after value extraction\n- Caller does NOT need to release critical section (handled internally)\n- Value at offset +0x7c (0x1f * 4 bytes) in the hash table node structure",
