      "comment": "Removes a hash table entry by ID with throttled logging.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if hash table processing enabled (offset 0xbd0)\n2. Validate and enter critical section (offset 0x894)\n3. Calculate bucket index: dwEntryId % tableSize (offset 0x8b0)\n4. Load bucket head from array (offset 0x8ac)\n5. Iterate linked list searching for matching entry ID\n6. On match: unlink entry from list (update prev->next or bucket head)\n7. Deallocate matched entry via DeallocateResourcePoolElement\n8. Decrement entry count (offset 0x890)\n9. Leave critical section\n10. If 2000ms elapsed since last log, log hacklist size\n\nParameters:\ndwEntryId (uint, stack): Entry ID to remove from hash table\nIMPLICIT: in_EAX contains context block pointer (pContextBlock)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Entry removed as side effect, no return value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x7d0 (2000): Throttle interval in milliseconds\n0x4bf (1215): Validation line number for critical section\n0x4cc (1228): Deallocation source line (middle removal)\n0x4d3 (1235): Deallocation source line (head removal)\n\nStructure Offsets (pContextBlock):\nOffset | Size | Description\n0x890  | 4    | dwEntryCount - active hash entries\n0x894  | 24   | criticalSection - thread synchronization\n0x8ac  | 4    | ppBucketArray - pointer to bucket array\n0x8b0  | 4    | dwTableSize - hash table bucket count\n0xbd0  | 4    | fEnabled - hash table processing flag\n\nHashEntry Structure (16 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field       | Description\n0x0    | 4    | dwEntryId   | Entry identifier for matching\n0xc    | 4    | pNext       | Pointer to next entry in chain",
