      "comment": "Removes a hacked IP address from the hack list for an entity and logs the removal.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the entity pointer parameter from stack frame\n2. Check if entity is valid by testing the validity flag at offset 0xbd0\n3. If entity is invalid (flag is zero), skip all removal operations and exit\n4. If entity is valid, load the IP address bytes from the stack parameter\n5. Call inet_ntoa() to convert the IP address structure to a dotted-decimal string\n6. Push the IP string address along with the format string and module tag onto stack\n7. Call InitializeNetworkConnection() to log the IP removal event with formatted message\n8. Push the IP address value and call RemoveHashTableEntry() to delete entry from hack table\n9. Clean up the stack frame and return to caller with __stdcall cleanup (RET 0x10)\n\nParameters:\n  pEntity (void *): Pointer to entity/player structure whose hack IP is being removed\n    - Validity checked at offset 0xbd0 to prevent processing of invalid entities\n  ipAddress (in_addr): IP address structure containing bytes to be removed from hack list\n    - Converted to string format for logging before removal\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value, performs side effect of removing IP from hash table and logging\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If entity validity check at offset 0xbd0 is zero, entire removal is skipped\n  - IP address conversion and logging occurs only if entity is valid\n  - Remote function call to InitializeNetworkConnection() performs actual logging",
