      "comment": "Processes incoming network messages from a QServer connection in a loop.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if message processing callback is registered at pServerContext+0xBC0\n2. Enter main processing loop:\n   a. Lock connection critical section, retrieve ClientConnection pointer\n   b. Invoke message processing callback with buffer state parameters\n   c. Handle callback result codes:\n      - 2 (QUEUE_MESSAGE): Check spam throttle, allocate/reuse message buffer,\n        copy message data, timestamp it, enqueue to worker thread queue\n      - 3 (COMPLETE): Exit processing loop\n      - 4 (PACKET_INVALID): Log hacklist entry, track socket, return\n      - 5 (CONTINUE): Continue to next iteration\n   d. Update receive buffer by removing processed bytes via memmove\n   e. Loop until callback unregistered or returns COMPLETE\n\nParameters:\n  pServerContext - Server state structure containing:\n    +0x854: Queue critical section\n    +0x870: Queue head array pointer\n    +0x874: Queue tail array pointer  \n    +0x878: Free message buffer list head\n    +0x87C: Maximum queue index\n    +0xBC0: Message processing callback function pointer\n    +0xBD0: Spam check enabled flag\n  pConnectionData - Client connection data structure containing:\n    +0x00: Socket identifier\n    +0x18: Client IP address (in_addr)\n    +0x20: Connection flags\n    +0x2C: Critical section for connection\n    +0xA8: Current receive buffer length\n    +0xB0: Receive data buffer (0x5B4 bytes max)\n\nReturns: void\n\nError Handling:\n  - If queue index exceeds max (0x87C), triggers fatal error 0x69C\n  - If buffer overflow (>0x5B4 bytes), triggers fatal error 0x6A8\n  - Spam/invalid packets logged to HACKLIST and connection tracked\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x5C0 - Message buffer allocation size (includes header)\n  0x5B4 - Maximum receive buffer size\n  0x5BC - Offset to next pointer in message buffer (linked list)\n  0x5B4 - Message data size offset\n  0x5B8 - Timestamp offset in message buffer\n\nSource: ..\\\\Source\\\\Fog\\\\Src\\\\QServer\\\\QServer.cpp",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLEE_14", "CALLER_2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "NET_SERVER", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "SRC_QServer.cpp", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "API_NETWORK", "PROP_LARGE", "PARAM_2", "LIB_FOG_NET", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
