      "comment": "Creates and initializes a QServer (Queue Server) instance for network communication.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate main QServer structure (0xC4C bytes / 3148 bytes)\n2. Zero-initialize the structure (0x313 dwords = 787 entries)\n3. Copy global configuration values into structure fields\n4. Allocate and initialize client connection arrays (g_dwMaxClientConnections entries)\n5. Allocate critical section array for per-connection locking (0x18 bytes each)\n6. Initialize all critical sections for client connections\n7. Allocate pending packet queue arrays (g_dwMaxPendingPackets entries)\n8. Allocate message queue arrays (g_dwMaxMessageQueues entries)\n9. Set buffer size and packet configuration from parameters\n10. Initialize various critical sections for thread synchronization\n11. Allocate session management arrays (nMaxSessions entries)\n12. Check Windows version for IOCP (I/O Completion Port) support\n13. Initialize Winsock and start appropriate listener based on server type\n\nParameters:\n- nServerType: Server mode (1=dedicated, 2=listen, other=full network)\n- nMaxSessions: Maximum concurrent game sessions\n- wPort: Network port to listen on\n- nForceCompletionPort: If non-zero, disables IOCP even on NT\n- nRecvBufferSize: Receive buffer size per connection\n- nSendBufferSize: Send buffer size per connection\n- nMaxPacketSize: Maximum packet size\n- nPacketTimeout: Timeout for packet operations\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to initialized QServer structure on success\n- NULL should not occur (allocation failures logged but continue)\n\nStructure Layout (QServer at offset):\n0x000: fUseCompletionPorts (1 if IOCP, 0 for select)\n0x008: dwMaxClientConnections\n0x00C: dwServerSocketOptions\n0x010: dwMaxPendingPackets\n0x014: pClientSocketArray\n0x018: dwClientArraySize\n0x01C: pCriticalSectionArray\n0x020: pClientStateArray\n0x024: dwActiveConnections\n0x028: csMainLock (CRITICAL_SECTION)\n0x040: pPendingPacketArray\n0x044: dwPendingPacketCount\n0x84C: dwTotalBytesSent\n0x850: dwTotalBytesRecv\n0x854: csSessionLock (CRITICAL_SECTION)\n0x86C: nServerType\n0x870: pSessionIdArray\n0x874: pSessionStateArray\n0x878: dwActiveSessionCount\n0x87C: dwMaxSessions\n0x880: dwPendingSessionCount\n0x884: fServerStarted\n0x888: hListenSocket (-1 = invalid)\n0x894: csSendLock (CRITICAL_SECTION)\n0x8AC: pMessageQueueArray\n0x8B0: dwMaxMessageQueues\n0x8B4: csMessageLock (CRITICAL_SECTION)\n0xB90-0xB9C: reserved handles (set to -1)\n0xBC0: nRecvBufferSize\n0xBC4: nSendBufferSize\n0xBC8: nMaxPacketSize\n0xBCC: nPacketTimeout\n0xBD0: fInitialized (1 when ready)\n0xC18: dwServerStartTime\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xC4C (3148): Total QServer structure size\n0x313 (787): Number of DWORDs in structure\n0x18 (24): Size of CRITICAL_SECTION\n0x94 (148): OSVERSIONINFOA structure size\n0x101: Winsock version 1.1 (MAKEWORD(1,1))\nPlatformId 2: VER_PLATFORM_WIN32_NT",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "CALLEE_6", "STRUCT_Control", "SRC_QServer.cpp", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "API_NETWORK", "PROP_LARGE", "PARAM_8", "LIB_FOG_NET", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
