      "comment": "Writes realm startup information to log file including computer name and timestamp.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 68-byte stack frame for computer name buffer (64 chars) and size variable\n2. Initialize dwComputerNameSize to MAX_COMPUTERNAME_LENGTH (0x40)\n3. Call GetComputerNameA(szComputerName, &dwComputerNameSize) to retrieve local computer name\n4. If GetComputerNameA fails (returns FALSE), null-terminate buffer to use empty string\n5. Write separator line (63 dashes) to log file via WriteFormattedWideStringToFile\n6. Read timestamp from g_stGameStartTime SYSTEMTIME structure fields\n7. Format and write startup message with computer name and timestamp\n8. Write closing separator line to log file\n9. Return (void function)\n\nParameters:\n- pLogFile (ESI, FILE*, IMPLICIT): Output file stream handle for logging\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value; output written directly to pLogFile stream\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- GetComputerNameA failure: Empty string used instead of computer name\n- Buffer size: 64-byte buffer accommodates MAX_COMPUTERNAME_LENGTH + null terminator\n- Assumes pLogFile is valid and open in wide-character mode\n\nGlobal References:\n- g_stGameStartTime (0x6ff99db0): SYSTEMTIME structure containing game start timestamp\n  - wYear: 4-digit year\n  - wMonth: Month (1-12)\n  - wDayOfWeek: Day of week (unused)\n  - wDay: Day of month (1-31)\n  - wHour: Hour (0-23)\n  - wMinute: Minute (0-59)\n  - wSecond: Second (0-59)\n  - wMilliseconds: Millisecond (0-999)\n\nFormat String:\n- \"%s Realm startup at %04d-%02d-%02d %02d:%02d:%02d.%03u\n\"\n- Output: \"COMPUTERNAME Realm startup at YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS.mmm\"",
