      "comment": "Performs graceful shutdown of logging and network resources before exit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if logging system is initialized via g_fLoggingInitialized flag\n2. If not initialized, skip error logging and jump to cleanup phase\n3. If initialized, call GetReturnAddress to capture caller context\n4. Call ReportError to log shutdown with context information\n5. Recursive call to self (unreachable error path)\n6. Call WSACleanup to terminate Winsock networking subsystem\n7. Call GetTickCount to initialize timeout tracking (dwStartTick)\n8. Enter wait loop for pending deallocation queue to drain:\n   a. Enter critical section g_csMessageQueue (0x6ffa6e8c)\n   b. Read g_pDeallocQueueHead (0x6ffa6ec4) to check pending items\n   c. Calculate conditional value: if queue count <= 0, result = 0\n   d. Leave critical section\n   e. If items pending (dwQueueItemCount != 0), Sleep(10ms)\n   f. Call GetTickCount again (dwCurrentTick)\n   g. Check elapsed time: if (dwCurrentTick - dwStartTick) >= 1000ms, exit loop\n   h. Otherwise continue loop\n9. Initialize ppFileHandle pointer to start of g_apLogFileHandles array\n10. Enter file handle cleanup loop:\n    a. Enter critical section g_csLogFileArray (0x6ffa6ea4)\n    b. Read current handle from array via ppFileHandle\n    c. If handle is non-null, call CloseFileStreamIfNotLocked\n    d. Clear handle to NULL after closing\n    e. Leave critical section\n    f. Increment ppFileHandle by 4 bytes\n    g. Compare against end address 0x6ff99ec8 (20 entries)\n    h. Continue loop if more handles remain\n11. Pop saved registers and return\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: Does not return normally - terminates after cleanup\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n- g_fLoggingInitialized (0x6ff99e70): Boolean flag for logging state\n- g_csMessageQueue (0x6ffa6e8c): CRITICAL_SECTION for message queue\n- g_pDeallocQueueHead (0x6ffa6ec4): Head pointer of deallocation queue\n- g_csLogFileArray (0x6ffa6ea4): CRITICAL_SECTION for log file array\n- g_apLogFileHandles (0x6ff99e78): Array of 20 file handle pointers\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3E8 (1000): Queue drain timeout in milliseconds\n- 0x0A (10): Sleep interval between queue checks in milliseconds\n- 0x6ff99ec8: End boundary of log handle array (base + 20*4)\n\nError Handling:\n- Logs fatal error context before initiating shutdown sequence\n- Gracefully waits for pending queue operations with timeout\n- Iterates all file handles ensuring proper cleanup",
