      "comment": "Performs periodic cleanup of resource files on a 24-hour interval with thread-safe synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load last cleanup timestamp from global variable\n2. If no prior cleanup or 24+ hours elapsed (86399999ms threshold):\n   a. Save current tick count as new cleanup timestamp\n   b. Release and reacquire critical section lock for synchronization\n   c. Call ShutdownResourcesAndExit to reload resources\n3. Get current system time and convert to Windows FILETIME format\n4. Initialize resource path buffer and extract module directory path\n5. If path lookup succeeds, append path component and process directory\n6. Build search pattern string using format specifier for log file discovery\n7. Find first file matching search pattern in resource directory\n8. If valid handle obtained:\n   a. Iterate through matching files:\n      i. Build full file path from directory and filename\n      ii. Call DeleteFileIfOlderThanThreshold to process file\n      iii. Find next matching file\n   b. Close file search handle when iteration complete\n9. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global state and critical section\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Synchronized with critical section (g_hCrashDumpMutex) to prevent concurrent access\n- 24-hour throttle (86399999ms) prevents excessive cleanup operations\n- DAT_6ffa6ed8 stores last cleanup tick count\n- Resource path determined by ExtractModuleDirectory lookup\n- File search uses FindFirstFileA/FindNextFileA for enumeration\n- Failed path lookup skips directory processing but completes normally",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLEE_14", "CALLER_1", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
