      "comment": "Formats a log message using printf-style arguments and enqueues it for processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if logging is disabled (g_fLoggingDisabled) or not initialized (g_fLoggingInitialized)\n2. Install SEH exception handler for allocation protection\n3. Format the message string using __vsnprintf into 4KB stack buffer\n4. If nApplyPathSuffix == 1, append error context suffix string to formatted message\n5. Calculate total buffer size: category string length + message length + 2 (null terminators)\n6. Enter critical section to protect message list operations\n7. Allocate MessageNode via AllocateMessageNode with calculated size\n8. Leave critical section after allocation\n9. Initialize MessageNode header fields:\n   - Set sentinel to total size + 0x24 (header overhead)\n   - Set allocation flag to 1\n   - Set message type flag based on nMessageType == 1 comparison\n   - Record current local time via GetLocalTime\n10. Copy category name string to payload area at offset +0x24\n11. Copy formatted message after category string (null-terminated concatenation)\n12. Re-enter critical section for list insertion\n13. If node was previously linked, unlink from old position using doubly-linked list logic\n14. Insert node at tail of global message list (g_pMessageListTail)\n15. Increment global message counter (g_dwMessageCount)\n16. Add node size to cumulative byte counter (g_dwTotalMessageBytes)\n17. Leave critical section and restore SEH chain\n\nParameters:\n  szCategoryName - Null-terminated category label for log grouping (e.g., \"Network\", \"Memory\")\n  nMessageType - Message severity level; 1 indicates error/critical message\n  nApplyPathSuffix - If 1, appends error location suffix (\"\n%s Error\") to message\n  szFormatString - Printf-style format string for message content\n  vaArguments - Variable argument list matching format specifiers\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; message enqueued asynchronously\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns immedia