      "comment": "Enqueues a log message to a thread-safe message queue with optional payload.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify initialization by checking g_fLoggingDisabled (should be 0) and \n   g_fLoggingInitialized (should be non-zero); exit immediately if not initialized\n2. If dwSkipDataCopy is 0, validate pbDataBuffer readability via IsBadReadPtr; set \n   dwSkipDataCopy to 1 if buffer is unreadable\n3. Calculate total allocation size: sum string lengths of lpszModulePrefix and \n   lpszFunctionName, add 0x16 for header, plus dwBufferSize if dwSkipDataCopy is 0\n4. Enter critical section for thread-safe allocation\n5. Allocate message node from g_pMessageListManager pool via AllocateMessageNode with \n   calculated nTotalSize; exit critical section\n6. Initialize message header at node offsets:\n   - Offset +0x8: payload offset = nTotalSize + 0x24\n   - Offset +0xc: marker value 0x2\n   - Offset +0x10: marker value 0x1\n7. Call GetLocalTime to fill SYSTEMTIME structure at offset +0x14\n8. Store message metadata at offset +0x24:\n   - +0x0: pbDataBuffer (original buffer pointer)\n   - +0x4: dwBufferSize (data size)\n   - +0x8: dwMessageType (message type code)\n   - +0xc: dwSkipDataCopy (copy flag)\n   - +0x10: dwReserved flag converted to boolean (1 if dwReserved==0)\n9. If dwSkipDataCopy is 0, copy pbDataBuffer into payload area at calculated offset:\n   - Copy DWORD units: dwBufferSize >> 2 iterations\n   - Copy remainder bytes: dwBufferSize & 3 individual bytes\n10. Enter critical section for queue manipulation\n11. If message has previous node (pNext != 0), unlink it from temporary list by \n    updating forward/backward pointers\n12. Insert message at queue head g_pMessageListTail:\n    - Set node pNext to current head\n    - Copy head's pPrevOrOffset to new node's pPrevOrOffset\n    - Update old head's pPrevOrOffset to point to new node\n13. Increment g_dwMessageCount message counter\n14. Add node size (nTotalSize + 0x24) to g_dwTotalMessageBytes total counter\n15. Update g_pMessageListTail to point to new node\n16. Exit critical section and return\n\nParameters:\n  lpszModulePrefix: Pointer to null-terminated module/component name string (0-256 bytes)\n  lpszFunctionName: Pointer to null-terminated function name string (0-256 bytes)\n  pbDataBuffer: Pointer to optional binary data buffer to include in message; may be NULL\n  dwBufferSize: Size in bytes of pbDataBuffer payload (0 to skip copying)\n  dwMessageType: Message type code/classification (0-0xFFFFFFFF)\n  dwSkipDataCopy: If non-zero, do not copy pbDataBuffer into message node (store pointer only)\n  dwReserved: Flag parameter; converted to boolean (1 if dwReserved==0, 0 otherwise)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; function always returns via RET instruction\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If initialization flags are not met, function exits immediately without queuing\n  - If dwSkipDataCopy is 0 and IsBadReadPtr returns true, automatically sets dwSkipDataCopy \n    to 1 to prevent reading invalid memory\n  - Message node unlink operation handles both forward and backward pointer updates for\n    nodes in temporary list before queue insertion\n  - All queue operations are protected by g_csMessageQueue critical section to ensure\n    thread-safe access to g_pMessageListTail queue head and counters\n  - Total allocation size is nTotalSize + 0x24 bytes (header + string lengths + payload)\n  - Function uses two critical section enter/exit pairs: one for allocation, one for \n    queue integration\n\nMessage Node Structure (allocated from g_pMessageListManager pool):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type        Description\n  0x0     4     pNext                ptr         Forward list pointer (to previous node)\n  0x4     4     pPrevOrOffset        int         Backward list pointer or offset adjustment\n  0x8     4     payloadOffset        uint        Offset to payload area (nTotalSize + 0x24)\n  0xc     4     marker1              uint        Marker value 0x2\n  0x10  