      "comment": "Performs final cleanup and deallocation of queued message entries during application shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load event handle from g_hWorkerThread (at 0x6ff818a0)\n2. Set shutdown in-progress flag at g_dwWorkerThreadShutdownFlag to 1\n3. Call WaitForSingleObject with 30000ms (30-second) timeout to allow pending operations\n4. Close the event handle using CloseHandle\n5. Enter critical section at g_CriticalSection (0x6ffa6e8c) to protect list traversal\n6. Initialize loop counter EDI to 0\n7. Load list head pointer from g_pMemoryDeallocQueueHead (0x6ffa6ec4)\n8. Loop while list pointer is non-zero:\n   a. Save list entry pointer to ESI\n   b. Call RemoveListEntrySEH to remove entry from doubly-linked list\n   c. Call DeallocateMemory with entry pointer, RTTI descriptor, -2 context flag, and 0\n   d. Continue to next entry\n9. Clear all state variables to 0:\n   - g_dwMemoryDeallocEntryCount (0x6ff816f0)\n   - g_dwMemoryDeallocTotalBytes (0x6ff81848)\n   - g_hWorkerThread (0x6ff818a0)\n   - g_dwWorkerThreadId (0x6ff819a4)\n   - g_dwWorkerThreadReady (0x6ff818f8)\n   - g_dwWorkerThreadShutdownFlag (0x6ff819a0)\n10. Release critical section lock\n11. Return to caller\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses 30-second (30000 milliseconds) timeout for WaitForSingleObject to allow graceful\n  shutdown of worker threads processing pending operations\n- Critical section protects linked list traversal from concurrent modifications\n- Parameter value -2 (0xFFFFFFFE) passed to DeallocateMemory indicates queue cleanup context\n- Clears entire state after successful deallocation to prevent reuse\n- Assumes list entry pointers are valid before removal (no null checks within loop)\n\nStructure Layout:\nList entries follow standard _LIST_ENTRY doubly-linked list format with Flink/Blink pointers.\nState variables cleared represent queue infrastructure:\n  g_pMemoryDeallocQueueHead - Head of queue (list pointer)\n  g_dwMemoryDeallocEntryCount - Count of entries in queue (DWORD)\n  g_dwMemoryDeallocTotalBytes - Total bytes queued for deallocation (DWORD)\n  g_hWorkerThread - Handle to worker thread event (HANDLE)\n  g_dwWorkerThreadId - Worker thread identifier (DWORD)\n  g_dwWorkerThreadReady - Worker thread readiness flag (DWORD)\n  g_dwWorkerThreadShutdownFlag - Shutdown initiation flag (DWORD)",
