      "instructions": ["0x16250|SUB|ESP, 0x24", "0x16253|PUSH|EBX", "0x16254|PUSH|EBP", "0x16255|PUSH|ESI", "0x16256|PUSH|EDI", "0x16257|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff75080]", "0x1625D|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x38]", "0x16261|MOV|DL, byte ptr [ECX]", "0x16263|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EAX", "0x16267|OR|EAX, 0xffffffff", "0x1626A|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EAX", "0x1626E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0x16272|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x16274|TEST|DL, DL", "0x16276|SETNZ|AL"],
      "comment": "Finds an existing log file slot or creates a new one for the specified file name.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current tick count for timestamp tracking\n2. Initialize search variables: nEmptySlotIndex, nUnusedSlotIndex, nOldestSlotIndex\n3. Loop through all 20 log file slots (index 0-19):\n   a. Compare lpszLogFileName with g_aszLogFileNames[nSlotIndex] using inline strcmp\n   b. If match found and file handle exists, return handle immediately\n   c. If slot name is empty, track as candidate empty slot\n   d. If slot has no file handle, track as candidate unused slot (prefer oldest)\n   e. If slot has file handle, track oldest access time for eviction\n4. Select best slot: empty > unused > oldest active (evict)\n5. If evicting an active slot, close existing file handle\n6. Copy new file name to slot (max 16 chars validated by CalculateStringLength)\n7. Call CreateCrashDumpLogFile to open/create the log file\n8. Store timestamps and file handle in global arrays\n9. Call WriteLogFileHeader if needed, or WriteRealmStartupInfo\n10. Return FILE* handle and slot index\n\nParameters:\nlpszLogFileName - ANSI string filename (max 15 chars + null terminator)\npnOutSlotIndex  - Output pointer to receive slot index (0-19), or NULL\n\nReturns:\nFILE* - Valid file handle on success, NULL on failure\n\nGlobal Data Arrays (20 slots each):\ng_aszLogFileNames (0x6ff99c70)         - char[16] per slot, stores log file names\ng_adwLogFileLastAccessTime (0x6ff99e20) - uint per slot, last access tick count\ng_apLogFileHandles (0x6ff99e78)         - FILE* per slot, open file handles\ng_adwLogFileFirstAccessTime (0x6ff99ec8) - uint per slot, creation tick count\n\nSlot Selection Priority:\n1. Exact match - reuse existing handle\n2. Empty slot (name[0] == 0)\n3. Unused slot (name set but handle NULL)\n4. Oldest slot by last access time (evicts existing handle)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x14 (20)  - Maximum log file slots\n0x10 (16)  - Bytes per file name entry (stride)\n0x335 (821) - Error code for filename too long",
      "tags": ["CALLEE_10", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_2", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "RET_STRUCT_PTR", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "API_NETWORK", "PROP_LARGE", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY"]
