      "comment": "Validates parameter string initialization and controls application startup flow.\n\nIf the parameter is NULL, the function executes a controlled shutdown sequence that\ncleans up WSA socket resources, logs the error, performs resource deallocation,\nand terminates the process. If the parameter is valid, it passes control to the\nmain initialization routine.\n\nALGORITHM:\n1. Load parameter from stack (ESP + 0x4)\n2. Test parameter for NULL condition\n3. If NULL: execute error shutdown sequence\n   - Capture return address context via GetReturnAddress()\n   - Clean up WSA (Windows Socket API) resources with WSACleanup()\n   - Log error with code 0x6, size 0x118, and message pointer\n   - Call ShutdownResourcesAndExit() for resource deallocation\n   - Exit process with status -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n4. If valid: call LogFormattedMessage() with parameter and two flag arguments\n5. Return to caller\n\nPARAMETERS:\n- szParameterString (char *): Input string parameter requiring validation.\n  NULL indicates initialization failure and triggers shutdown sequence.\n\nRETURNS:\n- void: Function does not return normally. On NULL parameter, calls _exit(-1)\n  and terminates the process. On valid parameter, returns to caller after logging.\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n- NULL parameter triggers immediate shutdown instead of graceful return\n- Magic number 0x118 represents error message buffer size\n- Error code 0x6 indicates parameter validation failure\n- GetReturnAddress() captures caller context for error reporting",
