      "instructions": ["0x16660|SUB|ESP, 0x158", "0x16666|PUSH|ESI", "0x16667|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x16669|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0xc], 0x2", "0x1666D|JZ|0x6ff666a1", "0x1666F|CALL|0x6ff6c9f0", "0x16674|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x16676|CALL|0x6ff5cc86", "0x1667B|PUSH|ESI", "0x1667C|PUSH|0x6ff77284", "0x16681|PUSH|0x36b", "0x16686|PUSH|0x6ff766a3", "0x1668B|PUSH|0x6", "0x1668D|CALL|0x6ff6dc10", "0x16692|ADD|ESP, 0x14"],
      "comment": "Exports memory region data to output file with hex and ASCII representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate region type field (offset +0xc) must equal 2\n2. Extract data path from configuration at offset +0x24\n3. Calculate start of region metadata by adding path string length + 1\n4. Determine data buffer location based on type flag\n5. Open output log file using path string via FindOrCreateLogFile\n6. Extract and format four 16-bit header values\n7. Write formatted time header line to output file\n8. Initialize loop counter and load byte count from offset +0x4\n9. Begin main processing loop for memory chunks up to 16 bytes\n10. Calculate current memory address based on type flag\n11. Write address/name header line to output file\n12. Validate memory readability using IsBadReadPtr\n13. Build hex dump string by formatting each byte as %02X\n14. Check ASCII display flag to append ASCII representation\n15. Convert non-printable bytes to period character (0x2e)\n16. Write complete formatted line (hex + ASCII) to output file\n17. Advance data pointer and decrement remaining byte count\n18. Continue loop until all bytes processed\n\nParameters:\n- pRegionConfig (in EAX, IMPLICIT): Pointer to region configuration structure\n  +0x0: Data pointer for direct access\n  +0x4: Byte count to process\n  +0x8: Type flag (0=direct, non-zero=indirect)\n  +0xc: Region type validation field (must equal 2)\n  +0x10: ASCII display flag\n  +0x14: Name string (32-byte buffer)\n  +0x24: Output path string (32-byte buffer)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value. Output written to file on success.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Region type validation: If +0xc != 2, calls error handler\n- Memory validation: Uses IsBadReadPtr before reading\n- Non-printable ASCII: Bytes < 0x20 replaced with period\n- Chunk size: Up to 16 bytes per line",
