      "instructions": ["0x168E0|PUSH|ECX", "0x168E1|PUSH|EBX", "0x168E2|PUSH|EBP", "0x168E3|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [0x6ff750ec]", "0x168E9|PUSH|ESI", "0x168EA|PUSH|EDI", "0x168EB|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], 0x0", "0x168F3|PUSH|0x6ffa6e8c", "0x168F8|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff7504c]", "0x168FE|MOV|EAX, [0x6ffa6ec4]", "0x16903|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x16905|JLE|0x6ff66923", "0x16907|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x16909|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x1690B|JZ|0x6ff6695d"],
      "comment": "Worker thread function for processing memory deallocation queue entries.\n\nThis is a long-running worker thread that continuously processes a doubly-linked list\nof memory deallocation queue entries. It operates in two modes: normal operation where\nit processes entries with periodic cleanup, and shutdown mode where it drains the queue\nwith a 15-second timeout before exiting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter main loop; acquire critical section for list access\n2. Load queue head pointer from g_pMemoryDeallocQueueHead; validate it is a valid pointer\n3. If queue head has forward link (Flink), extract backward link (Blink) and perform\n   pointer arithmetic to calculate the target insertion point for list manipulation\n4. If Blink is negative, negate it via bitwise NOT to get the target address; otherwise\n   calculate target by adding offset difference to Blink value\n5. Store the next entry's forward pointer at the calculated target to maintain list integrity\n6. Update the next entry's backward pointer to reference the saved Blink value\n7. Clear both the queue head's forward and backward pointers after list manipulation\n8. Decrement g_dwMemoryDeallocEntryCount and subtract entry size from g_dwMemoryDeallocTotalBytes\n9. Leave critical section and check g_dwWorkerThreadShutdownFlag\n10. If shutdown requested and this is the first shutdown iteration, record current tick count in\n    nShutdownStartTickCount; return immediately if queue is empty\n11. If shutdown active, calculate elapsed time; return if exceeds 15000ms (15-second timeout)\n12. Set nElapsedMilliseconds to 50ms if queue empty, 0ms if entry exists for sleep delay\n13. If entry exists: enter critical section, check entry type field at offset +0xc (accessed via\n    pQueueEntry[1].Blink due to array indexing of _LIST_ENTRY structure with 2 DWORD fields):\n    - Type 1 (value 1): call LogResourceAccessToFile for resource type handling\n    - Type 2 (value 2): call DumpMemoryRegionToFile for memory dump type handling\n14. Leave critical section; call RemoveListEntrySEH to unlink entry from list\n15. Call DeallocateMemory with szDeleteOperationString parameter to free entry memory\n16. Check g_dwWorkerThreadShutdownFlag again; if set (non-zero), jump back to main loop\n17. If normal operation (not shutting down), call Sleep with calculated delay\n18. Acquire critical section; call ProcessStaleFileHandles and ProcessPeriodicResourceCleanup\n    for maintenance operations; release critical section\n19. Jump back to main loop start for next iteration (infinite loop pattern)\n20. Function returns 1 on shutdown with empty queue; never returns in normal operation\n\nParameters:\n  (none) - Thread entry point function, called by Windows thread creation API\n\nReturns:\n  DWORD - Thread exit code (1 = shutdown complete with queue drained, function never\n  returns in normal operation mode as it loops indefinitely)\n\nCalling Convention:\n  __stdcall - Standard Windows calling convention for thread functions; callee cleans\n  stack with RET 0x4 (note: analyzed return shows RET 0x4 but actual signature shows no\n  parameters, typical for Win32 thread functions that take single parameter via argument)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic number 0x3a98 = 15000 milliseconds (15-second graceful shutdown timeout)\n  - Magic number 0x32 = 50 milliseconds (sleep delay when queue is empty in normal mode)\n  - Complex pointer math using conditional negation: Blink field can contain negative\n    values that are negated via bitwise NOT (~) to produce valid target addresses\n  - Type dispatch uses 1-based indexing: type values 1 and 2 are decremented before\n    comparison; after first decrement, value 1 jumps to type 1 handler; after second\n    decrement, only value 2 proceeds to type 2 handler\n  - List manipulation is complex but maintains doubly-linked list invariants by updating\n    both forward and backward pointers across multiple list nodes\n  - Critical section g_MemoryDeallocCriticalSection (distinct from g_CriticalSection) is\n    used for type dispatch, indicating separate synchronization domain\n  - Function operates as infinite loop in normal mode; only exits via shutdown flag\n  - Shutdown uses tick count for timeout to implement graceful drain with time limit\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Queue Entry (_LIST_ENTRY-based):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name      Type        Description\n  ------  ----  ---------       -------     ----------------------------------------\n  +0      4     Flink           PLIST_ENTRY Forward link to next entry\n  +4      4     Blink           PLIST_ENTRY Backward link to prev entry or type field\n  +8      4     dwSize          DWORD       Memory allocation size in bytes\n  +C      4     dwType          DWORD       Entry type (1=resource, 2=memory dump, etc)\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_CriticalSection - Main critical section for protecting queue list access\n  g_MemoryDeallocCriticalSection - Secondary critical section for type dispatch handling\n  g_pMemoryDeallocQueueHead - Pointer to head of doubly-linked deallocation queue\n  g_dwMemoryDeallocEntryCount - Current count of entries in queue (decremented on removal)\n  g_dwMemoryDeallocTotalBytes - Total bytes allocated in queue (decremented on removal)\n  g_dwWorkerThreadShutdownFlag - Shutdown control flag (0=running, non-zero=shutdown requested)\n  szDeleteOperationString - String literal \"delete\" passed to DeallocateMemory\n  g_pfnGetTickCount - Function pointer to GetTickCount API\n  g_pfnSleep - Function pointer to Sleep API\n  g_pEnterCriticalSectionFunc - Function pointer to EnterCriticalSection API\n  g_pLeaveCriticalSectionFunc - Function pointer to LeaveCriticalSection API\n\nRelated Functions:\n  RemoveListEntrySEH - Removes entry from doubly-linked list with SEH protection\n  DeallocateMemory - Deallocates memory block with logging\n  LogResourceAccessToFile - Type 1 handler for resource deallocation\n  DumpMemoryRegionToFile - Type 2 handler for memory dump deallocation\n  ProcessStaleFileHandles - Maintenance function for file handle cleanup\n  ProcessPeriodicResourceCleanup - Maintenance function for resource cleanup\n\nlpStartAddress parameter of CreateThread\n",
      "tags": ["CALLEE_10", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
