      "comment": "Initializes the game engine's global state and creates the worker thread\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear worker thread idle flag (g_fLoggingDisabled = 0)\n2. Create worker thread via CreateThread with ProcessMemoryDeallocQueue as entry point\n3. Store returned thread handle in g_hWorkerThread for lifecycle management\n4. Set logging initialized flag (g_fLoggingInitialized = 1) to mark logging ready\n5. Get current system time via GetLocalTime and store in lpSystemTime_6ff99db0\n6. Initialize all 20 game subsystem flags (g_dwSubsystemFlag0-19) to 1 (enabled)\n   - Each flag controls whether a corresponding game subsystem is operational\n   - All subsystems start enabled and can be disabled individually at runtime\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - Initialization routine with no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Thread creation uses NULL security attributes and zero stack size (system default)\n  - Thread starts immediately (dwCreationFlags = 0, no CREATE_SUSPENDED)\n  - Thread handle stored globally for later CloseHandle cleanup\n  - GetLocalTime captures exact moment of engine initialization completion\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\n  g_fLoggingDisabled      [0x6ff99f18] - Set to 0 (logging enabled)\n  g_hWorkerThread         [0x6ff99e18] - Handle to worker thread\n  g_fLoggingInitialized   [0x6ff99e70] - Set to 1 (logging ready)\n  lpSystemTime_6ff99db0   [0x6ff99db0] - Game start time (SYSTEMTIME struct)\n  g_dwSubsystemFlag0-19   [0x6ff99dc8-0x6ff99e14] - All set to 1 (enabled)\n\nThread Information:\n  Entry Point: ProcessMemoryDeallocQueue (0x6ff668e0)\n  Purpose: Background memory deallocation queue processing\n  Thread ID stored at: lpThreadId_6ff99f1c",
