      "instructions": ["0x16B00|SUB|ESP, 0x14", "0x16B03|PUSH|EBX", "0x16B04|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x1c]", "0x16B08|PUSH|ESI", "0x16B09|PUSH|EDI", "0x16B0A|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x16B0C|TEST|EBX, EBX", "0x16B0E|JNZ|0x6ff66b42", "0x16B10|CALL|0x6ff6c9f0", "0x16B15|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x16B17|CALL|0x6ff5cc86", "0x16B1C|PUSH|ESI", "0x16B1D|PUSH|0x6ff77284", "0x16B22|PUSH|0x97", "0x16B27|PUSH|0x6ff766a3"],
      "comment": "Decodes a bit stream and fills output buffer with decoded characters using lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate all input parameters (pBasisValue, pOutputBuffer, initParam)\n2. Check that *pBasisValue (bit width) is non-zero\n3. Calculate maximum characters: (nBufferSize * 8 + 7) / bitWidth\n4. Clamp to min(calculated, nMaxIterations - 1)\n5. Initialize the character filter buffer with stream parameters\n6. Loop: extract bits from stream and lookup character at offset 0x103\n7. Store decoded character to output buffer\n8. Terminate early if null character decoded\n9. Null-terminate the output buffer\n\nParameters:\n  pBasisValue    - int* - Pointer to bit width value used for stream decoding\n  pOutputBuffer  - byte* - Destination buffer for decoded character string\n  initParam      - int - Stream initialization parameter passed to filter buffer\n  nBufferSize    - int - Size of input data in bytes for bit calculation\n  nMaxIterations - int - Maximum number of characters to decode (buffer limit)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Output written directly to pOutputBuffer (null-terminated)\n  Function aborts on null parameters or zero bit width\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pBasisValue: Logs error 0x97 and aborts\n  - NULL pOutputBuffer: Logs error 0x98 and aborts\n  - Zero initParam: Logs error 0x99 and aborts\n  - Zero *pBasisValue: Logs error 0x9A via CleanupAndAbort\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x103 - Character lookup table offset from pBasisValue base\n  0x97-0x9A - Error codes for parameter validation failures\n  8 - Bits per byte for stream calculation\n  7 - Rounding constant for ceiling division",
