      "comment": "Converts four consecutive bytes into a packed 32-bit color value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer to 4-byte color array from stack parameter\n2. Extract byte[3], zero-extend to 32-bit, multiply by 0xFF to prepare for accumulation\n3. Extract byte[2], zero-extend to 32-bit, add to accumulated result\n4. Multiply intermediate result by 0xFF to scale for next byte\n5. Extract byte[1], zero-extend to 32-bit, add to accumulated result\n6. Multiply intermediate result by 0xFF to scale for final byte\n7. Extract byte[0] (LSB), zero-extend to 32-bit\n8. Add byte[1] contribution and multiply by 0xFF for final scaling\n9. Add byte[0] and magic constant 0xFF01FE00 to complete packing\n10. Return final packed color value in EAX\n\nParameters:\npColorBytes (byte*): Pointer to 4-byte array in little-endian format [B0, B1, B2, B3]\n\nReturns:\nuint: Packed 32-bit color value computed as ((B3 * 0xFF + B2) * 0xFF + B1) * 0xFF + B0 + 0xFF01FE00\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Constant 0xFF01FE00 (two's complement: -0xFE0200) indicates preprocessing/encoding\nByte Order: Little-endian access from base pointer (B0 at offset +0, B3 at offset +3)\nData Types: All bytes zero-extended to 32-bit before arithmetic to prevent sign extension",
