      "comment": "Monitors a socket for readiness to receive data or write data using non-blocking select().\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate connection state pointer is non-null\n2. Check error flag at offset 0x2c (must be 0)\n3. Verify connection valid flag at offset 0x0 (must be non-zero)\n4. Load socket handle from connection state at offset 0x8\n5. Initialize read and exception file descriptor sets with socket handle\n6. Set fd_count to 1 for both sets\n7. Initialize timeval structure with tv_sec=0, tv_usec=100000 (100ms non-blocking timeout)\n8. Call select() with read set, NULL write set, exception set, and timeout\n9. Re-validate connection state flags (offset 0x2c and 0x0) after select returns\n10. If select returned -1 (error): retrieve WSA error code, store at offset 0x34, set error status 4 at offset 0x30, return 1\n11. If select returned 0 (timeout): return 0 (no socket ready)\n12. Check if socket is set in exception set via __WSAFDIsSet (indicates write ready)\n13. If not in exception set, check if socket is set in read set via __WSAFDIsSet (data available)\n14. Return 1 if socket ready in either set, else return 0\n\nParameters:\n  pConnectionState (ClientConnection*): Pointer to connection state containing socket handle and status\n    Offset 0x00: Connection validity flag (must be non-zero to proceed)\n    Offset 0x08: SOCKET handle for monitoring\n    Offset 0x2c: Error/active flag (must be 0 to proceed)\n    Offset 0x30: Error status (0xc * 4, written on select error)\n    Offset 0x34: WSA error code (0xd * 4, stored on select failure)\n\nReturns:\n  int: 1 if socket ready for I/O or error occurred, 0 if timeout or validation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Timeout is hardcoded to 100ms (100000 microseconds) for non-blocking readiness check\n  - Error status value 4 indicates select() call failed with WSA error\n  - All state validations are repeated after select to detect external state changes\n  - Returns 1 on any error condition to signal caller to handle exception",
      "tags": ["API_NETWORK", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "CALLEE_3", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
