      "instructions": ["0x17220|SUB|ESP, 0x1a0", "0x17226|PUSH|ESI", "0x17227|PUSH|EDI", "0x17228|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1722A|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0xc]", "0x1722E|PUSH|EAX", "0x1722F|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x18]", "0x17233|PUSH|ECX", "0x17234|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x10]", "0x17238|PUSH|EDX", "0x17239|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x1c]", "0x1723D|PUSH|EAX", "0x1723E|PUSH|0x6ff77b98", "0x17243|PUSH|ESI", "0x17244|XOR|EDI, EDI"],
      "comment": "Resolves a hostname or IP address string to a canonical dotted-decimal IP address.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse input string as IPv4 address using sscanf with format \"%d.%d.%d.%d\"\n2. If all 4 octets parsed successfully, return input string unchanged\n3. Attempt DNS lookup via gethostbyname(addressString) to resolve hostname\n4. Validate hostent structure: verify pointer non-null, h_addr_list exists, first address is non-null\n5. If validation succeeds, jump to address conversion (step 8)\n6. If DNS lookup fails, check WSA error code against 0x276d (WSAHOST_NOT_FOUND)\n7. If error matches, initialize Winsock via WSAStartup(0x101, &wsaData)\n   If WSAStartup succeeds, set wsaInitialized flag and retry DNS lookup from step 3\n   If WSAStartup fails, return NULL\n8. Convert resolved address to dotted-decimal string via inet_ntoa(address)\n9. Copy result string byte-by-byte to global buffer at 0x6ff819c8\n10. If Winsock was initialized, call WSACleanup() to release resources\n11. Return pointer to global buffer on success, NULL on all failure paths\n\nParameters:\n- addressString (char*): Input hostname or IP address string to resolve\n\nReturns:\n- char*: Pointer to static buffer at 0x6ff819c8 containing resolved IP on success\n- NULL: If hostname cannot be resolved after initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- IPv4 pattern \"D.D.D.D\" (digits and dots) matches immediately without DNS lookup\n- Magic constant 0x276d: WSAHOST_NOT_FOUND error code triggers lazy Winsock initialization\n- Magic constant 0x101: WSA version 1.01 requested in WSAStartup\n- Static buffer at 0x6ff819c8: Shared global, overwrites on each call\n- Winsock initialized flag ensures WSACleanup() called only if WSAStartup() succeeded",
      "tags": ["API_NETWORK", "CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "PARAM_1", "CALLEE_6", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
