      "comment": "Retrieves the local machine IP address using two fallback methods.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Winsock subsystem with WSAStartup (version 0x101)\n2. Call gethostname() to get the local machine hostname\n3. If hostname obtained, call gethostbyname() to resolve it to an IPv4 address\n4. Extract the resolved IP from the hostent structure (first h_addr_list entry)\n5. If hostname method fails or returns null, create a UDP socket (AF_INET, SOCK_DGRAM)\n6. Set socket address family to AF_INET (value 2)\n7. Convert port 7 (Echo protocol) to network byte order with htons()\n8. Convert gateway IP 209.67.136.168 to network byte order with ConvertIPStringToAddress()\n9. Attempt to connect the UDP socket to the gateway address on port 7\n10. If connection succeeds, call getsockname() to retrieve the local IP bound to the socket\n11. Close the socket with closesocket()\n12. Format the IP address as a dotted-decimal string \"d.d.d.d\" using sprintf()\n13. Clean up Winsock resources with WSACleanup()\n14. Return pointer to g_szLocalIPAddress buffer\n\nReturns:\nchar * - Pointer to static 16-byte buffer containing formatted IP address string (e.g., \"192.168.1.100\")\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function takes no parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If gethostname() fails (returns -1), skips to socket fallback method\n- If gethostbyname() returns null, skips to socket fallback method\n- If socket creation fails (returns INVALID_SOCKET=-1), returns \"0.0.0.0\"\n- If connect() fails (returns -1), does not call getsockname(), uses dwResolvedIP=0\n- Port 7 is the Echo protocol, used as a gateway detection method\n- Gateway address 209.67.136.168 is a known public IP for routing detection\n- IP extraction from dwResolvedIP uses byte shifts: (dwResolvedIP >> 24) & 0xff for first octet\n- Return buffer is static and shared across all callers (not thread-safe)\n\nStructure Layout:\nsockaddr structure at [ESP+0x1c] after socket creation:\n  Offset 0: sa_family (WORD) - Set to 2 (AF_INET)\n  Offset 2: sa_data[2] (WORD) - Port in network byte order (htons(7) = 0x0700)\n  Offset 4: sa_data[4] (DWORD) - IPv4 address in network byte order",
      "tags": ["API_NETWORK", "CALLEE_11", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "STRUCT_Skill", "PARAM_0", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
