      "instructions": ["0x17400|SUB|ESP, 0x1c8", "0x17406|PUSH|EBP", "0x17407|PUSH|ESI", "0x17408|PUSH|EDI", "0x17409|PUSH|0xc4", "0x1740E|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x18], EDX", "0x17412|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], ECX", "0x17416|PUSH|0x6ff77be8", "0x1741B|MOV|EDX, 0x78", "0x17420|XOR|ECX, ECX", "0x17422|CALL|0x6ff5e0c0", "0x17427|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x17429|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x1742B|JNZ|0x6ff67446", "0x1742D|PUSH|0x6ff766a3"],
      "comment": "Creates a TCP socket connection to the specified IP address and port.\n\nAllocates a TcpConnection structure from the resource pool, initializes Winsock,\ncreates a TCP socket with optimized settings (TCP_NODELAY, SO_KEEPALIVE, SO_RCVTIMEO),\nand connects to the remote server. Optionally creates a worker thread for async I/O.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x78-byte TcpConnection structure from resource pool\n2. Zero-initialize the structure (0x1E DWORDs)\n3. Copy connection name to structure offset 0x38 (max 0x40 bytes)\n4. Initialize critical section at offset 0x0C for thread safety\n5. Call WSAStartup(0x101) for Winsock 1.1\n6. Create AF_INET SOCK_STREAM socket (TCP)\n7. Set socket options:\n   - TCP_NODELAY (level=6, opt=1) - disable Nagle algorithm\n   - SO_KEEPALIVE (level=0xFFFF, opt=8) - enable keepalive\n   - SO_RCVTIMEO (level=0xFFFF, opt=0x1005) - 3000ms receive timeout\n8. If non-blocking flag set, call ioctlsocket(FIONBIO=1)\n9. Build sockaddr_in and connect to remote host\n10. If blocking mode, set connection state to connected\n11. Cache local IP address in global g_szLocalIpAddr if not set\n12. If thread proc provided, spawn worker thread\n\nParameters:\n  lpszIpAddress (ECX) - Null-terminated IP address string (e.g., \"192.168.1.1\")\n  wPort (DX) - TCP port number in host byte order\n  lpfnThreadProc - Optional worker thread function, NULL for sync mode\n  lpThreadParam - Parameter passed to worker thread\n  lpszConnectionName - Debug name for connection, NULL defaults to \"UNKNOWN\"\n  dwFlags - Bit 0: 1=non-blocking mode, 0=blocking mode\n\nReturns:\n  Success: Pointer to TcpConnection structure\n  Failure: NULL with error stored in structure before deallocation\n\nError Codes (stored at offset 0x30 before cleanup):\n  0x01 - WSAStartup failed (WSA error at 0x34)\n  0x02 - socket() failed (WSA error at 0x34)\n  0x03 - connect() failed (WSA error at 0x34, unless WSAEWOULDBLOCK in async)\n\nStructure Layout (TcpConnection, 0x78 bytes):\n  0x00: DWORD dwConnected - 1 if connected\n  0x04: DWORD dwConnecting - 1 if connection in progress\n  0x08: SOCKET hSocket - Windows socket handle\n  0x0C: CRITICAL_SECTION cs - Thread synchronization (24 bytes)\n  0x24: HANDLE hThread - Worker thread handle\n  0x28: DWORD dwThreadId - Worker thread ID\n  0x30: DWORD dwErrorStage - Error code (1=WSA, 2=socket, 3=connect)\n  0x34: DWORD dwLastError - WSA error code\n  0x38: char szName[64] - Connection name for debugging\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x101 - Winsock version 1.1\n  0x78 - TcpConnection structure size (120 bytes)\n  0x1E - DWORD count for zeroing (30 DWORDs = 120 bytes)\n  0x40 - Max connection name length (64 bytes)\n  0x2733 - WSAEWOULDBLOCK (10035) - non-blocking connect pending\n  0xBB8 - SO_RCVTIMEO value (3000ms)\n  0x8004667E - FIONBIO ioctl code for non-blocking mode\n\nSource: Safesock.cpp line 0xC4 (196)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_2", "CALLEE_16", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "API_NETWORK", "PARAM_6", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_Safesock.cpp"]
