      "comment": "GetSocketName - Thread-safe wrapper for getsockname()\n\nRetrieves the local name (address) for a socket, protected by a critical section\nto ensure thread-safety in multi-threaded network operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute critical section pointer from socket context structure (offset +0xC)\n2. Validate and enter the critical section using magic number 0x22B\n3. Call getsockname() on the socket handle (offset +0x8 in context)\n4. Leave the critical section\n5. Return true if getsockname() succeeded, false on SOCKET_ERROR\n\nParameters:\n  pSocketContext (ECX) - Pointer to SocketContext structure containing:\n                         +0x08: SOCKET handle (hSocket)\n                         +0x0C: CRITICAL_SECTION for thread synchronization\n  pSockAddr (EDX) - Pointer to sockaddr structure to receive local address\n  pnNameLen (Stack+0x4) - Pointer to size of sockaddr buffer (in/out)\n\nReturns:\n  bool - true if getsockname() succeeded (return != SOCKET_ERROR/-1)\n         false if getsockname() failed (return == SOCKET_ERROR/-1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Critical section validation uses magic number 0x22B for debugging\n  - Socket must be bound before calling this function\n  - Returns false if socket is invalid or not bound\n\nOrdinal: 10262 (0x2816)",
