      "comment": "Retrieves the peer address of a connected socket in a thread-safe manner.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get critical section pointer from socket context (offset +0xC)\n2. Validate and enter the critical section for thread safety\n3. Call getpeername to retrieve the remote socket address\n4. Leave critical section\n5. Return success status (true if getpeername succeeded)\n\nParameters:\n  pSocketContext - Pointer to SocketContext structure (IMPLICIT: passed in ECX)\n    +0x08: SOCKET handle\n    +0x0C: CRITICAL_SECTION for thread synchronization\n  pSockAddr - Output buffer to receive the peer sockaddr structure (IMPLICIT: passed in EDX)\n  pnAddrLen - Pointer to sockaddr buffer size; updated with actual size on return\n\nReturns:\n  bool - true if getpeername succeeded, false if SOCKET_ERROR (-1)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x21a (538) - Line number passed to ValidateCriticalSection for debugging\n  0x08 - Offset to SOCKET handle in socket context\n  0x0C - Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION in socket context\n\nThread Safety:\n  Uses EnterCriticalSection/LeaveCriticalSection to protect socket access",
