      "comment": "Sends data through a socket with thread synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate socket context pointer is non-null\n2. Check if socket is not in error/closed state (offset 0x2c == 0)\n3. Acquire critical section at offset 0x0c for thread safety\n4. Call Winsock send() with buffer and length\n5. If send fails (bytes sent != requested length):\n   a. Get error code via WSAGetLastError()\n   b. Store error code at offset 0x34\n   c. Set error state flag to 4 at offset 0x30\n   d. Return 0 to indicate failure\n6. Release critical section\n7. Return bytes sent on success\n\nParameters:\n  pSocketContext (ECX) - Pointer to SocketContext structure containing:\n    +0x08: SOCKET handle\n    +0x0c: CRITICAL_SECTION for synchronization\n    +0x2c: Connection closed flag (0 = active)\n    +0x30: Error state enum (4 = send error)\n    +0x34: Last error code from WSAGetLastError()\n  pbBuffer (EDX) - Pointer to data buffer to send\n  nLength (stack+4) - Number of bytes to send\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of bytes sent on success\n      - 0 on failure (null context, closed socket, or send error)\n\nError Handling:\n  - Returns 0 if pSocketContext is NULL\n  - Returns 0 if socket already closed (offset 0x2c != 0)\n  - On send() failure, stores WSA error code and returns 0",
      "tags": ["API_NETWORK", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "CALLER_1", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "CALLEE_5", "STRUCT_Control"]
