      "comment": "Receives network data from a socket with critical section protection and error handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate session config pointer is non-NULL\n2. Check if session is active (session state field at offset +0x2c must be 0)\n3. If validation passes: acquire critical section lock, call recv(), release lock\n4. On recv error (return < 1): get error code and store error status\n5. Return bytes received count (positive on success, 0 on validation fail, negative on error)\n\nParameters:\npSessionConfig: Pointer to GameSessionConfig (contains socket handle, locks, state)\npBuffer: Destination buffer for received network data\nnBufferSize: Maximum bytes to receive into buffer\n\nReturns:\nEAX: Bytes received count (positive=success, 0=config invalid/inactive, negative=recv error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nCritical section at offset +0xc prevents concurrent socket access\nSession state at offset +0x2c (0=active, non-zero=inactive)\nSocket handle at offset +0x8 must be valid SOCKET descriptor\nError status 4 indicates recv() failed or connection closed",
