      "api_count": 4,
      "api_calls": ["ValidateCriticalSection", "ValidateCriticalSection", "closesocket", "WSAGetLastError"],
      "instructions": ["0x178D0|PUSH|ECX", "0x178D1|PUSH|EBX", "0x178D2|PUSH|ESI", "0x178D3|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x178D5|PUSH|EDI", "0x178D6|LEA|EDI, [ESI + 0xc]", "0x178D9|MOV|EDX, 0x14f", "0x178DE|MOV|ECX, EDI", "0x178E0|CALL|0x6ff6e0e0", "0x178E5|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [0x6ff7504c]", "0x178EB|PUSH|EDI", "0x178EC|CALL|EBX", "0x178EE|PUSH|EDI", "0x178EF|MOV|dword ptr [ESI + 0x2c], 0x1", "0x178F6|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff750ec]"],
      "comment": "Safely closes a network resource connection and releases all associated Windows system resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract critical section pointer from resource structure offset 0x0C\n2. Enter critical section for thread-safe resource state modification\n3. Set resource active flag at offset 0x2C to 1 to signal closure in progress\n4. Leave critical section to allow waiting thread to proceed\n5. Check if event handle at offset 0x24 is non-zero (indicates event object exists)\n6. If event exists, call WaitForSingleObject with 5-second timeout (0x1388 ms)\n7. Re-enter critical section for secondary cleanup phase\n8. Check event handle again and close it with CloseHandle if non-zero\n9. Clear event handle field to prevent use-after-close\n10. Load socket handle from offset 0x08 and zero both field 0x08 and field 0x00\n11. Call closesocket() to close the TCP/UDP socket connection\n12. Check return value: if -1 (SOCKET_ERROR), retrieve and store WSA error code\n13. Delete the critical section object with DeleteCriticalSection()\n14. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement() to return resource memory to pool\n\nParameters:\npResource (NetworkResourceContext *): Pointer to network resource context structure\n  - Field +0x00: Base pointer (cleared during cleanup)\n  - Field +0x08: Socket handle (SOCKET type)\n  - Field +0x0C: Critical section (CRITICAL_SECTION, 24 bytes)\n  - Field +0x24: Event handle (HANDLE, may be NULL)\n  - Field +0x2C: Active flag (DWORD, set to 1 during closure)\n  - Field +0x30: Error code (int, set to 5 on socket error)\n  - Field +0x34: WSA error status (DWORD, populated by WSAGetLastError)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns to caller after all resources are released\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Event handle may be NULL: WaitForSingleObject is skipped if event == 0x0\n- Socket closure failure: Returns -1, WSAGetLastError() retrieves error code\n- Error code 5: Indicates socket close failure with WSA error saved\n- Timeout value 5000ms: Prevents indefinite wait on event if listener hung\n- Resource pool: DeallocateResourcePoolElement handles magic offset 0x27c\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type              | Description\n0x00   | 4    | baseData         | uint              | Base pointer (cleared)\n0x08   | 4    | socketHandle     | SOCKET            | Network connection handle\n0x0C   | 24   | criticalSection  | CRITICAL_SECTION  | Thread synchronization\n0x24   | 4    | eventHandle      | HANDLE            | Event object (nullable)\n0x2C   | 4    | reservedField2C  | DWORD             | Active flag during closure\n0x30   | 4    | errorCode        | int               | Error status code\n0x34   | 4    | errorStatus      | DWORD             | WSA error from GetLastError",
      "tags": ["CALLEE_9", "API_NETWORK", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "SRC_Safesock.cpp", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control"]
