      "comment": "Decodes a Huffman-encoded bit stream into raw bytes using pre-computed lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize bit buffer (bitBuffer=0) and bit position counter (bitPosition=32)\n2. Enter main loop: While bit position counter is valid (≤32 bits)\n3. Refill bit buffer phase: While <8 bits available AND input bytes remain\n4. Decrement bit position by 8, read input byte, shift into bit buffer\n5. Lookup phase: Extract high byte of buffer as index into Huffman table\n6. Read bit length from table (1-11 bits), calculate shift amount\n7. Extract code bits from buffer using shift and mask from 0x6ff7f310\n8. Lookup decoded symbol from table at offset+1\n9. Read symbol bit length from 0x6ff7f210[symbol]\n10. Advance bit position by adding symbol length\n11. If bit position > 32, exit loop (overflow detected)\n12. If output buffer full (nOutputBytesRemaining=0), return 0\n13. Write symbol byte to output, shift bits from buffer\n14. Loop back to refill phase for next symbol\n\nParameters:\npOutput (ECX): Pointer to output byte buffer\nnMaxOutputBytes (EDX): Maximum bytes to write\npInput (stack): Pointer to compressed Huffman stream\nnInputBytes (stack): Number of input bytes available\n\nReturns:\nEAX: Bytes successfully decoded (or 0 on buffer overflow)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBit position=32 means buffer empty; refill triggers when >8 bits\nOverflow when bitPosition>32; Early exit when output buffer full",
