      "comment": "Decompresses bit-packed Huffman-encoded data using lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output cursor, bit counter (8 bits remaining), and partial byte accumulator\n2. For each input byte:\n   a. Look up bit length from g_abHuffmanCodeBitLengths table\n   b. Look up symbol bits from g_abHuffmanSymbolBits table\n   c. While extracted bits >= bits remaining in output byte:\n      - Extract high bits, combine with partial byte, write to output\n      - Reset partial byte accumulator, decrement output size counter\n      - Return 0 immediately if output buffer is exhausted\n   d. Accumulate remaining bits into partial byte for next iteration\n3. After all input processed, flush any remaining partial byte if bits were accumulated\n4. Return count of bytes written to output buffer\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer (ECX): Destination buffer for decompressed data\n- nOutputSize (EDX): Maximum output buffer capacity in bytes  \n- pInputBuffer (Stack+4): Source buffer containing Huffman-encoded data\n- nInputSize (Stack+8): Number of input bytes to decode\n\nReturns:\n- int: Number of bytes written to output buffer on success\n- 0: If output buffer capacity exceeded (early termination)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nInputSize is 0, returns 0 immediately (no bytes written)\n- Partial bytes are properly flushed at end of stream",
