      "comment": "Updates Huffman tree statistics by processing input byte buffer for compression analysis.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize accumulators: byte index = 0, total bit length = 0\n2. If buffer is empty (dwBufferLength == 0), skip to step 5\n3. Loop through each byte in pByteBuffer:\n   a. Read byte value from buffer at current index\n   b. Increment 64-bit frequency counter for this byte value in g_aqdwHuffmanByteFrequency[byte*2]\n   c. Handle carry propagation to high dword using ADC pattern\n   d. Look up Huffman code bit length from g_abHuffmanCodeBitLengths[byte]\n   e. Accumulate bit length total\n   f. Increment byte index, repeat while index < dwBufferLength\n4. Calculate encoded byte size: (totalBitLength + 7) / 8 + 1\n5. Determine encoding type based on 0xEF threshold:\n   - If encoded size <= 0xEF: use type 1 (single-byte length prefix)\n   - If encoded size > 0xEF: add 1 to size, use type 2 (two-byte length prefix)\n6. Update global 64-bit statistics with carry propagation:\n   - g_qwTotalBytesProcessed += dwBufferLength\n   - g_qwTotalEncodedSize += calculated encoded size\n   - g_qwEncodingTypeCount += encoding type (1 or 2)\n\nParameters:\n  pByteBuffer (ECX) - Pointer to byte array containing source data to analyze\n  dwBufferLength (EDX) - Number of bytes to process from input buffer\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xEF (239) - Maximum encoded size for single-byte length prefix encoding\n  0x07 - Added to bit count for ceiling division by 8 (round up to full bytes)\n  0x03 - Right shift count to divide by 8 (convert bits to bytes)\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  g_aqdwHuffmanByteFrequency[256*2] - 64-bit frequency counter per byte value\n  g_qwTotalBytesProcessed - Running total of all bytes processed\n  g_qwTotalEncodedSize - Running total of calculated encoded sizes\n  g_qwEncodingTypeCount - Running count of encoding type selections\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty buffer (dwBufferLength == 0): Skips processing loop, still updates statistics with 0\n  - 64-bit arithmetic uses CARRY4/ADC pattern for overflow handling",
