      "comment": "Sifts an element down a binary heap to restore heap property.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save the element to be sifted (value at current index)\n2. While current node has children within heap bounds:\n   a. Calculate left child index (2*i + 1)\n   b. If right child exists and is smaller than left child, use right child\n   c. Get value of selected child\n   d. If saved element <= child value, exit loop\n   e. Move child value up to parent position\n   f. Move to child position and continue\n3. Place saved element at final position\n\nParameters:\n- pHeapArray: Pointer to integer array representing heap (base address in EDI)\n- nHeapSize: Size of heap (number of elements)\n- Implicit EAX: Starting index for sift operation (passed in EAX, non-standard)\n- Implicit EDI: Heap array base address (passed in EDI, non-standard)\n\nReturns:\n- void: Modifies heap in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Index 0 (root) sifts all the way down to leaves\n- Single-element heaps (index 0) require no sifting\n- Function uses implicit EAX parameter for current index (non-standard calling convention)\n- EDI register holds heap base address (implicit parameter)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field        | Type     | Description\n-------|------|--------------|----------|----------------------------------\n+0     | 4    | element[0]   | int      | First heap element\n+4     | 4    | element[1]   | int      | Second element (child of 0)\n+8     | 4    | element[2]   | int      | Third element (child of 0)\n+12    | 4    | element[3]   | int      | Fourth element (child of 1)\n...    | ...  | ...          | ...      | Array continues, stride=4 bytes",
      "tags": ["CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "CALLEE_0", "PARAM_1", "PROP_LEAF"]
