      "instructions": ["0x18190|PUSH|ECX", "0x18191|PUSH|EBX", "0x18192|PUSH|EBP", "0x18193|PUSH|ESI", "0x18194|PUSH|EDI", "0x18195|MOV|EDI, EAX", "0x18197|CDQ|", "0x18198|SUB|EAX, EDX", "0x1819A|SAR|EAX, 0x1", "0x1819C|MOV|EBP, EAX", "0x1819E|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x181A0|JZ|0x6ff681e3", "0x181A2|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ECX + EBP*0x4 + -0x4]", "0x181A6|DEC|EBP", "0x181A7|CMP|EBP, EAX"],
      "comment": "Sorts an integer array in ascending order using the heapsort algorithm.\n\nHeapsort is an in-place comparison-based sorting algorithm with O(n log n) time\ncomplexity. It works by first building a max-heap from the array, then repeatedly\nextracting the maximum element and restoring the heap property.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate heap size as nCount / 2 (number of non-leaf nodes)\n2. Build max-heap phase: Starting from last non-leaf node, sift down each parent\n   to establish heap property where parent >= children\n3. Extract phase: Swap root (maximum) with last unsorted element, reduce heap size\n4. Restore heap phase: Sift down the new root to restore heap property\n5. Repeat steps 3-4 until all elements are sorted\n\nParameters:\n  pnArray (ECX) - Pointer to integer array to sort in place\n  nCount (EAX) - Number of elements in the array (passed via EAX register)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Array is sorted in place in ascending order\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nCount <= 1, function returns immediately (nothing to sort)\n  - Array must be valid and have at least nCount elements\n\nHeap Property:\n  For any parent at index i, children are at indices 2i+1 and 2i+2\n  Parent value must be >= both child values in max-heap\n\nComplexity:\n  Time: O(n log n) worst, average, and best case\n  Space: O(1) auxiliary (in-place sorting)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "CALLEE_0", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "PROP_LEAF"]
