      "comment": "Appends a backslash path separator to a path string if not already present.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate both pPath and bufferCapacity are non-null and non-zero\n2. Call Strlen to get the current length of the path string\n3. Check if path is empty (length == 0) or path already ends with backslash (0x5c)\n4. If either condition is true, exit without modification (early return to cleanup_and_exit)\n5. Calculate required buffer space: pathLength + 2 (for backslash and null terminator)\n6. Verify calculated space does not exceed bufferCapacity (pathLength + 1 < capacity)\n7. If space is insufficient, exit without modification\n8. Append backslash character (0x5c) at pPath[pathLength]\n9. Append null terminator (0x00) at pPath[pathLength + 1]\n10. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npPath (ECX): Pointer to null-terminated path string buffer to modify in place. Must point to valid memory.\nbufferCapacity (EDX): Total capacity in bytes of the buffer pointed to by pPath, including space for null terminator.\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function modifies the input string in place by appending a backslash character if conditions are met.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pPath is NULL, function returns without action (early exit at 0x6ff67c08)\n- If bufferCapacity is 0, function returns without action (early exit at 0x6ff67c0c)\n- If path length is 0, backslash is appended (creates single-character path \"\\\")\n- If path already ends with backslash (0x5c), no modification occurs\n- If buffer has insufficient space (requires at least pathLength + 2 bytes), no modification occurs\n- Buffer overflow is prevented by the (pathLength + 1 < bufferCapacity) check before writing",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "CALLEE_1", "PROP_SMALL"]
    },
