      "api_calls": ["QueryRegistryData", "FindLastCharInString", "SetRegistryValue", "CalculateStringLength"],
      "instructions": ["0x184D0|PUSH|ESI", "0x184D1|PUSH|EDI", "0x184D2|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x184D4|PUSH|EDI", "0x184D5|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x184D7|PUSH|ESI", "0x184D8|PUSH|0x0", "0x184DA|PUSH|0x6ff77b88", "0x184DF|PUSH|0x6ff77628", "0x184E4|CALL|0x6ff5cd04", "0x184E9|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x184EB|JNZ|0x6ff684ef", "0x184ED|MOV|byte ptr [ESI], AL", "0x184EF|PUSH|ESI", "0x184F0|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff750c0]"],
      "comment": "Retrieves the Diablo II installation path with trailing backslash.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query registry for HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Blizzard Entertainment\\Diablo II\\InstallPath\n2. If registry query fails or path is empty, clear buffer\n3. Validate path exists using GetFileAttributesA\n4. If path invalid (INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES), fall back to module directory:\n   a. Get current module path via GetModuleFileNameA\n   b. Null-terminate at buffer boundary for safety\n   c. Find last backslash and truncate to get directory\n   d. Update registry with discovered path\n5. Ensure path ends with trailing backslash if buffer space allows\n\nParameters:\n  pszPathBuffer - Output buffer to receive the install path (ECX, __fastcall)\n  dwBufferSize  - Size of the output buffer in bytes (EDX, __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Path stored in pszPathBuffer, empty string on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty/missing registry key: Falls back to module directory\n  - Invalid path in registry: Falls back to module directory\n  - Path without trailing backslash: Backslash appended if buffer allows\n  - Buffer too small for backslash append: Path left without trailing backslash\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x5C - ASCII backslash '\\\\'\n  0xFFFFFFFF - INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES from GetFileAttributesA",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "CALLER_2", "CALLEE_6"]
