      "instructions": ["0x185D0|PUSH|ESI", "0x185D1|PUSH|EDI", "0x185D2|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x185D4|PUSH|EDI", "0x185D5|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x185D7|PUSH|ESI", "0x185D8|PUSH|0x0", "0x185DA|PUSH|0x6ff77b7c", "0x185DF|PUSH|0x6ff77628", "0x185E4|CALL|0x6ff5cd04", "0x185E9|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x185EB|JNZ|0x6ff685ef", "0x185ED|MOV|byte ptr [ESI], AL", "0x185EF|PUSH|ESI", "0x185F0|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff750c0]"],
      "comment": "Retrieves or initializes the Diablo II save directory path from registry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query registry for existing \"Save Path\" value under \"Diablo II\" key\n2. If registry query fails, clear the buffer to empty string\n3. Validate the path exists on filesystem using GetFileAttributesA\n4. If path is invalid (INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES) or empty:\n   a. Get the game install path as base directory\n   b. Append \"Save\\\\\" subdirectory to create save path\n   c. Store the new path in registry for future use\n5. Check if path already ends with backslash separator\n6. If no trailing backslash and buffer has room, append one\n7. Create the directory structure recursively if it doesn't exist\n\nParameters:\n  lpszSavePathBuffer (ECX) - Buffer to receive the null-terminated save directory path\n  dwBufferSize (EDX) - Size of the buffer in bytes, must accommodate path plus trailing backslash\n\nReturns:\n  void - The save path is written directly to lpszSavePathBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If registry value doesn't exist, creates default path from install directory\n  - If directory doesn't exist on disk, creates it recursively via CreateDirectoryPathRecursive\n  - Always ensures trailing backslash on output path for proper path concatenation\n  - Handles case where buffer is too small to append trailing backslash\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x5C - ASCII backslash character '\\\\'\n  0xFFFFFFFF - INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES indicating path doesn't exist\n\nRegistry Keys:\n  HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\Software\\Blizzard Entertainment\\Diablo II\\Save Path",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "CALLER_1", "CALLEE_7"]
