      "instructions": ["0x18660|PUSH|ESI", "0x18661|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x18663|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x18665|PUSH|EDI", "0x18666|MOV|EDI, EDX", "0x18668|JZ|0x6ff686a0", "0x1866A|CMP|dword ptr [ESI + 0x20], EDI", "0x1866D|JNZ|0x6ff68674", "0x1866F|POP|EDI", "0x18670|MOV|EAX, ESI", "0x18672|POP|ESI", "0x18673|RET|", "0x18674|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x24]", "0x18677|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x18679|JZ|0x6ff6868a"],
      "comment": "Recursively searches a binary search tree for a node with a matching value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if current node is null - return null if empty\n2. Compare current node's value (at offset +0x20) with search value\n3. If match found, return current node pointer in EAX\n4. If no match and node's left child (at offset +0x24) exists, recursively search left subtree\n5. Compare recursive result with null sentinel - return if found\n6. If not found in left subtree, check node's right child (at offset +0x28)\n7. If right child exists, recursively search right subtree\n8. Return result from right subtree search or null if not found anywhere\n\nParameters:\npNode (ECX): Pointer to current TreeNode, contains:\n  +0x20: int value - node's search key value\n  +0x24: TreeNode* - pointer to left child node\n  +0x28: TreeNode* - pointer to right child node\nsearchValue (EDX): int value to search for in tree\n\nReturns:\nEAX: Pointer to matching TreeNode if found, or null pointer if not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses g_pNullTreeNodeSentinel (0x6ff7fc70) as null pointer sentinel value for comparisons\n- Recursive implementation searches depth-first, left subtree before right\n- No value modification, read-only tree search\n\nStructure Layout:\nTreeNode layout (28 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type      Description\n  0x20    4     value         int       Node's search key value\n  0x24    4     pLeftChild    TreeNode* Pointer to left child (lesser values)\n  0x28    4     pRightChild   TreeNode* Pointer to right child (greater values)",
      "tags": ["PARAM_2", "CALLER_2", "CALLEE_1", "RET_STRUCT_PTR"]
