      "comment": "Searches a StringIndexTable for an entry matching the given index and copies\nthe 4-character string code to the output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate entries pointer is non-null, return 0 if null\n2. Validate nSearchIndex is in range [0, entryCount), return 0 if out of range\n3. Linear search through entries array comparing index values\n4. On match, copy 4-char code to output buffer, converting spaces to null\n5. Null-terminate the output buffer and return 1\n6. Return 0 if no matching index found\n\nParameters:\n  pDataTable     - Pointer to StringIndexTable containing entries array and count\n  nSearchIndex   - Index value to search for in the table\n  szOutputBuffer - Output buffer to receive 4-char string code (must be 5+ bytes)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Successfully found index and copied string code to buffer\n  0 - Failed: null entries, index out of range, or index not found\n\nStructure Layout (StringIndexEntry, 8 bytes per entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Description\n  0x00    4     szCode      4-character string code (space-padded)\n  0x04    4     nIndex      Integer index value for lookup\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x20 (' ')  - Space character used as padding, converted to null on output\n\nDecompiler Temporaries (register-allocated, cannot be renamed):\n  pvVar1  - pEntries: Pointer to entries array\n  uVar2   - dwEntryCount: Number of entries in table\n  iVar3   - nIterIndex: Loop iteration counter\n  piVar4  - pnIndexPtr: Pointer to current entry's index field\n  cVar5   - cChar: Current character being processed",
