      "comment": "Inserts a node into a binary search tree using string key comparison.\n\nTraverses the tree comparing the new node's string key against existing nodes,\nnavigating left or right based on lexicographic comparison. If a duplicate key\nis found, deallocates the new node and logs an error.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if tree root pointer is NULL (empty tree case)\n2. If tree empty, insert new node as root and return\n3. Enter tree traversal loop:\n   a. Load current tree node pointer from [EAX]\n   b. Compare key strings byte-by-byte (unrolled 2 bytes per iteration)\n   c. Compute comparison result: -1 (less), 0 (equal), +1 (greater)\n   d. If less: move to left child (node+0x24), check if NULL\n   e. If greater: move to right child (node+0x28), check if NULL\n   f. If equal: duplicate key - call DeallocateResourcePoolElement and return\n4. When NULL child found, store new node pointer at that location\n\nParameters:\n    in_EAX (IMPLICIT) - BinarySearchTreeNode**: Pointer to tree root pointer\n                        or pointer to parent's left/right child pointer\n    pNewNode - BinarySearchTreeNode*: Node to insert with key at offset 0x00\n\nReturns:\n    void - Node inserted into tree or deallocated if duplicate\n\nError Handling:\n    Duplicate key: Logs error at line 1191 (0x4A7) from source file at 0x6ff77b50,\n    then calls DeallocateResourcePoolElement to free the duplicate node\n\nStructure Layout (BinarySearchTreeNode, 44 bytes):\n    Offset  Size  Field        Type                    Description\n    0x00    32    szKey        char[32]                String key for comparison\n    0x20    4     nSortIndex   int                     Entry index for ordering\n    0x24    4     pLeftChild   BinarySearchTreeNode*   Left subtree (lesser keys)\n    0x28    4     pRightChild  BinarySearchTreeNode*   Right subtree (greater keys)\n\nDecompiler Variables (SSA temporaries - register based):\n    pBVar3 (EDI): Current tree node being compared (BinarySearchTreeNode*)\n    pbVar2 (ESI): Pointer into current node's key string (byte*)  \n    pbVar6 (EAX temp): Pointer into new node's key string (byte*)\n    bVar1 (DL): Current byte from new node's key\n    bVar7 (BL): Current byte from tree node's key\n    iVar4 (EAX): String comparison result (-1, 0, +1)\n    uVar5: Intermediate 3-byte value during SBB comparison trick\n\nRegister Usage:\n    EAX - Current node pointer address (updated during traversal)\n    EBP - New node pointer (preserved from parameter)\n    EDI - Current tree node being compared\n    ESI - Pointer into current node's key string\n    EBX, ECX, DL - Temporaries for byte comparison\n\nSource: ..\\\\Source\\\\Fog\\\\Src\\\\Excel\\\\Excel.cpp",
