      "comment": "Searches a binary search tree for a key after applying case-insensitive transformation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy the input key string to a local buffer (max 32 bytes)\n2. Transform each character using the case-folding lookup table (uppercase -> lowercase)\n3. Validate tree structure - must have valid root or first node pointer\n4. Traverse tree: compare transformed key with each node's stored key\n5. Use strcmp-like byte comparison (compares 2 bytes per iteration for optimization)\n6. Navigate left child (offset +0x24) if key < node, right child (offset +0x28) if key > node\n7. Return node's associated value (offset +0x20) on match, or -1 if not found\n\nParameters:\n  pRootNode        - Pointer to BinarySearchTreeNode containing tree metadata\n                     transformedKey+0x00: Node count or validation flag\n                     transformedKey+0x0C: Pointer to first tree node\n  dwKeyValue       - Pointer to null-terminated key string to search for (cast as uint)\n\nReturns:\n  void* - Associated value from matching node (offset +0x20) on success\n  -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) - Key not found or empty tree\n\nNode Structure Layout (inferred):\n  +0x00: Key string (null-terminated, case-transformed)\n  +0x20: Associated value pointer (returned on match)\n  +0x24: Left child pointer (keys < this node)\n  +0x28: Right child pointer (keys > this node)\n\nError Handling:\n  - Triggers fatal error via LogErrorWithContext if tree is malformed\n    (has count but null first node pointer)\n  - Error code 0x475 (1141) with \"Unrecoverable internal error\" message\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty tree (count=0, first node=null): Returns -1 immediately\n  - Null node during traversal: Returns -1 (not found)",
