      "instructions": ["0x18B00|MOV|EAX, 0x1128", "0x18B05|CALL|0x6ff58270", "0x18B0A|PUSH|EBX", "0x18B0B|PUSH|EBP", "0x18B0C|PUSH|ESI", "0x18B0D|PUSH|EDI", "0x18B0E|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESP + 0x1144]", "0x18B15|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EDI + 0x4]", "0x18B18|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x18B1A|CMP|ECX, EBX", "0x18B1C|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EBX", "0x18B20|MOV|EAX, EDI", "0x18B22|JZ|0x6ff68b60", "0x18B24|MOV|EDX, 0x5", "0x18B29|MOV|ESI, 0x1"],
      "comment": "Builds a string index table by mapping search strings to entry array indices.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x1128 bytes of stack space via __chkstk\n2. Validate entry array chain has type=5 marker at proper positions\n3. Clear 0x400 byte hash bucket table (256 buckets x 4 bytes)\n4. Build hash table of entry strings:\n   a. For each entry with valid type marker (type != 0)\n   b. Compute case-insensitive hash via ComputeStringHash\n   c. Reduce hash to 8-bit bucket index using XOR folding\n   d. Insert hash node into bucket chain\n5. For each search string:\n   a. Compute hash and look up in hash table\n   b. Walk bucket chain, comparing hash values\n   c. On hash match, do full case-insensitive string compare\n   d. On match: compute entry index = (entry_ptr - base) / 20\n   e. On no match: output 0x7FFF (not found sentinel)\n6. Populate output array with remaining unmatched hash node indices\n7. Return total count of output indices\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputIndices - short*: Output buffer for entry indices (0x7FFF = not found)\n  pSearchStrings - void*: String table to search for, with count at offset 0xC\n  pEntryArray - void*: Array of 20-byte entries, string ptr at offset 0, next type at +0x18\n\nReturns:\n  void (count returned in EAX as side effect)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field          Type       Description\n  ------  ----  -----          ----       -----------\n  Entry Array (20 bytes each):\n  0x00    4     pString        char*      Pointer to null-terminated string\n  0x04    4     dwEntryType    uint       Entry type marker (5 = valid)\n  0x08    4     dwNextIndex    uint       Index of next entry\n  0x14    -     (next entry)   -          Stride to next entry\n\n  Search String Table:\n  0x00    4     pStringData    char*      Pointer to packed string buffer\n  0x0C    4     dwStringCount  uint       Number of search strings\n\n  Hash Node (12 bytes each):\n  0x00    4     pNext          node*      Next node in bucket chain\n  0x04    4     dwHash         uint       Full 32-bit string hash\n  0x08    4     pEntry         entry*     Pointer to entry in pEntryArray\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x400  - Size of hash bucket table (256 x 4 bytes)\n  0x118  - Maximum hash node count (280 entries)\n  0x0C   - Size of each hash node structure\n  0x14   - Size of each entry in pEntryArray (20 bytes)\n  0x5    - Entry type marker for valid entries\n  0xFF   - Mask for 8-bit hash bucket index\n  0x7FFF - Not found sentinel value (INT16_MAX)\n  0x66666667 - Magic multiplier for fast division by 20\n\nError Handling:\n  - Reports error at line 0xC4 if entry chain type validation fails\n  - Reports error at line 0xCC if hash node count exceeds 0x118 (280)\n  - Both errors call ShutdownResourcesAndExit(-1) after reporting",
