      "comment": "Registers a 32-byte key in an Excel binary search tree if not already present.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate implicit EBX parameter (BinarySearchTreeNode*) is not NULL\n2. Verify tree is in valid state (offset +8 field must be 0)\n3. Search tree for the key using SearchBinaryTreeForTransformedKey\n4. If key not found (negative result):\n   a. Allocate 0x2C (44) byte entry from resource pool\n   b. Zero-fill the allocated buffer (11 DWORDs)\n   c. Copy 32-byte key to entry\n   d. Apply character transformation to the key\n   e. Store parent pointer at entry+0x20\n   f. Insert entry into binary search tree\n   g. Increment tree node count\n\nParameters:\n  pbKey - Pointer to 32-byte key string to register\n  IMPLICIT EBX - BinarySearchTreeNode* containing tree root and metadata\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nEntry Structure (0x2C bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Description\n  0x00    0x20  Key data (32 bytes, transformed)\n  0x20    0x04  Parent/root pointer\n  0x24    0x08  Reserved/padding\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fatal error if EBX is NULL (calls ReportError with -1)\n  - Fatal error if tree state invalid (offset+8 != 0)\n  - Logs warning if allocation fails but continues\n\nSource: Excel.cpp line 1228-1241 (0x4CC-0x4D9)",
