      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a 16-byte node structure with all fields zeroed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call AllocateFromResourcePool with NULL pool and size 0x10 (16 bytes)\n2. If allocation fails (returns NULL), log error with context info\n3. Zero-initialize all 4 DWORD fields of the allocated node\n4. Return pointer to the initialized node\n\nParameters:\n  lpszContext (char *) - Error context string for logging on allocation failure\n  dwLineNumber (uint) - Source line number for error diagnostics\n\nReturns:\n  undefined4 * - Pointer to allocated 16-byte node with all fields zeroed\n                 NULL case: Error logged but execution continues (potential crash)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Allocation failure logs error but does NOT return early - continues to dereference NULL\n  - This appears to be a bug: should return NULL on allocation failure\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x10 - Node allocation size (16 bytes = 4 DWORDs)\n  0x0  - NULL pool parameter uses default global resource pool\n  2    - Error severity level passed to LogErrorWithContext",
