      "comment": "Parses a tab-separated value (TSV) buffer from Excel data files.\n\nReads raw buffer data, replaces delimiters with null terminators,\nand builds an ExcelRecord structure containing pointers and counts\nfor efficient field access.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate buffer end pointer from lpszBufferData + nBufferSize\n2. Allocate 16-byte ExcelRecord structure from resource pool\n3. Initialize record: buffer start ptr at [0], zeros at [1-3]\n4. Parse header row: iterate chars until first CRLF\n   - Replace TAB (0x09) with NULL, increment column count\n   - Replace CR (0x0D) with NULL, verify LF follows\n5. Validate column count does not exceed 280 (0x118)\n6. Store data row start pointer at record[1]\n7. Parse remaining rows: process TABs and CRLFs\n8. Check if row starts with \"Expansion\" (case-insensitive)\n   - If match, copy remaining data over expansion row\n   - Decrement row count to exclude expansion content\n9. Return ExcelRecord pointer on success, NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n  lpszBufferData - char * - Pointer to raw TSV buffer data\n  nBufferSize - int - Size of buffer in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  uint * - Pointer to ExcelRecord structure:\n           [0] = pBufferStart - original buffer pointer\n           [1] = pDataRowStart - first data row after header\n           [2] = dwDataRowCount - number of data rows\n           [3] = dwColumnCount - columns per row (TAB count + 1)\n  NULL - On allocation failure or no data rows found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10 (16) - Size of ExcelRecord structure in bytes\n  0x118 (280) - Maximum column count limit\n  0x09 - TAB character (column delimiter)\n  0x0D - Carriage Return (row delimiter part 1)\n  0x0A - Line Feed (row delimiter part 2)\n\nError Handling:\n  Line 0x4D - Logs warning if allocation fails\n  Line 0x5C - Fatal if header CR not followed by LF\n  Line 0x67 - Fatal if column count exceeds 280\n  Line 0x75 - Fatal if data CR not followed by LF\n\nSource: ..\\\\Source\\\\Fog\\\\Src\\\\Excel\\\\Excel.cpp",
