      "comment": "Processes format string data by parsing metadata and descriptors.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwValidationCheck is non-zero, call error handler and exit if invalid\n2. Validate dwRowStride is non-zero, call error handler and exit if invalid\n3. Build string index table from pMetadata and pDescriptors via BuildStringIndexTable\n4. Iterate through metadata fields (max pMetadata->fieldCount) checking field types\n5. For each field type (0x0A-0x12), process differently:\n   - Type 0x0A/0x0E: Write 4-byte DWORD values\n   - Type 0x0C/0x10: Write single bytes\n   - Type 0x0D/0x11: Write 2-byte WORD values\n   - Type 0x13-0x15: String copy with null termination\n   - Type 0x16-0x18: Lookup and indexed value storage\n6. Check for newline (0x0A) delimiter to advance to next row\n7. Handle remaining unprocessed fields with default values (-1, 0, 0xFFFF, 0xFF)\n8. Call Ordinal_10216 (InsertSortedValueIntoArray) for sorted insertion operations\n\nParameters:\npMetadata     - FormatMetadata* - Pointer to metadata structure with field definitions\npDescriptors  - FormatDescriptor* - Array of field descriptors defining data layout\ndwBaseOffset  - uint - Base offset for calculating output addresses\ndwValidationCheck - uint - Validation flag (must be non-zero)\ndwRowStride   - uint - Byte stride between consecutive rows\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; modifies output buffer via pDescriptors\n\nError Handling:\n- Calls LogErrorWithContext, ReportError, and ShutdownResourcesAndExit on validation failure\n- Uses WSACleanup for network cleanup before error exit\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x7FFF - Sentinel value indicating skip/ignore field\n0x0A   - Newline delimiter between rows",
