      "comment": "Initialize high-resolution performance counter system for timing measurements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 8-byte stack buffer for LARGE_INTEGER structure\n2. Call QueryPerformanceFrequency to obtain system counter frequency\n3. Calculate millisecond conversion factor (frequency / 1,000)\n4. Store millisecond factor at g_dwPerformanceTicksPerMillisecond\n5. Calculate microsecond conversion factor (frequency / 1,000,000)\n6. Store microsecond factor at g_dwPerformanceTicksPerMicrosecond\n7. Zero entire accumulator array (24,576 DWORD elements = 0x6000) using REP STOSD\n8. Call GetTickCount to capture baseline system tick count\n9. Store baseline at g_dwPerformanceStartTick for relative timing\n\nParameters:\nNone - Initializes global timing state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x3E8 (1,000) - Divisor for millisecond conversion\n0xF4240 (1,000,000) - Divisor for microsecond conversion\n0x6000 (24,576) - Number of DWORD elements in performance accumulator array\n\nSpecial Cases:\nQueryPerformanceFrequency may fail on systems without high-resolution timer support",
