      "comment": "Queues data for transmission on a network connection.\n\nAllocates a buffer node from the resource pool with 8-byte header space,\ncopies the source data into the payload area, and appends the node to\nthe connection's send queue (linked list at offset 0x74).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate buffer of size dwDataSize + 8 bytes from resource pool\n2. Log error if allocation fails (but continue - potential bug)\n3. Copy data in DWORD chunks (dwDataSize >> 2 iterations)\n4. Copy remaining bytes (dwDataSize & 3 iterations)\n5. Initialize node header: [0]=size, [4]=NULL (next pointer)\n6. If queue empty: set as head at pContext+0x74\n7. Else: traverse to tail and append\n\nParameters:\n  pContext - Server/connection context structure (offset 0x74 = queue head)\n  pData - Source data buffer to copy\n  dwDataSize - Size of data in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nBuffer Node Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field       Description\n  0x00    4     dwSize      Data payload size\n  0x04    4     pNext       Next node pointer (linked list)\n  0x08    N     abPayload   Copied data payload\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Allocation failure is logged but function continues with NULL pointer\n    This could cause crash - appears to be a latent bug",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "SRC_QServerNT.cpp", "LIB_FOG_NET", "PARAM_3", "CALLER_1", "CALLEE_2", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
