      "comment": "Releases a slot resource in a thread-safe pool using critical section protection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract object pointer and slot index from parameter structure at offsets 0x0 and 0x4\n2. Call parameter validator to ensure structure integrity\n3. Check initialization flag at offset 0xc18 - if not set, log error and exit with failure\n4. Load slot value from pool array at offset (object + slotIndex*4 + 0xc3c)\n5. Enter wait loop: While slot value is 0, call wait function and recheck slot availability\n6. Once slot becomes available (non-zero), acquire critical section at offset 0x854\n7. Clear the slot to 0 within critical section to mark as released/deallocated\n8. Release critical section and return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pParams (int *): Pointer to parameter structure containing:\n    - [0x0]: Object pointer (base address of pool object)\n    - [0x4]: Slot index (zero-based index into slot array)\n\nReturns:\n  int: Returns 1 on successful release; Does not return on initialization failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Offset 0xc18: Object initialization state flag (0=uninitialized, non-zero=ready)\n  - Offset 0xc3c: Base address of pool slot array (array of 4-byte slot values)\n  - Offset 0x854: Critical section object for thread synchronization\n  - Slot value 0: Indicates slot is unavailable/being processed (triggers wait)\n  - Non-zero slot: Indicates slot is available and can be released\n  - Function exits via _exit() on validation failure (does not return normally)\n  - __stdcall calling convention: Callee cleans 4-byte parameter from stack\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Parameter Structure at pParams:\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type     Description\n  0x0     4     pObjectBase     pointer  Base address of pool object\n  0x4     4     slotIndex       int      Zero-based slot index in pool array\n\nPool Object Layout (referenced offsets):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type     Description\n  0x854   16    criticalSection CRITICAL_SECTION  Thread synchronization object\n  0xc18   4     initFlag        dword    Initialization state (0=uninit, else=ready)\n  0xc3c+  4*N   slotArray       int[]    Pool slot availability array\nlpStartAddress parameter of CreateThread\n",
