      "comment": "Calculates elapsed time in seconds since initialization with periodic thread priority management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current system tick count in milliseconds via GetTickCount\n2. Retrieve previously stored tick count and accumulated seconds from g_qwLastValidationTimestamp\n3. Calculate time delta: currentTick - previousTick in milliseconds\n4. Compare delta against 30-second threshold (30000 ms = 0x7530)\n5. If delta > 30 seconds:\n   a. Get current thread handle via GetCurrentThread\n   b. Query current thread priority level via GetThreadPriority\n   c. If priority is not THREAD_PRIORITY_ERROR (0x7fffffff):\n      - Reset thread priority to its current value via SetThreadPriority\n   d. Get current system time via ConvertFileTimeToUnixTime32\n   e. Store updated tick count and system time via CompareAndSwap64Atomic\n6. Calculate final elapsed time using fixed-point arithmetic:\n   - Multiply time delta by 0x10624dd3 (magic constant for division by 1000)\n   - Extract upper 32 bits of result (EDX register)\n   - Right-shift by 6 bits to complete integer division\n   - Add accumulated elapsed seconds to get final result\n7. Return total elapsed time in seconds\n\nReturns:\nint - Elapsed time in seconds. Uses fixed-point multiplication (0x10624dd3) followed\n      by right-shift by 6 bits to implement fast integer division by approximately 1000,\n      avoiding floating-point overhead.\n\nParameters:\nNone - Uses global state stored at g_qwLastValidationTimestamp (8-byte structure containing\n       previous tick count and accumulated seconds).\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Thread priority error (0x7fffffff) is treated as invalid; skips priority reset\n- Interval-based updates occur only when delta > 30 seconds for efficiency\n- Fixed-point arithmetic avoids floating-point coprocessor overhead\n- Magic constant 0x10624dd3 with right-shift by 6 approximates division by 1000\n- Stack-based parameters for tick counts and system time are used for atomic updates\n\nGlobal Data:\n- g_qwLastValidationTimestamp: 8-byte storage for previous tick count and accumulated seconds\n- g_pfnGetTickCount: Function pointer to Windows GetTickCount API\n- g_pfnGetCurrentThread: Function pointer to Windows GetCurrentThread API  \n- g_pfnGetThreadPriority: Function pointer to Windows GetThreadPriority API\n- g_pfnSetThreadPriority: Function pointer to Windows SetThreadPriority API",
