      "instructions": ["0x1B3A0|SUB|ESP, 0x428", "0x1B3A6|PUSH|EBX", "0x1B3A7|PUSH|ESI", "0x1B3A8|MOV|EDX, 0x400", "0x1B3AD|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0x30]", "0x1B3B1|CALL|0x6ff685d0", "0x1B3B6|PUSH|0x6ff779ec", "0x1B3BB|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff7508c]", "0x1B3C1|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x1B3C3|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x1B3C5|CMP|ESI, EBX", "0x1B3C7|JZ|0x6ff6b41f", "0x1B3C9|PUSH|0x6ff779d8", "0x1B3CE|PUSH|ESI", "0x1B3CF|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff75088]"],
      "comment": "Queries the available free disk space in bytes for the current drive.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get the current working directory using BuildSaveGamePath (max 1024 bytes)\n2. Load kernel32.dll via LoadLibraryA to access extended disk space APIs\n3. Attempt to get GetDiskFreeSpaceExA function pointer via GetProcAddress:\n   - If modern API available, initialize 6 DWORD output buffers to 0\n   - Call GetDiskFreeSpaceExA with root path and output pointers at ESP+0x28, ESP+0x24, ESP+0x1c\n   - Unload kernel32.dll via FreeLibrary\n   - Return 64-bit available space from EDX:EAX (high:low dword pair)\n4. If modern API unavailable, use legacy GetDiskFreeSpaceA fallback:\n   - Search current directory path for backslash character (0x5c) delimiter\n   - Scan loop up to 0x400 (1024) characters or until backslash found\n   - Null-terminate path at position after backslash to isolate drive root\n   - Call GetDiskFreeSpaceA with root path and 5 output parameter pointers\n5. Calculate total available space: diskSpaceInfo[0] × clustersAvailable × bytesPerSector\n6. Return 64-bit result (EDX holds high dword, EAX holds low dword)\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function uses no parameters. Implicitly uses BuildSaveGamePath for directory access.\n\nReturns:\nulonglong - Total available disk space in bytes as a 64-bit unsigned integer.\nReturns EDX:EAX pair where EDX contains high 32 bits and EAX contains low 32 bits.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If LoadLibraryA fails or GetDiskFreeSpaceExA not found, falls back to legacy API\n- If neither API succeeds, returns 0 (both EAX and EDX zeroed)\n- Path length capped at 1024 bytes via BuildSaveGamePath\n- Fallback search loop uses 0x400 as maximum iterations (prevents infinite loop)\n- Uses backslash (0x5c) as path delimiter for drive root extraction (e.g., \"C:\\\")\n\nData Structures:\ndiskSpaceInfo array (32 bytes total, 8 DWORDs):\n- offset 0x0-0x3: sectorsPerCluster (GetDiskFreeSpaceA output)\n- offset 0x4-0x7: bytesPerSector (GetDiskFreeSpaceA output)\n- offset 0x8-0xb: freeClusters (GetDiskFreeSpaceA output)\n- offset 0xc-0xf: totalClusters (GetDiskFreeSpaceA output)\nFor GetDiskFreeSpaceExA, array repurposed for: availableClusters, totalClusters, freeClusters",
