      "comment": "Signals a worker thread to terminate and waits for completion.\n\nThis function sets a termination flag within a container object and\nthen waits for the worker thread to signal completion via an event.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate critical section address at container+0x854\n2. Validate the critical section with 100ms timeout\n3. Enter the critical section to protect flag modification\n4. Set termination flag at container+0xBF8 to 1\n5. Leave the critical section\n6. Wait for completion event at container+0xBD8 with 2000ms timeout\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT EDI (pContainer): Pointer to container object with worker state.\n                             Contains CRITICAL_SECTION at +0x854,\n                             completion HANDLE at +0xBD8, and\n                             termination flag at +0xBF8.\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Function blocks until worker acknowledges or timeout.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x854 - Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION in container\n  0xBD8 - Offset to completion event HANDLE\n  0xBF8 - Offset to termination flag (1 = terminate)\n  0x64 (100) - Critical section validation timeout in milliseconds\n  0x7D0 (2000) - WaitForSingleObject timeout in milliseconds",
