      "instructions": ["0x1B600|SUB|ESP, 0x848", "0x1B606|PUSH|EBX", "0x1B607|PUSH|EBP", "0x1B608|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x854]", "0x1B60F|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x1B611|PUSH|ESI", "0x1B612|PUSH|EDI", "0x1B613|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EAX", "0x1B617|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x10], EAX", "0x1B61B|JMP|0x6ff6b620", "0x1B620|MOV|EAX, EBP", "0x1B622|CALL|0x6ff644b0", "0x1B627|XOR|EAX, EAX", "0x1B629|LEA|EDI, [EBP + 0x854]", "0x1B62F|MOV|EDX, 0xa7"],
      "comment": "Server Connection Handler Thread - Main I/O multiplexing event loop\n\nImplements a select()-based socket polling mechanism for handling multiple concurrent\nclient connections. Manages incoming connections via accept() and processes incoming data\nfrom established connections using recv(). Implements connection validation, timestamp\nfreshness checks, rate limiting, and anti-spam protections before accepting new connections.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop main_loop_start: Call ProcessConnectionTimeouts() to expire old connections\n2. Initialize readfdSet and writefdSet as empty (fd_count = 0)\n3. Validate server context integrity via ValidateDataStructureIntegrity()\n4. Enter critical section lock on server context (offset +0x854)\n5. Add server listen socket (offset +0xb90) to both fd_sets if space available (<0x40)\n6. Walk linked list of active connections (starting at offset +0x14) by index:\n   - Load list head at connectionList[currentListIndex]\n   - Walk backwards using listTraversalCounter to find first non-null entry\n   - Break if reached top of list or connection count exceeded\n7. For each active connection (loop_check_active_connections), add socket at offset +0x10\n   to both fd_sets if space available, max 0x40 entries per set\n8. Calculate timeout: 100000 microseconds / (activeConnectionCount + 1), rounded down\n9. Release critical section lock via LeaveCriticalSection()\n10. Call select() with calculated timeout on both fd_sets\n11. Branch on select() result:\n    - If timeout (0): Check shutdown flag at offset +0xbf8, exit thread if set\n    - If error (-1): Jump back to main_loop_start\n    - If success (>0): Process both readable and writable sockets\n12. For listen socket (accept_connection_loop):\n    - Call accept() to accept new connection\n    - If accept fails with EAGAIN (0x2733), retry up to 100 times\n    - If other error: Format error message, output debug string, exit thread\n    - On success: Validate connection against:\n      a. FindAndActivateHashTableEntry() - check if address already active\n      b. CheckElementTimestampValid() - verify timestamp freshness\n      c. TrackConnectionUsageAndValidateLimit() - check rate limit\n    - If validation fails: Initialize tracking, close socket immediately\n    - If validation passes: InitializeServerConnection(), call callback if set\n13. For client sockets (handle_client_socket_read):\n    - Find connection node via FindItemById()\n    - If connection not found: recv() and discard data\n    - If connection found:\n      a. Acquire connection's critical section (offset +0x2c within node)\n      b. Load buffer offset at (connection + 0xa8), validate 0 <= offset < 0x5b4\n      c. recv() data into connection buffer at (connection + 0xb0 + offset)\n      d. Update buffer offset if recv() succeeded\n      e. Release critical section\n      f. Call ProcessClientConnectionData() to parse received message\n      g. SetEvent() on completion event (offset +0xbd4)\n14. Continue to next_socket_iteration, loop back to process more sockets\n15. Jump back to main_loop_start to repeat\n\nParameters:\n  pServerContext (void*) - Pointer to server context structure with offsets:\n    Offset +0x14: Pointer to connection list array (array of linked list heads)\n    Offset +0x18: Connection list size/rotation modulo value\n    Offset +0x854: Critical section for thread synchronization (0xbb bytes)\n    Offset +0x880: Current number of active connections (int)\n    Offset +0xb90: Server listen socket (SOCKET, 4 bytes)\n    Offset +0xbc4: Optional callback function pointer (void*)\n    Offset +0xbd4: Completion event handle (HANDLE)\n    Offset +0xbf8: Shutdown flag (int, non-zero = shutdown requested)\n\nReturns: void (infinite loop, terminates via ExitThread(0) on shutdown)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Connection list rotation: Uses modulo operation to round-robin through list entries\n  - Accept EAGAIN retry: Retries up to 100 times on WSAEWOULDBLOCK (0x2733) error\n  - Rate limiting: Rejects connections exceeding rate via InsertOrUpdateTrackedAddressInHashTable\n  - Duplicate detection: Rejects addresses already in active hash table\n  - Timestamp validation: Rejects addresses with invalid/stale timestamps\n  - Zero-copy recv: Appends directly to connection buffer without intermediate memcpy\n  - Orphaned socket cleanup: Receives and discards data from sockets without connection nodes\n  - Fd_set capacity: Handles up to 0x40 (64) sockets per read/write set\n  - Buffer overflow protection: Validates received offset stays within 0x5b4 (1460) byte limit\n\nStructure Layout - ClientConnection (connection node):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name              Type          Description\n  +0x00   4     socket                  SOCKET        Client socket descriptor\n  +0x04   4     pNext                   ptr           Link to next connection in list\n  +0x10   4     socket_copy             SOCKET        Duplicate socket for fd_set\n  +0x2c   0xbb  criticalSection         CRITICAL_SEC  Per-connection synchronization lock\n  +0xa8   4     bufferOffset            int           Current receive buffer offset\n  +0xb0   0x5b4 receiveBuffer           byte[1460]    Client message receive buffer\n  Total size: 0x668 bytes (1640 bytes)\nlpStartAddress parameter of CreateThread\n",
      "tags": ["CALLEE_24", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_ItemData", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "API_NETWORK", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "LIB_FOG_NET", "STRUCT_Skill", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "SRC_QServer98.cpp"]
