      "comment": "Initializes a TCP server socket for network communication and launches\nthe network acceptance thread.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set network mode flag (offset 0x884) to active (1)\n2. Create TCP socket (AF_INET=2, SOCK_STREAM=1, IPPROTO_TCP=0)\n3. Return 0 if socket creation fails\n4. Store socket handle in game context at offset 0xb90\n5. Configure TCP_NODELAY (disable Nagle buffering for responsiveness)\n6. Configure SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE (prevents socket address hijacking)\n7. Configure SO_REUSEADDR (allows socket rebinding after restart)\n8. Set non-blocking mode via FIONBIO ioctl (0x8004667e)\n9. Initialize sockaddr_in with AF_INET family, INADDR_ANY address\n10. Convert serverPort to network byte order via htons()\n11. Store port in game context at offset 0xba0\n12. Bind socket to INADDR_ANY:serverPort\n13. Return 0 if bind fails\n14. Call listen() with backlog of 25 connections\n15. Close socket and return 0 if listen fails\n16. Create auto-reset event for thread synchronization (offset 0xbd4)\n17. Create network acceptance thread (ServerConnectionHandlerThread)\n18. Store thread handle in game context at offset 0xbd8\n19. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT EDI - Game context pointer (pGameContext)\n  wServerPort (ushort) - TCP port number for server to listen on\n\nReturns:\n  1 = Success (socket initialized, thread created)\n  0 = Failure (socket creation, bind, or listen failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic values: 0x19 (25) is listen backlog, 0x8004667e is FIONBIO ioctl\n  Socket options applied in order: TCP_NODELAY, SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE, SO_REUSEADDR\n  Thread launched with game context (EDI) as LPVOID parameter\n\nStructure Layout (Game Context offsets):\n  Offset  Size  Field               Type      Description\n  0x884   4     dwNetworkModeActive uint      1=network active, 0=inactive\n  0xb90   4     hServerSocket       SOCKET    TCP server socket handle\n  0xba0   2     wServerPort         ushort    Server port (host byte order)\n  0xbd4   4     hThreadEvent        HANDLE    Auto-reset event for sync\n  0xbd8   4     hConnectionThread   HANDLE    Network acceptance thread\n  0xbe8   4     dwThreadId          uint      Thread ID output location\n\nCalled by: CreateQueueServer, InitializeNetworkMode\nCalls: socket, setsockopt, ioctlsocket, htons, bind, listen,\n       CloseSocket, CreateEventA, CreateThread",
