      "instructions": ["0x1BCC0|PUSH|ECX", "0x1BCC1|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6ff9af64]", "0x1BCC7|PUSH|EDI", "0x1BCC8|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x1BCCA|CMP|ECX, EDI", "0x1BCCC|JZ|0x6ff6bd35", "0x1BCCE|MOV|EAX, [0x6ff9af60]", "0x1BCD3|PUSH|EBX", "0x1BCD4|XOR|EBX, EBX", "0x1BCD6|CMP|EAX, EDI", "0x1BCD8|JBE|0x6ff6bd0f", "0x1BCDA|PUSH|EBP", "0x1BCDB|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [0x6ff7506c]", "0x1BCE1|PUSH|ESI", "0x1BCE2|LEA|ESI, [EDI + ECX*0x1]"],
      "comment": "Closes all async event handles and deallocates the associated resource pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_pEventSlotArray is NULL; if so, skip to step 8\n2. Cache the array pointer in pEventSlotArray\n3. Check if g_dwEventSlotCount is zero; if so, skip to step 7\n4. Initialize loop: dwSlotIndex=0, nByteOffset=0\n5. Loop through each slot:\n   a. Calculate phCurrentHandle = &pEventSlotArray->hEvent + nByteOffset\n   b. If handle pointer is non-NULL and handle value is non-NULL:\n      - Call CloseHandle() to release the OS resource\n      - Reload pEventSlotArray from global (may have changed)\n      - Zero out the handle slot\n   c. Increment dwSlotIndex by 1\n   d. Advance nByteOffset by 0xC (12 bytes per EventHandleSlot)\n   e. Continue while dwSlotIndex < g_dwEventSlotCount\n6. End loop\n7. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to free the pool memory\n8. Clear g_pEventSlotArray to NULL\n9. Clear g_dwEventSlotCount to 0\n10. Clear g_fAsyncIOEnabled to 0\n11. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global state only\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL array pointer: Only clears g_fAsyncIOEnabled flag\n- Zero slot count: Still deallocates the pool structure\n- NULL handle entries: Safely skipped without CloseHandle call\n- CloseHandle failures: Not checked; handles zeroed regardless\n\nStructure Layout (EventHandleSlot):\nOffset  Size  Field   Type    Description\n0x0     4     hEvent  HANDLE  Windows event handle\n0x4     4     field1  uint    Unknown field\n0x8     4     field2  uint    Unknown field\nTotal: 0xC (12) bytes per slot\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xC (12) - Stride per EventHandleSlot entry\n0xAE (174) - Pool element identifier for DeallocateResourcePoolElement",
