      "instructions": ["0x1BD40|MOV|EAX, [0x6ff9af5c]", "0x1BD45|PUSH|EBX", "0x1BD46|PUSH|EBP", "0x1BD47|PUSH|ESI", "0x1BD48|PUSH|EDI", "0x1BD49|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x1BD4B|CMP|EAX, EDI", "0x1BD4D|JZ|0x6ff6bdf8", "0x1BD53|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [0x6ff9af60]", "0x1BD59|XOR|EDX, EDX", "0x1BD5B|CMP|ECX, EDI", "0x1BD5D|JBE|0x6ff6bd71", "0x1BD5F|MOV|EAX, [0x6ff9af64]", "0x1BD64|CMP|dword ptr [EAX + 0x4], EDI", "0x1BD67|JNZ|0x6ff6bdda"],
      "comment": "Allocates or reuses an event handle slot from a global async event pool.\n\nManages a pool of pre-allocated and dynamically-created EventHandleSlot structures,\neach containing a Windows event handle. Implements a three-phase allocation strategy:\nfirst attempts to reuse inactive slots, then polls for signaled events that can be\nrecycled, and finally creates new slots if pool capacity allows.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_fAsyncIOEnabled flag - return NULL if async I/O not initialized\n2. Phase 1 - Inactive Slot Search: Iterate g_pEventSlotArray looking for bActive != 0\n3. If found, clear bActive to 0 and return pointer to that slot\n4. Phase 2 - Signaled Event Poll: Iterate slots calling WaitForSingleObject(hEvent, 0)\n5. If WAIT_OBJECT_0 returned, call CleanupResourcesAndResetContext, clear bActive, return slot\n6. Phase 3 - New Slot Creation: If g_dwEventSlotCount < 0x400 (1024 max):\n   a. Calculate new slot address: g_pEventSlotArray + g_dwEventSlotCount\n   b. Increment g_dwEventSlotCount\n   c. Call CreateEventA(NULL, bManualReset=1, bInitialState=0, NULL)\n   d. Store HANDLE in slot->hEvent, clear slot->bActive to 0\n   e. Return pointer to new slot\n7. Return NULL if pool at capacity\n\nParameters:\nNone (operates on globals: g_fAsyncIOEnabled, g_dwEventSlotCount, g_pEventSlotArray)\n\nReturns:\nEventHandleSlot* - Pointer to allocated slot structure (12 bytes), or NULL on failure\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field     Type       Description\n0x00    4     hEvent    HANDLE     Windows event handle for Wait operations\n0x04    4     bActive   DWORD      Activity flag (0=available, non-zero=in use)\n0x08    4     reserved  DWORD      Reserved/context data field\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Pool limit: Hard maximum of 0x400 (1024) event slots\n- Slot stride: Each EventHandleSlot is exactly 0xC (12) bytes\n- Manual reset events: All created events use bManualReset=1\n- Non-blocking poll: WaitForSingleObject uses 0ms timeout\n- Reuse priority: Inactive slots > Signaled slots > New allocation",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "CALLEE_2", "PARAM_0", "RET_STRUCT_PTR"]
