      "instructions": ["0x1C2A0|PUSH|ECX", "0x1C2A1|PUSH|ESI", "0x1C2A2|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1C2A4|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x1C2A6|JNZ|0x6ff6c2da", "0x1C2A8|CALL|0x6ff6c9f0", "0x1C2AD|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x1C2AF|CALL|0x6ff5cc86", "0x1C2B4|PUSH|ESI", "0x1C2B5|PUSH|0x6ff77284", "0x1C2BA|PUSH|0x295", "0x1C2BF|PUSH|0x6ff766a3", "0x1C2C4|PUSH|0x6", "0x1C2C6|CALL|0x6ff6dc10", "0x1C2CB|ADD|ESP, 0x14"],
      "comment": "Destroys a game entity and releases all associated resources\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pEntity pointer is non-null, exit fatally if null\n2. Load and validate entity magic number at offset +0x48, mask with 0xfffffff0\n3. Compare masked magic against 0x41737960, exit fatally if invalid\n4. Check entity linked flag (bit 3 of magic number)\n5. If linked, traverse global entity list at g_pEntityListHead until entity found\n6. Unlink entity by updating next pointer chain at offset +0x50\n7. Call ValidateContextAndWaitHandle to check for pending cleanup requirements\n8. If cleanup returned true, skip resource cleanup and proceed to pending check\n9. If cleanup returned false, call CloseHandle on handle at offset +0x3c\n10. If cleanup returned false, call WaitForSingleObject on resource at offset +0x38\n11. Call CleanupContextResourceAndReset to perform cleanup operations\n12. Check entity pending flag (bit 1 of magic number at offset +0x48)\n13. If pending flag set, validate context pointer at offset +0x3c is non-null, exit fatally if null\n14. If pending flag set, call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to destroy context\n15. If pending flag set, clear context pointer at offset +0x3c to 0\n16. If pending flag set, mask magic number to clear bits 4+ (keep only type in bits 0-3)\n17. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to deallocate entity structure itself\n18. Return (void return type)\n\nParameters:\npEntity: void * - Pointer to entity structure with layout:\n  +0x04: Reserved/state field\n  +0x38: Pointer to resource handle (HANDLE pointer)\n  +0x3c: Context pointer for cleanup operations\n  +0x48: Magic number with flags (0x41737960 masked with 0xfffffff0)\n         Bit 0-3: Entity type identifier\n         Bit 1: Pending cleanup flag\n         Bit 3: Linked in entity list flag\n  +0x50: Next entity pointer (linked list chain)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return if validation fails (calls _exit with status -1)\n       Returns normally only when validation succeeds and cleanup completes\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic validation: 0x41737960 is the valid entity magic number. The mask 0xfffffff0\nkeeps the high 28 bits but masks out the low 4 bits (entity type identifier).\nEntity linking: Entities can be linked in a global doubly-linked or singly-linked list.\nUnlink requires traversing from list head and updating pointer chain.\nContext cleanup: If pending flag is set, context MUST be non-null or causes fatal error.\nResource cleanup: Called twice - once for context, once for entity itself.\n\nStructure Layout (Entity at pEntity):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type        Description\n------  ----  -------                 -----       -----\n+0x00   0x04  reserved0               DWORD       Unknown/unused\n+0x04   0x04  stateFlags              DWORD       State/reserved flags\n+0x38   0x04  pResourceHandle         HANDLE*     Pointer to handle value\n+0x3C   0x04  pContext                void*       Context pointer for cleanup\n+0x48   0x04  magicAndFlags           DWORD       Magic (0x41737960) + type + flags\n+0x50   0x04  pNextEntity             void*       Next entity in linked list",
