      "comment": "Loads a file from the archive system into a newly allocated buffer context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Conditionally select pool node (use default if g_pDefaultResourcePool is set and pPoolNode is null)\n2. Allocate a FileLoadContext structure (0x54 bytes) from the resource pool\n3. Initialize the context structure (zero-fill 0x15 dwords, set magic 0x41737960)\n4. Open the file via OpenFileWithDefaultArchive\n5. If file offset specified, seek to position via SetFilePosition\n6. Determine file size (use provided or query via GetFileSize)\n7. Allocate data buffer if not pre-allocated (set dwBufferSize, mark ownership flag)\n8. Copy callback info if provided (7 dwords at offset 0x1C)\n9. If async mode requested and available, allocate event handle and read async\n10. Otherwise perform synchronous read and invoke callback if present\n11. Cleanup context and return pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pPoolNode (ECX) - Resource pool for allocations, or NULL to use default\n  szFilePath (EDX) - Path to file within archive\n  nFileOffset - Starting offset in file (0 for beginning)\n  dwFileSize - Size to read (0 to read entire file)\n  dwBufferSize - Pre-allocated buffer size hint\n  dwFlags - Processing flags for read operation\n  pCallbackInfo - Optional callback structure (7 dwords copied to context+0x1C)\n  pUserData - User data pointer stored at context+0x44\n  dwAllocLineNumber - Debug line number for allocation tracking\n  dwAllocFlags - Allocation flags for buffer\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to FileLoadContext on success (contains file handle, buffer, size info)\n  NULL on failure (file open failed, allocation failed, or async event unavailable)\n\nStructure Layout (FileLoadContext at EBP, 0x54 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x00    4     hFileHandle   File handle from OpenFileWithDefaultArchive\n  0x04    4     pPoolNode     Back-reference to resource pool\n  0x08    4     pEventSlot    Async event context (or local buffer pointer)\n  0x10    4     nFileOffset   Stored file offset for async reads\n  0x18    4     dwUnknown18   Copied from event slot\n  0x1C    28    abCallback    Callback info (7 dwords copied from pCallbackInfo)\n  0x38    4     pEventHandle  Event handle slot pointer\n  0x3C    4     pDataBuffer   Allocated data buffer pointer\n  0x40    4     dwDataSize    Size of data to read\n  0x44    4     pUserData     User data from parameter\n  0x48    4     dwStateFlags  State flags (bit 1 = buffer owned, magic = 0x41737960)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x54 (84)     - Size of FileLoadContext structure\n  0x15 (21)     - Number of dwords to zero-initialize\n  0x41737960    - Magic marker for valid context (\"Asy`\" reversed)\n  0x12D (301)   - Allocation tracking line for context\n  0x13A (314)   - Allocation tracking line for cleanup on error\n  0x147 (327)   - Error log line for seek failure\n  0x189 (393)   - Deallocation line for buffer\n  0x18B (395)   - Deallocation line for context\n\nError Handling:\n  - Returns NULL if context allocation fails (logs error with ReportError)\n  - Returns NULL if file open fails (deallocates context)\n  - Fatal error (ShutdownResourcesAndExit) if seek fails on valid file\n  - Returns NULL if async event slot unavailable (deallocates buffer and context)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "CALLEE_15", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "STRUCT_StatList", "API_NETWORK", "PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Path", "STRUCT_Skill", "SRC_AsyncData.cpp", "PARAM_10", "LIB_FOG_ASYNC"]
