      "comment": "Hash table lookup function that searches for a matching string hash and returns associated values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute hash value from input string using ComputeStringHash\n2. Check if hash table has entries (count at offset +4)\n3. If empty, jump to lookup_not_found\n4. Initialize entry pointer to table start (offset +8) and index counter to 0\n5. Enter loop: compare entry hash with computed hash value\n6. If match found, output value1 (offset +4) and value2 (offset +8) and return 0\n7. If no match, increment counter and advance pointer by 12 bytes (entry stride)\n8. Continue loop until counter reaches table entry count\n9. Return error code 0x16 (22) if no match found\n\nParameters:\n  pKeyString (char *) - Pointer to null-terminated string key to look up\n  pHashTable (int *) - Pointer to hash table structure containing:\n      Offset 0: Reserved/unused (2 dwords)\n      Offset +4: Number of entries in hash table\n      Offset +8: Array of hash table entries (each 12 bytes: hash, value1, value2)\n  pOutValue1 (int *) - Output pointer to receive first associated value\n  pOutValue2 (int *) - Output pointer to receive second associated value\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Successfully found matching entry and populated output values\n  0x16 (22) - No matching hash found in table\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic number 0x16 (22) is standard error code for \"not found\"\n  Entry stride is 12 bytes (3 dwords per entry)\n  Hash table entries are structured as: [hash_value][value1][value2]\n  Empty table (count=0) returns 0x16 immediately",
