      "comment": "Parses and validates a BOND-prefixed data structure from a buffer.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load remaining buffer size from pBytesRemaining parameter\\n2. Validate that remaining buffer is at least 8 bytes (minimum for BOND header)\\n3. Load the data pointer from pDataPointer parameter (pointer to pointer)\\n4. Load magic number from offset +0 and verify it matches BOND (0x444e4f42)\\n5. If magic invalid, return NULL immediately\\n6. Load element count from offset +0x4\\n7. Calculate required size: (count * 3) << 2 = count * 0xc bytes, plus 0x8 byte header = count*12 + 8\\n8. Validate calculated size is less than 0x401 (1025 bytes maximum allowed)\\n9. Validate calculated size does not exceed remaining buffer capacity\\n10. If any validation fails, return NULL\\n11. Calculate next structure pointer: base + (count * 12 + 8) bytes\\n12. Update pDataPointer to point to next structure\\n13. Decrement pBytesRemaining by the consumed size\\n14. Return pointer to the parsed BOND structure\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pDataPointer (ECX, __fastcall): Pointer to pointer to BOND data structure (IN/OUT parameter, updated to next element)\\n- pBytesRemaining (EDX, __fastcall): Pointer to remaining buffer size in bytes (IN/OUT parameter, decremented by parsed size)\\n\\nReturns:\\n- Success (EAX): Void pointer to the parsed BOND structure (original *pDataPointer value before update)\\n- Failure (EAX): NULL pointer if any validation check fails\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Returns NULL if remaining buffer has less than 8 bytes\\n- Returns NULL if BOND magic number does not match 0x444e4f42\\n- Returns NULL if calculated size exceeds 1024 bytes (hardcoded maximum)\\n- Returns NULL if calculated size exceeds available buffer space\\n- Structure Layout: BOND data format is [offset 0] = magic (0x444e4f42), [offset 4] = element count (DWORD), [offset 8+] = element array\\n- Element stride: Each element is 12 bytes (0xc bytes)\\n- Total structure size calculation: 8 byte header + (element_count * 12) bytes",
