      "comment": "Adds a hashed string entry to a collection with associated values.\n\nComputes a case-insensitive hash of the input string key and stores it\nalong with two user-defined values in the next available slot of the\ncollection's entry array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute case-insensitive hash of szStringKey via ComputeStringHash\n2. Load current entry count from pHashCollection->nEntryCount\n3. Calculate byte offset for new entry: (count * 12) + 0x14 header\n4. Check if adding entry would exceed 0x400 (1024) byte limit\n5. If collection full, return error code 0xE\n6. Store hash at aEntries[count].dwHash\n7. Store dwValue1 at aEntries[count].dwValue1\n8. Store dwValue2 at aEntries[count].dwValue2\n9. Increment nEntryCount\n10. Return 0 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  szStringKey (ECX)        - Null-terminated string to hash as entry key\n  dwValue1 (EDX)           - First user-defined value to associate with key\n  dwValue2 (Stack+0x4)     - Second user-defined value to associate with key\n  pHashCollection (Stack+0x8) - Pointer to HashedStringCollection structure\n\nReturns:\n  0     - Success, entry added to collection\n  0xE   - Error: Collection full (would exceed 0x400 byte limit)\n\nStructure Layout (HashedStringCollection):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Type                    Description\n  0x00    4     dwUnknown0   uint                    Reserved/unknown field\n  0x04    4     nEntryCount  uint                    Current number of entries\n  0x08    996   aEntries     HashedStringEntry[83]   Array of hash entries\n\nEntry Layout (HashedStringEntry, 12 bytes each):\n  Offset  Size  Field     Type  Description\n  0x00    4     dwHash    uint  Computed string hash\n  0x04    4     dwValue1  uint  First associated value\n  0x08    4     dwValue2  uint  Second associated value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x400 (1024) - Maximum collection size in bytes\n  0x14 (20)    - Header size before entry array\n  12           - Size of each HashedStringEntry\n  83           - Maximum entries: (1024 - 20) / 12\n\nCalling Convention: __fastcall\n  - szStringKey in ECX, dwValue1 in EDX\n  - dwValue2 and pHashCollection on stack\n  - Caller cleans stack (RET 0x8)",
