      "comment": "Strips the source file path prefix from file paths for error display.\n\nThis utility function calculates and removes a common source file path prefix from file paths,\ntypically used when displaying file information in error messages or logs. The prefix offset is\ncomputed once based on the difference between two baseline string path lengths and cached globally\nfor performance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if the path prefix offset has been initialized (cached in g_dwSourcePathPrefixOffset)\n2. If not initialized, compute the offset by getting the length difference between two baseline paths:\n   - szBaselineSourcePath: \"..\\Source\\Fog\\Src\\ErrorManager.cpp\" (source build path)\n   - szBaselineCompiledPath: \"Fog\\Src\\ErrorManager.cpp\" (compiled path)\n3. If the computed offset is negative, reset it to zero (indicates stripping not applicable)\n4. Measure the length of the input file path parameter\n5. If the input path length is greater than the cached prefix offset, return pointer advanced by the offset\n6. Otherwise, return the original pointer unchanged\n\nParameters:\n- pFilePath: Pointer to the file path string to process (passed in ECX via __fastcall)\n\nReturns:\n- char * - Pointer to the file path substring with common prefix removed, or original pointer if\n  stripping cannot be applied or input path is too short\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Prefix offset is computed only once and cached in g_dwSourcePathPrefixOffset for performance\n- If offset computation results in negative value (baseline source is shorter), offset is reset to 0\n- Paths shorter than or equal to the prefix offset are returned unmodified\n- Uses two hardcoded baseline path strings to determine offset dynamically",
