      "api_count": 2,
      "api_calls": ["CopyMemoryAndDetectTerminator", "CopyMemoryAndDetectTerminator"],
      "instructions": ["0x1CB90|SUB|ESP, 0x1c", "0x1CB93|PUSH|EBX", "0x1CB94|PUSH|EBP", "0x1CB95|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x28]", "0x1CB99|PUSH|EDI", "0x1CB9A|MOV|EBX, EAX", "0x1CB9C|PUSH|EBX", "0x1CB9D|PUSH|0x6ff77430", "0x1CBA2|PUSH|EBP", "0x1CBA3|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x1CBA5|CALL|0x6ff5ccb6", "0x1CBAA|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x30]", "0x1CBAE|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x34]", "0x1CBB2|PUSH|0x1c", "0x1CBB4|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x10]"],
      "comment": "Finds the PE section containing a given address within a module.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output parameters (sectionIndex and offsetInSection) to 0\n2. Call VirtualQuery to get memory information for the module\n3. If VirtualQuery fails, call the string function with szUnknownString parameter twice and return\n4. Verify the VirtualQuery result is valid\n5. If result is invalid, retrieve the module handle via GetModuleHandleA\n6. Call GetModuleFileNameA to get the module file path\n7. If GetModuleFileNameA fails, call the string function again and return\n8. Validate the module has a valid MZ header (0x5A4D signature)\n9. If not valid MZ, return without finding section\n10. Read PE header offset from module base + 0x3C\n11. Validate PE signature at calculated offset is 0x4550\n12. If not valid PE, return without finding section\n13. Extract section count from PE header at offset +0x6\n14. Extract optional header size from PE header at offset +0x14\n15. Calculate section table address: PE header + optional header size + 0x18\n16. Loop through each section comparing the target address against each section's range\n17. For each section, read VirtualSize and RawSize, use the larger value\n18. Check if target offset falls between section's RawOffset and RawOffset+Size\n19. If match found, store 1-based section index and offset within section to output pointers\n20. If no section found, return with output parameters unchanged\n\nParameters:\n  this (ECX): Context object pointer (implicit __thiscall parameter)\n  pModuleContext: Pointer to module context/memory information structure\n  pFilePath: Pointer to file path string buffer\n  pSectionIndex: Pointer to DWORD for storing result (1-based section index or 0 if not found)\n  pOffsetInSection: Pointer to DWORD for storing result (offset within the located section)\n\nReturns:\n  void (all results returned via output pointer parameters)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If VirtualQuery fails, function calls string function twice and returns\n  - If GetModuleFileNameA fails, function calls string function and returns\n  - Invalid MZ header (not 0x5A4D) causes immediate return with no section found\n  - Invalid PE header (not 0x4550) causes immediate return with no section found\n  - If target address doesn't fall in any section, returns with sectionIndex=0\n  - Section indices are 1-based (first section = 1, not 0)\n  - Uses maximum of VirtualSize and RawSize for section size calculation\n\nStructure Layout:\n  PE Section Entry (28 bytes each):\n    Offset 0x00: Section name (8 bytes)\n    Offset 0x08: VirtualSize (DWORD)\n    Offset 0x0C: VirtualAddress (DWORD)\n    Offset 0x10: RawSize (DWORD)\n    Offset 0x14: RawOffset (DWORD)\n    Offset 0x18-0x27: Additional PE section fields\n\n  Memory regions accessed:\n    Module base + 0x00: MZ header (0x5A4D expected)\n    Module base + 0x3C: PE header offset\n    PE header + 0x00: PE signature (0x4550 expected)\n    PE header + 0x06: Section count (WORD)\n    PE header + 0x14: Optional header size (WORD)",
