      "instructions": ["0x1D300|SUB|ESP, 0x10", "0x1D303|PUSH|ESI", "0x1D304|MOV|ESI, EAX", "0x1D306|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x1D308|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x4], ESI", "0x1D30C|JNZ|0x6ff6d315", "0x1D30E|POP|ESI", "0x1D30F|ADD|ESP, 0x10", "0x1D312|RET|0x4", "0x1D315|JGE|0x6ff6d31e", "0x1D317|LEA|EAX, [ESI + 0x1]", "0x1D31A|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x4], EAX", "0x1D31E|CMP|EBX, 0x2", "0x1D321|JLE|0x6ff6d32c", "0x1D323|LEA|ECX, [EBX + 0x1]"],
      "comment": "Calculate Julian Day Number offset for date calculations\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: return 0 if day value is zero\n2. Apply sign adjustment: add 1 for negative day values\n3. Calculate divisor based on month parameter:\n   - For months < 3 (Jan/Feb): use month + 13 (Zeller's congruence)\n   - For months >= 3 (Mar-Dec): use month + 1\n4. Apply day adjustment: subtract 1 for months < 3\n5. Perform FPU calculations:\n   a. divisor * g_dblMonthDays (~30.6 average days/month)\n   b. adjustedDay * g_dblDaysPerYear (365.25 days/year)\n6. Convert FPU result to 64-bit integer\n7. Check compound index against 0x8FC1D (589853 = leap year threshold)\n8. Apply correction factor if beyond threshold\n9. Return calculated offset value\n\nParameters:\nnDayValue [EAX, IMPLICIT]: Input day value (1-31)\nnMonthParam [EBX, IMPLICIT]: Month parameter (1-12, where Jan=1, Feb=2)\nqwBaseValue [ESI:EDI, IMPLICIT]: 64-bit base accumulator value\n\nReturns:\nEAX: Julian Day Number offset as signed 32-bit integer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0D (13) - Month adjustment for Jan/Feb (Zeller's congruence)\n0x0C (12) - Months per year multiplier\n0x1F (31) - Days per month multiplier (max)\n0x8FC1D (589853) - Leap year correction threshold\n\nGlobal Constants:\ng_dblMonthDays (0x6ff78f80): ~30.6 (average days per month)\ng_dblDaysPerYear (0x6ff78fd0): 365.25 (days per Julian year)\n\nRelated Functions:\nDeleteHistoricalFiles (caller) - Uses offset for log file retention",
