      "api_calls": ["FormatStringBuffer", "CopyMemoryAndDetectTerminator", "FormatStringBuffer", "FormatStringBuffer", "FormatStringBuffer", "FormatStringBuffer", "FormatStringBuffer"],
      "instructions": ["0x1D470|SUB|ESP, 0x39c", "0x1D476|PUSH|ESI", "0x1D477|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x1D479|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x1D47B|PUSH|EDI", "0x1D47C|MOV|EDI, ECX", "0x1D47E|JNZ|0x6ff6d485", "0x1D480|MOV|ESI, 0x6ff6cb60", "0x1D485|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x10]", "0x1D489|PUSH|EAX", "0x1D48A|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff75050]", "0x1D490|LEA|ECX, [ESP + 0xc]", "0x1D494|PUSH|ECX", "0x1D495|LEA|EDX, [ESP + 0x64]", "0x1D499|PUSH|EDX"],
      "comment": "Constructs and formats Diablo II game log header by collecting system information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate callback function pointer (ECX parameter); if null, use AppendPathComponentWithNewline\n2. Retrieve current system time via GetLocalTime() into SYSTEMTIME structure\n3. Get local user name via GetUserNameA() with 64-byte buffer; on failure, null-terminate first byte\n4. Get computer name via GetComputerNameA() with 64-byte buffer; on failure, null-terminate first byte\n5. Test version string (g_szVersionString) for empty/null\n6. If version string empty: call ImportTrampoline_Ordinal_501_JmpTarget for default path\n7. If version string present: format path via sprintf(pathBuffer, g_szVersionFormatString, g_szDiabloIIGameTitle, g_szVersionString)\n8. Format and output 5 log entries by invoking callback for each:\n   a. Program info line: sprintf with g_szProgramInfoFormat and versionPathBuffer\n   b. Computer name line: sprintf with g_szComputerNameFormat and computerNameBuffer\n   c. User name line: sprintf with g_szUserNameFormat and userNameBuffer\n   d. System time line: sprintf with g_szSystemTimeFormat and extracted WORD fields (year/month/day/hour/minute/second/milliseconds)\n   e. Separator line: sprintf with g_szLogSeparatorLine\n9. Invoke callback function (ESI = pCallbackFunction) for each formatted entry\n\nParameters:\npCallbackFunction (ECX): Pointer to callback function invoked for each formatted log line. Receives formatted text in logEntryBuffer. If null, uses AppendPathComponentWithNewline for path construction instead of direct callback.\npPathString (EDX): Pointer to optional path string. Used when version string is unavailable. If null, default path component is used.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. All output processed through callback function invocations.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Both GetUserNameA and GetComputerNameA can fail; failures result in empty strings via null-termination\n- Version string (g_szVersionString) determines conditional path formatting\n- All buffer sizes are fixed: userName 64 bytes, computerName 64 bytes, logEntryBuffer 512 bytes, versionPathBuffer 260 bytes\n- Stack allocation: 0x39c bytes (924 bytes) for all buffers and structures\n- System time extracted as individual WORD fields from SYSTEMTIME: wYear, wMonth, wDay, wHour, wMinute, wSecond, wMilliseconds\n- Callback invoked exactly 5 times with different formatted content (program, computer, user, time, separator)\n\nStructure Layout:\nSYSTEMTIME contains 8 WORD fields at offsets:\nOffset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n0x00    2     wYear           WORD    4-digit year value\n0x02    2     wMonth          WORD    1-12 month value\n0x04    2     wDayOfWeek      WORD    0-6 day of week (unused)\n0x06    2     wDay            WORD    1-31 day of month\n0x08    2     wHour           WORD    0-23 hour value\n0x0A    2     wMinute         WORD    0-59 minute value\n0x0C    2     wSecond         WORD    0-59 second value\n0x0E    2     wMilliseconds   WORD    0-999 milliseconds value",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "CALLER_3", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "CALLEE_6", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
