      "instructions": ["0x1D7F0|MOV|EAX, 0x1010", "0x1D7F5|CALL|0x6ff58270", "0x1D7FA|PUSH|EBX", "0x1D7FB|MOV|BL, byte ptr [ESP + 0x1018]", "0x1D802|TEST|BL, 0x4", "0x1D805|MOV|byte ptr [ESP + 0x14], 0x0", "0x1D80A|JZ|0x6ff6d846", "0x1D80C|LEA|EAX, [ESP + 0x4]", "0x1D810|PUSH|EAX", "0x1D811|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff75050]", "0x1D817|MOVZX|ECX, word ptr [ESP + 0x12]", "0x1D81C|MOVZX|EDX, word ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x1D821|MOVZX|EAX, word ptr [ESP + 0xe]", "0x1D826|PUSH|ECX", "0x1D827|MOVZX|ECX, word ptr [ESP + 0x10]"],
      "comment": "Formats and conditionally logs debug messages with optional timestamps and system state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 4KB (0x1000) stack buffer for message formatting\n2. If timestamp flag (bDebugFlags & 0x4) set, call GetLocalTime() to retrieve current system time\n3. Format timestamp as \"HH:MM:SS.mmm \" using __snprintf with szTimestampFormatString\n4. Scan buffer to find null terminator and calculate remaining buffer space\n5. Format variadic arguments using __vsnprintf with user format string\n6. Null-terminate the complete formatted message buffer\n7. If skip output flag (bDebugFlags & 0x2) NOT set, call OutputDebugStringA with buffer\n8. If network init flag (bDebugFlags & 0x1) set, call ValidateAndInitializeNetworkConfig\n9. If caps lock check flags (bDebugFlags & 0x18) set, call GetKeyState(VK_CAPITAL=0x14)\n10. Clean up 0x1010 (4112) bytes stack and return via __stdcall\n\nParameters:\nbDebugFlags (byte): Bit flags controlling function behavior\n  0x01: Enable network configuration initialization\n  0x02: Skip OutputDebugStringA (suppress debug output)\n  0x04: Prepend system timestamp to message\n  0x18: Check caps lock state via GetKeyState\nlpszFormatString (char*): Format string for variadic arguments (printf-style)\nvaArgs (va_list): Variable argument list for format string substitution\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value (__stdcall convention: callee cleans 0xc bytes from stack)\n\nFlag Bits:\n0x01 - DEBUG_FLAG_NETWORK_INIT: Trigger network configuration validation\n0x02 - DEBUG_FLAG_SUPPRESS_OUTPUT: Skip OutputDebugStringA call\n0x04 - DEBUG_FLAG_TIMESTAMP: Prepend HH:MM:SS.mmm timestamp\n0x08 - DEBUG_FLAG_CAPSLOCK_1: Part of caps lock check mask\n0x10 - DEBUG_FLAG_CAPSLOCK_2: Part of caps lock check mask\n0x18 - Combined caps lock check (0x08 | 0x10)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Timestamp format: \"%02d:%02d:%02d.%03d    \" (includes trailing spaces)\n- Buffer size: Fixed at 0x1000 (4096 bytes); risk of overflow if format exceeds this\n- Null-terminator scan: Manual loop using char-by-char comparison\n- Multiple flags: Can be active simultaneously; each checked independently\n- szLogPrefix at 0x6ff777b0 contains \"LOG\" string for config calls\n\nMemory Layout:\nOffset    Size    Field           Type\n-0x1010   16      systemTime      _SYSTEMTIME\n-0x1000   4092    szMessageBuffer char[4092]\n-0x4      4       uStack_4        uint (return address save)",
