      "comment": "Formats a debug message with variadic arguments and outputs it to the debugger and log system.\n\nUses __vsnprintf to safely format the message into a 4096-byte stack buffer, then outputs\nthe formatted string via OutputDebugStringA for debugger capture. Finally logs the message\nthrough the internal logging subsystem with \"LOG\" prefix.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Allocate 4096-byte stack buffer via __chkstk probe\n  2. Initialize buffer with null terminator at position 0\n  3. Calculate current string length using inline strlen loop\n  4. Format message into buffer using __vsnprintf with remaining space\n  5. Ensure null termination at buffer boundary (offset 0xFFF)\n  6. Output formatted message to debugger via OutputDebugStringA\n  7. Log message to internal log system via ValidateAndInitializeNetworkConfig\n\nParameters:\n  szFormatString - printf-style format string for message formatting\n  ...            - Variadic arguments matching format specifiers\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; outputs to debug console and log system\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Buffer overflow prevented by __vsnprintf size limit (0x1000 - current_len)\n  - Empty format string results in empty output\n  - Null terminator forced at szMessageBuffer[0xFFF] for safety\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x1000 (4096) - Stack buffer size for formatted message\n  0xFFF (4095)  - Maximum string index (buffer_size - 1)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size   Field            Type       Description\n  0x0     4096   szMessageBuffer  char[4096] Formatted message output buffer\n  0x1004  4      szFormatString   char*      Format string parameter (stack)\n  0x1008  N      varargs          ...        Variadic arguments on stack",
