      "comment": "Conditionally outputs a formatted debug string when Scroll Lock key is active.\n\nThis function provides a developer toggle for debug output by checking the Scroll Lock\nkey state. When active, formats the input string with variadic arguments and outputs\nthe result to the attached debugger via OutputDebugStringA.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 4KB stack buffer for formatted output\n2. Check Scroll Lock key state via GetAsyncKeyState(VK_SCROLL)\n3. If key is pressed (low bit set), proceed with output\n4. Initialize buffer and calculate string length using manual null-terminator scan\n5. Format the input string with variadic args using _vsnprintf into remaining buffer\n6. Null-terminate output buffer to ensure safety\n7. Output formatted string to debugger via OutputDebugStringA\n\nParameters:\n  szFormatString (char *) - Printf-style format string, followed by variadic arguments\n                            on stack at offset +0x8 and beyond\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; output is sent to debugger if Scroll Lock active\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x14 (VK_SCROLL) - Virtual key code for Scroll Lock\n  0x1000 (4096)    - Size of stack-allocated debug output buffer\n  0xFFFFFF         - Mask applied to return address (purpose unclear, possibly anti-debug)\n\nError Handling:\n  No explicit error handling. If Scroll Lock is not active, function exits immediately.\n  Buffer overflow is prevented by _vsnprintf size parameter.",
