      "instructions": ["0x1DC10|PUSH|EBP", "0x1DC11|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x1DC13|SUB|ESP, 0x8", "0x1DC16|PUSH|EBX", "0x1DC17|PUSH|ESI", "0x1DC18|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EBP + 0x8]", "0x1DC1B|CMP|ESI, 0xa", "0x1DC1E|PUSH|EDI", "0x1DC1F|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x4], 0x0", "0x1DC26|JNZ|0x6ff6dc35", "0x1DC28|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBP + 0xc]", "0x1DC2B|MOV|dword ptr [EBP + -0x4], EAX", "0x1DC2E|MOV|EDI, 0x6ff7718c", "0x1DC33|JMP|0x6ff6dc38", "0x1DC35|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [EBP + 0xc]"],
      "comment": "Log error with context information and optionally dump thread state.\n\nCentral error logging function (Fog.dll Ordinal_10028) that handles various\nerror severity levels, captures thread context, and triggers application\nshutdown for critical errors.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nErrorSeverity is 10 (0xA) - special thread context mode\n   a. If yes, store szSourceFile as hThreadHandle and use default source path\n   b. If no, use szSourceFile directly as the source file path\n2. Call InitializeNetworkErrorHandler to check for nested error handling\n3. If nested error detected, return immediately (avoid infinite recursion)\n4. Set g_dwLastError flag to 1 to indicate error handling in progress\n5. If szErrorMessage is NULL, substitute default \"<no reason given>\" string\n6. Call HandleFatalErrorWithMessage to format and log the error message\n7. Initialize g_ThreadContext structure (0x2CC bytes) with CONTEXT_FULL flags\n8. Capture thread context:\n   a. If hThreadHandle is valid, use GetThreadContext API\n   b. If NULL, manually capture EIP, ESP, EBP from current stack frame\n9. For severity levels 2, 5, 6, 7, 10 (critical errors):\n   a. Call LogErrorContextAndInitiateShutdown with stack/code context\n   b. Call DumpThreadCallStackWithSymbols for stack trace\n10. Check g_pfnErrorCallback and invoke if registered\n11. Log \"---finished error callback---\" message\n12. Call ShutdownResourcesAndExit for cleanup\n13. For non-critical severities (not 2, 5, 6), clear g_dwLastError flag\n\nParameters:\n  nErrorSeverity (int): Error severity level determining behavior:\n    - 2: Critical error with stack dump\n    - 5: Fatal error with stack dump\n    - 6: Fatal error with stack dump (most common)\n    - 7: Fatal error with stack dump\n    - 10 (0xA): Thread context error - szSourceFile is thread handle\n  szSourceFile (char *): Source file path or thread handle if severity is 10\n  dwErrorCode (uint): Numeric error code for logging (e.g., 0x160, 0x7c7)\n  szErrorMessage (char *): Error message format string, NULL uses default\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function may not return for fatal errors\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xA (10) - Special severity for thread context capture mode\n  0x10007 - CONTEXT_CONTROL | CONTEXT_INTEGER | CONTEXT_SEGMENTS flags\n  0x2CC (716) - Size of CONTEXT structure for x86\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_dwLastError (0x6ff9af48): Flag indicating error handling in progress\n  g_pfnErrorCallback (0x6ff9af44): Optional error callback function pointer\n  g_ThreadContext (0x6ff80808): Thread CONTEXT structure for debugging\n  g_dwErrorInstructionPtr (0x6ff808c0): Captured EIP at error time\n  g_dwErrorStackPtr (0x6ff808cc): Captured ESP at error time\n  g_dwErrorFramePtr (0x6ff808bc): Captured EBP at error time",
      "tags": ["CALLER_88", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_4", "SRC_ErrorManager.cpp", "LIB_FOG_ERROR", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData", "CALLEE_8"]
