      "comment": "Windows Unhandled Exception Filter callback for crash handling.\n\nRegistered via SetUnhandledExceptionFilter, this function handles fatal \nexceptions by logging comprehensive crash information, dumping the call \nstack with symbols, writing a crash dump file, and displaying an error \nmessage box to the user before shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Atomically increment reentrancy guard to prevent recursive exceptions\n2. If first entry (guard == 0):\n   a. Set global error flag to 1\n   b. Log separator and build Diablo log header\n   c. Translate exception code to human-readable message\n   d. Log exception type and fault address with PE section info\n   e. Log all CPU register values (EAX-EDI, EBP, ESP, EIP, flags)\n   f. Log segment registers (CS, DS, ES, SS, FS, GS)\n   g. Initiate error context logging and shutdown preparation\n   h. Duplicate current thread handle for stack walking\n   i. Dump complete thread call stack with debug symbols\n   j. Close duplicated thread handle\n   k. Write crash minidump file to disk\n   l. Call optional error callback if registered\n   m. Format and display MessageBox with exception details\n3. Decrement reentrancy guard\n4. Return EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER (1) to terminate process\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionInfo - Pointer to EXCEPTION_POINTERS containing:\n    [+0x00] EXCEPTION_RECORD* - Exception code, flags, fault address\n    [+0x04] CONTEXT* - CPU register state at exception point\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 1 (EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER) instructing Windows to \n  terminate the process after cleanup.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Reentrancy protection: If exception occurs during handler, skips to cleanup\n  - Optional callback: g_pfnErrorCallback invoked if non-NULL for custom handling\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x10b002d - Minidump type flags for WriteCrashDumpFile\n  0x30 - MB_ICONEXCLAMATION | MB_OK for MessageBoxA\n  0x100 - Buffer size for caption string (256 bytes)\n  0x1000 - Buffer size for message body (4096 bytes)\n\nStructure Layout (EXCEPTION_POINTERS):\n  Offset  Size  Field             Type               Description\n  0x00    4     ExceptionRecord   EXCEPTION_RECORD*  Exception details\n  0x04    4     ContextRecord     CONTEXT*           CPU register snapshot\n\nStructure Layout (CONTEXT offsets accessed):\n  0x9C    4     SegGs             DWORD              GS segment register\n  0xA0    4     SegFs             DWORD              FS segment register\n  0xA4    4     SegEs             DWORD              ES segment register\n  0xA8    4     SegDs             DWORD              DS segment register\n  0xAC    4     SegCs             DWORD              CS segment register\n  0xB0    4     SegSs             DWORD              SS segment register\n  0xB4    4     Edi               DWORD              EDI register\n  0xB8    4     Ebp               DWORD              EBP register\n  0xBC    4     Esi               DWORD              ESI register (logged at end)\n  0xC0    4     Eax               DWORD              EAX register\n  0xC4    4     Eip               DWORD              Instruction pointer\n  0xC8    4     EFlags            DWORD              CPU flags register",
      "tags": ["PROP_LARGE", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLEE_15", "CALLER_0", "PROP_NOCALLER", "STRUCT_Skill", "STRUCT_Room2", "PARAM_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
