      "api_calls": ["LogAppendFormat", "EnqueueLogMessage", "EnqueueLogMessage", "GetReturnAddress", "WSACleanup", "LogErrorWithContext"],
      "instructions": ["0x1E0E0|MOV|EAX, [0x6ff9af4c]", "0x1E0E5|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1E0E7|PUSH|ESI", "0x1E0E8|MOV|ESI, ECX", "0x1E0EA|JZ|0x6ff6e206", "0x1E0F0|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0x1E0F2|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x1E0F4|PUSH|EBX", "0x1E0F5|PUSH|EDI", "0x1E0F6|MOV|EAX, 0x1", "0x1E0FB|JZ|0x6ff6e185", "0x1E101|TEST|CL, 0x3", "0x1E104|MOV|EAX, 0x2", "0x1E109|JNZ|0x6ff6e185", "0x1E10B|CMP|ECX, 0x7fffffff"],
      "comment": "Validates integrity of a critical section container structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if Windows NT mode is enabled (g_fIsWindowsNT != 0)\n2. If not in NT mode, skip all validation and return immediately\n3. Load and validate primary pointer (maxCapacity field at +0x0):\n   - Must be non-null\n   - Must be 4-byte aligned (ptr & 3 == 0)\n   - Must be below 0x7FFFFFFF (valid user-mode address)\n4. Validate capacity field (+0x4): must be <= 10 or 0xFFFFFFFF sentinel\n5. Validate pData field (+0x8): must be <= 10\n6. Validate back-reference: nested structure at ptr+4 must point to container\n7. Validate nested pointer at ptr+8: non-null, aligned, valid address\n8. Validate nested pointer at ptr+0xC: non-null, aligned, valid address\n9. On any failure: log error, dump memory, and terminate process\n\nParameters:\npContainer (ECX) - Pointer to ContainerData structure to validate\n  [+0x0] maxCapacity: Primary pointer to nested structure\n  [+0x4] capacity: Count field (0-10 or 0xFFFFFFFF sentinel)\n  [+0x8] pData: Count field (must be <= 10)\ndwUnused (EDX) - IMPLICIT, not used in function body\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Returns normally on success, terminates process on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x7FFFFFFF - Maximum valid user-mode address boundary\n0xFFFFFFFF - Sentinel value bypassing capacity bounds check\n0x3        - Alignment mask (4-byte alignment check)\n10 (0xA)   - Maximum valid capacity/count value\n0x165      - Error code for unrecoverable internal error\n0x18       - Container structure dump size (24 bytes)\n0x20       - Nested structure dump size (32 bytes)\n\nError Handling:\nOn validation failure, logs \"FogValidateCriticalSection - bad critical section\"\nthen dumps both container and nested structures before terminating",
      "tags": ["API_NETWORK", "CALLER_78", "STRUCT_Act", "STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_2", "STRUCT_ItemData", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "STRUCT_Control", "CALLEE_7", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
