      "comment": "Gathers and displays comprehensive system diagnostics during game initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x115c (4444) bytes on stack for local buffers and structures\n2. Print decorative separator line via diagnostic output system\n3. Call GetLocalTime() to retrieve current system time\n4. Format and print timestamp (year-month-day hour:minute:second)\n5. Load OS type from g_dwOSType and dispatch via jump table (1-9)\n6. Copy appropriate OS version string based on detected OS type:\n   - Case 1: Windows 95 | Case 2: Windows 98 | Case 3: Windows ME\n   - Case 4: Windows NT | Case 5: Windows 2000 | Case 6: Windows XP\n   - Case 7: Windows .NET Server | Case 8: MacOS | Case 9: MacOS X\n   - Default: Unknown OS\n7. Load CPU speed from g_flVersionInfo and print OS info with version\n8. Call PrintCpuVendorAndVersion() for CPU vendor/model output\n9. Load physical memory from g_dwTotalPhysicalMemory\n10. Convert memory bytes to MB (multiply by 1/1024.0 scaling factor)\n11. Print total physical memory in MB\n12. Call ExtractModuleDirectory() to get application path (260-byte buffer)\n13. If path retrieval succeeds, print application path\n14. Call RetrieveLocalIPAddress() to get and print local IP\n15. Call GetComputerNameA() with 64-byte buffer for NetBIOS name\n16. If GetComputerName fails, clear buffer to empty string\n17. Print computer name and final separator line\n18. Call ValidateParameterOrShutdown() for cleanup\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - function performs diagnostic output only, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- OS type 0 or >9 defaults to \"unknown\" string\n- Memory value may need magic offset conversion for negative values\n- GetComputerName failure results in empty string output\n- Application path buffer: MAX_PATH (260 bytes)\n- Computer name buffer: MAX_COMPUTERNAME_LENGTH (64 bytes)\n\nCalled By:\nInitializeGameInstance (game startup sequence)\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- g_dwOSType: OS type identifier (1-9)\n- g_flVersionInfo: CPU speed in MHz (float)\n- g_dwTotalPhysicalMemory: Physical memory in bytes",
