      "comment": "Initializes the game instance and core system components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy command line arguments to internal buffers using CopyMemoryAndDetectTerminator\n2. Check if already initialized via g_fSystemInitialized flag - return early if set\n3. If previous instance exists and system initialized, call ReportError and exit\n4. Zero-initialize OSVERSIONINFOA structure (0x94 bytes / 37 DWORDs) on stack\n5. Call GetVersionExA to detect Windows version information\n6. Set g_fIsWindowsNT flag to 1 if dwMajorVersion equals 2 (Windows NT family)\n7. Initialize two critical sections (g_csResourceLock, g_csMemoryLock) for thread sync\n8. Set g_fSystemInitialized to 1 to mark core initialization complete\n9. Call InitializeGameState to set up core game subsystem\n10. Parse configuration value using ParseConfigurationValue and store in g_dwDebugFlags\n11. Initialize memory pool allocator with 256KB primary and 32KB secondary sizes\n12. Set unhandled exception filter to custom handler for crash recovery\n13. Call DetectSystemConfiguration for hardware and system detection\n14. Validate bit patterns in configuration tables across 32 iterations\n15. Call InitializeDebugSymbolHandler and InitializeGameValidation subsystems\n16. If lpCmdLine is non-null, call ReportError for command line processing\n17. Initialize performance counters via AddToDynamicBufferWithErrorCode\n18. Store instance handle in global and call InitializeMemoryPoolAllocator\n\nParameters:\n  hInstance     - HINSTANCE - Application instance handle from WinMain entry point\n  hPrevInstance - HINSTANCE - Previous instance handle (obsolete Win16, used for reentry check)\n  lpCmdLine     - LPSTR - Command line string pointer, triggers debug mode if non-null\n  nCmdShow      - int - Window show state from WinMain (unused in this initialization)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No explicit return value\n  Exits process with code -1 on bit validation failure (error 947 or 948)\n\nError Handling:\n  Calls ShutdownResourcesAndExit(-1) on configuration table validation failure\n  Uses SetUnhandledExceptionFilter to install custom crash handler at 0x6ff6de50\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x104    - MAX_PATH (260) buffer size for command line copy operations\n  0x94     - sizeof(OSVERSIONINFOA) = 148 bytes\n  0x25     - 37 DWORDs to zero-initialize (148 / 4 = 37)\n  0x40000  - Memory pool primary allocation size (262144 bytes = 256KB)\n  0x8000   - Memory pool secondary allocation size (32768 bytes = 32KB)\n  0x20     - 32 iterations for bit validation loop (one per bit position)\n  0x3b3    - Error code 947 for positive bit table validation failure\n  0x3b4    - Error code 948 for negative bit table validation failure",
