      "comment": "Selects a pointer from a lookup table based on the first non-zero byte in a packed index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dwPackedByteIndex is zero, return -1 if so (invalid index)\n2. Check byte 0 (bits 0-7): If non-zero, look up pointer at g_apnByteIndexToPointerTable[byte0]\n3. Check byte 1 (bits 8-15): If non-zero, look up pointer and add offset 0x8\n4. Check byte 2 (bits 16-23): If non-zero, look up pointer and add offset 0x10\n5. Check byte 3 (bits 24-31): If non-zero, look up pointer and add offset 0x18\n6. Return -1 if all bytes are zero\n\nParameters:\n  dwPackedByteIndex - Packed 32-bit value containing up to 4 byte indices; the first\n                      non-zero byte (starting from LSB) determines which table entry\n                      to retrieve and what offset to apply\n\nReturns:\n  int - Pointer value from lookup table plus byte-position offset (0x0, 0x8, 0x10, 0x18)\n        Returns -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) if dwPackedByteIndex is 0 or all bytes are zero\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8  - Offset for byte 1 (8 bits from base pointer)\n  0x10 - Offset for byte 2 (16 bits from base pointer)  \n  0x18 - Offset for byte 3 (24 bits from base pointer)\n\nStructure:\n  g_apnByteIndexToPointerTable - 256-entry pointer lookup table (1024 bytes)\n                                  indexed by byte value 0x00-0xFF",
