      "comment": "Computes a rolling checksum over a byte buffer using left-rotation with carry.\n\nThe algorithm processes each byte sequentially, maintaining an accumulating checksum\nthat is left-shifted by 1 bit before adding each new byte value. If the previous\nchecksum was negative (sign bit set), a carry of 1 is added to the new byte value\nbefore accumulation. This creates a position-sensitive hash where byte order matters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize checksum accumulator to 0 and byte index to 0\n2. Return 0 immediately if buffer length is <= 0 (empty buffer check)\n3. For each byte in the buffer (index 0 to nBufferLength-1):\n   a. Read the byte at current index from pBuffer\n   b. Determine carry bit: 1 if current checksum is negative, else 0\n   c. Add carry to the byte value\n   d. Compute new checksum: (checksum * 2) + byte + carry (left rotate with carry)\n   e. Increment byte index\n4. Return final accumulated checksum value\n\nParameters:\n  pBuffer (byte*) - Pointer to the input byte buffer to checksum. Must be valid\n                    for nBufferLength bytes. NULL not explicitly checked.\n  nBufferLength (int) - Number of bytes to process. If <= 0, returns 0.\n\nReturns:\n  uint - The computed checksum value. Returns 0 for empty or zero-length buffers.\n         The result is position-sensitive; different byte orderings produce\n         different checksums.",
