      "comment": "Extracts a variable-length sequence of bits from a bit-stream decoder context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate available bits: (nWordIndex * 8 - nByteIndex) + nBitOffset + nNumBits\n2. If result is negative, clamp overflow amount to 0 and set dwOverflowFlag\n3. Compute actual bits to extract: nNumBits - overflow\n4. Initialize accumulator (dwAccumulatedBits = 0) and output shift position (nOutputShift = 0)\n5. Loop while nBitsRemaining > 0:\n   a. Read current nBitOffset from pDecoder[3]\n   b. Calculate available bits in current byte: nBitsAvailable = 8 - nBitOffset\n   c. Determine bits to extract this iteration: min(nBitsAvailable, nBitsRemaining)\n   d. Read byte from pDecoder[0] pointer\n   e. Apply g_abBitOffsetMasks[nBitOffset] to mask bits from current position\n   f. Shift right by nBitOffset to align extracted bits to bit 0\n   g. Apply g_adwBitWidthMasks[nBitsToExtract] to mask exact width needed\n   h. Shift left by nOutputShift and accumulate into result\n   i. Update nBitOffset, advance nOutputShift by bits extracted\n   j. If nBitOffset reaches 8: advance pCurrentByte, reset nBitOffset, increment nWordIndex\n6. Return accumulated bit value\n\nParameters:\nnNumBits (int, Stack[0x4]): Number of bits to extract from stream (typically 1-32)\nIMPLICIT pDecoder (BitStreamDecoder*, ESI): Pointer to decoder context structure:\n  +0x00: pCurrentByte  - Pointer to current byte in encoded buffer\n  +0x04: nByteIndex    - Consumed byte count (for bounds checking)\n  +0x08: nWordIndex    - Total bytes processed (incremented at byte boundaries)\n  +0x0C: nBitOffset    - Bit position within current byte (0-7)\n  +0x10: dwOverflowFlag - Set to 1 if requested bits exceed available space\n\nReturns:\nuint: Extracted bit value, right-aligned in 32-bit integer\n\nLookup Tables:\ng_abBitOffsetMasks (0x6ff77014): byte[8] = {0xFF,0xFE,0xFC,0xF8,0xF0,0xE0,0xC0,0x80}\n  Masks bits starting at position N through bit 7\n\ng_adwBitWidthMasks (0x6ff76ff0): uint[9] = {0,1,3,7,0xF,0x1F,0x3F,0x7F,0xFF}\n  Masks exactly N bits (0-8)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Overflow detection: Sets pDecoder[4] = 1 when buffer exhausted\n- Byte boundary: Automatically advances pointer when 8 bits consumed\n- Bit ordering: LSB-first extraction, accumulated from low bits to high",
