      "comment": "XORs two memory regions byte-by-byte and stores result in destination buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate number of DWORD-aligned iterations from byte count\n  2. Process bulk data in DWORD (4-byte) XOR operations for performance\n  3. Handle 0-3 remainder bytes via individual byte XOR operations (tail processing)\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceBuffer1 (byte*): First source buffer to XOR\n  pSourceBuffer2 (byte*): Second source buffer to XOR against\n  pDestBuffer (byte*): Destination buffer for XOR result\n  dwByteCount (uint): Number of bytes to process\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result stored directly in pDestBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero-length input: No processing performed\n  - Unaligned sizes: Handled via byte-wise tail loop (1-3 bytes)\n\nPerformance Notes:\n  - Uses DWORD-aligned XOR for bulk processing (4 bytes per iteration)\n  - Fall-through switch handles 1, 2, or 3 remainder bytes efficiently",
