      "comment": "Performs bitwise OR operation combining two byte buffers with bit-field precision.\nThe function processes data in dword-aligned chunks for efficiency, then handles\nany remaining bytes individually.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Round nBitCount up to nearest byte boundary: (nBitCount + 7) / 8\n2. Round byte count up to nearest 4-byte (dword) boundary for aligned processing\n3. Process full dwords in loop: load from pbSrc2, OR with pbSrc1, store to pbDst\n4. Calculate remainder bytes: nByteCount modulo 4 (partial bytes after dword processing)\n5. Handle remainder bytes (1, 2, or 3) using cascading byte operations\n\nParameters:\npbSrc1 (byte*): First source buffer, base for offset calculations\npbSrc2 (byte*): Second source buffer, reference base for pointer math\npbDst (byte*): Destination buffer, receives bitwise OR result of both sources\nnBitCount (int): Total number of bits to process, determines byte counts and remainder\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies pbDst in place with OR'd values from both source buffers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses register-relative addressing for pointer math (pbSrc1 - pbSrc2 offset)\n- Handles non-byte-aligned bit counts by rounding to full bytes\n- Processes remainder bytes in descending order (3 bytes down to 1 byte)\n- Zero bit count results in no operation (early exit)",
