      "instructions": ["0x1F070|TEST|ESI, ESI", "0x1F072|JZ|0x6ff6f0da", "0x1F074|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x110]", "0x1F07A|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1F07C|JZ|0x6ff6f0da", "0x1F07E|CMP|dword ptr [EAX], 0x0", "0x1F081|JZ|0x6ff6f0da", "0x1F083|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EAX + 0x8]", "0x1F086|TEST|ECX, ECX", "0x1F088|JZ|0x6ff6f0da", "0x1F08A|PUSH|EDI", "0x1F08B|LEA|EDI, [EAX + 0xc]", "0x1F08E|MOV|EDX, 0x119", "0x1F093|MOV|ECX, EDI", "0x1F095|CALL|0x6ff6e0e0"],
      "comment": "Closes an active network socket and resets connection state.\n\nCalled when shutting down network receive operations to cleanly release socket resources\nand clear connection flags. Uses critical section for thread-safe access.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate connection context (ESI) is non-null\n2. Get connection state pointer from context+0x110\n3. Verify connection state is initialized (state[0] != 0)\n4. Verify socket handle is valid (state[2] != 0, i.e., offset 0x8)\n5. Validate and enter critical section at state+0xC\n6. Close the socket via ProcessInventoryItem (closesocket wrapper)\n7. Clear socket handle field (state+0x8 = 0)\n8. Clear connection initialized flag (state+0x0 = 0)\n9. Leave critical section\n10. Return\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ESI (void*): Pointer to connection context structure containing:\n  - Offset 0x110: Pointer to connection state structure\n\nConnection State Structure Layout (at context+0x110):\nOffset  Size  Field              Description\n0x00    4     dwInitialized      Non-zero when connection active\n0x08    4     hSocket            SOCKET handle for network I/O\n0x0C    24    csSocketLock       CRITICAL_SECTION protecting socket\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Silent no-op if context is NULL or connection not initialized\n- Socket handle cleared to 0 to prevent double-close\n- Thread-safe via critical section around socket operations\n- Called from ReceiveNetworkDataLoop on shutdown or error",
      "tags": ["API_NETWORK", "STRUCT_Inventory", "CALLER_1", "PARAM_0", "CALLEE_4"]
