      "comment": "Marks a network resource as requiring update/processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate ESI context pointer (implicit parameter from caller)\n2. Retrieve NetworkResourceContext pointer from [ESI + 0x110]\n3. Validate resource context and its critical section field at offset 0x24\n4. Set pending flag at [ESI + 0x124] to 1\n5. Acquire critical section at [resource + 0xc] via ValidateCriticalSection and EnterCriticalSection\n6. Set dirty flag at [resource + 0x2c] to 1\n7. Release critical section via LeaveCriticalSection\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ESI - Pointer to parent context structure containing NetworkResourceContext at offset 0x110\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if ESI is NULL\n  - Early exit if [ESI + 0x110] (resource pointer) is NULL\n  - Early exit if [resource + 0x24] (critical section initialized flag) is 0\n\nStructure Layout (Parent Context accessed via ESI):\n  Offset   Size   Field                    Type                      Description\n  0x110    4      pNetworkResource         NetworkResourceContext*   Pointer to network resource\n  0x124    4      fPendingUpdate           uint                      Flag set when resource marked dirty\n\nStructure Layout (NetworkResourceContext):\n  Offset   Size   Field                    Type                      Description\n  0x0C     24     criticalSection          CRITICAL_SECTION          Thread synchronization\n  0x24     4      fCriticalSectionValid    uint                      Non-zero if CS initialized\n  0x2C     4      fDirty                   uint                      Set to 1 when resource modified\n\nThread Safety:\n  Uses EnterCriticalSection/LeaveCriticalSection for thread-safe flag update",
      "tags": ["CALLER_2", "PARAM_0", "CALLEE_3"]
