      "instructions": ["0x1F190|PUSH|ECX", "0x1F191|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x8]", "0x1F195|PUSH|EBP", "0x1F196|PUSH|ESI", "0x1F197|PUSH|EDI", "0x1F198|MOV|ESI, EDX", "0x1F19A|LEA|EBX, [EBX]", "0x1F1A0|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EBX + 0x11c]", "0x1F1A6|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x18]", "0x1F1AA|MOVZX|EDI, word ptr [ECX + ESI*0x1]", "0x1F1AE|MOV|ECX, dword ptr [EBX + 0x118]", "0x1F1B4|MOV|EAX, EDX", "0x1F1B6|SUB|EAX, ESI", "0x1F1B8|ADD|EAX, EBP", "0x1F1BA|CMP|EAX, ECX"],
      "comment": "Processes received network packets from the receive buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize buffer position pointer to start of received data\n2. Loop while unprocessed data remains in buffer:\n   a. Read 2-byte packet size header from current position\n   b. Validate packet size against buffer bounds and minimum size threshold\n   c. If packet size exceeds maximum (0x2064), report error and shutdown\n   d. Validate packet callback function pointer via IsBadCodePtr\n   e. If callback invalid, report error and shutdown\n   f. Call packet handler callback with packet data and context\n   g. Signal completion event via SetEvent\n   h. Advance buffer position by packet size\n3. Copy any remaining partial packet data to buffer start using MOVSD/MOVSB\n\nParameters:\n  pRecvBuffer (byte*) - Pointer to network receive buffer containing raw packet data\n  nBytesReceived (int) - Total number of bytes received in this batch\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Packet size >= 0x2064 triggers fatal error (ReportError, WSACleanup, ShutdownResourcesAndExit)\n  - Invalid callback pointer triggers same fatal error path\n  - Partial packets at buffer end are preserved via memory copy for next receive\n\nStructure Layout (Network Context at EBX):\n  Offset  | Size | Field            | Description\n  --------|------|------------------|----------------------------------\n  +0x114  | 4    | hCompletionEvent | Event handle signaled after packet\n  +0x118  | 4    | nMinPacketSize   | Minimum valid packet size\n  +0x11c  | 4    | pPacketSizeTable | Pointer to packet size lookup\n  +0x168  | 4    | pfnPacketHandler | Callback for packet processing\n  +0x16c  | 4    | pHandlerContext  | Context passed to callback\n  +0x170  | ?    | packetWorkBuffer | Working buffer for packet data\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2064 - Maximum allowed packet size\n  0xB5, 0xBB - Error line numbers for ReportError calls\n\nError Handling:\n  - Oversized packets: Log error at line 0xB5, cleanup and exit\n  - Bad callback ptr: Log error at line 0xBB, cleanup and exit",
      "tags": ["API_NETWORK", "PARAM_2", "CALLER_1", "PROP_LOOPHEAVY", "STRUCT_Control", "CALLEE_7"]
