      "comment": "Sends data to a connection's socket in a thread-safe manner.\n\nValidates the connection and socket before sending. Uses a critical\nsection to ensure thread safety during the send operation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate connection pointer is non-null\n2. Get socket structure from connection at offset 0x110\n3. Validate socket pointer and socket state (first dword != 0)\n4. Enter critical section at socket offset 0xC\n5. If data buffer and size are valid, send data via SendDataToSocket\n6. Leave critical section\n7. Return true if all bytes were sent, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\npConnection - Pointer to ClientConnection structure with socket at +0x110\nlpszData    - Pointer to data buffer to send\nwDataSize   - Number of bytes to send (max 65535)\n\nReturns:\ntrue  - All bytes were successfully sent (wDataSize == wBytesSent)\nfalse - Connection/socket invalid, or partial/failed send\n\nError Handling:\nReturns false immediately if pConnection is NULL, socket pointer at\npConnection+0x110 is NULL, or socket state (first dword) is 0.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x110 - Offset to socket pointer within connection structure\n0xC   - Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION within socket structure\n0x1C9 - Critical section validation code (457 decimal)",
