      "instructions": ["0x1F3F0|MOV|EAX, 0x2068", "0x1F3F5|CALL|0x6ff58270", "0x1F3FA|PUSH|EBP", "0x1F3FB|MOV|EBP, dword ptr [ESP + 0x2070]", "0x1F402|TEST|EBP, EBP", "0x1F404|JZ|0x6ff6f52b", "0x1F40A|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBP + 0x110]", "0x1F410|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1F412|JZ|0x6ff6f52b", "0x1F418|CMP|dword ptr [EAX], 0x0", "0x1F41B|JZ|0x6ff6f52b", "0x1F421|CMP|dword ptr [EBP + 0x118], 0x4", "0x1F428|PUSH|EBX", "0x1F429|PUSH|ESI", "0x1F42A|PUSH|EDI"],
      "comment": "Sends data through a socket connection with a length-prefixed header.\n\nValidates the context and its socket pointer before sending. Supports two packet\nformats based on context type flags at offsets 0x118 and 0x11c:\n- Type (4,2): Prepends 4-byte header containing prefix byte from context+0x120 and first data byte\n- Other types: Prepends 2-byte length header\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pContext is non-null and has valid socket pointer at offset 0x110\n2. Check context type flags at offsets 0x118 and 0x11c\n3. For type (4,2) contexts:\n   a. Validate data pointer and length (must be 1-0x205F bytes)\n   b. Copy payload data to stack buffer (length-1 bytes)\n   c. Build 4-byte header: [prefix byte from context+0x120][first data byte][adjusted length]\n   d. Total packet size = original length + 3\n4. For other context types:\n   a. Calculate total length = data length + 2\n   b. Validate total length < 0x2064\n   c. Copy 2-byte length header to buffer\n   d. Copy source data after header if present\n5. Call Ordinal_10007 (SendDataToSocket) to send the packet\n6. Return true if bytes sent equals expected total length\n\nParameters:\n  pContext - Pointer to socket context structure containing:\n             +0x110: Socket object pointer (must be non-null with valid socket)\n             +0x118: Context type field (checked for value 4)\n             +0x11c: Context subtype field (checked for value 2)\n             +0x120: Packet prefix byte for type (4,2) contexts\n  pbData   - Pointer to data buffer to send (may be NULL for empty packets)\n  wDataLen - Length of data in bytes (max 0x205F for type 4,2; 0x2061 for others)\n\nReturns:\n  true  - All bytes were successfully sent\n  false - Context validation failed or send operation failed\n\nError Handling:\n  Calls CleanupAndAbort with line 0x3A (58) for type (4,2) validation failures\n  Calls CleanupAndAbort with line 0x4E (78) for length overflow in other types\n  Does not return after calling ReportError(-1)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2060 - Maximum data length for type (4,2) contexts\n  0x2064 - Maximum total packet length for other context types\n  0x3A   - Error line for type (4,2) data validation failure (58 decimal)\n  0x4E   - Error line for packet length overflow (78 decimal)",
