      "instructions": ["0x1F5A0|MOV|EAX, 0x2068", "0x1F5A5|CALL|0x6ff58270", "0x1F5AA|PUSH|EBX", "0x1F5AB|MOV|EBX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x2070]", "0x1F5B2|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBX + 0x110]", "0x1F5B8|PUSH|EBP", "0x1F5B9|PUSH|ESI", "0x1F5BA|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x1F5BC|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1F5BE|PUSH|EDI", "0x1F5BF|JNZ|0x6ff6f5ec", "0x1F5C1|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [0x6ff75014]", "0x1F5C7|JMP|0x6ff6f5d0", "0x1F5D0|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBX + 0x124]", "0x1F5D6|TEST|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Receives network data from a socket in a continuous loop, parsing and processing received packets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x2068 (8292) byte receive buffer on stack via __chkstk\n2. Load connection state pointer from pConnectionContext+0x110\n3. Spin-wait with Sleep(0) until connection state is initialized (non-null)\n4. Check shutdown flag at pConnectionContext+0x124; if set, exit immediately\n5. Verify connection validity: state pointer non-null, error flags at +0x2C and +0x30 are zero\n6. Call CheckSocketReadiness() to verify socket can receive data\n7. Re-validate state after setup call to handle race conditions\n8. If socket ready, enter main receive loop:\n   a. Load current connection state from pConnectionContext+0x110\n   b. Validate critical section at state+0x0C using ValidateCriticalSection(0x183)\n   c. Acquire critical section via EnterCriticalSection for thread-safe socket access\n   d. Call recv() on socket (state+0x08) to read up to (0x2064 - nBufferOffset) bytes\n   e. Release critical section via LeaveCriticalSection\n   f. If recv returned error (<=0), store WSAGetLastError() at state+0x34 and set error flag 4 at state+0x30\n   g. Check error status at state+0x30; if non-zero or recv returned 0, exit loop\n   h. Call ProcessReceivedNetworkPackets() to parse and dispatch received data\n   i. If dwBytesReceived < dwRemainingCapacity, exit inner loop (partial buffer fill)\n   j. Otherwise check shutdown flag and continue receiving\n9. Exit main loop when shutdown flag set, error detected, or connection closed\n10. Call CloseNetworkSocket() for cleanup before returning\n11. Return 0 (success)\n\nParameters:\npConnectionContext (ClientConnection *): Pointer to connection context structure containing:\n  - Offset 0x08: SOCKET handle for recv() operations\n  - Offset 0x0C: CRITICAL_SECTION (24 bytes) protecting socket access\n  - Offset 0x110: Pointer to connection state/initialization data\n  - Offset 0x124: Shutdown flag (non-zero = terminate loop and exit)\n\nConnection State Structure Layout (at pConnectionContext+0x110):\n  Offset  Size  Field            Description\n  0x00    4     dwInitMarker     State initialization marker (non-zero = initialized)\n  0x08    4     hSocket          SOCKET handle for network I/O\n  0x0C    24    csSocketLock     CRITICAL_SECTION for thread synchronization\n  0x2C    4     dwErrorFlag      Flag indicating error/invalid state (non-zero = error)\n  0x30    4     dwStatusCode     Status code (0=ok, 4=recv error)\n  0x34    4     dwWsaError       WSA error code from WSAGetLastError()\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 0 (success) - actual errors stored in connection state structure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Initial spin-wait loop runs indefinitely until connection initialized (no timeout)\n- Critical section serializes all socket recv() operations across threads\n- Fixed buffer size 0x2064 (8292) bytes determines maximum data per recv() call\n- Loop exits on: shutdown flag set, recv error, recv returns 0, or incomplete buffer fill\n- WSA error codes stored at state+0x34 for error diagnostics by caller\n- Inner loop continues reading only if buffer completely filled (recv == remaining capacity)",
