      "comment": "Thread worker function for game state processing initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load game state context pointer from stack parameter (offset +0x8 due to PUSH ESI prologue)\n2. Extract processing function pointer from game state context at offset 0x10c\n3. Prepare callback function reference (ReceiveNetworkDataLoop at 0x6ff6e9c0)\n4. Calculate memory addresses for substructures:\n   - Worker context substructure at context + 0x8\n   - Data buffer reference at context + 0x128\n5. Call InitializeSocketConnection with six parameters:\n   - Worker context (context + 0x8)\n   - Function pointer from context[0x10c]\n   - Callback handler (ReceiveNetworkDataLoop)\n   - Game state context (pGameState)\n   - Data buffer address (context + 0x128)\n   - Cleanup flag (0)\n6. Store InitializeSocketConnection result at context offset 0x110\n7. Return 1 (thread exit code indicating successful completion)\n\nParameters:\npGameState: Pointer to game state structure created by CreateThread in InitializeGameThreadState\n  Offset 0x0:   HANDLE hThreadHandle - Thread handle returned by CreateThread\n  Offset 0x4:   DWORD dwThreadId - Thread ID assigned by CreateThread\n  Offset 0x8:   void* pWorkerContext - Substructure passed to InitializeSocketConnection\n  Offset 0x10c: void* pfnProcessor - Function pointer for processing logic\n  Offset 0x110: void* pProcessingResult - Output: result from InitializeSocketConnection\n  Offset 0x114: HANDLE hSyncEvent - Event handle for synchronization (created in InitializeGameThreadState)\n  Offset 0x124: DWORD dwStateFlag - State initialization flag (cleared at start)\n  Offset 0x128: void* pDataBuffer - Data buffer address for processing\n\nReturns:\nuint - Always returns 1 (Windows thread worker exit code for successful completion)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This function is a thread worker entry point (LPTHREAD_START_ROUTINE callback)\n- Created by CreateThread in InitializeGameThreadState with pGameState as context\n- Return value