      "instructions": ["0x1F8D0|PUSH|EBP", "0x1F8D1|LEA|EBP, [EBX + 0x4]", "0x1F8D4|PUSH|EDI", "0x1F8D5|MOV|EDX, 0x68", "0x1F8DA|MOV|ECX, EBP", "0x1F8DC|CALL|0x6ff6e0e0", "0x1F8E1|PUSH|EBP", "0x1F8E2|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff7504c]", "0x1F8E8|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBX + 0x1c]", "0x1F8EB|TEST|EAX, EAX", "0x1F8ED|JZ|0x6ff6f958", "0x1F8EF|MOV|CX, word ptr [EAX]", "0x1F8F2|CMP|CX, word ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x1F8F7|PUSH|ESI", "0x1F8F8|JBE|0x6ff6f904"],
      "comment": "Dequeues the first element from a thread-safe linked list queue, copies its payload data to the destination buffer, and deallocates the node back to the resource pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate critical section structure integrity via ValidateCriticalSection (param 0x68)\n2. Enter critical section to acquire exclusive lock on the linked list\n3. Load list head pointer from context block at offset +0x1c\n4. If list is empty (head == NULL), return 0 without error\n5. Read node data size from first word of node header (offset +0x0)\n6. Compare node size against destination buffer capacity (dwBufferSize)\n7. If buffer too small: set error flag at context+0x0, return 0\n8. Perform optimized bulk memory copy using REP MOVSD/MOVSB:\n   - Calculate dword count (size >> 2) for aligned transfer\n   - Copy dwords from node+0x8 to pbDestBuffer\n   - Copy remaining 0-3 bytes individually\n9. Read next node pointer from current node at offset +0x4\n10. Deallocate current node via DeallocateResourcePoolElement\n11. Update list head pointer in context block to next node\n12. If list is now empty (next == NULL), clear list state flag at context+0x20\n13. Release critical section lock and return copied byte count\n\nParameters:\n  pbDestBuffer (byte*): Destination buffer to receive dequeued node data. Must be large\n    enough to hold the node payload. Passed via stack at ESP+0x4.\n  dwBufferSize (uint): Size of destination buffer in bytes. If smaller than node data\n    size, operation fails with error flag set. Passed via stack at ESP+0x8.\n  IMPLICIT pdwContextBlock (EBX): Pointer to queue context structure containing:\n    +0x00: Error flag (set to 1 on buffer size mismatch)\n    +0x04: CRITICAL_SECTION for thread synchronization\n    +0x1c: Linked list head pointer (first node or NULL)\n    +0x20: List state flag (cleared when list becomes empty)\n\nReturns:\n  ushort: Number of bytes copied from dequeued node to destination buffer.\n    Returns 0 if list was empty or buffer size was insufficient.\n    On success, returns the actual node data size (1-65535 bytes).\n\nNode Structure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field        Description\n  0x00    2     wDataSize    Payload data size in bytes\n  0x02    2     wReserved    Padding for alignment\n  0x04    4     pNextNode    Pointer to next node in list (NULL if last)\n  0x08    N     abData       Variable-length payload data (N = wDataSize bytes)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty list: Returns 0, no error flag set, critical section still released\n  - Buffer undersized: Sets error flag at context+0x0=1, returns 0\n  - Last node dequeued: Clears list state flag at context+0x20 after removal\n  - Thread safety: Full operation protected by critical section lock\n\nError Handling:\n  0x68: Validation code passed to ValidateCriticalSection for integrity check\n  Error flag location: pdwContextBlock[0] set to 1 on buffer size failure",
