      "comment": "Enqueues data to a thread-safe message queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that data size is non-zero; if zero, triggers fatal error\n2. Lock the queue's critical section for thread-safe access\n3. Allocate a queue node of size (wDataSize + 8) from resource pool\n4. Initialize node header: set size field and clear next pointer\n5. Copy source data into node's data region using optimized DWORD + byte copy\n6. If queue is empty, set both head and tail to new node\n7. Otherwise, append node to tail and update tail pointer\n8. Release critical section and return\n\nParameters:\npQueue - Pointer to MessageQueue structure containing critical section and head/tail pointers\npData - Pointer to source data buffer to copy into queue node\nIMPLICIT wDataSize (AX) - Size of data in bytes to enqueue\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nStructure Layout:\nMessageQueue:\nOffset  Size  Field                   Type\n0x00    4     dwReserved              uint\n0x04    24    criticalSection         CRITICAL_SECTION\n0x1c    4     pHead                   QueueNode*\n0x20    4     pTail                   QueueNode*\n\nQueueNode:\nOffset  Size  Field                   Type\n0x00    2     wDataSize               ushort\n0x02    2     wReserved               ushort\n0x04    4     pNext                   QueueNode*\n0x08    N     abData                  byte[wDataSize]\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x4e - Critical section validation code\n0x50 - Source line number in D2QSQueue.cpp\n\nError Handling:\nZero data size triggers GetReturnAddress, WSACleanup, LogErrorWithContext, \nShutdownResourcesAndExit, and fatal ReportError(-1)\nAllocation failure logs error but continues (potentially dangerous)\n\nSource: ..\\\\Source\\\\Fog\\\\Src\\\\D2QSQueue.cpp",
