      "instructions": ["0x1FA80|PUSH|ECX", "0x1FA81|PUSH|EBX", "0x1FA82|LEA|EBX, [ESI + 0x4]", "0x1FA85|PUSH|EDI", "0x1FA86|MOV|EDX, 0x22", "0x1FA8B|MOV|ECX, EBX", "0x1FA8D|CALL|0x6ff6e0e0", "0x1FA92|PUSH|EBX", "0x1FA93|CALL|dword ptr [0x6ff7504c]", "0x1FA99|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [ESI + 0x1c]", "0x1FA9C|TEST|EDI, EDI", "0x1FA9E|JZ|0x6ff6fac5", "0x1FAA0|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI + 0x1c]", "0x1FAA3|MOV|EDI, dword ptr [EDI + 0x4]", "0x1FAA6|PUSH|0x29"],
      "comment": "Deallocates and clears all elements from a resource pool linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load critical section pointer from context + 0x4\n2. Initialize resource list head pointer from context + 0x1c\n3. Test if list is empty (head pointer is null)\n4. If empty, skip to cleanup (JZ to cleanup_and_return at 0x6ff67ba5)\n5. If not empty, enter critical section to ensure thread-safe access\n6. Call Ordinal_10251 with critical section for pre-clear operations\n7. Call EnterCriticalSection to acquire exclusive access\n8. For each element in the linked list:\n   a. Load current element from context + 0x1c\n   b. Load next element pointer from current element + 0x4\n   c. Store next pointer temporarily on stack (uStack_4)\n   d. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to deallocate current element\n   e. Update list head pointer (context + 0x1c) to next element\n   f. Test if next element exists (TEST EDI,EDI)\n   g. If not null, loop back to process next element (JNZ loop_process_resource at 0x6ff67b80)\n9. Exit loop when list becomes empty\n10. Clear context + 0x20 (secondary pointer) to 0\n11. Clear context + 0x1c (list head pointer) to 0\n12. Call DeleteCriticalSection to release critical section\n\nParameters:\npResourceManager (implicit in ESI): Pointer to game context/resource manager containing linked list of resources. Offset +0x4 points to critical section, offset +0x1c points to list head element.\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty list: If head pointer at +0x1c is zero, function skips all processing and goes directly to cleanup\n- Critical section: Thread synchronization is used to prevent concurrent access during deallocation\n- Resource cleanup: Each element has next pointer at offset +0x4 in the structure\n- Context offsets: +0x4=critical section, +0x1c=list head, +0x20=secondary list pointer\n- Magic number 0x29: Used in DeallocateResourcePoolElement call (possibly pool type/index)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name        | Type          | Description\n0x000  | 4    | unknown_0x0       | undefined     | Context data\n0x004  | 4    | pCriticalSection  | CRITICAL_SECT | Critical section for sync\n...    | ...  | ...               | undefined     | Additional context fields\n0x1c   | 4    | pListHead         | void *        | Pointer to first element\n0x20   | 4    | pListTail         | void *        | Pointer to last element (cleared)\n\nResource Element Structure:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type     | Description\n0x000  | ...  | elementData   | undefined| Element payload (type varies)\n0x004  | 4    | pNextElement  | void *   | Pointer to next element in list",
