      "comment": "Pops the next element from an evaluation stack.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load stack pointer from context offset 0x100 (number of elements)\n2. Test if stack pointer is greater than 0 (stack not empty)\n3. Jump to pop_element if stack has elements, else return 0\n4. Decrement stack pointer to get valid index\n5. Store decremented pointer back to context offset 0x100\n6. Calculate element address as context + (index * 4)\n7. Load and return the element value from calculated address\n\nParameters:\n  pStackContext (EvaluationStackContext *) - Pointer to evaluation stack context\n    Offset 0x000-0x0FF: Stack element storage (64 elements × 4 bytes each)\n    Offset 0x100: Current stack pointer (element count, 0 means empty)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - The popped value from top of stack, or 0 if stack was empty\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty stack: Stack pointer < 1 returns 0 without modifying state\n  - Single element: Pops last element, leaves stack pointer at 0\n  - Stack full: No bounds checking; caller responsible for not exceeding 64 elements\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type      Description\n  0x000   256   stackElements        uint[64]  Element storage area (64 × 4 bytes)\n  0x100   4     stackPointer         uint      Current element count (0-64)",
