      "comment": "Encodes expression tokens using a stack-based reduction algorithm.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local state: nEncodingStackDepth=0, nTokenStackIndex=0, fHasVariableLengthOutput=0\n2. Token provider loop: Repeatedly call ParseExpressionToken to fetch tokens from stream\n3. Token dispatch: For each token type (0x0-0x12), execute corresponding encoding operation\n   a) PUSH_TOKEN (0x0): Push token onto stack if space available (<0x40), mark with 0x2 end marker\n   b) POP_TOKEN (0x1): Pop and process stacked tokens with reduction rules, validate stack consistency\n   c) ENCODE_* (0x2-0xf): Call ProcessTokenEncoding with specific operation codes (0x3, 0x10-0x17)\n   d) LITERAL_INT (0x10): Encode integer value via EncodeIntegerValue\n   e) LITERAL_VARLEN (0x11): Encode variable-length integer via EncodeVariableLengthInteger\n   f) STACK_VALUE (0x12): Push raw value onto internal stack (limited to 0x40 entries)\n4. Post-loop finalization: Call ProcessTokenEncoding with operation code 0 to finalize\n5. Optimization pass: If output was generated without special flags, execute bytecode program on result\n6. Return encoded byte count or 0 on error (buffer overflow, invalid token sequence)\n\nParameters:\n- nModeFlag (int): Control/mode code passed to helper functions\n- pOutputBuffer (byte*): Target buffer for encoded output bytes\n- nMaxOutputSize (int): Maximum bytes available in pOutputBuffer (checked before each write)\n- pTokenProvider (void*): Opaque callback function pointer to token stream provider\n- pCallbackFunction (void*): Optional callback for token type 0x1 reduction operations\n- pContextData (void*): Opaque context parameter passed to token provider callback\n\nReturns:\n- Positive integer: Number of bytes written to pOutputBuffer (final encoded size)\n- Zero: Error condition (buffer overflow, invalid token sequence, or stack violation)\n\nLocal Variables (decompiler SSA names -> semantic meaning):\n- bVar1 -> fOutputGenerated: Bool flag indicating output has been generated\n- pcVar2 -> pszTokenResult: Pointer to parsed token result string\n- iVar3 -> nStackCost: Stack depth cost for current token reduction\n- pbVar4 -> pbCurrentOutput: Current write position in output buffer\n- iVar5 -> nCurrentStackDepth: Tracked stack depth during reduction\n- pbVar6 -> pbNextOutput: Next output position after write\n- bVar7 -> byTokenOpcode: Current token opcode byte being processed\n- nValue -> dwOptimizedValue: Result from bytecode optimization pass\n\nSpecial Cases and Magic Numbers:\n- Stack size limit: 0x40 (64 decimal) = maximum entries in abyTokenStackBuffer\n- End marker: 0x2 = marks section boundaries in token stack\n- Type 1 marker: 0x1 = special token requiring callback invocation\n- Type 0x15 stack cost: 3 items (special reduction rule)\n- Type 0x16 stack cost: 1 item\n- Default stack cost: 2 items for most operations\n- Reduction operation codes: 0x3, 0x10-0x17 map to specific encoding transformations\n\nStructure Layout (stack frame):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type        Description\n-0x4    4     nEncodingStackDepth     int         Encoding depth counter\n-0x8    4     nTokenStackIndex        int         Current token stack index\n-0x148  60    abyTokenStackBuffer     byte[60]    Token type stack (LIFO)\n-0x14c  4     nStackEntryData         int         Data value for current stack entry\n-0x150  4     nStackBaseAddress       int         Base address for stack access\n-0x154  4     fHasVariableLengthOutput int        Flag for variable length output\n-0x158  4     nTokenValue             int         Parsed token value\n-0x10c  260   aiStack_10c             int[65]     Parallel data values for stack tokens",
