      "comment": "Validates existence of the Diablo II expansion MPQ file (d2exp.mpq).\nChecks multiple installation directories to locate the expansion data file.\n\nAlgorithm\n1. Check if validation already performed via g_dwExpMpqValidationChecked flag\n2. If already validated, return cached result from g_dwExpMpqFound\n3. Set g_dwExpMpqValidationChecked = 1 to mark validation as performed\n4. Call GetInstallPath to retrieve base game directory into szFilePath buffer (MAX_PATH=260)\n5. Append d2exp.mpq to path using CopyStringBounded\n6. Call GetFileAttributesA to check if file exists at primary location\n7. If file found (attributes != 0xFFFFFFFF), set g_dwExpMpqFound = 1 and return 1\n8. If first attempt fails, try alternate path using CopyMemoryAndDetectTerminator\n9. Call GetFileAttributesA again for second location\n10. If file found at second location, set g_dwExpMpqFound = 1 and return 1\n11. If both attempts fail, return cached g_dwExpMpqFound value (0)\n\nParameters\nNone - This is a parameterless query function\n\nReturns\nint - Non-zero (1) if d2exp.mpq found at either location, zero (0) if not found\nUses caching: subsequent calls return g_dwExpMpqFound without re-checking filesystem\n\nSpecial Cases\n- Uses memoization pattern: first call performs actual check, subsequent calls return cached result\n- GetFileAttributesA returns INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES (0xFFFFFFFF) for non-existent files\n- Two paths are checked to support standard and alternate D2 installation configurations\n- First path: Game install directory + d2exp.mpq (via CopyStringBounded)\n- Second path: Alternate location (via CopyMemoryAndDetectTerminator)\n\nMagic Numbers\n0x104 (260): MAX_PATH constant for Windows file path buffers\n0xFFFFFFFF: INVALID_FILE_ATTRIBUTES - returned by GetFileAttributesA for missing files\n\nGlobals\ng_dwExpMpqValidationChecked @ 6ffa6ed0 - DWORD flag, 1 if validation performed\ng_dwExpMpqFound @ 6ffa6ecc - DWORD result, 1 if expansion MPQ found",
