      "comment": "Generates a sequence of floating-point values into an output buffer with format conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nNumElements parameter (must be 1=byte, 2=word, or 4=dword)\n2. Validate nOutputFormat is non-negative; error 0x0f if negative\n3. Validate dStartValue is within range [0.0, 100.0); error 0x10 if out of range\n4. Initialize FPU state if g_dwFPUConfigEnabled is set via DispatchExtendedPrecisionFloatOperation\n5. Calculate iteration limit as (nEndValue - 1.0)\n6. Main loop: call ComputePowerWithCPUCheck for value calculation\n7. Convert result to 64-bit integer via ConvertFloatingPointTo64BitInteger\n8. Store result in buffer based on nNumElements format (byte/word/dword)\n9. Advance output pointer by element size (1, 2, or 4 bytes)\n10. Increment dCurrentValue by 1.0; repeat until >= iteration limit\n\nParameters:\n- nOutputFormat (int, ECX): Element count validation (must be >= 0)\n- pOutputBuffer (void*, EDX): Output buffer pointer for storing generated values\n- dStartValue (double, Stack+0x4): Initial value for sequence generation (range 0.0 to 100.0)\n- nNumElements (int, Stack+0xc): Element storage format (1=byte, 2=word, 4=dword)\n- nEndValue (int, Stack+0x10): Upper bound for iteration count\n\nReturns: void (calls error handlers on validation failures; does not return on error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error 0x0e: nNumElements not in {1, 2, 4}\n- Error 0x0f: nOutputFormat < 0\n- Error 0x10: dStartValue outside [0.0, 100.0)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x0e, 0x0f, 0x10: Error codes for validation failures\n- 1, 2, 4: Valid element sizes (byte, word, dword)\n- 100.0: Maximum value threshold (g_dMaxValueThreshold)\n- 1.0: Loop increment step (g_dOne)\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n- g_dwFPUConfigEnabled (0x6ff805c8): FPU extended precision mode flag\n- g_dMaxValueThreshold (0x6ff78fe0): Maximum valid start value (100.0)\n- g_dZero (0x6ff78fe8): Zero constant (0.0)\n- g_dOne (0x6ff78fd8): One constant (1.0)\n- g_dScaleFactor (0x6ff78fc0): Scale m