      "instructions": ["0x211A0|PUSH|EDI", "0x211A1|PUSH|ESI", "0x211A2|PUSH|EBP", "0x211A3|XOR|EDI, EDI", "0x211A5|XOR|EBP, EBP", "0x211A7|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x14]", "0x211AB|OR|EAX, EAX", "0x211AD|JGE|0x6ff711c4", "0x211AF|INC|EDI", "0x211B0|INC|EBP", "0x211B1|MOV|EDX, dword ptr [ESP + 0x10]", "0x211B5|NEG|EAX", "0x211B7|NEG|EDX", "0x211B9|SBB|EAX, 0x0", "0x211BC|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x14], EAX"],
      "comment": "Performs signed 64-bit integer division with remainder (divmod).\n\nThis is a Microsoft Visual C++ runtime library helper function that divides\na signed 64-bit dividend by a signed 64-bit divisor, returning both the\nquotient and remainder. The function handles sign conversion internally.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EDI, ESI, EBP registers on stack\n2. Initialize sign tracking flags (EDI=quotient sign, EBP=remainder sign)\n3. If dividend is negative: negate to positive, toggle both sign flags\n4. If divisor is negative: negate to positive, toggle quotient sign flag\n5. If divisor high dword is zero (32-bit divisor):\n   a. Divide dividend high dword by divisor -> quotient high\n   b. Divide (remainder:dividend low) by divisor -> quotient low\n   c. Compute remainder = divisor * quotient low (for verification)\n6. Else (full 64-bit divisor):\n   a. Normalize: shift both dividend and divisor right until divisor fits 32 bits\n   b. Divide normalized dividend by normalized divisor -> estimated quotient\n   c. Multiply divisor by estimated quotient to verify\n   d. If product > dividend: decrement quotient, adjust product\n   e. Remainder = dividend - (divisor * quotient)\n7. Apply sign corrections:\n   a. If remainder needs negation (EBP was toggled odd times): negate ECX:EBX\n   b. If quotient needs negation (EDI was toggled odd times): negate EDX:EAX\n8. Return quotient in EDX:EAX, remainder in EBX:ECX\n\nParameters:\n  dwDividendLo - Low 32 bits of signed 64-bit dividend [Stack+0x10]\n  dwDividendHi - High 32 bits of signed 64-bit dividend (contains sign) [Stack+0x14]\n  dwDivisorLo  - Low 32 bits of signed 64-bit divisor [Stack+0x18]\n  dwDivisorHi  - High 32 bits of signed 64-bit divisor (contains sign) [Stack+0x1C]\n\nReturns:\n  EDX:EAX - Signed 64-bit quotient (dividend / divisor)\n  EBX:ECX - Signed 64-bit remainder (dividend % divisor)\n  Note: Remainder has same sign as dividend (C99 truncation toward zero)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Division by zero: Undefined behavior (hardware exception)\n  - Overflow (LLONG_MIN / -1): Undefined behavior\n  - Zero dividend: Returns quotient=0, remainder=0\n\nRegister Usage:\n  EAX - Dividend low / quotient low / scratch\n  EDX - Dividend high / quotient high / scratch\n  EBX - Quotient high (temp) / remainder low\n  ECX - Divisor low / remainder high\n  ESI - Quotient low (temp)\n  EDI - Quotient sign flag (0=positive, 1=negative)\n  EBP - Remainder sign flag (0=positive, 1=negative)\n\nCalling Convention: __stdcall (callee cleans 16 bytes from stack via RET 0x10)",
