      "comment": "C++ Exception Frame Handler - Entry point for structured exception handling.\n\nThunk function that forwards exception handling to the internal implementation.\nReceives function-specific exception info via implicit EAX register parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save registers and establish stack frame\n2. Store implicit FuncInfo pointer from EAX to local stack variable\n3. Clear EAX and push three zero arguments (recursive, nested frame, catch depth)\n4. Push implicit FuncInfo pointer\n5. Push four explicit exception parameters\n6. Call ___InternalCxxFrameHandler to process the exception\n7. Store result disposition and restore registers\n8. Return exception disposition to OS\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionRecord (EHExceptionRecord *) - Exception record with code and flags\n  pRegistrationNode (EHRegistrationNode *) - Current frame registration node\n  pContext (_CONTEXT *) - CPU context at exception point\n  pDispatcherContext (void *) - Dispatcher context from OS\n  IMPLICIT pFuncInfo (_s_FuncInfo * in EAX) - Function-specific exception info table\n\nReturns:\n  int - Exception disposition value:\n    0 = ExceptionContinueExecution (exception handled)\n    1 = ExceptionContinueSearch (propagate to next handler)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - EAX contains implicit FuncInfo pointer from compiler-generated SEH setup\n  - Passes zeros for recursive flag, nested frame, and catch depth (top-level call)\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release",
