      "comment": "SEH translator guard handler for C++ exception translation in VS2003 CRT.\nValidates the security cookie, handles nested frame unwinding, and invokes\nthe internal C++ exception frame handler for SEH-to-C++ exception translation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare guard info security cookie (offset 0x8) against g_dwSecurityCookie\n2. If cookie mismatch: set EXCEPTION_NONCONTINUABLE_EXCEPTION flag (0x8), return 1\n3. Check exception flags (offset 0x4) for EH_UNWINDING|EH_EXIT_UNWIND|EH_NESTED_CALL (0x66)\n4. If unwinding flags set: mark guard info didCatch field (offset 0x24) = 1, return 1\n5. Call ___InternalCxxFrameHandler with guard info fields to process C++ exception\n6. If didCatch not set: call _UnwindNestedFrames to unwind nested SEH frames\n7. Call _CallSETranslator with magic 0x123 to get continuation address\n8. Jump to continuation address to resume exception handling\n\nParameters:\npExceptionRecord   - EHExceptionRecord*  - Pointer to exception record with code/flags\npGuardInfo         - TranslatorGuardRN*  - Guard registration node with cookie and EH info\npContext           - CONTEXT*            - CPU context at time of exception\npDispatcherContext - void*               - Dispatcher context (unused in this handler)\n\nReturns:\n1 - ExceptionContinueSearch: Continue searching for handler up the stack\nnDisposition - Result from continuation address jump (non-local return)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Cookie mismatch indicates stack corruption, sets EXCEPTION_NONCONTINUABLE_EXCEPTION\n- Flags 0x66 indicates unwinding phase, not initial dispatch\n- Magic value 0x123 passed to _CallSETranslator for translator mode\n\nStructure Layout (TranslatorGuardRN):\nOffset  Size  Field              Type                  Description\n0x00    4     prev               EHRegistrationNode*   Previous registration node\n0x04    4     handler            void*                 Handler function pointer\n0x08    4     securityCookie     uint                  Security cookie