      "comment": "FPU Division Wrapper - Pops ST0 and ST1, performs extended precision division via helper.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 44 bytes (0x2c) of stack space for two 80-bit extended precision values\n2. Pop ST0 (dividend) to stack at [ESP] as 10-byte extended double\n3. Pop ST1 (divisor) to stack at [ESP+0xc] as 10-byte extended double\n4. Call ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision to compute ST1/ST0 with exception handling\n5. Deallocate stack space and return (result left in FPU ST0)\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT in_ST0 (float10): Dividend value from FPU stack top\n  IMPLICIT in_ST1 (float10): Divisor value from FPU stack second position\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result is returned implicitly in FPU ST0 register after division\n\nAssembly-Only Variables (Phantom):\n  local_20 (float10 at Stack[-0x20]): Temporary storage for ST0 dividend\n  local_2c (float10 at Stack[-0x2c]): Temporary storage for ST1 divisor\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Division by zero handled by ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision\n  - NaN/Infinity propagation follows IEEE 754 semantics\n  - This is a Visual Studio CRT library function for FPU division workarounds\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio CRT",
