      "comment": "Performs FPU divide-reverse-and-pop (FDIVRP ST(i), ST(0)) operation.\n\nLibrary Function: Visual Studio C Runtime - Software FPU emulation helper.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x2c bytes on stack for two extended precision values\n2. Store ST(0) to stack at [ESP+0x0c] (ldDivisor - 10 bytes)\n3. Store ST(1) to stack at [ESP] (ldDividend - 10 bytes)\n4. Call ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision with split mantissa/exponent\n5. Clean up stack (ADD ESP, 0x2c)\n6. Return with result in ST(0)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT in_ST0 (float10): Divisor - FPU stack register 0\n- IMPLICIT in_ST1 (float10): Dividend - FPU stack register 1\n\nReturns:\n- void: Result pushed to FPU stack ST(0) = ST(1) / ST(0)\n- FPU stack is popped once (ST(1) and ST(0) consumed, result in new ST(0))\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles denormalized numbers via ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision\n- Handles infinity and NaN via lookup table classification\n- Division by zero produces IEEE 754 infinity result\n\nStack Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field        Type      Description\n0x00    10    ldDividend   float10   Extended precision dividend (ST1)\n0x0c    10    ldDivisor    float10   Extended precision divisor (ST0)\n0x16    6     padding      byte[6]   Stack alignment padding\n0x2c    -     (ESP orig)   -         Original stack pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2c (44): Stack frame size for two float10 values + alignment",
