      "comment": "CPU Capability Detection and Power Function Router\n\nValidates CPU and FPU state before computing base^exponent. Routes to optimized\nSSE2 path if hardware and precision requirements are met, otherwise falls back\nto safer standard library implementation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_fSse2Available flag for SSE2 CPU capability\n2. If SSE2 unavailable, jump to fallback path at LAB_6ff725a4\n3. Save MXCSR register and verify exception masks (bits 0x1f80 set)\n4. Save FPU control word and verify precision bits (0x7f mask)\n5. If both checks pass, jump to ComputeBaseToExponentPower (optimized)\n6. Otherwise, call __fload_withFB for standard fallback computation\n\nParameters:\n- dBase (double): Base value for exponentiation, passed via FPU stack ST0/ST1\n- dExponent (double): Exponent value, passed via stack at [ESP+0xC]\n- dwBaseHigh (uint): High 32 bits of base double (IEEE 754 format)\n- dwExponentHigh (uint): High 32 bits of exponent double\n\nReturns:\n- double: Result of pow(dBase, dExponent) computation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- SSE2 disabled: g_fSse2Available == 0 forces fallback path\n- SSE exception masks: MXCSR bits 0x1f80 must all be set (IM|DM|ZM|OM|UM|PM)\n- FPU precision: Control word bits 0x7f must be set for extended precision\n- State corruption: Either check failure routes to safe fallback\n- Infinity/NaN: Special handling via __powhlp helper function\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1f80: SSE exception mask bits (Invalid|Denormal|DivZero|Overflow|Underflow|Precision)\n- 0x7f: x87 FPU exception mask (same 6 exceptions)\n- 0x27f: Default FPU control word (extended precision, all exceptions masked)\n- 0x7ff00000: IEEE 754 exponent mask for detecting infinity/NaN\n- 0x80000000: Sign bit mask for negative number detection\n\nError Handling:\n- FPU exceptions handled via HandleExtendedPrecisionFpuException\n- Uses g_szPowFunctionName (\"pow\") for error reporting\n- g_fUseFpuExceptionHandling controls exception behavior\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n- g_fSse2Available (0x6ffa8284): SSE2 CPU feature flag\n- g_ldNegativeTwo (0x6ff801d0): Constant -2.0 for special cases\n- g_fUseFpuExceptionHandling (0x6ff805c4): Exception handling mode\n- g_szPowFunctionName (0x6ff80168): \"pow\" string for error messages\n\nNote: SSA variables (uVar*, fVar*, extraout_*) are decompiler artifacts from\ncomplex FPU stack manipulation and cannot be directly renamed. The function\nextensively uses x87 FPU instructions for floating-point operations.",
