      "comment": "Computes base raised to the power of exponent (dBase^dExponent).\nImplements the standard C library pow() function with full IEEE 754 compliance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save and validate FPU control word (check if 0x27F precision mode)\n2. Extract exponent bits to detect NaN/Infinity special cases\n3. If exponent is NaN/Infinity, branch to special case handling\n4. Load base and exponent onto FPU stack via __fload_withFB\n5. Check base for zero/denormal values\n6. For negative base: test if exponent is integer via CountDecimalDigits\n7. For valid inputs: compute y*log2(x) via FYL2X instruction\n8. Call ComputePowerOfTwo for 2^(y*log2(x)) = x^y\n9. Handle sign negation if needed\n10. Call __powhlp for edge cases (domain errors, overflow)\n11. Restore FPU state and return result\n\nParameters:\n  dBase (Stack[0x4]): Base value as IEEE 754 double-precision float\n  dExponent (Stack[0xC]): Exponent value as IEEE 754 double-precision float\n  IMPLICIT EAX: Upper 32 bits of base for quick NaN/Infinity check\n\nReturns:\n  ST0: Result as extended precision float10 (80-bit)\n  EAX: Status code:\n    0 = Normal computation success\n    1 = Special case handled (zero, one, infinity)\n    2 = Infinity result\n    7 = NaN result (domain error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  0^(positive) = 0        | 0^(zero or negative) = Infinity/NaN\n  1^x = 1 for any x       | (-base)^(non-integer) = NaN (domain error)\n  Inf^(positive) = Inf    | Inf^(negative) = 0\n  base^0 = 1              | NaN^x = NaN, x^NaN = NaN\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x27F - FPU control word for extended precision (64-bit mantissa)\n  0x7FF00000 - IEEE 754 double exponent mask (bits 52-62 of high word)\n  0xFFFFF - IEEE 754 double mantissa mask (lower 20 bits of high word)\n  0x1D - Function identifier for pow in exception handler table",
