      "comment": "Exception filter for C++ exception unwinding during stack cleanup.\n\nDetects C++ exceptions using the Visual Studio magic code (0xE06D7363 = \"msc\" + 0x60)\nand forces process termination when a C++ exception is thrown during stack unwinding.\nThis prevents exception handling corruption when an exception occurs while unwinding\nfrom a previous exception.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dereference implicit EAX parameter to get EXCEPTION_RECORD pointer\n2. Compare ExceptionCode against C++ exception magic (0xE06D7363)\n3. If not a C++ exception, return EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH (0)\n4. If C++ exception detected during unwind:\n   a. Get thread-local storage context via GetOrCreateTlsContext()\n   b. Clear the _purecall handler pointer to prevent callback loops\n   c. Call terminate() to abort the process (noreturn)\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionPtrs (_EXCEPTION_POINTERS*) - Standard exception filter parameter (unused)\n  IMPLICIT pdwExceptionRecord (uint* via EAX) - Pointer to EXCEPTION_RECORD structure\n\nReturns:\n  0 (EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH) - Exception is not a C++ exception, continue search\n  Does not return - If C++ exception detected, calls terminate()\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xE06D7363 - Visual C++ exception magic code (\"msc\" in ASCII + exception flag)\n\nLibrary: Visual Studio 2003 Release CRT",
