      "comment": "Unwinds the C++ exception handling stack frame to a target exception state.\n\nThis is a core MSVC C++ exception handling runtime function from Visual Studio 2003.\nIt walks back through the exception registration stack, executing destructor calls\nfor each try block state until the target state is reached.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve the current exception state from the registration node offset +8\n2. Get the TLS context and increment the pure virtual call counter (re-entrancy guard)\n3. Loop while current state differs from target state:\n   a. Validate current state is within bounds (0 to maxState-1)\n   b. Calculate offset into unwind map table (state * 8 bytes per entry)\n   c. Read the next state from unwind entry offset +0 (toState)\n   d. If unwind entry offset +4 is non-null, call the cleanup handler via __CallSettingFrame@12\n   e. Update current state to the next state in chain\n4. Decrement pure virtual call counter after all unwinding complete\n5. Final validation that current state matches target state\n6. Store final state back to registration node offset +8\n\nParameters:\npRegistration (EHRegistrationNode*) - Pointer to the exception registration node on the stack\npContext (_CONTEXT*) - Reserved CPU context pointer (unused in VS2003 implementation)\npFuncInfo (FuncInfo*) - Pointer to the function's exception handling table\nnTargetState (int) - The target exception state to unwind to (-1 for full unwind)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns after unwinding is complete or calls _inconsistency on error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x103 - Cleanup flags passed to __CallSettingFrame@12 (EH_MAGIC_NUMBER1)\n8 - Size of each UnwindMapEntry in bytes (toState: 4 bytes, pHandler: 4 bytes)\n\nError Handling:\nCalls _inconsistency() if:\n- Current state is negative (invalid state)\n- Current state exceeds max state count in FuncInfo\n- Final state after loop does not match target state\n\nStructure Layout - EHRegistrationNode:\nOffset  Size  Field      