      "comment": "Adjusts a base pointer using PMD (Pointer-to-Member Displacement) data for C++ exception handling and RTTI.\nThis is a Visual Studio C++ runtime library function that computes the adjusted pointer based on member displacement (mdisp) and optionally virtual base class displacement (pdisp/vdisp) for objects with virtual inheritance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Add base member displacement (pPmdData->mdisp) to base pointer\n2. Check if virtual base adjustment required (pPmdData->pdisp >= 0)\n3. If virtual adjustment needed:\n   a. Locate vtable using (pBasePointer + pPmdData->pdisp)\n   b. Read virtual base offset from vtable[pPmdData->vdisp]\n   c. Add both pdisp and virtual base offset to result\n4. Return the fully adjusted pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pBasePointer (void*, IMPLICIT in EAX) - Base object pointer to adjust; must be valid non-null pointer to C++ object\n  pPmdData (PMD*, IMPLICIT in ECX) - Pointer to PMD structure containing displacement fields:\n    - mdisp (offset 0x0): Member displacement, always applied\n    - pdisp (offset 0x4): Virtual table displacement, -1 if no virtual base\n    - vdisp (offset 0x8): Virtual base offset index in vtable\n\nReturns:\n  void* (in EAX) - Adjusted pointer after applying all displacements\n  - If pdisp == -1: Returns pBasePointer + mdisp (simple offset)\n  - If pdisp >= 0: Returns pBasePointer + mdisp + pdisp + vtable[vdisp]\n  - Never returns null if input is valid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - pdisp == -1: No virtual inheritance, only mdisp applied\n  - Used by BuildCatchObject for C++ exception handling catch block adjustments\n\nStructure Layout (PMD):\n  Offset  Size  Field   Type  Description\n  0x0     4     mdisp   int   Member displacement (always applied)\n  0x4     4     pdisp   int   Virtual table displacement (-1 = none)\n  0x8     4     vdisp   int   Virtual base offset index in vtable\n\nCalling Convention: __cdecl with implicit EAX/ECX register parameters",
