      "comment": "Executes a C++ exception catch handler block with proper SEH frame management.\n\nThis function wraps the actual catch block execution with SEH protection and\nensures proper TLS context management for nested exception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Setup SEH frame via __SEH_prolog for structured exception handling\n2. Save current TLS context (exception record and context pointers at offsets 0x7c, 0x80)\n3. Create FrameInfo structure linking this catch frame to the exception chain\n4. Update TLS context with current exception record and context\n5. Call ExecuteCatchBlockHandler to execute the actual catch block code\n6. On completion or nested exception, call CleanupExceptionUnwind\n7. Restore saved TLS context state\n8. Cleanup via __SEH_epilog and return catch result\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionRecord - Pointer to the EH exception record being handled\n  pRegistrationNode - SEH registration node for the current frame\n  pContext - CPU context at the point of exception\n  pFuncInfo - Function info table with try/catch block mappings\n  pCatchObject - Pointer to the caught exception object (may be null)\n  nContinuationAddress - Address to continue execution after catch block\n  dwFlags - Exception handling flags (bit 0 = 0x40 for catch semantics)\n\nReturns:\n  void* - Result from catch block execution (typically continuation address)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Nested exception during catch block triggers CleanupExceptionUnwind\n  - C++ exception signature check: 0xE06D7363 with magic 0x19930520/0x19930521\n  - Exception object at offset 0x1c determines if catch result is valid\n\nTLS Context Layout (at TlsContext pointer):\n  Offset 0x7c: Pointer to current EHExceptionRecord\n  Offset 0x80: Pointer to current _CONTEXT",
