      "comment": "Builds a catch object during C++ exception handling by copying or constructing the caught exception object from the thrown object based on the catchable type information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate ThrowInfo structure - check if throwInfo->pCatchableTypeArray is non-null\n2. Verify catchable type array has at least one entry (check byte at offset 8)\n3. Check if copy constructor info exists or if IS_SIMPLE_TYPE flag (0x80) is set\n4. If throwInfo flags indicate non-negative (positive type info), adjust destination pointer by adding offset 0xC\n5. Get source object pointer from exception record at offset 0x18\n6. Branch based on throwInfo flags (bit 3 = 0x8 indicates pointer type):\n   a. If pointer type (flag 0x8): Validate source/dest, copy pointer directly, then adjust via PMD\n   b. If simple copy (flag 0x1): Validate, memmove data, handle 4-byte pointer adjustment\n   c. If no copy constructor (offset 0x18 == 0): Validate, adjust source, memmove data\n   d. If has copy constructor: Validate executable, dispatch to copy constructor via jump table\n7. On validation failure at any step, call _inconsistency() to handle error\n\nParameters:\npExceptionRecord (EHExceptionRecord*) - Exception record containing thrown object info at offset 0x18\npThrowInfo (_s_ThrowInfo*) - Throw information structure with type flags and catchable type array\npHandlerType (_s_HandlerType*) - Handler type information (passed to subroutines via registers)\npCatchableType (_s_CatchableType*) - Catchable type info with copy semantics (passed via ECX, stored in ESI)\nIMPLICIT in_EDX (int*) - Destination buffer for catch object construction\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No explicit return value. Catch object is constructed at destination (in_EDX/EDI).\nOn failure: Calls _inconsistency() which does not return (terminates exception handling).\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null catchable type array: Early return without object construction\n- Empty type array: Early return without object construction  \n- Simple type without copy constructor: Direct memory copy via memmove\n- Pointer types (flag 0x8): Copy pointer value, then adjust via AdjustPointer\n- Reference semantics (flag 0x1): Copy with potential pointer adjustment for 4-byte types\n- Virtual base adjustment: Uses PMD structure via AdjustPointer for proper offset calculation\n\nFlag Bits (ThrowInfo flags at offset 0):\n0x01 - CT_IsSimpleType: Simple type, use direct copy\n0x04 - CT_ByReferenceOnly: Reference-only semantics\n0x08 - CT_IsPointer: Type is a pointer, copy pointer value\n0x80 - (offset+3) IS_SIMPLE_TYPE: No copy constructor required\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x18 - Offset in exception record to thrown object pointer\n0x14 - Offset in CatchableType to copy size\n0x18 - Offset in CatchableType to copy constructor\n0x0C - Base offset added for positive type adjustment\n\nError Handling:\n_ValidateRead() - Validates memory is readable before access\n_ValidateExecute() - Validates copy constructor is executable\n_inconsistency() - Called on validation failure, terminates exception handling",
