      "comment": "Executes a C++ exception catch block handler after matching a thrown exception.\n\nThis is a core MSVC C++ exception handling runtime function from Visual Studio 2003.\nIt orchestrates the complete catch block execution sequence: building the catch object,\nunwinding nested frames and stack states, executing the actual handler, and jumping\nto the continuation point.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If bDoDestroy is non-zero, call BuildCatchObject to construct the catch parameter\n   from the thrown exception object using pCatchableType for type conversion\n2. Determine the unwind target: use pCatchableType if non-null, otherwise use pFrame\n3. Call _UnwindNestedFrames to unwind any nested exception frames back to this handler\n4. Call ___FrameUnwindToState to execute destructors for objects constructed between\n   the try block entry and the throw point (unwind to nTryLevel+1)\n5. Update pFrame state to pHandler->nCatchState+1 for proper destructor sequencing\n6. Call ExecuteCatchHandlerBlock with the handler's continuation address\n7. If ExecuteCatchHandlerBlock returns a non-zero continuation address, call\n   _JumpToContinuation to transfer control (does not return)\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionRecord (EHExceptionRecord*) - The exception record being processed\n  pFrame (EHRegistrationNode*) - Current function's SEH registration node\n  pContext (_CONTEXT*) - CPU context at exception point (used for stack walking)\n  pCatchObject (void*) - Destination for catch block's exception parameter\n  pFuncInfo (_s_FuncInfo*) - Function's exception handling metadata table\n  pHandler (_s_HandlerType*) - Matching catch handler descriptor\n  pCatchableType (_s_CatchableType*) - Type descriptor for the caught exception\n  pTryBlockMap (_s_TryBlockMapEntry*) - Try block map entry for this catch\n  nTryLevel (int) - Try block nesting level for state unwinding\n  pRegistrationNode (EHRegistrationNode*) - Registration node for nested unwinding\n  bDoDestroy (uchar) - Non-zero if catch object needs construction\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return normally; jumps to catch block continuation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If bDoDestroy is 0, BuildCatchObject is skipped (catch by reference, no copy needed)\n- If pCatchableType is NULL, uses pFrame for _UnwindNestedFrames target\n- ExecuteCatchHandlerBlock may not return if catch block throws or re-throws\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x100 - dwFlags passed to ExecuteCatchHandlerBlock (EH_CATCH_BLOCK_MAGIC)\n\nStructure Layout - _s_HandlerType:\n  Offset  Size  Field          Type    Description\n  +0x00   4     adjectives     uint    Handler adjectives/flags\n  +0x04   4     nCatchState    int     State to transition to in catch block\n\nError Handling:\n  If ExecuteCatchHandlerBlock returns 0, function returns without jumping\n  (indicates nested exception or catch block completed without continuation)",
