      "comment": "Searches for a matching exception handler in the function's try/catch blocks.\n\nThis is a core MSVC C++ exception handling function that traverses the try block\nmap to find a suitable catch block for the current exception. It validates exception\nsignatures and performs type matching between thrown and catchable types.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate current exception state against function info bounds\n2. Check if exception is a C++ exception (code 0xe06d7363)\n3. If nested search, retrieve exception from TLS context and validate\n4. Get range of try blocks to check for current state\n5. For each try block in range:\n   a. Check if current state falls within try block bounds\n   b. Get catchable type array from exception record\n   c. For each catchable type, call TypeMatch to check compatibility\n   d. If match found, call CatchIt to transfer control to handler\n6. If no nested and no match, call FindHandlerForForeignException\n7. If nested search, call ___DestructExceptionObject for cleanup\n\nParameters:\n  pException          - Pointer to exception record being processed\n  pRegistration       - Pointer to current exception registration node\n  pContext            - Pointer to thread context at exception time\n  pDispatcher         - Dispatcher context for unwinding (opaque)\n  pFuncInfo           - Function-specific exception handling info\n  bSearchingNested    - TRUE if searching nested exception context\n  iState              - Current exception state index in function\n  pLastRegistration   - Previous registration node in chain\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return value; transfers control via CatchIt\n         or returns normally if no handler found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xe06d7363 - MSVC C++ exception signature ('msc' + SEH flag)\n  0x19930520 - MSVC exception magic (version 1.0)\n  0x19930521 - MSVC exception magic (version 1.1)\n  0x3         - Minimum parameter count for valid C++ exception\n  0x10        - Size of _s_HandlerType structure (16 bytes)\n  0x14        - Size of _s_TryBlockMapEntry structure (20 bytes)\n\nError Handling:\n  - Calls _inconsistency if state validation fails\n  - Calls terminate via CatchIt if catch block throws",
