      "comment": "Internal C++ exception frame handler for MSVC structured exception handling.\n\nProcesses C++ exceptions by validating the FuncInfo structure, checking exception\nstate flags, and dispatching to appropriate handlers. Supports recursive handling\nand exception translation via custom handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate FuncInfo magic number (0x19930520) against masked bbtFlags\n2. Call _inconsistency() if magic validation fails\n3. Check exception flags byte for unwinding status (0x66 mask)\n4. If unwinding (flags & 0x66 != 0):\n   a. Check if maxState > 0 and nCatchDepth == 0\n   b. Call ___FrameUnwindToState to unwind to state -1\n5. If not unwinding (flags & 0x66 == 0):\n   a. Skip if no try blocks defined (nTryBlocks == 0)\n   b. Check for C++ exception signature (0xE06D7363)\n   c. Verify exception version > 0x19930520\n   d. If translator handler exists, call it recursively\n   e. Otherwise call FindHandler to locate catch block\n\nParameters:\npExceptRec      - EHExceptionRecord* - Exception record with exception info\npRegNode        - EHRegistrationNode* - Current registration frame\npContext        - _CONTEXT* - CPU context at exception point\npDispatcherContext - void* - Dispatcher context (passed to unwind)\npFuncInfo       - _s_FuncInfo* - Function info with try/catch tables\nnCatchDepth     - int - Current catch nesting depth (0 = top level)\npMarkerRegNode  - EHRegistrationNode* - Marker for unwind boundary\nbRecursive      - uchar - Recursive handling flag\n\nReturns:\n1 - Exception was handled or unwinding completed\ndwResult - Result from translator handler if called\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x19930520 - MSVC EH magic number (May 20, 1993 - VC++ 2.0 release date)\n0x1FFFFFFF - Mask to extract magic from bbtFlags field\n0xE06D7363 - C++ exception signature ('msc' | 0xE0000000)\n0x66       - Unwinding flags mask (EH_UNWINDING | EH_EXIT_UNWIND | flags)\n-1         - Target state for complete frame unwind",
