      "instructions": ["0x230B9|MOVLPD|XMM0, qword ptr [ESP + 0x4]", "0x230BF|MOVLPD|XMM7, qword ptr [0x6ff7c8e0]", "0x230C7|MOVLPD|XMM2, qword ptr [0x6ff7c8f0]", "0x230CF|ANDPD|XMM7, XMM0", "0x230D3|MOVSD|XMM4, XMM0", "0x230D7|PSRLQ|XMM0, 0x2c", "0x230DC|PEXTRW|EAX, XMM0, 0x0", "0x230E1|ORPD|XMM7, XMM2", "0x230E5|PEXTRW|ECX, XMM4, 0x3", "0x230EA|AND|EAX, 0xff", "0x230EF|ADD|EAX, 0x1", "0x230F2|AND|EAX, 0x1fe", "0x230F7|MULSD|XMM7, qword ptr [EAX*0x4 + 0x6ff79050]", "0x23100|MOVLPD|XMM5, qword ptr [EAX*0x4 + 0x6ff79050]", "0x23109|ADD|EAX, EAX"],
      "comment": "Computes base raised to the power of exponent using SSE2 SIMD instructions.\n\nThis is an optimized implementation of the pow() function from the C math library,\ndesigned for x86 processors with SSE2 support. Uses table-driven polynomial\napproximations for logarithm and exponential calculations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponent and mantissa from base using IEEE 754 bit manipulation\n2. Check for special cases: NaN, infinity, zero, negative base with non-integer exponent\n3. Compute log2(base) using table lookup and polynomial approximation\n4. Multiply by exponent to get log2(result)\n5. Compute 2^(log2(result)) using table lookup and polynomial approximation\n6. Handle overflow/underflow with scaled computation paths\n7. Return result via FPU stack (ST0)\n\nParameters:\n  dBase (double via XMM0/stack) - The base value for exponentiation\n  dExponent (double via stack offset 0xC) - The exponent value\n\nReturns:\n  double via ST0 (FPU stack) - base^exponent\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - pow(x, 0) = 1.0 for any x (including NaN)\n  - pow(1, y) = 1.0 for any y\n  - pow(x, NaN) = NaN\n  - pow(NaN, y) = NaN (y != 0)\n  - pow(+inf, y) = +inf (y > 0), 0 (y < 0)\n  - pow(-inf, y) = depends on integer parity of y\n  - pow(0, y) = 0 (y > 0), +inf (y < 0)\n  - pow(negative, non-integer) = NaN\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x7FEF = Maximum biased exponent before infinity (2046)\n  0x3FF0 = IEEE 754 exponent bias (1023) << 4\n  0x3FE7F = Exponent offset for table indexing\n  0x43F0 = Scale factor exponent for denormal handling\n  0x80000000 = Sign bit mask for doubles\n  0x7FF00000 = Infinity exponent pattern\n  0x40A0, 0x3C70 = Overflow/underflow threshold exponents\n  0x1FF80 = Exponent adjustment for scaled computation\n\nError Handling:\n  Calls ___libm_error_support with error codes:\n    0x18 = Overflow\n    0x19 = Underflow  \n    0x1A = Zero divide (0^negative)\n    0x1B = Invalid (0^0 with negative base)\n    0x1C = Domain error (negative^non-integer)\n    0x1D = Range error\n    0x3EE = Propagate NaN\n\nLookup Tables:\n  g_adPowLog2Table1 @ 0x6ff79050 - Primary log2 approximation table\n  g_adPowLog2Table2 @ 0x6ff79460 - Secondary log2 coefficients\n  g_adPowExpTable1-4 - Exponential approximation tables\n  g_adPowExpCoeffs @ 0x6ff7c0d0 - Polynomial coefficients per index",
