      "comment": "Clears FPU stack and loads negative two constant for pow() error handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Pop two values from FPU stack (FSTP ST0 x2) to clear pending operands\n2. Load extended precision -2.0 constant from g_ldNegativeTwo\n3. Check caller's error flag at [EBP-0x90]\n4. If flag is <= 0, set it to 1 to indicate error condition\n5. Return -2.0 in ST0 as error sentinel value\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses caller's stack frame via preserved EBP)\n- IMPLICIT: EBP - Preserved base pointer providing access to caller's local variables\n\nReturns:\n- float10: Always returns -2.0 (extended precision) as error indicator\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called from pow() when computing power of negative base with non-integer exponent\n- The -2.0 return value serves as a domain error sentinel\n- Error flag at [EBP-0x90] belongs to caller's stack frame (pow function)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0xffffff70: Signed offset -0x90 (caller's error flag location)\n- 0x01: Error flag set value indicating domain error occurred",
