      "comment": "Determines the integer type classification of a double-precision floating-point value.\n\nUsed by power helper functions to identify whether the exponent is an integer and,\nif so, whether it is even (divisible by 2) or odd. This enables special-case\noptimizations in power calculations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Classify the input using __fpclass to detect special values (NaN, Inf)\n2. If special value (mask 0x90: _FPCLASS_NINF | _FPCLASS_PINF | _FPCLASS_SNAN), return 0\n3. Round the value using __frnd and compare to original\n4. If not equal to its rounded form, return 0 (not an integer)\n5. Divide by 2.0 and round the result\n6. If halved value equals its rounded form, return 2 (even integer)\n7. Otherwise return 1 (odd integer)\n\nParameters:\n    dValue - The double-precision value to classify\n\nReturns:\n    0 - Value is not an integer (fractional, NaN, or infinity)\n    1 - Value is an odd integer\n    2 - Value is an even integer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n    0x90 - _FPCLASS_NINF (0x04) | _FPCLASS_PINF (0x10) | _FPCLASS_SNAN (0x80) check mask\n    0x44 - FPU status word mask for checking equality (C3 and C0 flags)\n    2.0  - Divisor stored at g_dTwo for even/odd determination\n\nCalled By:\n    __powhlp - Power helper to determine exponent type for x^n calculations",
