      "instructions": ["0x2422A|PUSH|EBP", "0x2422B|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x2422D|PUSH|ECX", "0x2422E|PUSH|ECX", "0x2422F|FLD|double ptr [EBP + 0x8]", "0x24232|PUSH|ESI", "0x24233|FCOM|double ptr [0x6ff78fe8]", "0x24239|XOR|EDX, EDX", "0x2423B|XOR|ESI, ESI", "0x2423D|FNSTSW|AX", "0x2423F|TEST|AH, 0x5", "0x24242|JP|0x6ff74246", "0x24244|FCHS|", "0x24246|MOV|EAX, 0x7ff00000", "0x2424B|FSTP|double ptr [EBP + -0x8]"],
      "comment": "Power function helper for IEEE 754 special case handling.\n\nHandles edge cases for pow(base, exponent) when base or exponent are\nspecial floating-point values (infinity, zero, NaN). This is a CRT\nlibrary function from Visual Studio 2003 Release.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reconstruct double base from split 32-bit halves (nBaseLo, nBaseHi)\n2. Compute absolute value of base for comparison\n3. Check if exponent is +Infinity (0x7FF0000000000000):\n   - If |base| > 1: result = +Infinity\n   - If |base| == 1: result = NaN (indeterminate 1^inf)\n   - If |base| < 1: result = 0\n4. Check if exponent is -Infinity (0xFFF0000000000000):\n   - If |base| > 1: result = 0\n   - If |base| == 1: result = NaN\n   - If |base| < 1: result = +Infinity\n5. Check if base is +Infinity:\n   - If exponent > 0: result = +Infinity\n   - If exponent == 0: result = 1\n   - If exponent < 0: result = 0\n6. Check if base is -Infinity:\n   - Call __d_inttype to check if exponent is odd/even integer\n   - If exponent > 0 and odd: result = -Infinity\n   - If exponent > 0 and even: result = +Infinity\n   - If exponent < 0 and odd: result = -0\n   - If exponent < 0 and even: result = 0\n   - If exponent == 0: result = 1\n7. Store result and return status\n\nParameters:\n  nBaseLo - Low 32 bits of base value (IEEE 754 double mantissa low)\n  nBaseHi - High 32 bits of base value (IEEE 754 double sign/exp/mantissa high)\n  dExponent - Exponent value for power operation\n  pdResult - Output pointer to store computed result\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Normal case (no special handling applied, caller should compute normally)\n  1 - Special case handled, result stored in *pdResult (indeterminate form)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - 1^(+/-inf) = NaN (indeterminate form, returns 1)\n  - (+inf)^0 = 1\n  - (-inf)^0 = 1\n  - 0^(+inf) = 0\n  - 0^(-inf) = +inf\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7FF00000 - IEEE 754 +Infinity exponent field (high 32 bits)\n  0xFFF00000 - IEEE 754 -Infinity exponent field (high 32 bits, signed)\n  0x41 - FPU status: C0|C3 flags (equal or unordered)\n  0x05 - FPU status: C0|C2 flags (less than or parity)",
