      "instructions": ["0x2444A|PUSH|EBP", "0x2444B|MOV|EBP, ESP", "0x2444D|AND|ESP, 0xfffffff0", "0x24450|SUB|ESP, 0x84", "0x24456|MOV|EAX, [0x6ff7e990]", "0x2445B|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0x80], EAX", "0x24462|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [EBP + 0x10]", "0x24465|MOVZX|ECX, word ptr [EAX]", "0x24468|PUSH|EBX", "0x24469|PUSH|ESI", "0x2446A|MOV|ESI, dword ptr [EBP + 0xc]", "0x2446D|MOV|EAX, dword ptr [ESI]", "0x2446F|DEC|EAX", "0x24470|PUSH|EDI", "0x24471|MOV|dword ptr [ESP + 0xc], ECX"],
      "comment": "FPU Exception Handler (Visual Studio 2003 CRT __87except)\n\nProcesses floating-point unit (FPU) exceptions by mapping exception types to IEEE 754\nexception flags, invoking user-defined exception handlers, and raising structured\nexceptions if the handler does not suppress the error. Implements the x87 FPU exception\ndispatch mechanism for MSVC C runtime.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save stack canary for buffer overflow detection\n2. Extract FPU status word from pwStatusWord parameter\n3. Read exception type from pExceptionState[0] and map to IEEE 754 exception mask:\n   - Type 1 (Invalid): Overflow exception (0x08)\n   - Type 2 (Denormal): Underflow exception (0x04)\n   - Type 3 (Divide-by-zero): Inexact exception (0x11)\n   - Type 4 (Overflow): Invalid operation (0x12)\n   - Type 5 (Underflow): Overflow exception (0x08)\n   - Type 7: Set exception type to 1 (Invalid)\n   - Type 8: Stack fault (0x10)\n4. Call __handle_exc with mapped exception flags and operand pointer\n5. If handler returns zero (unhandled):\n   a. For exception codes 0x10, 0x16, 0x1D: copy operand and set precision bits\n   b. Otherwise: clear inexact exception bit\n   c. Call __raise_exc to generate structured exception\n6. Restore FPU control word via __ctrlfp\n7. If exception type is not stack fault (8) and exception handling is disabled:\n   a. Call GetUnitX to validate exception state\n   b. If validation fails, call ProcessParameterValue\n8. Verify stack canary and return\n\nParameters:\n  nExceptionCode (int) - Windows exception code from exception record\n      0x10: FLT_DENORMAL_OPERAND\n      0x16: FLT_OVERFLOW\n      0x1D: FLT_UNDERFLOW\n  pExceptionState (int*) - Pointer to FPU exception state structure:\n      [0] Exception type (1-8)\n      [2-3] Input operand (double)\n      [4-5] Result operand (double)\n      [6-7] Output location (double*)\n  pwStatusWord (ushort*) - Pointer to FPU status word containing exception flags\n\nReturns:\n  void - Does not return a value\n  Side effects: May raise structured exception via __raise_exc\n  May modify FPU control word and exception state\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x04 - FE_UNDERFLOW (underflow exception flag)\n  0x08 - FE_OVERFLOW (overflow exception flag)\n  0x10 - FE_STACKFAULT (stack fault exception flag)\n  0x11 - FE_INEXACT (inexact result exception flag)\n  0x12 - FE_INVALID (invalid operation exception flag)\n  0xFFFFFFE3 - Mask to clear precision control bits (bits 2-4)\n  0x03 - Extended precision (64-bit mantissa)\n  0xFFFFFFFE - Mask to clear inexact exception bit (bit 0)",
      "tags": ["STRUCT_Inventory", "PARAM_3", "CALLER_1", "STRUCT_UnitAny", "CALLEE_6", "STRUCT_Control", "STRUCT_PlayerData"]
