      "comment": "Classifies IEEE 754 double-precision floating-point value into category.\n\nStandard C library function (_fpclass) from Visual Studio 2003 runtime.\nReturns classification code indicating the type of floating-point value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponent bits from the double value (bits 52-62)\n2. If exponent is 0x7FF (all ones), value is special (INF, NaN):\n   a. Call __sptype to distinguish infinity from NaN types\n   b. Return 1=SNAN, 2=QNAN, 4=NINF/PINF, or 0x200=INF based on __sptype result\n3. If exponent is zero, check for denormalized or zero:\n   a. If mantissa bits are non-zero, value is denormalized\n   b. Return 0x80 (positive denormal) or 0x10 (negative denormal)\n4. If value equals zero (compare with g_dZero constant):\n   a. Return 0x40 (positive zero) or 0x20 (negative zero)\n5. Otherwise value is normal:\n   a. Return 0x100 (positive normal) or 0x08 (negative normal)\n\nParameters:\n  dValue - double precision floating-point value to classify\n\nReturns:\n  _FPCLASS_SNAN  (0x01) - Signaling NaN\n  _FPCLASS_QNAN  (0x02) - Quiet NaN\n  _FPCLASS_NINF  (0x04) - Negative infinity\n  _FPCLASS_PINF  (0x200) - Positive infinity\n  _FPCLASS_NN    (0x08) - Negative normal\n  _FPCLASS_PN    (0x100) - Positive normal\n  _FPCLASS_ND    (0x10) - Negative denormal\n  _FPCLASS_PD    (0x80) - Positive denormal\n  _FPCLASS_NZ    (0x20) - Negative zero\n  _FPCLASS_PZ    (0x40) - Positive zero\n\nIEEE 754 Double Layout:\n  Bit 63:      Sign bit (0=positive, 1=negative)\n  Bits 52-62:  Exponent (11 bits, biased by 1023)\n  Bits 0-51:   Mantissa/Significand (52 bits)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7FF0 - Exponent mask for bits 52-62 (after shift)\n  0x7FF0000000000000 - Full exponent mask for 64-bit double\n  0x8000000000000000 - Sign bit mask\n  0xFFFFF00000000 - Upper mantissa bits mask\n\nPhantom Variables:\n  local_c (Stack[-0xc]:8) - FPU stack temp for __sptype call parameter",
